cess to vCenter — no prior authentication needed —"]</data><data key="node_source_ids">["S44"]</data></node><node id="e_d7a9a8240245a715"><data key="node_label">An authentication issue was addressed with improved state management. This issue is fixed in macOS Sequoia 15.7.9, macOS Sonoma 14.8.9, macOS Tahoe 26.6.1. An attacker on the network may be able to authenticate to Screen Sharing without valid credentials</data><data key="node_entity_type">Description</data><data key="node_aliases">["An authentication issue was addressed with improved state management. This issue is fixed in macOS Sequoia 15.7.9, macOS Sonoma 14.8.9, macOS Tahoe 26.6.1. An attacker on the network may be able to authenticate to Screen Sharing without valid credentials"]</data><data key="node_source_ids">["S05"]</data></node><node id="e_d4cff6070f136c90"><data key="node_label">Analysts</data><data key="node_entity_type">Mention</data><data key="node_aliases">["Analysts"]</data><data key="node_source_ids">["S50", "S51", "S52"]</data></node><node id="e_b5b88d276861e80d"><data key="node_label">Analyzed</data><data key="node_entity_type">Value</data><data key="node_aliases">["Analyzed"]</data><data key="node_source_ids">["S02", "S03", "S04", "S05", "S06"]</data></node><node id="e_40c6b1966ffc355e"><data key="node_label">Apache/Nginx/app servers</data><data key="node_entity_type">Mention</data><data key="node_aliases">["Apache/Nginx/app servers"]</data><data key="node_source_ids">["S57"]</data></node><node id="e_a7153ecce496b016"><data key="node_label">Apple</data><data key="node_entity_type">Mention</data><data key="node_aliases">["Apple"]</data><data key="node_source_ids">["S15", "S17", "S55", "S56"]</data></node><node id="e_cd9606e3c678f437"><data key="node_label">Apple</data><data key="node_entity_type">Vendor</data><data key="node_aliases">["Apple"]</data><data key="node_source_ids">["S05"]</data></node><node id="e_d2d5965045d52d61"><data key="node_label">Apple heeft de state management mechanismen verbeterd om correcte validatie van inloggegevens</data><data key="node_entity_type">Mention</data><data key="node_aliases">["Apple heeft de state management mechanismen verbeterd om correcte validatie van inloggegevens"]</data><data key="node_source_ids">["S14"]</data></node><node id="e_a2792cb533a4b3bf"><data key="node_label">Apple macOS</data><data key="node_entity_type">Mention</data><data key="node_aliases">["Apple macOS"]</data><data key="node_source_ids">["S32"]</data></node><node id="e_4fdeccaa7798cef2"><data key="node_label">Apple security</data><data key="node_entity_type">Mention</data><data key="node_aliases">["Apple security"]</data><data key="node_source_ids">["S15", "S55", "S56"]</data></node><node id="e_8ebcaa1932cfd664"><data key="node_label">Apple security documents</data><data key="node_entity_type">Mention</data><data key="node_aliases">["Apple security documents"]</data><data key="node_source_ids">["S15", "S55", "S56"]</data></node><node id="e_9b28c50be6e7da88"><data key="node_label">Apply mitigations in accordance with vendor instructions, ensuring compliance with CISA’s BOD 26-04 Prioritizing Security Updates Based on Risk (see URL in Notes) guidance and CISA’s “Forensics Triage Requirements” (see URL in Notes). Follow applicable BOD 26-04 guidance for cloud services or discontinue use of the product if mitigations are unavailable. Stakeholders are responsible for evaluating each asset's internet exposure and ensuring adherence to BOD 26-04 patching guidelines</data><data key="node_entity_type">Mitigation</data><data key="node_aliases">["Apply mitigations in accordance with vendor instructions, ensuring compliance with CISA’s BOD 26-04 Prioritizing Security Updates Based on Risk (see URL in Notes) guidance and CISA’s “Forensics Triage Requirements” (see URL in Notes). Follow applicable BOD 26-04 guidance for cloud services or discontinue use of the product if mitigations are unavailable. Stakeholders are responsible for evaluating each asset's internet exposure and ensuring adherence to BOD 26-04 patching guidelines"]</data><data key="node_source_ids">["S02", "S03", "S04", "S05"]</data></node><node id="e_1d1ee485d508a2e3"><data key="node_label">Apply network-level controls</data><data key="node_entity_type">Mention</data><data key="node_aliases">["Apply network-level controls"]</data><data key="node_source_ids">["S17"]</data></node><node id="e_00b6e3067782d4ec"><data key="node_label">April</data><data key="node_entity_type">Mention</data><data key="node_aliases">["April"]</data><data key="node_source_ids">["S45"]</data></node><node id="e_980e49a4f0d05bbe"><data key="node_label">April 2026 Patch</data><data key="node_entity_type">Mention</data><data key="node_aliases">["April 2026 Patch"]</data><data key="node_source_ids">["S45"]</data></node><node id="e_34d1fc771dee0496"><data key="node_label">April 2026 security</data><data key="node_entity_type">Mention</data><data key="node_aliases">["April 2026 security"]</data><data key="node_source_ids">["S45"]</data></node><node id="e_ce88384c05221555"><data key="node_label">April 2026 security updates</data><data key="node_entity_type">Mention</data><data key="node_aliases">["April 2026 security updates"]</data><data key="node_source_ids">["S46"]</data></node><node id="e_a1963641021a625a"><data key="node_label">Assessing CVSS metrics</data><data key="node_entity_type">Mention</data><data key="node_aliases">["Assessing CVSS metrics"]</data><data key="node_source_ids">["S50"]</data></node><node id="e_4bf310a0cf7b17dd"><data key="node_label">Asset</data><data key="node_entity_type">Mention</data><data key="node_aliases">["Asset"]</data><data key="node_source_ids">["S51"]</data></node><node id="e_5a0c30db9530a8c8"><data key="node_label">Asset Class</data><data key="node_entity_type">Mention</data><data key="node_aliases">["Asset Class"]</data><data key="node_source_ids">["S51"]</data></node><node id="e_76edc2bdd4022652"><data key="node_label">Attack Complexity</