.rapid7.com/blog/post/ra-microsoft-sharepoint-jwt-token-authentication-bypass-cve-2026-55040/</data><data key="edge_chunk_id">S08_C10</data><data key="edge_json_path">None</data><data key="edge_evidence">We then begin to construct the malicious JWT</data><data key="edge_extraction_method">minie</data><data key="edge_polarity">positive</data><data key="edge_modality">asserted</data></edge><edge id="oe_061ab6436a0b8e94" source="e_7cf0100f3e7614f4" target="e_b0f325660b971761"><data key="edge_predicate_raw">contains</data><data key="edge_assertion_id">a_9406236b2d4719a0</data><data key="edge_source_id">S08</data><data key="edge_source_url">https://www.rapid7.com/blog/post/ra-microsoft-sharepoint-jwt-token-authentication-bypass-cve-2026-55040/</data><data key="edge_chunk_id">S08_C10</data><data key="edge_json_path">None</data><data key="edge_evidence">The audience (aud) claim contains the target systems hostname (win-b0i6kv698ls) and realm</data><data key="edge_extraction_method">heuristic</data><data key="edge_polarity">positive</data><data key="edge_modality">asserted</data></edge><edge id="oe_2ab7719316aa310e" source="e_be8e7b23b5ad882e" target="e_e41dcba38a6a6f27"><data key="edge_predicate_raw">represent</data><data key="edge_assertion_id">a_ee5ee6bffc88949b</data><data key="edge_source_id">S08</data><data key="edge_source_url">https://www.rapid7.com/blog/post/ra-microsoft-sharepoint-jwt-token-authentication-bypass-cve-2026-55040/</data><data key="edge_chunk_id">S08_C10</data><data key="edge_json_path">None</data><data key="edge_evidence">The Name ID (nameid) represent the SharePoint user we will identify as, in our example we use a SID of S-1-5-21-4203888158-2793536450-3921675298-500 which represent the domain admin that we want to authenticate as using the urn:office:idp:activedirectory identity provider</data><data key="edge_extraction_method">minie</data><data key="edge_polarity">positive</data><data key="edge_modality">asserted</data></edge><edge id="oe_466630ee