ng you can access the domain controller) than brute forcing potential UPN's, which is best suited to manual reconnaissance</data><data key="edge_extraction_method">minie</data><data key="edge_polarity">positive</data><data key="edge_modality">possible</data></edge><edge id="oe_32f0ce0a22f4b56a" source="e_3da4c5809c640a71" target="e_c7617d124b5e1f39"><data key="edge_predicate_raw">is reliable in</data><data key="edge_assertion_id">a_6a04d35fbe73b315</data><data key="edge_source_id">S08</data><data key="edge_source_url">https://www.rapid7.com/blog/post/ra-microsoft-sharepoint-jwt-token-authentication-bypass-cve-2026-55040/</data><data key="edge_chunk_id">S08_C10</data><data key="edge_json_path">None</data><data key="edge_evidence">However, discovering a valid SID is more reliable in an automated scenario (assuming you can access the domain controller) than brute forcing potential UPN's, which is best suited to manual reconnaissance</data><data key="edge_extraction_method">minie</data><data key="edge_polarity">positive</data><data key="edge_modality">possible</data></edge><edge id="oe_248747a5a317e5bf" source="e_5c980ac08d8e06db" target="e_f9f80c5f32da6ea9"><data key="edge_predicate_raw">access</data><data key="edge_assertion_id">a_dc1b3f9cbbcb202b</data><data key="edge_source_id">S08</data><data key="edge_source_url">https://www.rapid7.com/blog/post/ra-microsoft-sharepoint-jwt-token-authentication-bypass-cve-2026-55040/</data><data key="edge_chunk_id">S08_C10</data><data key="edge_json_path">None</data><data key="edge_evidence">However, discovering a valid SID is more reliable in an automated scenario (assuming you can access the domain controller) than brute forcing potential UPN's, which is best suited to manual reconnaissance</data><data key="edge_extraction_method">minie</data><data key="edge_polarity">positive</data><data key="edge_modality">possible</data></edge><edge id="oe_a1086f9824155a4b" source="e_ad16450d4d7b98f8" target="e_4d349aae7d59df71"><data key="edge_predicate_raw">be Inspecting</data><data key="edge_assertion_id">a_d74cc7af699abe03</data><data key="edge_source_id">S08</data><data key="edge_source_url">https://www.rapid7.com/blog/post/ra-microsoft-sharepoint-jwt-token-authentication-bypass-cve-2026-55040/</data><data key="edge_chunk_id">S08_C10</data><data key="edge_json_path">None</data><data key="edge_evidence">Inspecting the inner actortoken token, it will have a header as shown below, which includes the x5t value i_gz5qfYp5YPWAK1__0YhZnipLI corresponding to the SharePoint server's STS signing certificate</data><data key="edge_extraction_method">minie</data><data key="edge_polarity">positive</data><data key="edge_modality">asserted</data></edge><edge id="oe_62cba2382762e6e3" source="e_ad16450d4d7b98f8" target="e_32bf088eb1f5140a"><data key="edge_predicate_raw">have header</data><data key="edge_assertion_id">a_efa6fa7a16221372</data><data key="edge_source_id">S08</data><data key="edge_source_url">https://www.rapid7.com/blog/post/ra-microsoft-sharepoint-jwt-token-authentication-bypass-cve-2026-55040/</data><data key="edge_chunk_id">S08_C10</data><data key="edge_json_path">None</data><data key="edge_evidence">Inspecting the inner actortoken token, it will have a header as shown below, which includes the x5t value i_gz5qfYp5YPWAK1__0YhZnipLI corresponding to the SharePoint server's STS signing certificate</data><data key="edge_extraction_method">minie</data><data key="edge_polarity">positive</data><data key="edge_modality">asserted</data></edge><edge id="oe_3bc06d04a63726c5" source="e_62ce29afba0f48d9" target="e_775df4fb4f8f669f"><data key="edge_predicate_raw">is same as issuer of</data><data key="edge_assertion_id">a_834a29373db354f0</data><data key="edge_source_id">S08</data><data key="edge_source_url">https://www.rapid7.com/blog/post/ra-microsoft-sharepoint-jwt-token-authentication-bypass-cve-2026-55040/</data><data key="edge_chunk_id">S08_C11</data><data key="edge_json_path">None</data><data key="edge_evidence">Note the nameid of this token is the same as the issuer of the STS certificate, this allows a call to SPJsonWebSecurityBaseTokenHandlerV2.ValidateActorIsSelfIssuer to succeed</data><data key="edge_extraction_method">minie</data><data key="edge_polarity">positive</data><data key="edge_modality">asserted</data></edge><edge id="oe_059a07e854c6a133" source="e_e163460c91338b08" target="e_8264f38f98ed0f54"><data key="edge_predicate_raw">allows call to</data><data key="edge_assertion_id">a_2882bb725835a0b9</data><data key="edge_source_id">S08</data><data key="edge_source_url">https://www.rapid7.com/blog/post/ra-microsoft-sharepoint-jwt-token-authentication-bypass-cve-2026-55040/</data><data key="edge_chunk_id">S08_C11</data><data key="edge_json_path">None</data><data key="edge_evidence">Note the nameid of this token is the same as the issuer of the STS certificate, this allows a call to SPJsonWebSecurityBaseTokenHandlerV2.ValidateActorIsSelfIssuer to succeed</data><data key="edge_extraction_method">minie</data><data key="edge_polarity">positive</data><data key="edge_modality">asserted</data></edge><edge id="oe_0c1d6cc9594f964e" source="e_e163460c91338b08" target="e_9329b224df96eb01"><data key="edge_predicate_raw">allows call to</data><data key="edge_assertion_id">a_14c1ee61397bd893</data><data key="edge_source_id">S08</data><data key="edge_source_url">https://www.rapid7.com/blog/post/ra-microsoft-sharepoint-jwt-token-authentication-bypass-cve-2026-55040/</data><data key="edge_chunk_id">S08_C11</data><data key="edge_json_path">None</data><data key="edge_evidence">Note the nameid of this token is the same as the issuer of the STS certificate, this allows a call to SPJsonWebSecurityBaseTokenHandlerV2.ValidateActorIsSelfIssuer to succeed</data><data key="edge_extraction_method">minie</data><data key="edge_polarity">positive</data><data key="edge_modality">asserted</data></edge><edge id="oe_63ea4127e4609c74" source="e_be74ffef073dc8d3" target="e_6d930bf9f79f5d74"><data key="edge_predicate_raw">be Constructing</data><data key="edge_assertion_id">a_90c20026775bf646</data><data key="edge_source_id">S08</data><data key="edge_source_url">https://www.rapid7.com/blog/post/ra-microsoft-sharepoint-jwt-token-authentication-bypass-cve-2026-55040/</data><data key="edge_chunk_id">S08_C11</data><data key="edge_json_path">None</data><data key="edge_evidence">Constructing the above JWT, we can base64 encode it as a bearer token and make a request to an authenticated endpoint, such as /_api/web/currentuser and prove we are authenticating as a SharePoint user</data><data key="edge_extraction_method">minie</data><data key="edge_polarity">positive</data><data key="edge_modality">possible</data></edge><edge id="oe_4c1249a650e960e3" source="e_be74ffef073dc8d3" target="e_262dca47d4b181dc"><data key="edge_predicate_raw">base64</data><data key="edge_assertion_id">a_922241cc9b53bb92</data><data key="edge_source_id">S08</data><data key="edge_source_url">https://www.rapid7.com/blog/post/ra-microsoft-sharepoint-jwt-token-authentication-bypass-cve-2026-55040/</data><data key="edge_chunk_id">S08_C11</data><data key="edge_json_path">None</data><data key="edge_evidence">Constructing the above JWT, we can base64 encode it as a bearer token and make a request to an authenticated endpoint, such as /_api/web/currentuser and prove we are authenticating as a SharePoint user</data><data key="edge_extraction_method">minie</data><data key="edge_polarity">positive</data><data key="edge_modality">possible</data></edge><edge id="oe_c960ddf92e77905b" source="e_be74ffef073dc8d3" target="e_3f1f902e60091908"><data key="edge_predicate_raw">begin to</data><data key="edge_assertion_id">a_3f2a489c30fae2ab</data><data key="edge_source_id">S08</data><data key="edge_source_url">https://www.rapid7.com/blog/post/ra-microsoft-sharepoint-jwt-token-authentication-bypass-cve-2026-55040/</data><data key="edge_chunk_id">S08_C12</data><data key="edge_json_path">None</data><data key="edge_evidence">Whose response contains a new FormDigestValue we can begin to use</data><data key="edge_extraction_method">minie</data><data key="edge_polarity">positive</data><data key="edge_modality">possible</data></edge><edge id="oe_262b6f882a4954e7" source="e_950a3850a5a61adb" target="e_9155a32464fef75c"><data key="edge_predicate_raw">contains</data><data key="edge_assertion_id">a_8e4ef50087b98e62</data><data key="edge_source_id">S08</data><data key="edge_source_url">https://www.rapid7.com/blog/post/ra-microsoft-sharepoint-jwt-token-authentication-bypass-cve-2026-55040/</data><data key="edge_chunk_id">S08_C12</data><data key="edge_json_path">None</data><data key="edge_evidence">Whose response contains a new FormDigestValue we can begin to use</data><data key="edge_extraction_method">minie</data><data key="edge_polarity">positive</data><data key="edge_modality">possible</data></edge><edge id="oe_6b3eebc55f918d68" source="e_a3190aabb6292e9a" target="e_01e25e232b554862"><data key="edge_predicate_raw">exploit</data><data key="edge_assertion_id">a_e04dab42cc4254e9</data><data key="edge_source_id">S08</data><data key="edge_source_url">https://www.rapid7.com/blog/post/ra-microsoft-sharepoint-jwt-token-authentication-bypass-cve-2026-55040/</data><data key="edge_chunk_id">S08_C13</data><data key="edge_json_path">None</data><data key="edge_evidence">Join Rapid7's Stephen Fewer and Douglas McKee on Thursday, August 13 to walk through the full exploit chain, actionable next steps and more</data><data key="edge_extraction_method">heuristic</data><data key="edge_polarity">positive</data><data key="edge_modality">asserted</data></edge><edge id="oe_caccfc74f3b63b74" source="e_1e7e8c1028226135" target="e_2da887c9a54f6ac7"><data key="edge_predicate_raw">be affecting</data><data key="edge_assertion_id">a_ad7734dbd91a685e</data><data key="edge_source_id">S09</data><data key="edge_source_url">https://www.rapid7.com/blog/post/ra-microsoft-sharepoint-remote-code-execution-cve-2026-63520/</data><data key="edge_chunk_id">S09_C01</data><data key="edge_json_path">None</data><data key="edge_evidence">On August 11, 2026, Rapid7 and Microsoft disclosed CVE-2026-63520, a remote code execution (RCE) vulnerability affecting Microsoft SharePoint</data><data key="edge_extraction_method">minie</data><data key="edge_polarity">positive</data><data key="edge_modality">asserted</data></edge><edge id="oe_03ed79fe4e0724a8" source="e_be74ffef073dc8d3" target="e_8914ea73282ff98a"><data key="edge_predicate_raw">are publishing technical analysis of CVE-2026-63520</data><data key="edge_assertion_id">a_d6db46aea450049b</data><data key="edge_source_id">S09</data><data key="edge_source_url">https://www.rapid7.com/blog/post/ra-microsoft-sharepoint-remote-code-execution-cve-2026-63520/</data><data key="edge_chunk_id">S09_C01</data><data key="edge_json_path">None</data><data key="edge_evidence">Today we are publishing a technical analysis of CVE-2026-63520</data><data key="edge_extraction_method">minie</data><data key="edge_polarity">positive</data><data key="edge_modality">asserted</data></edge><edge id="oe_fcffb8638d8653d4" source="e_be74ffef073dc8d3" target="e_fbfb70a00355d68e"><data key="edge_predicate_raw">are publishing technical analysis of</data><data key="edge_assertion_id">a_ee9f7a98cf05942e</data><data key="edge_source_id">S09</data><data key="edge_source_url">https://www.rapid7.com/blog/post/ra-microsoft-sharepoint-remote-code-execution-cve-2026-63520/</data><data key="edge_chunk_id">S09_C01</data><data key="edge_json_path">None</data><data key="edge_evidence">Today we are publishing a technical analysis of CVE-2026-63520</data><data key="edge_extraction_method">minie</data><data key="edge_polarity">positive</data><data key="edge_modality">asserted</data></edge><edge id="oe_d7304f98292b4c02" source="e_7a95d1cf0f65f875" target="e_fbfb70a00355d68e"><data key="edge_predicate_raw">has been expedited as third party has published details of</data><data key="edge_assertion_id">a_29bed7d546ba81c8</data><data key="edge_source_id">S09</data><data key="edge_source_url">https://www.rapid7.com/blog/post/ra-microsoft-sharepoint-remote-code-execution-cve-2026-63520/</data><data key="edge_chunk_id">S09_C01</data><data key="edge_json_path">None</data><data key="edge_evidence">This analysis was originally scheduled for publication 30 days after disclosure; however, as a third party has published details of CVE-2026-63520, our timeline has been expedited</data><data key="edge_extraction_method">minie</data><data key="edge_polarity">positive</data><data key="edge_modality">asserted</data></edge><edge id="oe_72ae0ac578ac60ff" source="e_2d6bfbad72a7f245" target="e_090a49403d237e84"><data key="edge_predicate_raw">be execute arbitrary code on</data><data key="edge_assertion_id">a_760f9081288385c6</data><data key="edge_source_id">S09</data><data key="edge_source_url">https://www.rapid7.com/blog/post/ra-microsoft-sharepoint-remote-code-execution-cve-2026-63520/</data><data key="edge_chunk_id">S09_C01</data><data key="edge_json_path">None</data><data key="edge_evidence">A remote authenticated attacker can leverage CVE-2026-63520 to execute arbitrary code on a vulnerable SharePoint server with the privileges of the SharePoint Site’s service account</data><data key="edge_extraction_method">minie</data><data key="edge_polarity">positive</data><data key="edge_modality">possible</data></edge><edge id="oe_59d0a42607ac5d97" source="e_df8fab3acbb5e0a1" target="e_0ca0f00333e5caf7"><data key="edge_predicate_raw">is unauthenticated RCE against</data><data key="edge_assertion_id">a_5e134f5ab1d54280</data><data key="edge_source_id">S09</data><data key="edge_source_url">https://www.rapid7.com/blog/post/ra-microsoft-sharepoint-remote-code-execution-cve-2026-63520/</data><data key="edge_chunk_id">S09_C01</data><data key="edge_json_path">None</data><data key="edge_evidence">When combined with the authentication bypass, CVE-2026-55040, the resulting exploit chain is unauthenticated RCE against a vulnerable SharePoint server</data><data key="edge_extraction_method">minie</data><data key="edge_polarity">positive</data><data key="edge_modality">asserted</data></edge><edge id="oe_92def04fd8e88f51" source="e_be74ffef073dc8d3" target="e_82b91fdd0e399842"><data key="edge_predicate_raw">have exploited issue by</data><data key="edge_assertion_id">a_9c791c96742ebfbf</data><data key="edge_source_id">S09</data><data key="edge_source_url">https://www.rapid7.com/blog/post/ra-microsoft-sharepoint-remote-code-execution-cve-2026-63520/</data><data key="edge_chunk_id">S09_C01</data><data key="edge_json_path">None</data><data key="edge_evidence">When comparing the two analysis of CVE-2026-63520, we can see how we have exploited the issue by leveraging a Database Line-of-Business (LOB) system and an ObjectDataProvider based gadget chain, whilst the VulnCheck analysis has exploited the issue by leveraging a DotNetAssembly LOB system and a LosFormatter based gadget chain</data><data key="edge_extraction_method">minie</data><data key="edge_polarity">positive</data><data key="edge_modality">possible</data></edge><edge id="oe_6b1cbbf03a45277f" source="e_be74ffef073dc8d3" target="e_11f46ecc3d6429b6"><data key="edge_predicate_raw">have exploited issue by</data><data key="edge_assertion_id">a_4e4e92f2c863f662</data><data key="edge_source_id">S09</data><data key="edge_source_url">https://www.rapid7.com/blog/post/ra-microsoft-sharepoint-remote-code-execution-cve-2026-63520/</data><data key="edge_chunk_id">S09_C01</data><data key="edge_json_path">None</data><data key="edge_evidence">When comparing the two analysis of CVE-2026-63520, we can see how we have exploited the issue by leveraging a Database Line-of-Business (LOB) system and an ObjectDataProvider based gadget chain, whilst the VulnCheck analysis has exploited the issue by leveraging a DotNetAssembly LOB system and a LosFormatter based gadget chain</data><data key="edge_extraction_method">minie</data><data key="edge_polarity">positive</data><data key="edge_modality">possible</data></edge><edge id="oe_a27aa91013365afd" source="e_be74ffef073dc8d3" target="e_c7a7735bf61b8084"><data key="edge_predicate_raw">have exploited</data><data key="edge_assertion_id">a_c474b7a9c63e9ea9</data><data key="edge_source_id">S09</data><data key="edge_source_url">https://www.rapid7.com/blog/post/ra-microsoft-sharepoint-remote-code-execution-cve-2026-63520/</data><data key="edge_chunk_id">S09_C01</data><data key="edge_json_path">None</data><data key="edge_evidence">When comparing the two analysis of CVE-2026-63520, we can see how we have exploited the issue by leveraging a Database Line-of-Business (LOB) system and an ObjectDataProvider based gadget chain, whilst the VulnCheck analysis has exploited the issue by leveraging a DotNetAssembly LOB system and a LosFormatter based gadget chain</data><data key="edge_extraction_method">minie</data><data key="edge_polarity">positive</data><data key="edge_modality">possible</data></edge><edge id="oe_09692f741f530083" source="e_4e650f44977b3e60" target="e_7b90f8e055178aed"><data key="edge_predicate_raw">has exploited issue by</data><data key="edge_assertion_id">a_26c07c81dc019dd5</data><data key="edge_source_id">S09</data><data key="edge_source_url">https://www.rapid7.com/blog/post/ra-microsoft-sharepoint-remote-code-execution-cve-2026-63520/</data><data key="edge_chunk_id">S09_C01</data><data key="edge_json_path">None</data><data key="edge_evidence">When comparing the two analysis of CVE-2026-63520, we can see how we have exploited the issue by leveraging a Database Line-of-Business (LOB) system and an ObjectDataProvider based gadget chain, whilst the VulnCheck analysis has exploited the issue by leveraging a DotNetAssembly LOB system and a LosFormatter based gadget chain</data><data key="edge_extraction_method">minie</data><data key="edge_polarity">positive</data><data key="edge_modality">possible</data></edge><edge id="oe_97be6e64c4aa7375" source="e_4e650f44977b3e60" target="e_837e5805db9952ca"><data key="edge_predicate_raw">has exploited issue by</data><data key="edge_assertion_id">a_88c3fe9ad1311f86</data><data key="edge_source_id">S09</data><data key="edge_source_url">https://www.rapid7.com/blog/post/ra-microsoft-sharepoint-remote-code-execution-cve-2026-63520/</data><data key="edge_chunk_id">S09_C01</data><data key="edge_json_path">None</data><data key="edge_evidence">When comparing the two analysis of CVE-2026-63520, we can see how we have exploited the issue by leveraging a Database Line-of-Business (LOB) system and an ObjectDataProvider based gadget chain, whilst the VulnCheck analysis has exploited the issue by leveraging a DotNetAssembly LOB system and a LosFormatter based gadget chain</data><data key="edge_extraction_method">minie</data><data key="edge_polarity">positive</data><data key="edge_modality">possible</data></edge><edge id="oe_1d6fb16eaa6c7364" source="e_4e650f44977b3e60" target="e_c7a7735bf61b8084"><data key="edge_predicate_raw">has exploited</data><data key="edge_assertion_id">a_3748749d1cc0e968</data><data key="edge_source_id">S09</data><data key="edge_source_url">https://www.rapid7.com/blog/post/ra-microsoft-sharepoint-remote-code-execution-cve-2026-63520/</data><data key="edge_chunk_id">S09_C01</data><data key="edge_json_path">None</data><data key="edge_evidence">When comparing the two analysis of CVE-2026-63520, we can see how we have exploited the issue by leveraging a Database Line-of-Business (LOB) system and an ObjectDataProvider based gadget chain, whilst the VulnCheck analysis has exploited the issue by leveraging a DotNetAssembly LOB system and a LosFormatter based gadget chain</data><data key="edge_extraction_method">minie</data><data key="edge_polarity">positive</data><data key="edge_modality">possible</data></edge><edge id="oe_567ac6b997b126f8" source="e_086aa5bfb79357b0" target="e_c317df3fa3fa4265"><data key="edge_predicate_raw">account for this when</data><data key="edge_assertion_id">a_37a8e752d6d100b0</data><data key="edge_source_id">S09</data><data key="edge_source_url">https://www.rapid7.com/blog/post/ra-microsoft-sharepoint-remote-code-execution-cve-2026-63520/</data><data key="edge_chunk_id">S09_C01</data><data key="edge_json_path">None</data><data key="edge_evidence">Defenders should account for this when detecting CVE-2026-63520</data><data key="edge_extraction_method">minie</data><data key="edge_polarity">positive</data><data key="edge_modality">asserted</data></edge><edge id="oe_360268a1c55b7203" source="e_086aa5bfb79357b0" target="e_e163460c91338b08"><data key="edge_predicate_raw">account for</data><data key="edge_assertion_id">a_04fb86e1f125279d</data><data key="edge_source_id">S09</data><data key="edge_source_url">https://www.rapid7.com/blog/post/ra-microsoft-sharepoint-remote-code-execution-cve-2026-63520/</data><data key="edge_chunk_id">S09_C01</data><data key="edge_json_path">None</data><data key="edge_evidence">Defenders should account for this when detecting CVE-2026-63520</data><data key="edge_extraction_method">minie</data><data key="edge_polarity">positive</data><data key="edge_modality">asserted</data></edge><edge id="oe_a01944e709c62db9" source="e_592be3cc99760f9e" target="e_03c649f5f3e7a544"><data key="edge_predicate_raw">exists in</data><data key="edge_assertion_id">a_e8539c4766e663a6</data><data key="edge_source_id">S09</data><data key="edge_source_url">https://www.rapid7.com/blog/post/ra-microsoft-sharepoint-remote-code-execution-cve-2026-63520/</data><data key="edge_chunk_id">S09_C01</data><data key="edge_json_path">None</data><data key="edge_evidence">An RCE vulnerability exists in the Microsoft SharePoint Business Data Connectivity (BDC) subsystem</data><data key="edge_extraction_method">minie</data><data key="edge_polarity">positive</data><data key="edge_modality">asserted</data></edge><edge id="oe_77129be2be37445a" source="e_e163460c91338b08" target="e_ae8d6edb17b6529d"><data key="edge_predicate_raw">is due to</data><data key="edge_assertion_id">a_a3e5e27749ebd9dc</data><data key="edge_source_id">S09</data><data key="edge_source_url">https://www.rapid7.com/blog/post/ra-microsoft-sharepoint-remote-code-execution-cve-2026-63520/</data><data key="edge_chunk_id">S09_C01</data><data key="edge_json_path">None</data><data key="edge_evidence">This is due to an unrestricted .NET type instantiation and property-setting primitive in the DbTypeReflector class, which resolves arbitrary assembly-qualified type names from BDC model XML without any allowlist or safety enforcement</data><data key="edge_extraction_method">minie</data><data key="edge_polarity">negative</data><data key="edge_modality">asserted</data></edge><edge id="oe_7788a10fbf96b139" source="e_985cab375dab17b5" target="e_334e3fd559093d72"><data key="edge_predicate_raw">resolves arbitrary assembly-qualified type names from</data><data key="edge_assertion_id">a_56a75e18bd0a7d80</data><data key="edge_source_id">S09</data><data key="edge_source_url">https://www.rapid7.com/blog/post/ra-microsoft-sharepoint-remote-code-execution-cve-2026-63520/</data><data key="edge_chunk_id">S09_C01</data><data key="edge_json_path">None</data><data key="edge_evidence">This is due to an unrestricted .NET type instantiation and property-setting primitive in the DbTypeReflector class, which resolves arbitrary assembly-qualified type names from BDC model XML without any allowlist or safety enforcement</data><data key="edge_extraction_method">minie</data><data key="edge_polarity">negative</data><data key="edge_modality">asserted</data></edge><edge id="oe_f6f6739af062be42" source="e_985cab375dab17b5" target="e_4139f702e143b880"><data key="edge_predicate_raw">resolves arbitrary assembly-qualified type names without</data><data key="edge_assertion_id">a_c25086b19cbdb394</data><data key="edge_source_id">S09</data><data key="edge_source_url">https://www.rapid7.com/blog/post/ra-microsoft-sharepoint-remote-code-execution-cve-2026-63520/</data><data key="edge_chunk_id">S09_C01</data><data key="edge_json_path">None</data><data key="edge_evidence">This is due to an unrestricted .NET type instantiation and property-setting primitive in the DbTypeReflector class, which resolves arbitrary assembly-qualified type names from BDC model XML without any allowlist or safety enforcement</data><data key="edge_extraction_method">minie</data><data key="edge_polarity">negative</data><data key="edge_modality">asserted</data></edge><edge id="oe_a7f33dba0871b324" source="e_985cab375dab17b5" target="e_904eea2c6691ab9e"><data key="edge_predicate_raw">resolves</data><data key="edge_assertion_id">a_d0bade8f52f8918e</data><data key="edge_source_id">S09</data><data key="edge_source_url">https://www.rapid7.com/blog/post/ra-microsoft-sharepoint-remote-code-execution-cve-2026-63520/</data><data key="edge_chunk_id">S09_C01</data><data key="edge_json_path">None</data><data key="edge_evidence">This is due to an unrestricted .NET type instantiation and property-setting primitive in the DbTypeReflector class, which resolves arbitrary assembly-qualified type names from BDC model XML without any allowlist or safety enforcement</data><data key="edge_extraction_method">minie</data><data key="edge_polarity">negative</data><data key="edge_modality">asserted</data></edge><edge id="oe_abbfc9a238ecb6d4" source="e_537e6ab50e8f2e44" target="e_16481add93a0689f"><data key="edge_predicate_raw">upload</data><data key="edge_assertion_id">a_dfc1322701b26be0</data><data key="edge_source_id">S09</data><data key="edge_source_url">https://www.rapid7.com/blog/post/ra-microsoft-sharepoint-remote-code-execution-cve-2026-63520/</data><data key="edge_chunk_id">S09_C01</data><data key="edge_json_path">None</data><data key="edge_evidence">An attacker who can upload a malicious .bdcm model file and trigger entity execution can instantiate any .NET type available in the Global Assembly Cache (GAC), set arbitrary properties on those instances, and leverage property-setter side-effects to achieve OS command execution</data><data key="edge_extraction_method">minie</data><data key="edge_polarity">positive</data><data key="edge_modality">possible</data></edge><edge id="oe_b3ba991e16050f0a" source="e_5c77927661666bef" target="e_c5dfb8860a56c364"><data key="edge_predicate_raw">be achieve</data><data key="edge_assertion_id">a_a21ef53dba8647d5</data><data key="edge_source_id">S09</data><data key="edge_source_url">https://www.rapid7.com/blog/post/ra-microsoft-sharepoint-remote-code-execution-cve-2026-63520/</data><data key="edge_chunk_id">S09_C01</data><data key="edge_json_path">None</data><data key="edge_evidence">An attacker who can upload a malicious .bdcm model file and trigger entity execution can instantiate any .NET type available in the Global Assembly Cache (GAC), set arbitrary properties on those instances, and leverage property-setter side-effects to achieve OS command execution</data><data key="edge_extraction_method">minie</data><data key="edge_polarity">positive</data><data key="edge_modality">possible</data></edge><edge id="oe_75c7e9ffd7a57c50" source="e_71704402a2035bf7" target="e_c5dfb8860a56c364"><data key="edge_predicate_raw">be achieve</data><data key="edge_assertion_id">a_2ad07dceeb9f80fa</data><data key="edge_source_id">S09</data><data key="edge_source_url">https://www.rapid7.com/blog/post/ra-microsoft-sharepoint-remote-code-execution-cve-2026-63520/</data><data key="edge_chunk_id">S09_C01</data><data key="edge_json_path">None</data><data key="edge_evidence">An attacker who can upload a malicious .bdcm model file and trigger entity execution can instantiate any .NET type available in the Global Assembly Cache (GAC), set arbitrary properties on those instances, and leverage property-setter side-effects to achieve OS command execution</data><data key="edge_extraction_method">minie</data><data key="edge_polarity">positive</data><data key="edge_modality">possible</data></edge><edge id="oe_fdd476362f9b17ef" source="e_db0111d55cfc1e1f" target="e_3ecd9f953ff0df40"><data key="edge_predicate_raw">be set arbitrary properties on</data><data key="edge_assertion_id">a_7cc03c23eb13fdb7</data><data key="edge_source_id">S09</data><data key="edge_source_url">https://www.rapid7.com/blog/post/ra-microsoft-sharepoint-remote-code-execution-cve-2026-63520/</data><data key="edge_chunk_id">S09_C01</data><data key="edge_json_path">None</data><data key="edge_evidence">An attacker who can upload a malicious .bdcm model file and trigger entity execution can instantiate any .NET type available in the Global Assembly Cache (GAC), set arbitrary properties on those instances, and leverage property-setter side-effects to achieve OS command execution</data><data key="edge_extraction_method">minie</data><data key="edge_polarity">positive</data><data key="edge_modality">possible</data></edge><edge id="oe_62eb08f1ced3e4fd" source="e_71704402a2035bf7" target="e_3ecd9f953ff0df40"><data key="edge_predicate_raw">be set arbitrary properties on</data><data key="edge_assertion_id">a_e6efd5d3ed6ab7ea</data><data key="edge_source_id">S09</data><data key="edge_source_url">https://www.rapid7.com/blog/post/ra-microsoft-sharepoint-remote-code-execution-cve-2026-63520/</data><data key="edge_chunk_id">S09_C01</data><data key="edge_json_path">None</data><data key="edge_evidence">An attacker who can upload a malicious .bdcm model file and trigger entity execution can instantiate any .NET type available in the Global Assembly Cache (GAC), set arbitrary properties on those instances, and leverage property-setter side-effects to achieve OS command execution</data><data key="edge_extraction_method">minie</data><data key="edge_polarity">positive</data><data key="edge_modality">possible</data></edge><edge id="oe_467bc0737b4fb1c1" source="e_0dd1994901856e68" target="e_5004a250dc4e7fbc"><data key="edge_predicate_raw">was helpful when</data><data key="edge_assertion_id">a_087942dee46ab91b</data><data key="edge_source_id">S09</data><data key="edge_source_url">https://www.rapid7.com/blog/post/ra-microsoft-sharepoint-remote-code-execution-cve-2026-63520/</data><data key="edge_chunk_id">S09_C01</data><data key="edge_json_path">None</data><data key="edge_evidence">Note that there is prior work in this space that was very helpful when conducting this research</data><data key="edge_extraction_method">minie</data><data key="edge_polarity">positive</data><data key="edge_modality">asserted</data></edge><edge id="oe_44300a60f1b020fe" source="e_fa57f6906d6bad6d" target="e_2d31e1284f8f402d"><data key="edge_predicate_raw">discusses leveraging BDC models for</data><data key="edge_assertion_id">a_1f80c870151d49d3</data><data key="edge_source_id">S09</data><data key="edge_source_url">https://www.rapid7.com/blog/post/ra-microsoft-sharepoint-remote-code-execution-cve-2026-63520/</data><data key="edge_chunk_id">S09_C01</data><data key="edge_json_path">None</data><data key="edge_evidence">The writeup of CVE-2019-1257 by the ZDI research team discusses leveraging BDC models for unsafe .NET type instantiation</data><data key="edge_extraction_method">minie</data><data key="edge_polarity">positive</data><data key="edge_modality">asserted</data></edge><edge id="oe_97b71368d780432c" source="e_e163460c91338b08" target="e_daf25f98f399f9b3"><data key="edge_predicate_raw">allows</data><data key="edge_assertion_id">a_5dc381dadb90416b</data><data key="edge_source_id">S09</data><data key="edge_source_url">https://www.rapid7.com/blog/post/ra-microsoft-sharepoint-remote-code-execution-cve-2026-63520/</data><data key="edge_chunk_id">S09_C01</data><data key="edge_json_path">None</data><data key="edge_evidence">Combined with a recursive instantiation and property-setting mechanism in the parent DotNetTypeReflector.Instantiate() method, this allows constructing a gadget chain that triggers Process.Start() through the System.Windows.Data.ObjectDataProvider class's property-setter side-effect (this gadget chain technique is well-known)</data><data key="edge_extraction_method">minie</data><data key="edge_polarity">positive</data><data key="edge_modality">asserted</data></edge><edge id="oe_88c93264179ae1c8" source="e_e163460c91338b08" target="e_817274aa2528c10a"><data key="edge_predicate_raw">allows constructing gadget chain Combined with</data><data key="edge_assertion_id">a_9ccc420fa7e6b317</data><data key="edge_source_id">S09</data><data key="edge_source_url">https://www.rapid7.com/blog/post/ra-microsoft-sharepoint-remote-code-execution-cve-2026-63520/</data><data key="edge_chunk_id">S09_C01</data><data key="edge_json_path">None</data><data key="edge_evidence">Combined with a recursive instantiation and property-setting mechanism in the parent DotNetTypeReflector.Instantiate() method, this allows constructing a gadget chain that triggers Process.Start() through the System.Windows.Data.ObjectDataProvider class's property-setter side-effect (this gadget chain technique is well-known)</data><data key="edge_extraction_method">minie</data><data key="edge_polarity">positive</data><data key="edge_modality">asserted</data></edge><edge id="oe_5a218254d8a22f13" source="e_6e4cb313974c3956" target="e_907db598668d5ba6"><data key="edge_predicate_raw">triggers</data><data key="edge_assertion_id">a_ca2a9b66cb4644a3</data><data key="edge_source_id">S09</data><data key="edge_source_url">https://www.rapid7.com/blog/post/ra-microsoft-sharepoint-remote-code-execution-cve-2026-63520/</data><data key="edge_chunk_id">S09_C01</data><data key="edge_json_path">None</data><data key="edge_evidence">Combined with a recursive instantiation and property-setting mechanism in the parent DotNetTypeReflector.Instantiate() method, this allows constructing a gadget chain that triggers Process.Start() through the System.Windows.Data.ObjectDataProvider class's property-setter side-effect (this gadget chain technique is well-known)</data><data key="edge_extraction_method">minie</data><data key="edge_polarity">positive</data><data key="edge_modality">asserted</data></edge><edge id="oe_f684e234dec93a03" source="e_56b6e04e82934e27" target="e_b18d3845b358d980"><data key="edge_predicate_raw">uses type reflectors to</data><data key="edge_assertion_id">a_95e3302a6b2ebab8</data><data key="edge_source_id">S09</data><data key="edge_source_url">https://www.rapid7.com/blog/post/ra-microsoft-sharepoint-remote-code-execution-cve-2026-63520/</data><data key="edge_chunk_id">S09_C01</data><data key="edge_json_path">None</data><data key="edge_evidence">The BDC subsystem uses "type reflectors" to resolve .NET types from the TypeName attribute of TypeDescriptor elements in BDC model XML</data><data key="edge_extraction_method">minie</data><data key="edge_polarity">positive</data><data key="edge_modality">asserted</data></edge><edge id="oe_d4bcc0b91e322928" source="e_56b6e04e82934e27" target="e_7aaa7aa6d98b2c67"><data key="edge_predicate_raw">uses</data><data key="edge_assertion_id">a_7a8439ed5ecfca69</data><data key="edge_source_id">S09</data><data key="edge_source_url">https://www.rapid7.com/blog/post/ra-microsoft-sharepoint-remote-code-execution-cve-2026-63520/</data><data key="edge_chunk_id">S09_C01</data><data key="edge_json_path">None</data><data key="edge_evidence">The BDC subsystem uses "type reflectors" to resolve .NET types from the TypeName attribute of TypeDescriptor elements in BDC model XML</data><data key="edge_extraction_method">minie</data><data key="edge_polarity">positive</data><data key="edge_modality">asserted</data></edge><edge id="oe_035edc4a0ac2b4b8" source="e_791de43fccfd7f2f" target="e_5f19504dbb93dfd4"><data key="edge_predicate_raw">uses DbTypeReflector For</data><data key="edge_assertion_id">a_85513e16f0593acf</data><data key="edge_source_id">S09</data><data key="edge_source_url">https://www.rapid7.com/blog/post/ra-microsoft-sharepoint-remote-code-execution-cve-2026-63520/</data><data key="edge_chunk_id">S09_C01</data><data key="edge_json_path">None</data><data key="edge_evidence">For Database-type LobSystem definitions, SharePoint uses DbTypeReflector, which inherits from DotNetTypeReflector, as shown below</data><data key="edge_extraction_method">minie</data><data key="edge_polarity">positive</data><data key="edge_modality">asserted</data></edge><edge id="oe_64eab519596c55f1" source="e_791de43fccfd7f2f" target="e_cb9f5348cc19aca7"><data key="edge_predicate_raw">uses</data><data key="edge_assertion_id">a_59cb102841f1c22e</data><data key="edge_source_id">S09</data><data key="edge_source_url">https://www.rapid7.com/blog/post/ra-microsoft-sharepoint-remote-code-execution-cve-2026-63520/</data><data key="edge_chunk_id">S09_C01</data><data key="edge_json_path">None</data><data key="edge_evidence">For Database-type LobSystem definitions, SharePoint uses DbTypeReflector, which inherits from DotNetTypeReflector, as shown below</data><data key="edge_extraction_method">minie</data><data key="edge_polarity">positive</data><data key="edge_modality">asserted</data></edge><edge id="oe_b16e1dcbd5172b36" source="e_cb9f5348cc19aca7" target="e_0f096c4f79bb42fb"><data key="edge_predicate_raw">inherits from</data><data key="edge_assertion_id">a_624cf52ce93f1cfe</data><data key="edge_source_id">S09</data><data key="edge_source_url">https://www.rapid7.com/blog/post/ra-microsoft-sharepoint-remote-code-execution-cve-2026-63520/</data><data key="edge_chunk_id">S09_C01</data><data key="edge_json_path">None</data><data key="edge_evidence">For Database-type LobSystem definitions, SharePoint uses DbTypeReflector, which inherits from DotNetTypeReflector, as shown below</data><data key="edge_extraction_method">minie</data><data key="edge_polarity">positive</data><data key="edge_modality">asserted</data></edge><edge id="oe_8465bfe6ce73d77b" source="e_ad16450d4d7b98f8" target="e_b3674051a70df4f2"><data key="edge_predicate_raw">falls through to</data><data key="edge_assertion_id">a_30ab65014e325bb7</data><data key="edge_source_id">S09</data><data key="edge_source_url">https://www.rapid7.com/blog/post/ra-microsoft-sharepoint-remote-code-execution-cve-2026-63520/</data><data key="edge_chunk_id">S09_C02</data><data key="edge_json_path">None</data><data key="edge_evidence">System.Int32), it falls through to the base class DotNetTypeReflector.ResolveDotNetType(), which has a limited type lookup path</data><data key="edge_extraction_method">minie</data><data key="edge_polarity">positive</data><data key="edge_modality">asserted</data></edge><edge id="oe_58efa0228ec6822c" source="e_333716f10a881b90" target="e_33a72d714748e9b0"><data key="edge_predicate_raw">calls</data><data key="edge_assertion_id">a_4709aee24af9ba11</data><data key="edge_source_id">S09</data><data key="edge_source_url">https://www.rapid7.com/blog/post/ra-microsoft-sharepoint-remote-code-execution-cve-2026-63520/</data><data key="edge_chunk_id">S09_C02</data><data key="edge_json_path">None</data><data key="edge_evidence">System.Diagnostics.Process or System.Windows.Data.ObjectDataProvider), the method calls Type.GetType() directly</data><data key="edge_extraction_method">minie</data><data key="edge_polarity">positive</data><data key="edge_modality">asserted</data></edge><edge id="oe_2da2540b9578106a" source="e_200807ea700bfac2" target="e_6f30ccda3c04a8d9"><data key="edge_predicate_raw">Text</data><data key="edge_assertion_id">a_d7215c308477c6e8</data><data key="edge_source_id">S09</data><data key="edge_source_url">https://www.rapid7.com/blog/post/ra-microsoft-sharepoint-remote-code-execution-cve-2026-63520/</data><data key="edge_chunk_id">S09_C03</data><data key="edge_json_path">None</data><data key="edge_evidence">&lt;Property Name="RdbCommandType" Type="System.String"&gt;Text&lt;/Property&gt;</data><data key="edge_extraction_method">minie</data><data key="edge_polarity">positive</data><data key="edge_modality">asserted</data></edge><edge id="oe_ed64d780c00caf51" source="e_d740f2de2a062193" target="e_110bc4e010782d7f"><data key="edge_predicate_raw">be set to new instance of</data><data key="edge_assertion_id">a_659d79790e6daf8c</data><data key="edge_source_id">S09</data><data key="edge_source_url">https://www.rapid7.com/blog/post/ra-microsoft-sharepoint-remote-code-execution-cve-2026-63520/</data><data key="edge_chunk_id">S09_C04</data><data key="edge_json_path">None</data><data key="edge_evidence">The System.Diagnostics.Process instance will have its StartInfo member variable set to a new instance of System.Diagnostics.ProcessStartInfo, and this defines the arbitrary process to execute</data><data key="edge_extraction_method">minie</data><data key="edge_polarity">positive</data><data key="edge_modality">asserted</data></edge><edge id="oe_de515649fd2c1786" source="e_e163460c91338b08" target="e_67a82bd7acd7d8d0"><data key="edge_predicate_raw">defines arbitrary process to</data><data key="edge_assertion_id">a_5884f1cc13aa4689</data><data key="edge_source_id">S09</data><data key="edge_source_url">https://www.rapid7.com/blog/post/ra-microsoft-sharepoint-remote-code-execution-cve-2026-63520/</data><data key="edge_chunk_id">S09_C04</data><data key="edge_json_path">None</data><data key="edge_evidence">The System.Diagnostics.Process instance will have its StartInfo member variable set to a new instance of System.Diagnostics.ProcessStartInfo, and this defines the arbitrary process to execute</data><data key="edge_extraction_method">minie</data><data key="edge_polarity">positive</data><data key="edge_modality">asserted</data></edge><edge id="oe_d2d4d5532afbd656" source="e_3f2947ac831b67bc" target="e_e163460c91338b08"><data key="edge_predicate_raw">be showing</data><data key="edge_assertion_id">a_d0c20b813f73e532</data><data key="edge_source_id">S09</data><data key="edge_source_url">https://www.rapid7.com/blog/post/ra-microsoft-sharepoint-remote-code-execution-cve-2026-63520/</data><data key="edge_chunk_id">S09_C04</data><data key="edge_json_path">None</data><data key="edge_evidence">When the ObjectInstance is set to the System.Diagnostics.Process instance it triggers th