ules, encrypted and unencrypted PCAPs, and ASM queries</data><data key="edge_extraction_method">minie</data><data key="edge_polarity">positive</data><data key="edge_modality">asserted</data></edge><edge id="oe_7e89f2219811dc2e" source="e_f2caad7aabc9e1ca" target="e_e2818f68fdd4b51b"><data key="edge_predicate_raw">are available to</data><data key="edge_assertion_id">a_a63bb479449c414f</data><data key="edge_source_id">S10</data><data key="edge_source_url">https://www.vulncheck.com/blog/cve-2026-63520-sharepoint-unsafe-type-rce</data><data key="edge_chunk_id">S10_C01</data><data key="edge_json_path">None</data><data key="edge_evidence">These artifacts are available to Initial Access Intelligence customers, and the team’s analysis of the SharePoint RCE chain is below</data><data key="edge_extraction_method">minie</data><data key="edge_polarity">positive</data><data key="edge_modality">asserted</data></edge><edge id="oe_d72f79597063157e" source="e_7f1f6c82d4c24b3a" target="e_6203f55027291b6a"><data key="edge_predicate_raw">has analysis of</data><data key="edge_assertion_id">a_c4d23a5c5bb60e68</data><data key="edge_source_id">S10</data><data key="edge_source_url">https://www.vulncheck.com/blog/cve-2026-63520-sharepoint-unsafe-type-rce</data><data key="edge_chunk_id">S10_C01</data><data key="edge_json_path">None</data><data key="edge_evidence">These artifacts are available to Initial Access Intelligence customers, and the team’s analysis of the SharePoint RCE chain is below</data><data key="edge_extraction_method">minie</data><data key="edge_polarity">positive</data><data key="edge_modality">asserted</data></edge><edge id="oe_ec7c307bcef45b90" source="e_d87c6276d6d26d91" target="e_9193cb7c63ef871f"><data key="edge_predicate_raw">show differing counts of SharePoint servers on</data><data key="edge_assertion_id">a_5b6229b12a5c54c5</data><data key="edge_source_id">S10</data><data key="edge_source_url">https://www.vulncheck.com/blog/cve-2026-63520-sharepoint-unsafe-type-rce</data><data key="edge_chunk_id">S10_C01</data><data key="edge_json_path">None</data><data key="edge_evidence">ASM query engines show wildly differing counts of SharePoint servers on the open internet</data><data key="edge_extraction_method">minie</data><data key="edge_polarity">positive</data><data key="edge_modality">asserted</data></edge><edge id="oe_f21b4905b0654514" source="e_18d7ab68b870cdef" target="e_501580464fccb458"><data key="edge_predicate_raw">allows</data><data key="edge_assertion_id">a_5e04aaf52cdff848</data><data key="edge_source_id">S10</data><data key="edge_source_url">https://www.vulncheck.com/blog/cve-2026-63520-sharepoint-unsafe-type-rce</data><data key="edge_chunk_id">S10_C01</data><data key="edge_json_path">None</data><data key="edge_evidence">There’s a detailed write-up on CVE-2026-55040 here from the Rapid7 team, but the TL;DR is that a lack of proper validation in SharePoint’s JWT handling (SPJsonWebSecurityTokenHandlerV2) allows an unauthenticated attacker to forge JWT tokens and access the web application as a privileged account assuming you have certain information</data><data key="edge_extraction_method">heuristic</data><data key="edge_polarity">positive</data><data key="edge_modality">asserted</data></edge><edge id="oe_2addec871f14ebad" source="e_f5a675c0a7d7e06f" target="e_29851af70515593d"><data key="edge_predicate_raw">provided</data><data key="edge_assertion_id">a_ddc3171e0fbcfa4b</data><data key="edge_source_id">S10</data><data key="edge_source_url">https://www.vulncheck.com/blog/cve-2026-63520-sharepoint-unsafe-type-rce</data><data key="edge_chunk_id">S10_C01</data><data key="edge_json_path">None</data><data key="edge_evidence">For instance if you can obtain the SID or the user principal name (trusted identity provided must be configured for the latter) of a privileged SharePoint user, you can forge a JWT as that user to retrieve a FormDigestValue from a privileged endpoint</data><data key="edge_extraction_method">heuristic</data><data key="edge_polarity">positive</data><data key="edge_modality">possible</data></edge><edge id="oe_dd1b1c073c3aa9d3" source="e_c420a40e5d96594a" target="e_1898794d59ed4569"><data key="edge_predicate_raw">runs</data><data key="edge_assertion_id">a_ce1b8429cdc24fa0</data><data key="edge_source_id">S10</data><data key="edge_source_url">https://www.vulncheck.com/blog/cve-2026-63520-sharepoint-unsafe-type-rce</data><data key="edge_chunk_id">S10_C01</data><data key="edge_json_path">None</data><data key="edge_evidence">You can then use the forged JWT along with the digest value to access the application in “useful” ways, such as to make changes to the application via the Business Connectivity Services (BCS), or more specifically via BDC (Business Data Catalog), the core service on which BCS runs, to achieve RCE</data><data key="edge_extraction_method">minie</data><data key="edge_polarity">positive</data><data key="edge_modality">possible</data></edge><edge id="oe_c8134869a226ca66" source="e_5c980ac08d8e06db" target="e_25dee3ca44f377a6"><data key="edge_predicate_raw">use forged JWT along with</data><data key="edge_assertion_id">a_39ded00ae7619d33</data><data key="edge_source_id">S10</data><data key="edge_source_url">https://www.vulncheck.com/blog/cve-2026-63520-sharepoint-unsafe-type-rce</data><data key="edge_chunk_id">S10_C01</data><data key="edge_json_path">None</data><data key="edge_evidence">You can then use the forged JWT along with the digest value to access the application in “useful” ways, such as to make changes to the application via the Business Connectivity Services (BCS), or more specifically via BDC (Business Data Catalog), the core service on which BCS runs, to achieve RCE</data><data key="edge_extraction_method">minie</data><data key="edge_polarity">positive</data><data key="edge_modality">possible</data></edge><edge id="oe_8cd71520055c3d3b" source="e_5c980ac08d8e06db" target="e_7d8df9ff48bd5566"><data key="edge_predicate_raw">use forged JWT along with</data><data key="edge_assertion_id">a_a76be4b87ceb0456</data><data key="edge_source_id">S10</data><data key="edge_source_url">https://www.vulncheck.com/blog/cve-2026-63520-sharepoint-unsafe-type-rce</data><data key="edge_chunk_id">S10_C01</data><data key="edge_json_path">None</data><data key="edge_evidence">You can then use the forged JWT along with the digest value to access the application in “useful” ways, such as to make changes to the application via the Business Connectivity Services (BCS), or more specifically via BDC (Business Data Catalog), the core service on which BCS runs, to achieve RCE</data><data key="edge_extraction_method">minie</data><data key="edge_polarity">positive</data><data key="edge_modality">possible</data></edge><edge id="oe_1934e2205ca89a2d" source="e_5c980ac08d8e06db" target="e_c8dfaccf2a582233"><data key="edge_predicate_raw">use</data><data key="edge_assertion_id">a_2b4f9fc61559ac78</data><data key="edge_source_id">S10</data><data key="edge_source_url">https://www.vulncheck.com/blog/cve-2026-63520-sharepoint-unsafe-type-rce</data><data key="edge_chunk_id">S10_C01</data><data key="edge_json_path">None</data><data key="edge_evidence">You can then use the forged JWT along with the digest value to access the application in “useful” ways, such as to make changes to the application via the Business Connectivity Services (BCS), or more specifically via BDC (Business Data Catalog), the core service on which BCS runs, to achieve RCE</data><data key="edge_extraction_method">minie</data><data key="edge_polarity">positive</data><data key="edge_modality">possible</data></edge><edge id="oe_b6d0f0facc2d6b94" source="e_10c0749f7978a237" target="e_0a5137e8983f8adf"><data key="edge_predicate_raw">be access</data><data key="edge_assertion_id">a_5c7c8ec59da3d8cf</data><data key="edge_source_id">S10</data><data key="edge_source_url">https://www.vulncheck.com/blog/cve-2026-63520-sharepoint-unsafe-type-rce</data><data key="edge_chunk_id">S10_C01</data><data key="edge_json_path">None</data><data key="edge_evidence">You can then use the forged JWT along with the digest value to access the application in “useful” ways, such as to make changes to the application via the Business Connectivity Services (BCS), or more specifically via BDC (Business Data Catalog), the core service on which BCS runs, to achieve RCE</data><data key="edge_extraction_method">minie</data><data key="edge_polarity">positive</data><data key="edge_modality">possible</data></edge><edge id="oe_fe9af94b707d13a6" source="e_10c0749f7978a237" target="e_c5571af9c192ceba"><data key="edge_predicate_raw">be access</data><data key="edge_assertion_id">a_6327156810679cc8</data><data key="edge_source_id">S10</data><data key="edge_source_url">https://www.vulncheck.com/blog/cve-2026-63520-sharepoint-unsafe-type-rce</data><data key="edge_chunk_id">S10_C01</data><data key="edge_json_path">None</data><data key="edge_evidence">You can then use the forged JWT along with the digest value to access the application in “useful” ways, such as to make changes to the application via the Business Connectivity Services (BCS), or more specifically via BDC (Business Data Catalog), the core service on which BCS runs, to achieve RCE</data><data key="edge_extraction_method">minie</data><data key="edge_polarity">positive</data><data key="edge_modality">possible</data></edge><edge id="oe_a9b1cf721e82f904" source="e_63682437049c7097" target="e_78b456fbfbf7a2f4"><data key="edge_predicate_raw">be achieve</data><data key="edge_assertion_id">a_ab79086341148889</data><data key="edge_source_id">S10</data><data key="edge_source_url">https://www.vulncheck.com/blog/cve-2026-63520-sharepoint-unsafe-type-rce</data><data key="edge_chunk_id">S10_C01</data><data key="edge_json_path">None</data><data key="edge_evidence">You can then use the forged JWT along with the digest value to access the application in “useful” ways, such as to make changes to the application via the Business Connectivity Services (BCS), or more specifically via BDC (Business Data Catalog), the core service on which BCS runs, to achieve RCE</data><data key="edge_extraction_method">minie</data><data key="edge_polarity">positive</data><data key="edge_modality">possible</data></edge><edge id="oe_a84ef81c4b02790a" source="e_6f86ae8844c3ae87" target="e_fbfb70a00355d68e"><data key="edge_predicate_raw">has disclosure for</data><data key="edge_assertion_id">a_eb11e817803514e1</data><data key="edge_source_id">S10</data><data key="edge_source_url">https://www.vulncheck.com/blog/cve-2026-63520-sharepoint-unsafe-type-rce</data><data key="edge_chunk_id">S10_C01</data><data key="edge_json_path">None</data><data key="edge_evidence">Rapid7’s disclosure for CVE-2026-63520 describes the issue as unsafe .NET type instantiation within SharePoint’s Business Connectivity Services</data><data key="edge_extraction_method">minie</data><data key="edge_polarity">positive</data><data key="edge_modality">asserted</data></edge><edge id="oe_6a82efc01231f96b" source="e_000fbfcccde57e07" target="e_2d31e1284f8f402d"><data key="edge_predicate_raw">describes issue as</data><data key="edge_assertion_id">a_c86dabaf2ca7cfb6</data><data key="edge_source_id">S10</data><data key="edge_source_url">https://www.vulncheck.com/blog/cve-2026-63520-sharepoint-unsafe-type-rce</data><data key="edge_chunk_id">S10_C01</data><data key="edge_json_path">None</data><data key="edge_evidence">Rapid7’s disclosure for CVE-2026-63520 describes the issue as unsafe .NET type instantiation within SharePoint’s Business Connectivity Services</data><data key="edge_extraction_method">minie</data><data key="edge_polarity">positive</data><data key="edge_modality">asserted</data></edge><edge id="oe_8b3fb99fe00cc9ee" source="e_000fbfcccde57e07" target="e_c7a7735bf61b8084"><data key="edge_predicate_raw">describes</data><data key="edge_assertion_id">a_dc51a3223ecdc879</data><data key="edge_source_id">S10</data><data key="edge_source_url">https://www.vulncheck.com/blog/cve-2026-63520-sharepoint-unsafe-type-rce</data><data key="edge_chunk_id">S10_C01</data><data key="edge_json_path">None</data><data key="edge_evidence">Rapid7’s disclosure for CVE-2026-63520 describes the issue as unsafe .NET type instantiation within SharePoint’s Business Connectivity Services</data><data key="edge_extraction_method">minie</data><data key="edge_polarity">positive</data><data key="edge_modality">asserted</data></edge><edge id="oe_fb314d7cd0cd77e7" source="e_fc7dbd581d39a8a8" target="e_759453b03e46f7eb"><data key="edge_predicate_raw">bypass</data><data key="edge_assertion_id">a_16d9ac90703b4851</data><data key="edge_source_id">S10</data><data key="edge_source_url">https://www.vulncheck.com/blog/cve-2026-63520-sharepoint-unsafe-type-rce</data><data key="edge_chunk_id">S10_C01</data><data key="edge_json_path">None</data><data key="edge_evidence">After reproducing the authentication bypass in our own SharePoint environment, our team diffed KB5002893 to see what changed</data><data key="edge_extraction_method">heuristic</data><data key="edge_polarity">positive</data><data key="edge_modality">asserted</data></edge><edge id="oe_e759fbc1a95ece6a" source="e_725367bf832fa264" target="e_b27373d9a9c4626d"><data key="edge_predicate_raw">be found inside</data><data key="edge_assertion_id">a_46f034113ba864b0</data><data key="edge_source_id">S10</data><data key="edge_source_url">https://www.vulncheck.com/blog/cve-2026-63520-sharepoint-unsafe-type-rce</data><data key="edge_chunk_id">S10_C01</data><data key="edge_json_path">None</data><data key="edge_evidence">The most significant change was a new function, ValidateSafeBcsType, found inside Microsoft.SharePoint/Microsoft/SharePoint/BusinessData/Infrastructure/DotNetTypeReflector.cs</data><data key="edge_extraction_method">minie</data><data key="edge_polarity">positive</data><data key="edge_modality">asserted</data></edge><edge id="oe_64cf36bff348822e" source="e_9fba12bdfb8000f6" target="e_b27373d9a9c4626d"><data key="edge_predicate_raw">was new function found inside</data><data key="edge_assertion_id">a_c23871af6f86e881</data><data key="edge_source_id">S10</data><data key="edge_source_url">https://www.vulncheck.com/blog/cve-2026-63520-sharepoint-unsafe-type-rce</data><data key="edge_chunk_id">S10_C01</data><data key="edge_json_path">None</data><data key="edge_evidence">The most significant change was a new function, ValidateSafeBcsType, found inside Microsoft.SharePoint/Microsoft/SharePoint/BusinessData/Infrastructure/DotNetTypeReflector.cs</data><data key="edge_extraction_method">minie</data><data key="edge_polarity">positive</data><data key="edge_modality">asserted</data></edge><edge id="oe_1c8313b1ea159d15" source="e_725367bf832fa264" target="e_b372370472a7e178"><data key="edge_predicate_raw">was promising</data><data key="edge_assertion_id">a_8d582d9cc8119a9b</data><data key="edge_source_id">S10</data><data key="edge_source_url">https://www.vulncheck.com/blog/cve-2026-63520-sharepoint-unsafe-type-rce</data><data key="edge_chunk_id">S10_C02</data><data key="edge_json_path">None</data><data key="edge_evidence">Given the vulnerability’s reported root cause, the new function was promising</data><data key="edge_extraction_method">minie</data><data key="edge_polarity">positive</data><data key="edge_modality">reported</data></edge><edge id="oe_0d2777b646fda656" source="e_791de43fccfd7f2f" target="e_2f4f3cc513cdd23d"><data key="edge_predicate_raw">applies additional validation Starting with</data><data key="edge_assertion_id">a_ec18b598e8cf483f</data><data key="edge_source_id">S10</data><data key="edge_source_url">https://www.vulncheck.com/blog/cve-2026-63520-sharepoint-unsafe-type-rce</data><data key="edge_chunk_id">S10_C02</data><data key="edge_json_path">None</data><data key="edge_evidence">“Starting with the August 2026 CU, SharePoint applies additional validation to the .NET types that can be used by BCS models</data><data key="edge_extraction_method">minie</data><data key="edge_polarity">positive</data><data key="edge_modality">possible</data></edge><edge id="oe_3d6c1fe8c58dafb7" source="e_791de43fccfd7f2f" target="e_31a063fabc69d56a"><data key="edge_predicate_raw">applies</data><data key="edge_assertion_id">a_6e50ea4042d5833e</data><data key="edge_source_id">S10</data><data key="edge_source_url">https://www.vulncheck.com/blog/cve-2026-63520-sharepoint-unsafe-type-rce</data><data key="edge_chunk_id">S10_C02</data><data key="edge_json_path">None</data><data key="edge_evidence">“Starting with the August 2026 CU, SharePoint applies additional validation to the .NET types that can be used by BCS models</data><data key="edge_extraction_method">minie</data><data key="edge_polarity">positive</data><data key="edge_modality">possible</data></edge><edge id="oe_9749c098692bb3fc" source="e_791de43fccfd7f2f" target="e_2f4f3cc513cdd23d"><data key="edge_predicate_raw">be Starting with</data><data key="edge_assertion_id">a_1a6350e74a9faffb</data><data key="edge_source_id">S10</data><data key="edge_source_url">https://www.vulncheck.com/blog/cve-2026-63520-sharepoint-unsafe-type-rce</data><data key="edge_chunk_id">S10_C02</data><data key="edge_json_path">None</data><data key="edge_evidence">“Starting with the August 2026 CU, SharePoint applies additional validation to the .NET types that can be used by BCS models</data><data key="edge_extraction_method">minie</data><data key="edge_polarity">positive</data><data key="edge_modality">possible</data></edge><edge id="oe_330d2cfd689a02d4" source="e_41e517acc2965ff0" target="e_56bee0a7d5aada83"><data key="edge_predicate_raw">be used by</data><data key="edge_assertion_id">a_1d39c437bca92f1e</data><data key="edge_source_id">S10</data><data key="edge_source_url">https://www.vulncheck.com/blog/cve-2026-63520-sharepoint-unsafe-type-rce</data><data key="edge_chunk_id">S10_C02</data><data key="edge_json_path">None</data><data key="edge_evidence">“Starting with the August 2026 CU, SharePoint applies additional validation to the .NET types that can be used by BCS models</data><data key="edge_extraction_method">minie</data><data key="edge_polarity">positive</data><data key="edge_modality">possible</data></edge><edge id="oe_8e2bd7725b34b7e7" source="e_57be633689797476" target="e_a7eb60623ea959bd"><data key="edge_predicate_raw">included</data><data key="edge_assertion_id">a_76337d427bfb22d3</data><data key="edge_source_id">S10</data><data key="edge_source_url">https://www.vulncheck.com/blog/cve-2026-63520-sharepoint-unsafe-type-rce</data><data key="edge_chunk_id">S10_C02</data><data key="edge_json_path">None</data><data key="edge_evidence">Only types explicitly included in the farm’s BCSAllowedTypeNames allow list are permitted</data><data key="edge_extraction_method">heuristic</data><data key="edge_polarity">positive</data><data key="edge_modality">asserted</data></edge><edge id="oe_88e35542481b188e" source="e_6eac2ea8015cf2cc" target="e_f4957eaadf1d8c5f"><data key="edge_predicate_raw">are present in</data><data key="edge_assertion_id">a_46352ff4102d5fc2</data><data key="edge_source_id">S10</data><data key="edge_source_url">https://www.vulncheck.com/blog/cve-2026-63520-sharepoint-unsafe-type-rce</data><data key="edge_chunk_id">S10_C02</data><data key="edge_json_path">None</data><data key="edge_evidence">Types that are not present in this list are blocked to provide additional protection against potentially unsafe type usage.”</data><data key="edge_extraction_method">minie</data><data key="edge_polarity">negative</data><data key="edge_modality">possible</data></edge><edge id="oe_58905caf9da9a77f" source="e_6eac2ea8015cf2cc" target="e_71ed5a488ff96e7e"><data key="edge_predicate_raw">are blocked to provide additional protection against</data><data key="edge_assertion_id">a_92151ff5be43ee3e</data><data key="edge_source_id">S10</data><data key="edge_source_url">https://www.vulncheck.com/blog/cve-2026-63520-sharepoint-unsafe-type-rce</data><data key="edge_chunk_id">S10_C02</data><data key="edge_json_path">None</data><data key="edge_evidence">Types that are not present in this list are blocked to provide additional protection against potentially unsafe type usage.”</data><data key="edge_extraction_method">minie</data><data key="edge_polarity">negative</data><data key="edge_modality">possible</data></edge><edge id="oe_a1ccc53fb913ac54" source="e_78b456fbfbf7a2f4" target="e_60992c6628dd7335"><data key="edge_predicate_raw">involve</data><data key="edge_assertion_id">a_f5f9162bcda0e689</data><data key="edge_source_id">S10</data><data key="edge_source_url">https://www.vulncheck.com/blog/cve-2026-63520-sharepoint-unsafe-type-rce</data><data key="edge_chunk_id">S10_C02</data><data key="edge_json_path">None</data><data key="edge_evidence">Based on the excerpt above and the location of the code, we assessed that RCE would likely involve submitting a BDC (business data connectivity) model, or BDCM</data><data key="edge_extraction_method">minie</data><data key="edge_polarity">positive</data><data key="edge_modality">possible</data></edge><edge id="oe_e3528a5700cf14b4" source="e_9111a79bb0a0398b" target="e_58cd8d62d77655d5"><data key="edge_predicate_raw">allows</data><data key="edge_assertion_id">a_64bdc6f7ee879813</data><data key="edge_source_id">S10</data><data key="edge_source_url">https://www.vulncheck.com/blog/cve-2026-63520-sharepoint-unsafe-type-rce</data><data key="edge_chunk_id">S10_C02</data><data key="edge_json_path">None</data><data key="edge_evidence">BDC is a service that allows external data sources (e.g., databases, web services, .NET assemblies, etc) to be imported and used within SharePoint as though they were SharePoint-native data sources</data><data key="edge_extraction_method">minie</data><data key="edge_polarity">positive</data><data key="edge_modality">asserted</data></edge><edge id="oe_abbb4792539a2660" source="e_83af7d9153bfe2b1" target="e_791de43fccfd7f2f"><data key="edge_predicate_raw">be imported within</data><data key="edge_assertion_id">a_0067c05ecb1ad67c</data><data key="edge_source_id">S10</data><data key="edge_source_url">https://www.vulncheck.com/blog/cve-2026-63520-sharepoint-unsafe-type-rce</data><data key="edge_chunk_id">S10_C02</data><data key="edge_json_path">None</data><data key="edge_evidence">BDC is a service that allows external data sources (e.g., databases, web services, .NET assemblies, etc) to be imported and used within SharePoint as though they were SharePoint-native data sources</data><data key="edge_extraction_method">minie</data><data key="edge_polarity">positive</data><data key="edge_modality">asserted</data></edge><edge id="oe_2e5dccae7cead568" source="e_343e358f0dfc43f0" target="e_0f10ce41ef4efc53"><data key="edge_predicate_raw">are provided as</data><data key="edge_assertion_id">a_7856a75acd599d79</data><data key="edge_source_id">S10</data><data key="edge_source_url">https://www.vulncheck.com/blog/cve-2026-63520-sharepoint-unsafe-type-rce</data><data key="edge_chunk_id">S10_C02</data><data key="edge_json_path">None</data><data key="edge_evidence">These data sources are usually provided as LOB (Line of Business) systems in a metadata file</data><data key="edge_extraction_method">minie</data><data key="edge_polarity">positive</data><data key="edge_modality">asserted</data></edge><edge id="oe_a0c8326f34edb86c" source="e_343e358f0dfc43f0" target="e_3de73cd8c703a624"><data key="edge_predicate_raw">are provided as LOB systems in</data><data key="edge_assertion_id">a_b68000250b72f9af</data><data key="edge_source_id">S10</data><data key="edge_source_url">https://www.vulncheck.com/blog/cve-2026-63520-sharepoint-unsafe-type-rce</data><data key="edge_chunk_id">S10_C02</data><data key="edge_json_path">None</data><data key="edge_evidence">These data sources are usually provided as LOB (Line of Business) systems in a metadata file</data><data key="edge_extraction_method">minie</data><data key="edge_polarity">positive</data><data key="edge_modality">asserted</data></edge><edge id="oe_d64ba8ab60b39d06" source="e_0f10ce41ef4efc53" target="e_db9f7508f47976fd"><data key="edge_predicate_raw">is Line of</data><data key="edge_assertion_id">a_082d2bb765e65965</data><data key="edge_source_id">S10</data><data key="edge_source_url">https://www.vulncheck.com/blog/cve-2026-63520-sharepoint-unsafe-type-rce</data><data key="edge_chunk_id">S10_C02</data><data key="edge_json_path">None</data><data key="edge_evidence">These data sources are usually provided as LOB (Line of Business) systems in a metadata file</data><data key="edge_extraction_method">minie</data><data key="edge_polarity">positive</data><data key="edge_modality">asserted</data></edge><edge id="oe_b821f38ddedca6c0" source="e_329f63509bc4989a" target="e_322c7ab9c032d7e8"><data key="edge_predicate_raw">has been abused in</data><data key="edge_assertion_id">a_d407f1e5d8f367b9</data><data key="edge_source_id">S10</data><data key="edge_source_url">https://www.vulncheck.com/blog/cve-2026-63520-sharepoint-unsafe-type-rce</data><data key="edge_chunk_id">S10_C02</data><data key="edge_json_path">None</data><data key="edge_evidence">BDC has also been abused in past SharePoint exploits, which typically involved uploading a BDCM to the BusinessDataCatalog in order to exploit some weakness in the service</data><data key="edge_extraction_method">minie</data><data key="edge_polarity">positive</data><data key="edge_modality">asserted</data></edge><edge id="oe_a40da9159c008fc8" source="e_322c7ab9c032d7e8" target="e_38d5fd16c52b3b45"><data key="edge_predicate_raw">involved</data><data key="edge_assertion_id">a_a9dceffd135aa20c</data><data key="edge_source_id">S10</data><data key="edge_source_url">https://www.vulncheck.com/blog/cve-2026-63520-sharepoint-unsafe-type-rce</data><data key="edge_chunk_id">S10_C02</data><data key="edge_json_path">None</data><data key="edge_evidence">BDC has also been abused in past SharePoint exploits, which typically involved uploading a BDCM to the BusinessDataCatalog in order to exploit some weakness in the service</data><data key="edge_extraction_method">minie</data><data key="edge_polarity">positive</data><data key="edge_modality">asserted</data></edge><edge id="oe_aa603c090de71916" source="e_f89eee4e7388b9cf" target="e_22608c0889103676"><data key="edge_predicate_raw">is code injection RCE vulnerability disclosed in</data><data key="edge_assertion_id">a_2b62e3e0041ef853</data><data key="edge_source_id">S10</data><data key="edge_source_url">https://www.vulncheck.com/blog/cve-2026-63520-sharepoint-unsafe-type-rce</data><data key="edge_chunk_id">S10_C02</data><data key="edge_json_path">None</data><data key="edge_evidence">Two examples are CVE-2023-24955, a code injection RCE vulnerability disclosed in May 2023, and CVE-2019-1257, a code injection-to-BDC-deserialization vulnerability from September 2019</data><data key="edge_extraction_method">minie</data><data key="edge_polarity">positive</data><data key="edge_modality">possible</data></edge><edge id="oe_18b898c36162fb32" source="e_5cfe0e1e3074439f" target="e_22608c0889103676"><data key="edge_predicate_raw">be disclosed in</data><data key="edge_assertion_id">a_18d73fa2ea4fc0f2</data><data key="edge_source_id">S10</data><data key="edge_source_url">https://www.vulncheck.com/blog/cve-2026-63520-sharepoint-unsafe-type-rce</data><data key="edge_chunk_id">S10_C02</data><data key="edge_json_path">None</data><data key="edge_evidence">Two examples are CVE-2023-24955, a code injection RCE vulnerability disclosed in May 2023, and CVE-2019-1257, a code injection-to-BDC-deserialization vulnerability from September 2019</data><data key="edge_extraction_method">minie</data><data key="edge_polarity">positive</data><data key="edge_modality">possible</data></edge><edge id="oe_0a36cb436d359a28" source="e_f89eee4e7388b9cf" target="e_56faf9a1aadac785"><data key="edge_predicate_raw">is code injection-to-BDC-deserialization vulnerability from</data><data key="edge_assertion_id">a_7d0ca213bf738087</data><data key="edge_source_id">S10</data><data key="edge_source_url">https://www.vulncheck.com/blog/cve-2026-63520-sharepoint-unsafe-type-rce</data><data key="edge_chunk_id">S10_C02</data><data key="edge_json_path">None</data><data key="edge_evidence">Two examples are CVE-2023-24955, a code injection RCE vulnerability disclosed in May 2023, and CVE-2019-1257, a code injection-to-BDC-deserialization vulnerability from September 2019</data><data key="edge_extraction_method">minie</data><data key="edge_polarity">positive</data><data key="edge_modality">possible</data></edge><edge id="oe_dcae69eb099140df" source="e_be74ffef073dc8d3" target="e_e6d6e7369c1cdeb1"><data key="edge_predicate_raw">know similar structure to CVE-2026-63520 from</data><data key="edge_assertion_id">a_50da9ca794da5e7b</data><data key="edge_source_id">S10</data><data key="edge_source_url">https://www.vulncheck.com/blog/cve-2026-63520-sharepoint-unsafe-type-rce</data><data key="edge_chunk_id">S10_C02</data><data key="edge_json_path">None</data><data key="edge_evidence">CVE-2023-24955 in particular has a similar structure to CVE-2026-63520, which we know from implementing the 2023 flaw as part of a CVE-2023-29357 RCE chain</data><data key="edge_extraction_method">minie</data><data key="edge_polarity">positive</data><data key="edge_modality">asserted</data></edge><edge id="oe_e33effbea49b274a" source="e_be74ffef073dc8d3" target="e_d098afd82f814fa4"><data key="edge_predicate_raw">know</data><data key="edge_assertion_id">a_a8a47c3129275457</data><data key="edge_source_id">S10</data><data key="edge_source_url">https://www.vulncheck.com/blog/cve-2026-63520-sharepoint-unsafe-type-rce</data><data key="edge_chunk_id">S10_C02</data><data key="edge_json_path">None</data><data key="edge_evidence">CVE-2023-24955 in particular has a similar structure to CVE-2026-63520, which we know from implementing the 2023 flaw as part of a CVE-2023-29357 RCE chain</data><data key="edge_extraction_method">minie</data><data key="edge_polarity">positive</data><data key="edge_modality">asserted</data></edge><edge id="oe_3c2aab3a6730f1bf" source="e_d86bf1362e24a929" target="e_2d3885aa4dbbb2cf"><data key="edge_predicate_raw">patched</data><data key="edge_assertion_id">a_e95393d28212f793</data><data key="edge_source_id">S10</data><data key="edge_source_url">https://www.vulncheck.com/blog/cve-2026-63520-sharepoint-unsafe-type-rce</data><data key="edge_chunk_id">S10_C02</data><data key="edge_json_path">None</data><data key="edge_evidence">When we examined the decompiled patched code, we found that the new validation function was being called in at least 16 locations, which gave us a reasonable roadmap for further investigation since they are all likely guarding interesting sinks</data><data key="edge_extraction_method">heuristic</data><data key="edge_polarity">positive</data><data key="edge_modality">possible</data></edge><edge id="oe_543363916b786be0" source="e_ac2471b8c9b7713f" target="e_565f52125a26af7b"><data key="edge_predicate_raw">used</data><data key="edge_assertion_id">a_adf90529fce6fd0a</data><data key="edge_source_id">S10</data><data key="edge_source_url">https://www.vulncheck.com/blog/cve-2026-63520-sharepoint-unsafe-type-rce</data><data key="edge_chunk_id">S10_C02</data><data key="edge_json_path">None</data><data key="edge_evidence">In the very first decompiled file in the image above, where ValidateSafeBcsType is defined, it is also used at the very bottom of a function called ResolveDotNetType to check the type as a guard to the return</data><data key="edge_extraction_method">heuristic</data><data key="edge_polarity">positive</data><data key="edge_modality">asserted</data></edge><edge id="oe_87c18f957a942f92" source="e_e163460c91338b08" target="e_2d31e1284f8f402d"><data key="edge_predicate_raw">looked like right path towards</data><data key="edge_assertion_id">a_4441e5df3c6178a2</data><data key="edge_source_id">S10</data><data key="edge_source_url">https://www.vulncheck.com/blog/cve-2026-63520-sharepoint-