ey="edge_chunk_id">S10_C02</data><data key="edge_json_path">None</data><data key="edge_evidence">Just looking at the function signature, we know this function is parsing a type from a LobSystem</data><data key="edge_extraction_method">minie</data><data key="edge_polarity">positive</data><data key="edge_modality">asserted</data></edge><edge id="oe_87a7e9fa96ff2b8d" source="e_be74ffef073dc8d3" target="e_c8762019020c6b4f"><data key="edge_predicate_raw">be looking</data><data key="edge_assertion_id">a_3feb6696a67b595d</data><data key="edge_source_id">S10</data><data key="edge_source_url">https://www.vulncheck.com/blog/cve-2026-63520-sharepoint-unsafe-type-rce</data><data key="edge_chunk_id">S10_C02</data><data key="edge_json_path">None</data><data key="edge_evidence">Just looking at the function signature, we know this function is parsing a type from a LobSystem</data><data key="edge_extraction_method">minie</data><data key="edge_polarity">positive</data><data key="edge_modality">asserted</data></edge><edge id="oe_1f5d58c6cbbdeb18" source="e_be74ffef073dc8d3" target="e_26ace5ccbe099dc6"><data key="edge_predicate_raw">looked at</data><data key="edge_assertion_id">a_88c6224b65ae770a</data><data key="edge_source_id">S10</data><data key="edge_source_url">https://www.vulncheck.com/blog/cve-2026-63520-sharepoint-unsafe-type-rce</data><data key="edge_chunk_id">S10_C03</data><data key="edge_json_path">None</data><data key="edge_evidence">We looked at the surrounding code, and while various avenues looked interesting, the most direct “resolve, then create” pattern we found was the GetEntityObject function in DotNetAssemblyConnectionManager.cs</data><data key="edge_extraction_method">minie</data><data key="edge_polarity">positive</data><data key="edge_modality">asserted</data></edge><edge id="oe_01d993eed9477e4b" source="e_be74ffef073dc8d3" target="e_b14591135f9dd603"><data key="edge_predicate_raw">found was GetEntityObject function in</data><data key="edge_assertion_id">a_1ffbe1