ter, runs Activator.CreateInstance on that resolved type</data><data key="edge_extraction_method">minie</data><data key="edge_polarity">positive</data><data key="edge_modality">asserted</data></edge><edge id="oe_c252dc7dd8ded374" source="e_5706a0c83f4cd45f" target="e_d1e24208156be786"><data key="edge_predicate_raw">is known XML element of</data><data key="edge_assertion_id">a_f2a0297c5b059caa</data><data key="edge_source_id">S10</data><data key="edge_source_url">https://www.vulncheck.com/blog/cve-2026-63520-sharepoint-unsafe-type-rce</data><data key="edge_chunk_id">S10_C03</data><data key="edge_json_path">None</data><data key="edge_evidence">This function pulls from a Class property in an “entity” (a known XML element of a BDC model), resolves the type from it, and then, a few lines later, runs Activator.CreateInstance on that resolved type</data><data key="edge_extraction_method">minie</data><data key="edge_polarity">positive</data><data key="edge_modality">asserted</data></edge><edge id="oe_b4d990f6eb63e4dc" source="e_d833a6de9bf08b5e" target="e_b430718e5c7cf6ac"><data key="edge_predicate_raw">was to hit</data><data key="edge_assertion_id">a_437f294904efd7da</data><data key="edge_source_id">S10</data><data key="edge_source_url">https://www.vulncheck.com/blog/cve-2026-63520-sharepoint-unsafe-type-rce</data><data key="edge_chunk_id">S10_C03</data><data key="edge_json_path">None</data><data key="edge_evidence">Since that looked very close to what we were interested in, the next task was to hit the CreateInstance sink with a .NET type and method that we dictated</data><data key="edge_extraction_method">minie</data><data key="edge_polarity">positive</data><data key="edge_modality">asserted</data></edge><edge id="oe_74dbb8b00ee36832" source="e_be74ffef073dc8d3" target="e_ea78c12aa97286d0"><data key="edge_predicate_raw">make</data><data key="edge_assertion_id">a_ca52d676f17dcf5d</data><data key="edge_source_id">S10</data><data key="edge_source_url">https://www.vulncheck.com/blog/cve-2026-63520-sharepoint-unsafe-type-rce</data><data key="edge_chunk_id">S10_C03</data><data key="edge_json_path">None</data><data key="edge_evidence">XML-based specs tend to be confusing, and we'd rather not make this entire blog post about the intricacies of the BDC spec</data><data key="edge_extraction_method">minie</data><data key="edge_polarity">negative</data><data key="edge_modality">asserted</data></edge><edge id="oe_d98bd0a74e24c303" source="e_f79d3418b113114c" target="e_5195b730c0e7249f"><data key="edge_predicate_raw">tend to be</data><data key="edge_assertion_id">a_b79f6298b305951c</data><data key="edge_source_id">S10</data><data key="edge_source_url">https://www.vulncheck.com/blog/cve-2026-63520-sharepoint-unsafe-type-rce</data><data key="edge_chunk_id">S10_C03</data><data key="edge_json_path">None</data><data key="edge_evidence">XML-based specs tend to be confusing, and we'd rather not make this entire blog post about the intricacies of the BDC spec</data><data key="edge_extraction_method">minie</data><data key="edge_polarity">negative</data><data key="edge_modality">asserted</data></edge><edge id="oe_1820d1b4ebe75c54" source="e_ec83b364bf8bfdc4" target="e_73f5300c34d5dc10"><data key="edge_predicate_raw">included</data><data key="edge_assertion_id">a_0322da71fb8e0b93</data><data key="edge_source_id">S10</data><data key="edge_source_url">https://www.vulncheck.com/blog/cve-2026-63520-sharepoint-unsafe-type-rce</data><data key="edge_chunk_id">S10_C03</data><data key="edge_json_path">None</data><data key="edge_evidence">Instead we’ve focused the rest of this blog on what worked, provided the final requests that led to RCE, and included further reading resources on SharePoint’s BDC service for those who want to dig more deeply into the specs</data><data key="edge_extraction_method">heuristic</data><data key="edge_polarity">positive</data><data key="edge_modality">asserted</data></edge><edge id="oe_4a808ab3bcfb1f25" source="e_e1117a493f95433e" target="e_41977bbb956fd210"><data key="edge_predicate_raw">is interesting Type attribute in</data><data key="edge_assertion_id">a_b4ee4a918e5a2895</data><data key="edge_source_id">S10</data><data key="edge_source_url">https://www.vulncheck.com/blog/cve-2026-63520-sharepoint-unsafe-type-rce</data><data key="edge_chunk_id">S10_C03</data><data key="edge_json_path">None</data><data key="edge_evidence">The DotNetAssembly is the interesting Type attribute in this case, since it tells the BDC service to instantiate a .NET class and invoke some method on it</data><data key="edge_extraction_method">minie</data><data key="edge_polarity">positive</data><data key="edge_modality">asserted</data></edge><edge id="oe_53bab1b2de5b45f6" source="e_3b1f2c268c6ccf12" target="e_2279292c015b9359"><data key="edge_predicate_raw">document</data><data key="edge_assertion_id">a_4faa8e2efac5c991</data><data key="edge_source_id">S10</data><data key="edge_source_url">https://www.vulncheck.com/blog/cve-2026-63520-sharepoint-unsafe-type-rce</data><data key="edge_chunk_id">S10_C03</data><data key="edge_json_path">None</data><data key="edge_evidence">The official SharePoint GitHub docs actually document the BDCM schema in a parent-child hierarchy, which was helpful</data><data key="edge_extraction_method">minie</data><data key="edge_polarity">positive</data><data key="edge_modality">asserted</data></edge><edge id="oe_4ecb2762fb9a085d" source="e_3b1f2c268c6ccf12" target="e_04e845d79fb1f65f"><data key="edge_predicate_raw">document BDCM schema in</data><data key="edge_assertion_id">a_126afa2f3d260f6a</data><data key="edge_source_id">S10</data><data key="edge_source_url">https://www.vulncheck.com/blog/cve-2026-63520-sharepoint-unsafe-type-rce</data><data key="edge_chunk_id">S10_C03</data><data key="edge_json_path">None</data><data key="edge_evidence">The official SharePoint GitHub docs actually document the BDCM schema in a parent-child hierarchy, which was helpful</data><data key="edge_extraction_method">minie</data><data key="edge_polarity">positive</data><data key="edge_modality">asserted</data></edge><edge id="oe_aac153c0c1ab048a" source="e_077bb703d76c8bd6" target="e_af26fda364ba9e72"><data key="edge_predicate_raw">be needed to</data><data key="edge_assertion_id">a_df3572547bbcd611</data><data key="edge_source_id">S10</data><data key="edge_source_url">https://www.vulncheck.com/blog/cve-2026-63520-sharepoint-unsafe-type-rce</data><data key="edge_chunk_id">S10_C03</data><data key="edge_json_path">None</data><data key="edge_evidence">This told us roughly how the layout needed to look, and more importantly, which attributes exist for each XML element</data><data key="edge_extraction_method">minie</data><data key="edge_polarity">positive</data><data key="edge_modality">asserted</data></edge><edge id="oe_aabb2cadd1d9a63f" source="e_e163460c91338b08" target="e_a1dcdd289f57b065"><data key="edge_predicate_raw">told</data><data key="edge_assertion_id">a_94d6e13a734c3944</data><data key="edge_source_id">S10</data><data key="edge_source_url">https://www.vulncheck.com/blog/cve-2026-63520-sharepoint-unsafe-type-rce</data><data key="edge_chunk_id">S10_C03</data><data key="edge_json_path">None</data><data key="edge_evidence">This told us roughly how the layout needed to look, and more importantly, which attributes exist for each XML element</data><data key="edge_extraction_method">minie</data><data key="edge_polarity">positive</data><data key="edge_modality">asserted</data></edge><edge id="oe_9e49b70dee63b128" source="e_273431069120d1d4" target="e_76780e7dcca5f8b4"><data key="edge_predicate_raw">be hit</data><data key="edge_assertion_id">a_82f109704d55809d</data><data key="edge_source_id">S10</data><data key="edge_source_url">https://www.vulncheck.com/blog/cve-2026-63520-sharepoint-unsafe-type-rce</data><data key="edge_chunk_id">S10_C03</data><data key="edge_json_path">None</data><data key="edge_evidence">We eventually managed to get a valid BDCM model to hit Activator.CreateInstance and instantiate a System.Object, visible in the debugger (below)</data><data key="edge_extraction_method">minie</data><data key="edge_polarity">positive</data><data key="edge_modality">asserted</data></edge><edge id="oe_0c816f2db8644f09" source="e_92a321c0faea8af2" target="e_bfe79c02a6eadc4f"><data key="edge_predicate_raw">be hit System.Object visible in</data><data key="edge_assertion_id">a_c78cbc3cf7a28553</data><data key="edge_source_id">S10</data><data key="edge_source_url">https://www.vulncheck.com/blog/cve-2026-63520-sharepoint-unsafe-type-rce</data><data key="edge_chunk_id">S10_C03</data><data key="edge_json_path">None</data><data key="edge_evidence">We eventually managed to get a valid BDCM model to hit Activator.CreateInstance and instantiate a System.Object, visible in the debugger (below)</data><data key="edge_extraction_method">minie</data><data key="edge_polarity">positive</data><data key="edge_modality">asserted</data></edge><edge id="oe_67a9de04fe930439" source="e_be74ffef073dc8d3" target="e_686b22d113fc391d"><data key="edge_predicate_raw">managed to get</data><data key="edge_assertion_id">a_f432c20bc08e4dba</data><data key="edge_source_id">S10</data><data key="edge_source_url">https://www.vulncheck.com/blog/cve-2026-63520-sharepoint-unsafe-type-rce</data><data key="edge_chunk_id">S10_C03</data><data key="edge_json_path">None</data><data key="edge_evidence">We eventually managed to get a valid BDCM model to hit Activator.CreateInstance and instantiate a System.Object, visible in the debugger (below)</data><data key="edge_extraction_method">minie</data><data key="edge_polarity">positive</data><data key="edge_modality">asserted</data></edge><edge id="oe_31f0e22b18a85276" source="e_be74ffef073dc8d3" target="e_bfe79c02a6eadc4f"><data key="edge_predicate_raw">managed to get valid BDCM model instantiate System.Object visible in</data><data key="edge_assertion_id">a_59863db73739b2a5</data><data key="edge_source_id">S10</data><data key="edge_source_url">https://www.vulncheck.com/blog/cve-2026-63520-sharepoint-unsafe-type-rce</data><data key="edge_chunk_id">S10_C03</data><data key="edge_json_path">None</data><data key="edge_evidence">We eventually managed to get a valid BDCM model to hit Activator.CreateInstance and instantiate a System.Object, visible in the debugger (below)</data><data key="edge_extraction_method">minie</data><data key="edge_polarity">positive</data><data key="edge_modality">asserted</data></edge><edge id="oe_31d420638c3555f7" source="e_62d03bcfe7fbfed6" target="e_1010870ff6882c98"><data key="edge_predicate_raw">was passed to</data><data key="edge_assertion_id">a_3d1b434cb5374f7c</data><data key="edge_source_id">S10</data><data key="edge_source_url">https://www.vulncheck.com/blog/cve-2026-63520-sharepoint-unsafe-type-rce</data><data key="edge_chunk_id">S10_C03</data><data key="edge_json_path">None</data><data key="edge_evidence">As you can see above, System.Object was successfully passed to CreateInstance</data><data key="edge_extraction_method">minie</data><data key="edge_polarity">positive</data><data key="edge_modality">possible</data></edge><edge id="oe_abf5a82715d4b792" source="e_5c980ac08d8e06db" target="e_9005adc286dd64cf"><data key="edge_predicate_raw">see</data><data key="edge_assertion_id">a_6128135a2a7672ae</data><data key="edge_source_id">S10</data><data key="edge_source_url">https://www.vulncheck.com/blog/cve-2026-63520-sharepoint-unsafe-type-rce</data><data key="edge_chunk_id">S10_C03</data><data key="edge_json_path">None</data><data key="edge_evidence">As you can see above, System.Object was successfully passed to CreateInstance</data><data key="edge_extraction_method">minie</data><data key="edge_polarity">positive</data><data key="edge_modality">possible</data></edge><edge id="oe_63ca81a9f44fd9e7" source="e_22735a1094a79e52" target="e_87247967ea2b0721"><data key="edge_predicate_raw">appeared to be working at first When</data><data key="edge_assertion_id">a_6ef97257122bd4e4</data><data key="edge_source_id">S10</data><data key="edge_source_url">https://www.vulncheck.com/blog/cve-2026-63520-sharepoint-unsafe-type-rce</data><data key="edge_chunk_id">S10_C03</data><data key="edge_json_path">None</data><data key="edge_evidence">When trying to use Process, everything appeared to be working at first</data><data key="edge_extraction_method">minie</data><data key="edge_polarity">positive</data><data key="edge_modality">asserted</data></edge><edge id="oe_aacc38b8b14ab45d" source="e_22735a1094a79e52" target="e_29f374d3ae492bbc"><data key="edge_predicate_raw">appeared to be working at</data><data key="edge_assertion_id">a_dc62d0858636aa07</data><data key="edge_source_id">S10</data><data key="edge_source_url">https://www.vulncheck.com/blog/cve-2026-63520-sharepoint-unsafe-type-rce</data><data key="edge_chunk_id">S10_C03</data><data key="edge_json_path">None</data><data key="edge_evidence">When trying to use Process, everything appeared to be working at first</data><data key="edge_extraction_method">minie</data><data key="edge_polarity">positive</data><data key="edge_modality">asserted</data></edge><edge id="oe_2b1783bf86d8785b" source="e_7e00636ef9f5e6c5" target="e_364a616abcfb1054"><data key="edge_predicate_raw">provided</data><data key="edge_assertion_id">a_f04e50f00dbd04e7</data><data key="edge_source_id">S10</data><data key="edge_source_url">https://www.vulncheck.com/blog/cve-2026-63520-sharepoint-unsafe-type-rce</data><data key="edge_chunk_id">S10_C03</data><data key="edge_json_path">None</data><data key="edge_evidence">The debugger hit on the instantiation with Process as the type, but during execution, when the provided method name was resolved, it turned out that Instance types are checked first (and chosen if they exist) before any Static types</data><data key="edge_extraction_method">heuristic</data><data key="edge_polarity">positive</data><data key="edge_modality">asserted</data></edge><edge id="oe_8915bb610e8d51f0" source="e_e163460c91338b08" target="e_5523a40f730ea7d6"><data key="edge_predicate_raw">resulted in</data><data key="edge_assertion_id">a_f77b7685fc6c8e09</data><data key="edge_source_id">S10</data><data key="edge_source_url">https://www.vulncheck.com/blog/cve-2026-63520-sharepoint-unsafe-type-rce</data><data key="edge_chunk_id">S10_C03</data><data key="edge_json_path">None</data><data key="edge_evidence">This resulted in this Start() overload being chosen over the static Start(String) overload that we wanted</data><data key="edge_extraction_method">minie</data><data key="edge_polarity">positive</data><data key="edge_modality">asserted</data></edge><edge id="oe_a24b23e9e5a44ce5" source="e_f9ee5f0cdfa4269d" target="e_44b3712e02ffc5d5"><data key="edge_predicate_raw">is shown in</data><data key="edge_assertion_id">a_d68cb9805da03c9a</data><data key="edge_source_id">S10</data><data key="edge_source_url">https://www.vulncheck.com/blog/cve-2026-63520-sharepoint-unsafe-type-rce</data><data key="edge_chunk_id">S10_C03</data><data key="edge_json_path">None</data><data key="edge_evidence">This Instance-first method selection is shown in the decompiled DotNetAssembly/DotNetAssemblySystemUtility.cs code above, and from this we identified that for a useful gadget (i.e., a logical code object to use as an exploit primitive), we needed a Class that resolved a usable Instance type (or possibly a Class that had a useful Static type and no instance types, though we didn’t test this directly)</data><data key="edge_extraction_method">minie</data><data key="edge_polarity">negative</data><data key="edge_modality">asserted</data></edge><edge id="oe_2b454583320fda90" source="e_4881fab2f9c9099c" target="e_9005adc286dd64cf"><data key="edge_predicate_raw">code</data><data key="edge_assertion_id">a_76d7f3d75e9fa629</data><data key="edge_source_id">S10</data><data key="edge_source_url">https://www.vulncheck.com/blog/cve-2026-63520-sharepoint-unsafe-type-rce</data><data key="edge_chunk_id">S10_C03</data><data key="edge_json_p