<data key="edge_json_path">None</data><data key="edge_evidence">Based on our prior experience building .NET deserialization gadgets by hand, we knew that we could probably leverage System.Web.UI.LosFormatter, as it has a parameterless constructor with a useful Instance Method, Deserialize</data><data key="edge_extraction_method">minie</data><data key="edge_polarity">positive</data><data key="edge_modality">possible</data></edge><edge id="oe_878c67dc38732cda" source="e_be74ffef073dc8d3" target="e_935bce6bb24baa30"><data key="edge_predicate_raw">call Deserialize with base64-encoded string as</data><data key="edge_assertion_id">a_c107c53a50879bac</data><data key="edge_source_id">S10</data><data key="edge_source_url">https://www.vulncheck.com/blog/cve-2026-63520-sharepoint-unsafe-type-rce</data><data key="edge_chunk_id">S10_C04</data><data key="edge_json_path">None</data><data key="edge_evidence">We can call Deserialize with a base64-encoded string as the only argument, which in our case will be a deserialization gadget</data><data key="edge_extraction_method">minie</data><data key="edge_polarity">positive</data><data key="edge_modality">possible</data></edge><edge id="oe_950881521edef4b6" source="e_be74ffef073dc8d3" target="e_fa0f769c61f36203"><data key="edge_predicate_raw">call</data><data key="edge_assertion_id">a_8b81d4fbd309023d</data><data key="edge_source_id">S10</data><data key="edge_source_url">https://www.vulncheck.com/blog/cve-2026-63520-sharepoint-unsafe-type-rce</data><data key="edge_chunk_id">S10_C04</data><data key="edge_json_path">None</data><data key="edge_evidence">We can call Deserialize with a base64-encoded string as the only argument, which in our case will be a deserialization gadget</data><data key="edge_extraction_method">minie</data><data key="edge_polarity">positive</data><data key="edge_modality">possible</data></edge><edge id="oe_d521fdcab2983054" source="e_935bce6bb24baa30" target="e_41977bbb956fd210"><data key="edge_predicate_raw">be deserialization gadget in</data><data key="edge_assertion_id">a_7e5dda5416abfb16</data><data key="edge_source_id">S10</data><data key="edge_source_url">https://www.vulncheck.com/blog/cve-2026-63520-sharepoint-unsafe-type-rce</data><data key="edge_chunk_id">S10_C04</data><data key="edge_json_path">None</data><data key="edge_evidence">We can call Deserialize with a base64-encoded string as the only argument, which in our case will be a deserialization gadget</data><data key="edge_extraction_method">minie</data><data key="edge_polarity">positive</data><data key="edge_modality">possible</data></edge><edge id="oe_9bab271f964e56fe" source="e_be74ffef073dc8d3" target="e_b0afa75beb2e3c36"><data key="edge_predicate_raw">use type instantiation to instantiate class with</data><data key="edge_assertion_id">a_1a828bc83c5466df</data><data key="edge_source_id">S10</data><data key="edge_source_url">https://www.vulncheck.com/blog/cve-2026-63520-sharepoint-unsafe-type-rce</data><data key="edge_chunk_id">S10_C04</data><data key="edge_json_path">None</data><data key="edge_evidence">While CVE-2026-63520 is not a deserialization vulnerability, we can still use the type instantiation to instantiate a class with a method that can deserialize an object (and it’s familiar to us)</data><data key="edge_extraction_method">minie</data><data key="edge_polarity">negative</data><data key="edge_modality">possible</data></edge><edge id="oe_3732750912df7799" source="e_be74ffef073dc8d3" target="e_30f89804aa6408a5"><data key="edge_predicate_raw">use type instantiation to instantiate</data><data key="edge_assertion_id">a_9172e0c8cf46dfc7</data><data key="edge_source_id">S10</data><data key="edge_source_url">https://www.vulncheck.com/blog/cve-2026-63520-sharepoint-unsafe-type-rce</data><data key="edge_chunk_id">S10_C04</data><data key="edge_json_path">None</data><data key="edge_evidence">While CVE-2026-63520 is not a deserialization vulnerability, we can still use the type instantiation to instantiate a class 