uirso_de/active-exploitation-of-cve-2026-59310-361-victim-ips-across-47-countries-9783187cc6ff</data><data key="edge_chunk_id">None</data><data key="edge_json_path">None</data><data key="edge_evidence">These capabilities allowed the attacker to maintain an outbound control channel from compromised systems</data><data key="edge_extraction_method">minie</data><data key="edge_polarity">positive</data><data key="edge_modality">asserted</data></edge><edge id="oe_638d4df0dd367892" source="e_4d85ed61fba30342" target="e_f3fc57e64504979f"><data key="edge_predicate_raw">allowed attacker to maintain</data><data key="edge_assertion_id">a_b7bb0b1362ce2d5f</data><data key="edge_source_id">S12</data><data key="edge_source_url">https://medium.com/@quirso_de/active-exploitation-of-cve-2026-59310-361-victim-ips-across-47-countries-9783187cc6ff</data><data key="edge_chunk_id">None</data><data key="edge_json_path">None</data><data key="edge_evidence">These capabilities allowed the attacker to maintain an outbound control channel from compromised systems</data><data key="edge_extraction_method">minie</data><data key="edge_polarity">positive</data><data key="edge_modality">asserted</data></edge><edge id="oe_26990b880deac91d" source="e_b9b66982a40d9593" target="e_d8f973366a4526da"><data key="edge_predicate_raw">is useful to</data><data key="edge_assertion_id">a_a49b7e7746918321</data><data key="edge_source_id">S12</data><data key="edge_source_url">https://medium.com/@quirso_de/active-exploitation-of-cve-2026-59310-361-victim-ips-across-47-countries-9783187cc6ff</data><data key="edge_chunk_id">None</data><data key="edge_json_path">None</data><data key="edge_evidence">An outbound connection is particularly useful to an intruder because it can bypass security controls designed primarily to prevent unsolicited inbound access</data><data key="edge_extraction_method">minie</data><data key="edge_polarity">positive</data><data key="edge_modality">possible</data></edge><edge id="oe_0f7be31001e2d03b" source="e_ad16450d4d7b98f8" target="e_3da1d953b95fa2e5"><data key="edge_predicate_raw">bypass</data><data key="edge_assertion_id">a_056ae5532086819a</data><data key="edge_source_id">S12</data><data key="edge_source_url">https://medium.com/@quirso_de/active-exploitation-of-cve-2026-59310-361-victim-ips-across-47-countries-9783187cc6ff</data><data key="edge_chunk_id">None</data><data key="edge_json_path">None</data><data key="edge_evidence">An outbound connection is particularly useful to an intruder because it can bypass security controls designed primarily to prevent unsolicited inbound access</data><data key="edge_extraction_method">minie</data><data key="edge_polarity">positive</data><data key="edge_modality">possible</data></edge><edge id="oe_2dc32bedd43dfcf2" source="e_3709b11f96009c9b" target="e_f7bbf3d7131b8e6f"><data key="edge_predicate_raw">be designed to prevent</data><data key="edge_assertion_id">a_6bb1a85705621cb8</data><data key="edge_source_id">S12</data><data key="edge_source_url">https://medium.com/@quirso_de/active-exploitation-of-cve-2026-59310-361-victim-ips-across-47-countries-9783187cc6ff</data><data key="edge_chunk_id">None</data><data key="edge_json_path">None</data><data key="edge_evidence">An outbound connection is particularly useful to an intruder because it can bypass security controls designed primarily to prevent unsolicited inbound access</data><data key="edge_extraction_method">minie</data><data key="edge_polarity">positive</data><data key="edge_modality">possible</data></edge><edge id="oe_82dd08e17af18980" source="e_d264eaff12872f82" target="e_6081043cf04db8fb"><data key="edge_predicate_raw">be treated as proof of malicious activity by</data><data key="edge_assertion_id">a_1b50b74e01c8d18f</data><data key="edge_source_id">S12</data><data key="edge_source_url">https://medium.com/@quirso_de/active-exploitation-of-cve-2026-59310-361-victim-ips-across-47-countries-9783187cc6ff</data><data key="edge_chunk_id">None</data><data key="edge_json_path">None</data><data key="edge_evidence">The presence of reverse_ssh should not, by itself, be treated as proof of malicious activity</data><data key="edge_extraction_method">minie</data><data key="edge_polarity">negative</data><data key="edge_modality">asserted</data></edge><edge id="oe_0dcbd8132769fe09" source="e_d264eaff12872f82" target="e_09955cf838a9fa3b"><data key="edge_predicate_raw">be treated as proof of</data><data key="edge_assertion_id">a_95e895ac74a34063</data><data key="edge_source_id">S12</data><data key="edge_source_url">https://medium.com/@quirso_de/active-exploitation-of-cve-2026-59310-361-victim-ips-across-47-countries-9783187cc6ff</data><data key="edge_chunk_id">None</data><data key="edge_json_path">None</data><data key="edge_evidence">The presence of reverse_ssh should not, by itself, be treated as proof of malicious activity</data><data key="edge_extraction_method">minie</data><data key="edge_polarity">negative</data><data key="edge_modality">asserted</data></edge><edge id="oe_f654431dc63e4218" source="e_ad16450d4d7b98f8" target="e_f4a3ec080759bc2a"><data key="edge_predicate_raw">is high-priority indicator</data><data key="edge_assertion_id">a_ceb7cf7d8a500db3</data><data key="edge_source_id">S12</data><data key="edge_source_url">https://medium.com/@quirso_de/active-exploitation-of-cve-2026-59310-361-victim-ips-across-47-countries-9783187cc6ff</data><data key="edge_chunk_id">None</data><data key="edge_json_path">None</data><data key="edge_evidence">In combination with unauthorized installation, unexpected outbound connections or execution on a vulnerable vCenter appliance, however, it is a high-priority indicator requiring investigation</data><data key="edge_extraction_method">minie</data><data key="edge_polarity">positive</data><data key="edge_modality">asserted</data></edge><edge id="oe_597e2a7fe632c5d9" source="e_ad16450d4d7b98f8" target="e_2afbc49960d44fbe"><data key="edge_predicate_raw">is high-priority indicator requiring investiga