arePoint Server — was made publicly available</data><data key="edge_extraction_method">minie</data><data key="edge_polarity">positive</data><data key="edge_modality">asserted</data></edge><edge id="oe_72c8c8c0c2b8b8e7" source="e_bebdf23dc9b18acb" target="e_743f01e029ac14ee"><data key="edge_predicate_raw">exploit for CVE-2026-55040</data><data key="edge_assertion_id">a_a665f2c44b617779</data><data key="edge_source_id">S17</data><data key="edge_source_url">https://diesec.com/2026/08/top-5-cybersecurity-news-stories-august-21-2026/</data><data key="edge_chunk_id">S17_C02</data><data key="edge_json_path">None</data><data key="edge_evidence">On August 13, a proof-of-concept exploit for CVE-2026-55040 — a CVSS 9.1 authentication bypass in Microsoft SharePoint Server — was made publicly available</data><data key="edge_extraction_method">minie</data><data key="edge_polarity">positive</data><data key="edge_modality">asserted</data></edge><edge id="oe_be1ef69f98de4304" source="e_bebdf23dc9b18acb" target="e_743f01e029ac14ee"><data key="edge_predicate_raw">exploit</data><data key="edge_assertion_id">a_17d63884704881e3</data><data key="edge_source_id">S17</data><data key="edge_source_url">https://diesec.com/2026/08/top-5-cybersecurity-news-stories-august-21-2026/</data><data key="edge_chunk_id">S17_C02</data><data key="edge_json_path">None</data><data key="edge_evidence">On August 13, a proof-of-concept exploit for CVE-2026-55040 — a CVSS 9.1 authentication bypass in Microsoft SharePoint Server — was made publicly available</data><data key="edge_extraction_method">minie</data><data key="edge_polarity">positive</data><data key="edge_modality">asserted</data></edge><edge id="oe_07ed172b17ef2ba0" source="e_618d93742ee02dc6" target="e_24788b43fcb15abb"><data key="edge_predicate_raw">followed within</data><data key="edge_assertion_id">a_4c2e1575adc9177c</data><data key="edge_source_id">S17</data><data key="edge_source_url">https://diesec.com/2026/08/top-5-cybersecurity-news-stories-a