n internal service or cloud provider metadata endpoint — AWS IMDSv1, Azure IMDS, or GCP metadata API — returning cloud credentials and deployment tokens to the attacker without authentication</data><data key="edge_extraction_method">minie</data><data key="edge_polarity">negative</data><data key="edge_modality">possible</data></edge><edge id="oe_8b66c4a1197b7eae" source="e_b7dc1287759fb543" target="e_10b98e3a0cf77505"><data key="edge_predicate_raw">holds credentials for</data><data key="edge_assertion_id">a_2dabb4999d51bcc2</data><data key="edge_source_id">S17</data><data key="edge_source_url">https://diesec.com/2026/08/top-5-cybersecurity-news-stories-august-21-2026/</data><data key="edge_chunk_id">S17_C04</data><data key="edge_json_path">None</data><data key="edge_evidence">Metabase holds credentials for business databases</data><data key="edge_extraction_method">minie</data><data key="edge_polarity">positive</data><data key="edge_modality">asserted</data></edge><edge id="oe_36643221b95ace51" source="e_f2dca16215b933e8" target="e_c4631f903e1159e5"><data key="edge_predicate_raw">be compute</data><data key="edge_assertion_id">a_91741dd287ff1ec2</data><data key="edge_source_id">S17</data><data key="edge_source_url">https://diesec.com/2026/08/top-5-cybersecurity-news-stories-august-21-2026/</data><data key="edge_chunk_id">S17_C04</data><data key="edge_json_path">None</data><data key="edge_evidence">MLflow — as the lifecycle management platform for machine learning experiments, model training, and deployment pipelines — runs with privileged cloud IAM roles that provide access to GPU compute resources, data warehouses, training datasets in object storage, model registries, and in many cases production inference infrastructure</data><data key="edge_extraction_method">minie</data><data key="edge_polarity">positive</data><data key="edge_modality">asserted</data></edge><edge id="oe_b8f2303955427ee5" source="e_612de99d33269b61" target="e_c4631f903e1159e5"><data key="edge_predicate_raw">to compute</data><data key="edge_assertion_id">a_c55825ef3756bec2</data><data key="edge_source_id">S17</data><data key="edge_source_url">https://diesec.com/2026/08/top-5-cybersecurity-news-stories-august-21-2026/</data><data key="edge_chunk_id">S17_C04</data><data key="edge_json_path">None</data><data key="edge_evidence">MLflow — as the lifecycle management platform for machine learning experiments, model training, and deployment pipelines — runs with privileged cloud IAM roles that provide access to GPU compute resources, data warehouses, training datasets in object storage, model registries, and in many cases production inference infrastructure</data><data key="edge_extraction_method">minie</data><data key="edge_polarity">positive</data><data key="edge_modality">asserted</data></edge><edge id="oe_d2507d2329106609" source="e_28473cc1a846d1a6" target="e_0547b8ef547ee3fd"><data key="edge_predicate_raw">be attached to</data><data key="edge_assertion_id">a_7dde5c0e8bf8dccb</data><data key="edge_source_id">S17</data><data key="edge_source_url">https://diesec.com/2026/08/top-5-cybersecurity-news-stories-august-21-2026/</data><data key="edge_chunk_id">S17_C04</data><data key="edge_json_path">None</data><data key="edge_evidence">Stealing the cloud credentials attached to a production MLflow server can give an attacker standing access to a substantial share of an organisation’s cloud data estate</data><data key="edge_extraction_method">minie</data><data key="edge_polarity">positive</data><data key="edge_modality">possible</data></edge><edge id="oe_cba0418f1fb03d6d" source="e_d14079057f4dda71" target="e_3c3af70b47ed0249"><data key="edge_predicate_raw">give</data><data key="edge_assertion_id">a_a449f0734b3b0e6c</data><data key="edge_source_id">S17</data><data key="edge_source_url">https://diesec.com/2026/08/top-5-cybersecurity-news-stories-august-21-2026/</data><data key="edge_chunk_id">S17_C04</data><data key="edge_json_path">None</data><data key="edge_evidence">Stealing the cloud credentials attached to a production MLflow server can give an attacker standing access to a substantial share of an organisation’s cloud data estate</data><data key="edge_extraction_method">minie</data><data key="edge_polarity">positive</data><data key="edge_modality">possible</data></edge><edge id="oe_9f6ac956b5c93baf" source="e_53ec048dbc997fc9" target="e_bf79d7373ca5ab77"><data key="edge_predicate_raw">is deployed by</data><data key="edge_assertion_id">a_87ceafcad3c7dfc7</data><data key="edge_source_id">S17</data><data key="edge_source_url">https://diesec.com/2026/08/top-5-cybersecurity-news-stories-august-21-2026/</data><data key="edge_chunk_id">S17_C04</data><data key="edge_json_path">None</data><data key="edge_evidence">The risk is compounded by the fact that MLflow is routinely deployed by data science teams independently of central IT — frequently without appearing in the organisation’s asset inventory and without a formal patching SLA</data><data key="edge_extraction_method">minie</data><data key="edge_polarity">negative</data><data key="edge_modality">asserted</data></edge><edge id="oe_24d68f40913482c2" source="e_53ec048dbc997fc9" target="e_373d1b692756526e"><data key="edge_predicate_raw">is deployed by data science teams independently of</data><data key="edge_assertion_id">a_9f1c1c629cfc5485</data><data key="edge_source_id">S17</data><data key="edge_source_url">https://diesec.com/2026/08/top-5-cybersecurity-news-stories-august-21-2026/</data><data key="edge_chunk_id">S17_C04</data><data key="edge_json_path">None</data><data key="edge_evidence">The risk is compounded by the fact that MLflow is routinely deployed by data science teams independently of central IT — frequently without appearing in the organisation’s asset inventory and without a formal patching SLA</data><data key="edge_extraction_method">minie</data><data key="edge_polarity">negative</data><data key="edge_modality">asserted</data></edge><edge id="oe_9585a4368358ecd8" sourc