e_raw">has tracked</data><data key="edge_assertion_id">a_11e403504447dd83</data><data key="edge_source_id">S17</data><data key="edge_source_url">https://diesec.com/2026/08/top-5-cybersecurity-news-stories-august-21-2026/</data><data key="edge_chunk_id">S17_C06</data><data key="edge_json_path">None</data><data key="edge_evidence">The cross-layer distribution of this week’s active exploitation reflects the same systematic methodology that DIESEC has tracked throughout 2026</data><data key="edge_extraction_method">minie</data><data key="edge_polarity">positive</data><data key="edge_modality">asserted</data></edge><edge id="oe_9ac906af42006e17" source="e_7b038a5cdf1b0e0a" target="e_f5b7473ec1d67a8d"><data key="edge_predicate_raw">patching</data><data key="edge_assertion_id">a_19a97815efae6acf</data><data key="edge_source_id">S17</data><data key="edge_source_url">https://diesec.com/2026/08/top-5-cybersecurity-news-stories-august-21-2026/</data><data key="edge_chunk_id">S17_C06</data><data key="edge_json_path">None</data><data key="edge_evidence">When one category of infrastructure gets hardened — edge devices, identity platforms, backup systems — targeting shifts to adjacent categories that have received less patching attention: AI and ML infrastructure maintained by data science teams, macOS fleets that run on a different patch cycle than Windows, on-premises collaboration platforms where July patches were deferred</data><data key="edge_extraction_method">heuristic</data><data key="edge_polarity">positive</data><data key="edge_modality">asserted</data></edge><edge id="oe_409c5f8cb588fecd" source="e_9cd5dd8ec85fd44e" target="e_8e4c3aed111ac3a7"><data key="edge_predicate_raw">patch</data><data key="edge_assertion_id">a_64bc6814921fadbd</data><data key="edge_source_id">S17</data><data key="edge_source_url">https://diesec.com/2026/08/top-5-cybersecurity-news-stories-august-21-2026/</data><data key="edge_chunk_id">S17_C06</data><data key="edge_json_path">None</data><data key="edge_evidence">When one category of infrastructure gets hardened — edge devices, identity platforms, backup systems — targeting shifts to adjacent categories that have received less patching attention: AI and ML infrastructure maintained by data science teams, macOS fleets that run on a different patch cycle than Windows, on-premises collaboration platforms where July patches were deferred</data><data key="edge_extraction_method">heuristic</data><data key="edge_polarity">positive</data><data key="edge_modality">asserted</data></edge><edge id="oe_af6dc7371cc6ab36" source="e_50b91da09b60a00f" target="e_1037ae67db43cc26"><data key="edge_predicate_raw">patching</data><data key="edge_assertion_id">a_692719b01c7e01eb</data><data key="edge_source_id">S17</data><data key="edge_source_url">https://diesec.com/2026/08/top-5-cybersecurity-news-stories-august-21-2026/</data><data key="edge_chunk_id">S17_C06</data><data key="edge_json_path">None</data><data key="edge_evidence">They are standard deployments in organisations that, by conventional patching and compliance metrics, would consider themselves reasonably maintained</data><data key="edge_extraction_method">heuristic</data><data key="edge_polarity">positive</data><data key="edge_modality">asserted</data></edge><edge id="oe_1148c47fa8105e56" source="e_68c065c3d124b88e" target="e_a728d14dd6bf744f"><data key="edge_predicate_raw">is that</data><data key="edge_assertion_id">a_061ef28b1bc3323b</data><data key="edge_source_id">S17</data><data key="edge_source_url">https://diesec.com/2026/08/top-5-cybersecurity-news-stories-august-21-2026/</data><data key="edge_chunk_id">S17_C06</data><data key="edge_json_path">None</data><data key="edge_evidence">This week’s lesson is that conventional metrics measure something narrower than the actual attack surface</data><data key="edge_extraction_method">minie</data><data key="edge_polarity">positive</data><data key="edge_modality">asserted</data></edge><edge id="oe_77fdc5c89f7d343f" source=