risk</data><data key="edge_chunk_id">S19_C03</data><data key="edge_json_path">None</data><data key="edge_evidence">In this context, “low” means that the threat actor cannot reasonably make enough attempts to overcome obstacles, either physical or security-based, to achieve total control</data><data key="edge_extraction_method">minie</data><data key="edge_polarity">negative</data><data key="edge_modality">asserted</data></edge><edge id="oe_7037817752922db8" source="e_369bd17212f6a742" target="e_b949320ce0e8e557"><data key="edge_predicate_raw">be overcome</data><data key="edge_assertion_id">a_fed2f5ffc2318735</data><data key="edge_source_id">S19</data><data key="edge_source_url">https://www.cisa.gov/news-events/directives/bod-26-04-prioritizing-security-updates-based-risk</data><data key="edge_chunk_id">S19_C03</data><data key="edge_json_path">None</data><data key="edge_evidence">In this context, “low” means that the threat actor cannot reasonably make enough attempts to overcome obstacles, either physical or security-based, to achieve total control</data><data key="edge_extraction_method">minie</data><data key="edge_polarity">negative</data><data key="edge_modality">asserted</data></edge><edge id="oe_27bfe2c3b1c92c9b" source="e_4e27ce4dd545ed47" target="e_16adc802a4d40d41"><data key="edge_predicate_raw">be achieve</data><data key="edge_assertion_id">a_0de4aac2c226a53b</data><data key="edge_source_id">S19</data><data key="edge_source_url">https://www.cisa.gov/news-events/directives/bod-26-04-prioritizing-security-updates-based-risk</data><data key="edge_chunk_id">S19_C03</data><data key="edge_json_path">None</data><data key="edge_evidence">In this context, “low” means that the threat actor cannot reasonably make enough attempts to overcome obstacles, either physical or security-based, to achieve total control</data><data key="edge_extraction_method">minie</data><data key="edge_polarity">negative</data><data key="edge_modality">asserted</data></edge><edge id="oe_fd66924c138a9050" source="e_0fcd2c716d506553" target="e_16adc802a4d40d41"><data key="edge_predicate_raw">be achieve</data><data key="edge_assertion_id">a_0ecc868e2669ebac</data><data key="edge_source_id">S19</data><data key="edge_source_url">https://www.cisa.gov/news-events/directives/bod-26-04-prioritizing-security-updates-based-risk</data><data key="edge_chunk_id">S19_C03</data><data key="edge_json_path">None</data><data key="edge_evidence">In this context, “low” means that the threat actor cannot reasonably make enough attempts to overcome obstacles, either physical or security-based, to achieve total control</data><data key="edge_extraction_method">minie</data><data key="edge_polarity">negative</data><data key="edge_modality">asserted</data></edge><edge id="oe_9d1d5e08d695c528" source="e_7a31e528d22c7737" target="e_fbcd10d66336c321"><data key="edge_predicate_raw">is form of</data><data key="edge_assertion_id">a_0419d12aa173d702</data><data key="edge_source_id">S19</data><data key="edge_source_url">https://www.cisa.gov/news-events/directives/bod-26-04-prioritizing-security-updates-based-risk</data><data key="edge_chunk_id">S19_C03</data><data key="edge_json_path">None</data><data key="edge_evidence">A denial-of-service attack is a form of limited control over the behavior of the vulnerable component</data><data key="edge_extraction_method">minie</data><data key="edge_polarity">positive</data><data key="edge_modality">asserted</data></edge><edge id="oe_5556e36be27def9b" source="e_7a31e528d22c7737" target="e_0651ca14b1e582f2"><data key="edge_predicate_raw">is form over behavior of</data><data key="edge_assertion_id">a_bf8d76daf9659520</data><data key="edge_source_id">S19</data><data key="edge_source_url">https://www.cisa.gov/news-events/directives/bod-26-04-prioritizing-security-updates-based-risk</data><data key="edge_chunk_id">S19_C03</data><data key="edge_json_path">None</data><data key="edge_evidence">A denial-of-service attack is a form of limited control over the behavior of the vulnerable component</data><data key="edge_extraction_method">minie</data><data key="edge_polarity">positive</data><data key="edge_modality">asserted</data></edge><edge id="oe_303c9f4bee8429aa" source="e_de77fe2010e65318" target="e_5afdbff0a492f81a"><data key="edge_predicate_raw">exploit</data><data key="edge_assertion_id">a_1ce91bd2fb14bbcd</data><data key="edge_source_id">S19</data><data key="edge_source_url">https://www.cisa.gov/news-events/directives/bod-26-04-prioritizing-security-updates-based-risk</data><data key="edge_chunk_id">S19_C03</data><data key="edge_json_path">None</data><data key="edge_evidence">- Total control:6 The exploit gives the adversary total control over the behavior of the software, including if the exploit reliably reveals log-in credentials</data><data key="edge_extraction_method">heuristic</data><data key="edge_polarity">positive</data><data key="edge_modality">asserted</data></edge><edge id="oe_0c20c995110c3a9d" source="e_3b8e724ba04c0cda" target="e_e4b4d883a0566e87"><data key="edge_predicate_raw">does apply to contractors Unless directed by</data><data key="edge_assertion_id">a_618b2ddc7ed96fd1</data><data key="edge_source_id">S19</data><data key="edge_source_url">https://www.cisa.gov/news-events/directives/bod-26-04-prioritizing-security-updates-based-risk</data><data key="edge_chunk_id">S19_C03</data><data key="edge_json_path">None</data><data key="edge_evidence">Unless directed by the governing procurement contract, this Directive does not apply to contractors, but FCEB agencies must review all contracts to determine what modifications are necessary to comply with the required actions of this Directive, in consultation with the Contracting Officer</data><data key="edge_extraction_method">minie</data><data key="edge_polarity">negative</data><data key="edge_modality">asserted</data></edge><edge id="oe_af64ab0bfe298d0d" source="e_3b8e724ba04c0cda" target="e_e695c8c8c109d76a"><data key="edge_predicate_raw">does apply to</data><data key="edge_assertion_id">a_267bf71dce8f607c</data><data key="edge_source_id">S19</data><data key="edge_source_url">https://www.cisa.gov/news-events/directives/bod-26-04-prioritizing-security-updates-based-risk</data><data key="edge_chunk_id">S19_C03</data><data key="edge_json_path">None</data><data key="edge_evidence">Unless directed by the governing procurement contract, this Directive does not apply to contractors, but FCEB agencies must review all contracts to determine what modifications are necessary to comply with the required actions of this Directive, in consultation with the Contracting Officer</data><data key="edge_extraction_method">minie</data><data key="edge_polarity">negative</data><data key="edge_modality">asserted</data></edge><edge id="oe_903021ff30626fc4" source="e_111b10019ad56f3b" target="e_ef074f92207fc9d3"><data key="edge_predicate_raw">be hosted in</data><data key="edge_assertion_id">a_3126a22f1f838ce4</data><data key="edge_source_id">S19</data><data key="edge_source_url">https://www.cisa.gov/news-events/directives/bod-26-04-prioritizing-security-updates-based-risk</data><data key="edge_chunk_id">S19_C03</data><data key="edge_json_path">None</data><data key="edge_evidence">For federal information systems hosted in third-party environments, including Federal Risk and Authorization Management Program (FedRAMP) certified environments, each agency is responsible for maintaining an inventory of those systems, obtaining status updates pertaining to this Directive, and ensuring compliance with its requirements through collaborative continuous monitoring</data><data key="edge_extraction_method">minie</data><data key="edge_polarity">positive</data><data key="edge_modality">asserted</data></edge><edge id="oe_83679ee51d6fdc54" source="e_bf21db5511f1fea3" target="e_cc5cee2d4857ec74"><data key="edge_predicate_raw">be certified</data><data key="edge_assertion_id">a_59cec7da11551cc8</data><data key="edge_source_id">S19</data><data key="edge_source_url">https://www.cisa.gov/news-events/directives/bod-26-04-prioritizing-security-updates-based-risk</data><data key="edge_chunk_id">S19_C03</data><data key="edge_json_path">None</data><data key="edge_evidence">For federal information systems hosted in third-party environments, including Federal Risk and Authorization Management Program (FedRAMP) certified environments, each agency is responsible for maintaining an inventory of those systems, obtaining status updates pertaining to this Directive, and ensuring compliance with its requirements through collaborative continuous monitoring</data><data key="edge_extraction_method">minie</data><data key="edge_polarity">positive</data><data key="edge_modality">asserted</data></edge><edge id="oe_d3707fe2e139215d" source="e_64417465ac02d653" target="e_cc5cee2d4857ec74"><data key="edge_predicate_raw">be certified</data><data key="edge_assertion_id">a_063d7ce29d33f91f</data><data key="edge_source_id">S19</data><data key="edge_source_url">https://www.cisa.gov/news-events/directives/bod-26-04-prioritizing-security-updates-based-risk</data><data key="edge_chunk_id">S19_C03</data><data key="edge_json_path">None</data><data key="edge_evidence">For federal information systems hosted in third-party environments, including Federal Risk and Authorization Management Program (FedRAMP) certified environments, each agency is responsible for maintaining an inventory of those systems, obtaining status updates pertaining to this Directive, and ensuring compliance with its requirements through collaborative continuous monitoring</data><data key="edge_extraction_method">minie</data><data key="edge_polarity">positive</data><data key="edge_modality">asserted</data></edge><edge id="oe_3b8d73e4982189e9" source="e_9c96f7af452c73e7" target="e_3b8e724ba04c0cda"><data key="edge_predicate_raw">be pertaining to</data><data key="edge_assertion_id">a_b465a19f9f35f6e1</data><data key="edge_source_id">S19</data><data key="edge_source_url">https://www.cisa.gov/news-events/directives/bod-26-04-prioritizing-security-updates-based-risk</data><data key="edge_chunk_id">S19_C03</data><data key="edge_json_path">None</data><data key="edge_evidence">For federal information systems hosted in third-party environments, including Federal Risk and Authorization Management Program (FedRAMP) certified environments, each agency is responsible for maintaining an inventory of those systems, obtaining status updates pertaining to this Directive, and ensuring compliance with its requirements through collaborative continuous monitoring</data><data key="edge_extraction_method">minie</data><data key="edge_polarity">positive</data><data key="edge_modality">asserted</data></edge><edge id="oe_1301ba192754320d" source="e_20617c6c62d27119" target="e_09bcf74b412ab749"><data key="edge_predicate_raw">work For</data><data key="edge_assertion_id">a_9ef15440e6fc33d9</data><data key="edge_source_id">S19</data><data key="edge_source_url">https://www.cisa.gov/news-events/directives/bod-26-04-prioritizing-security-updates-based-risk</data><data key="edge_chunk_id">S19_C03</data><data key="edge_json_path">None</data><data key="edge_evidence">For FedRAMP certified cloud service offerings, agencies must work through the FedRAMP PMO to ensure compliance with this Directive</data><data key="edge_extraction_method">minie</data><data key="edge_polarity">positive</data><data key="edge_modality">asserted</data></edge><edge id="oe_9cd13aefcaa980e7" source="e_20617c6c62d27119" target="e_23e0514bf9a1ff39"><data key="edge_predicate_raw">work For</data><data key="edge_assertion_id">a_ebaade6332e78515</data><data key="edge_source_id">S19</data><data key="edge_source_url">https://www.cisa.gov/news-events/directives/bod-26-04-prioritizing-security-updates-based-risk</data><data key="edge_chunk_id">S19_C03</data><data key="edge_json_path">None</data><data key="edge_evidence">For FedRAMP certified cloud service offerings, agencies must work through the FedRAMP PMO to ensure com