ability/CVE-2026-55040</data><data key="edge_chunk_id">S39_C04</data><data key="edge_json_path">None</data><data key="edge_evidence">The information provided in the Microsoft Knowledge Base is provided "as is" without warranty of any kind</data><data key="edge_extraction_method">heuristic</data><data key="edge_polarity">negative</data><data key="edge_modality">asserted</data></edge><edge id="oe_491d7bbace80b42b" source="e_9f13e30fa831fb5b" target="e_126f875dc12c3db5"><data key="edge_predicate_raw">have been advised of possibility of</data><data key="edge_assertion_id">a_2e21191b40ea110e</data><data key="edge_source_id">S39</data><data key="edge_source_url">https://msrc.microsoft.com/update-guide/vulnerability/CVE-2026-55040</data><data key="edge_chunk_id">S39_C04</data><data key="edge_json_path">None</data><data key="edge_evidence">In no event shall Microsoft Corporation or its suppliers be liable for any damages whatsoever including direct, indirect, incidental, consequential, loss of business profits or special damages, even if Microsoft Corporation or its suppliers have been advised of the possibility of such damages</data><data key="edge_extraction_method">minie</data><data key="edge_polarity">negative</data><data key="edge_modality">asserted</data></edge><edge id="oe_edd0fb57dab88cff" source="e_5843f0b3893d5cec" target="e_126f875dc12c3db5"><data key="edge_predicate_raw">have been advised of possibility of</data><data key="edge_assertion_id">a_a4aefd1deb580489</data><data key="edge_source_id">S39</data><data key="edge_source_url">https://msrc.microsoft.com/update-guide/vulnerability/CVE-2026-55040</data><data key="edge_chunk_id">S39_C04</data><data key="edge_json_path">None</data><data key="edge_evidence">In no event shall Microsoft Corporation or its suppliers be liable for any damages whatsoever including direct, indirect, incidental, consequential, loss of business profits or special damages, even if Microsoft Corporation or its suppliers have been advised of the possibility of such damages</data><data key="edge_extraction_method">minie</data><data key="edge_polarity">negative</data><data key="edge_modality">asserted</data></edge><edge id="oe_cd6356fc90f040a4" source="e_ebf0ea69dfcb9176" target="e_448ea7fbd1aed0cf"><data key="edge_predicate_raw">do not allow</data><data key="edge_assertion_id">a_e6581fefaf146f59</data><data key="edge_source_id">S39</data><data key="edge_source_url">https://msrc.microsoft.com/update-guide/vulnerability/CVE-2026-55040</data><data key="edge_chunk_id">S39_C04</data><data key="edge_json_path">None</data><data key="edge_evidence">Some states do not allow the exclusion or limitation of liability for consequential or incidental damages so the foregoing limitation may not apply</data><data key="edge_extraction_method">heuristic</data><data key="edge_polarity">negative</data><data key="edge_modality">possible</data></edge><edge id="oe_997fe5fe95ae0850" source="e_5c980ac08d8e06db" target="e_422ecd83d8fd548b"><data key="edge_predicate_raw">are with</data><data key="edge_assertion_id">a_9162ec0b6855fe51</data><data key="edge_source_id">S39</data><data key="edge_source_url">https://msrc.microsoft.com/update-guide/vulnerability/CVE-2026-55040</data><data key="edge_chunk_id">S39_C04</data><data key="edge_json_path">None</data><data key="edge_evidence">How satisfied are you with the MSRC Security Update Guide?</data><data key="edge_extraction_method">minie</data><data key="edge_polarity">positive</data><data key="edge_modality">asserted</data></edge><edge id="oe_87108eb179a5c3de" source="e_1d193316489d99d7" target="e_2da887c9a54f6ac7"><data key="edge_predicate_raw">conducted zero-day research project against</data><data key="edge_assertion_id">a_8a141d390e2ce755</data><data key="edge_source_id">S40</data><data key="edge_source_url">https://www.rapid7.com/blog/post/ve-cve-2026-55040-microsoft-sharepoint-jwt-token-authentication-bypass-fixed/</data><data key="edge_chunk_id">None</data><data key="edge_json_path">None</data><data key="edge_evidence">Rapid7 Labs conducted a zero-day research project against Microsoft SharePoint, resulting in the discovery of two new vulnerabilities that, when chained together, achieve unauthenticated remote code execution (RCE) against a vulnerable SharePoint server</data><data key="edge_extraction_method">minie</data><data key="edge_polarity">positive</data><data key="edge_modality">asserted</data></edge><edge id="oe_b80079abc9bf5be1" source="e_6f86ae8844c3ae87" target="e_8914ea73282ff98a"><data key="edge_predicate_raw">are disclosing first vulnerability in chain</data><data key="edge_assertion_id">a_71246f6d325b78d1</data><data key="edge_source_id">S40</data><data key="edge_source_url">https://www.rapid7.com/blog/post/ve-cve-2026-55040-microsoft-sharepoint-jwt-token-authentication-bypass-fixed/</data><data key="edge_chunk_id">None</data><data key="edge_json_path">None</data><data key="edge_evidence">Today, both Rapid7 and Microsoft are disclosing the first vulnerability in this chain, the authentication bypass vulnerability CVE-2026-55040</data><data key="edge_extraction_method">minie</data><data key="edge_polarity">positive</data><data key="edge_modality">asserted</data></edge><edge id="oe_3aaf568572e7d799" source="e_8e81ce852cc92461" target="e_8914ea73282ff98a"><data key="edge_predicate_raw">are disclosing first vulnerability in chain</data><data key="edge_assertion_id">a_a0b3f36aa1f6d151</data><data key="edge_source_id">S40</data><data key="edge_source_url">https://www.rapid7.com/blog/post/ve-cve-2026-55040-microsoft-sharepoint-jwt-token-authentication-bypass-fixed/</data><data key="edge_chunk_id">None</data><data key="edge_json_path">None</data><data key="edge_evidence">Today, both Rapid7 and Microsoft are disclosing the first vulnerability in this chain, the authentication bypass vulnerability CVE-2026-55040</data><data key="edge_extraction_method">minie</data><data key="edge_polarity">positive</data><data key="edge_modality">asserted</data></edge><edge id="oe_e214811eac0808e8" source="e_6f86ae8844c3ae87" target="e_df8fab3acbb5e0a1"><data key="edge_predicate_raw">are disclosing first vulnerability in</data><data key="edge_assertion_id">a_71ea9a023d986c12</data><data key="edge_source_id">S40</data><data key="edge_source_url">https://www.rapid7.com/blog/post/ve-cve-2026-55040-microsoft-sharepoint-jwt-token-authentication-bypass-fixed/</data><data key="edge_chunk_id">None</data><data key="edge_json_path">None</data><data key="edge_evidence">Today, both Rapid7 and Microsoft are disclosing the first vulnerability in this chain, the authentication bypass vulnerability CVE-2026-55040</data><data key="edge_extraction_method">minie</data><data key="edge_polarity">positive</data><data key="edge_modality">asserted</data></edge><edge id="oe_bb511e865ec27cf7" source="e_8e81ce852cc92461" target="e_df8fab3acbb5e0a1"><data key="edge_predicate_raw">are disclosing first vulnerability in</data><data key="edge_assertion_id">a_8a55f095b7c972bf</data><data key="edge_source_id">S40</data><data key="edge_source_url">https://www.rapid7.com/blog/post/ve-cve-2026-55040-microsoft-sharepoint-jwt-token-authentication-bypass-fixed/</data><data key="edge_chunk_id">None</data><data key="edge_json_path">None</data><data key="edge_evidence">Today, both Rapid7 and Microsoft are disclosing the first vulnerability in this chain, the authentication bypass vulnerability CVE-2026-55040</data><data key="edge_extraction_method">minie</data><data key="edge_polarity">positive</data><data key="edge_modality">asserted</data></edge><edge id="oe_bef1174d8f542ec5" source="e_f537ed160d33281a" target="e_717198c8fabfa876"><data key="edge_predicate_raw">be patched by Microsoft in</data><data key="edge_assertion_id">a_1ac3ed4db92629e8</data><data key="edge_source_id">S40</data><data key="edge_source_url">https://www.rapid7.com/blog/post/ve-cve-2026-55040-microsoft-sharepoint-jwt-token-authentication-bypass-fixed/</data><data key="edge_chunk_id">None</data><data key="edge_json_path">None</data><data key="edge_evidence">The RCE component of the exploit chain is expected to be patched by Microsoft in the next update cycle for August 2026</data><data key="edge_extraction_method">minie</data><data key="edge_polarity">positive</data><data key="edge_modality">asserted</data></edge><edge id="oe_2d1eca846963e535" source="e_f537ed160d33281a" target="e_16042e0b9ffd47c2"><data key="edge_predicate_raw">be patched by Microsoft for</data><data key="edge_assertion_id">a_dbb3081c2100a7f9</data><data key="edge_source_id">S40</data><data key="edge_source_url">https://www.rapid7.com/blog/post/ve-cve-2026-55040-microsoft-sharepoint-jwt-token-authentication-bypass-fixed/</data><data key="edge_chunk_id">None</data><data key="edge_json_path">None</data><data key="edge_evidence">The RCE component of the exploit chain is expected to be patched by Microsoft in the next update cycle for August 2026</data><data key="edge_extraction_method">minie</data><data key="edge_polarity">positive</data><data key="edge_modality">asserted</data></edge><edge id="oe_63c41421154e950f" source="e_f537ed160d33281a" target="e_8e81ce852cc92461"><data key="edge_predicate_raw">be patched by</data><data key="edge_assertion_id">a_6657bb4fcc3d0d42</data><data key="edge_source_id">S40</data><data key="edge_source_url">https://www.rapid7.com/blog/post/ve-cve-2026-55040-microsoft-sharepoint-jwt-token-authentication-bypass-fixed/</data><data key="edge_chunk_id">None</data><data key="edge_json_path">None</data><data key="edge_evidence">The RCE component of the exploit chain is expected to be patched by Microsoft in the next update cycle for August 2026</data><data key="edge_extraction_method">minie</data><data key="edge_polarity">positive</data><data key="edge_modality">asserted</data></edge><edge id="oe_dd97cc5c5a9f16f5" source="e_79e97526fe049cc1" target="e_c2c7b769717ba7d1"><data key="edge_predicate_raw">was developed as entry for</data><data key="edge_asserti