"edge_evidence">- July 14, 2026: The blog is updated to reflect that Microsoft’s published advisory now scores CVE-2026-55040 as critical severity, rather than medium severity</data><data key="edge_extraction_method">minie</data><data key="edge_polarity">positive</data><data key="edge_modality">asserted</data></edge><edge id="oe_7e085d87f362d138" source="e_6f86ae8844c3ae87" target="e_8ea2d5e84baadda6"><data key="edge_predicate_raw">publishes technical details for</data><data key="edge_assertion_id">a_630f03a85bce08b0</data><data key="edge_source_id">S40</data><data key="edge_source_url">https://www.rapid7.com/blog/post/ve-cve-2026-55040-microsoft-sharepoint-jwt-token-authentication-bypass-fixed/</data><data key="edge_chunk_id">None</data><data key="edge_json_path">None</data><data key="edge_evidence">- August 11, 2026: Rapid7 publishes technical details for CVE-2026-55040</data><data key="edge_extraction_method">minie</data><data key="edge_polarity">positive</data><data key="edge_modality">asserted</data></edge><edge id="oe_bcded468aef6f1ab" source="e_01326512763d0754" target="e_663ef150532fa83f"><data key="edge_predicate_raw">is updated to reflect</data><data key="edge_assertion_id">a_ae1124038e56093a</data><data key="edge_source_id">S40</data><data key="edge_source_url">https://www.rapid7.com/blog/post/ve-cve-2026-55040-microsoft-sharepoint-jwt-token-authentication-bypass-fixed/</data><data key="edge_chunk_id">None</data><data key="edge_json_path">None</data><data key="edge_evidence">- August 18, 2026: The blog is updated to reflect CISA’s addition of CVE-2026-55040 to its KEV catalog</data><data key="edge_extraction_method">minie</data><data key="edge_polarity">positive</data><data key="edge_modality">asserted</data></edge><edge id="oe_40ce1594094cd0e7" source="e_1d193316489d99d7" target="e_2da887c9a54f6ac7"><data key="edge_predicate_raw">conducted zero-day research project against</data><data key="edge_assertion_id">a_3748b08e32dd0102</data><data key="edge_source_id">S41</data><data key="edge_source_url">https://www.rapid7.com/blog/post/etr-cve-2026-63520-microsoft-sharepoint-remote-code-execution-fixed/</data><data key="edge_chunk_id">S41_C01</data><data key="edge_json_path">None</data><data key="edge_evidence">Rapid7 Labs conducted a zero-day research project against Microsoft SharePoint, resulting in the discovery of two new vulnerabilities that, when chained together, achieve unauthenticated remote code execution (RCE) against a vulnerable SharePoint server</data><data key="edge_extraction_method">minie</data><data key="edge_polarity">positive</data><data key="edge_modality">asserted</data></edge><edge id="oe_d003c78c0bc804d0" source="e_6f86ae8844c3ae87" target="e_8914ea73282ff98a"><data key="edge_predicate_raw">are disclosing second vulnerability in chain</data><data key="edge_assertion_id">a_16e6376aba235b7f</data><data key="edge_source_id">S41</data><data key="edge_source_url">https://www.rapid7.com/blog/post/etr-cve-2026-63520-microsoft-sharepoint-remote-code-execution-fixed/</data><data key="edge_chunk_id">S41_C01</data><data key="edge_json_path">None</data><data key="edge_evidence">Today, both Rapid7 and Microsoft are disclosing the second vulnerability in this chain, the RCE vulnerability CVE-2026-63520</data><data key="edge_extraction_method">minie</data><data key="edge_polarity">positive</data><data key="edge_modality">asserted</data></edge><edge id="oe_83f66cd630a2bab1" source="e_8e81ce852cc92461" target="e_8914ea73282ff98a"><data key="edge_predicate_raw">are disclosing second vulnerability in chain</data><data key="edge_assertion_id">a_1f610deb12288987</data><data key="edge_source_id">S41</data><data key="edge_source_url">https://www.rapid7.com/blog/post/etr-cve-2026-63520-microsoft-sharepoint-remote-code-execution-fixed/</data><data key="edge_chunk_id">S41_C01</data><data key="edge_json_path">None</data><data key="edge_evidence">Today, both Rapid7 and Microsoft are disclosing the second vulnerability in this chain, the RCE vulnerability CVE-2026-63520</data><data key="edge_extraction_method">minie</data><data key="edge_polarity">positive</data><data key="edge_modality">asserted</data></edge><edge id="oe_ee4ac57f24dad883" source="e_6f86ae8844c3ae87" target="e_df8fab3acbb5e0a1"><data key="edge_predicate_raw">are disclosing second vulnerability in</data><data key="edge_assertion_id">a_464332b79caa4c8f</data><data key="edge_source_id">S41</data><data key="edge_source_url">https://www.rapid7.com/blog/post/etr-cve-2026-63520-microsoft-sharepoint-remote-code-execution-fixed/</data><data key="edge_chunk_id">S41_C01</data><data key="edge_json_path">None</data><data key="edge_evidence">Today, both Rapid7 and Microsoft are disclosing the second vulnerability in this chain, the RCE vulnerability CVE-2026-63520</data><data key="edge_extraction_method">minie</data><data key="edge_polarity">positive</data><data key="edge_modality">asserted</data></edge><edge id="oe_a2a4548b3bef43e0" source="e_8e81ce852cc92461" target="e_df8fab3acbb5e0a1"><data key="edge_predicate_raw">are disclosing second vulnerability in</data><data key="edge_assertion_id">a_cb5c328d9eecd70f</data><data key="edge_source_id">S41</data><data key="edge_source_url">https://www.rapid7.com/blog/post/etr-cve-2026-63520-microsoft-sharepoint-remote-code-execution-fixed/</data><data key="edge_chunk_id">S41_C01</data><data key="edge_json_path">None</data><data key="edge_evidence">Today, both Rapid7 and Microsoft are disclosing the second vulnerability in this chain, the RCE vulnerability CVE-2026-63520</data><data key="edge_extraction_method">minie</data><data key="edge_polarity">positive</data><data key="edge_modality">asserted</data></edge><edge id="oe_6f092d4a1be09eb6" source="e_a037966ba561efa0" target="e_e0732d8c6557cdf3"><data key="edge_predicate_raw">was disclosed by Rapid7</data><data key="edge_assertion_id">a_56b191aa4955cd94</data><data key="edge_source_id">S41</data><data key="edge_source_url">https://www.rapid7.com/blog/post/etr-cve-2026-63520-microsoft-sharepoint-remote-code-execution-fixed/</data><data key="edge_chunk_id">S41_C01</data><data key="edge_json_path">None</data><data key="edge_evidence">The first vulnerability in the chain, CVE-2026-55040, was disclosed by Rapid7 and Microsoft last month</data><data key="edge_extraction_method">minie</data><data key="edge_polarity">positive</data><data key="edge_modality">asserted</data></edge><edge id="oe_ac31d27b6599fd55" source="e_a037966ba561efa0" target="e_e0732d8c6557cdf3"><data key="edge_predicate_raw">was disclosed by Microsoft</data><data key="edge_assertion_id">a_9c0bcc4ba11ccd68</data><data key="edge_source_id">S41</data><data key="edge_source_url">https://www.rapid7.com/blog/post/etr-cve-2026-63520-microsoft-sharepoint-remote-code-execution-fixed/</data><data key="edge_chunk_id">S41_C01</data><data key="edge_json_path">None</data><data key="edge_evidence">The first vulnerability in the chain, CVE-2026-55040, was disclosed by Rapid7 and Microsoft last month</data><data key="edge_extraction_method">minie</data><data key="edge_polarity">positive</data><data key="edge_modality">asserted</data></edge><edge id="oe_0777f54d49610666" source="e_a037966ba561efa0" target="e_6f86ae8844c3ae87"><data key="edge_predicate_raw">was disclosed by</data><data key="edge_assertion_id">a_6cbd8f3453a08d0e</data><data key="edge_source_id">S41</data><data key="edge_source_url">https://www.rapid7.com/blog/post/etr-cve-2026-63520-microsoft-sharepoint-remote-code-execution-fixed/</data><data key="edge_chunk_id">S41_C01</data><data key="edge_json_path">None</data><data key="edge_evidence">The first vulnerability in the chain, CVE-2026-55040, was disclosed by Rapid7 and Microsoft last month</data><data key="edge_extraction_method">minie</data><data key="edge_polarity">positive</data><data key="edge_modality">asserted</data></edge><edge id="oe_0b7bde5fc5d83bb5" source="e_a037966ba561efa0" target="e_8e81ce852cc92461"><data key="edge_predicate_raw">was disclosed by</data><data key="edge_assertion_id">a_9cfe99fdd338eeec</data><data key="edge_source_id">S41</data><data key="edge_source_url">https://www.rapid7.com/blog/post/etr-cve-2026-63520-microsoft-sharepoint-remote-code-execution-fixed/</data><data key="edge_chunk_id">S41_C01</data><data key="edge_json_path">None</data><data key="edge_evidence">The first vulnerability in the chain, CVE-2026-55040, was disclosed by Rapid7 and Microsoft last month</data><data key="edge_extraction_method">minie</data><data key="edge_polarity">positive</data><data key="edge_modality">asserted</data></edge><edge id="oe_18108813a7576d32" source="e_2d6bfbad72a7f245" target="e_090a49403d237e84"><data key="edge_predicate_raw">be execute arbitrary code on</data><data key="edge_assertion_id">a_2d1a3b97735aafe3</data><data key="edge_source_id">S41</data><data key="edge_source_url">https://www.rapid7.com/blog/post/etr-cve-2026-63520-microsoft-sharepoint-remote-code-execution-fixed/</data><data key="edge_chunk_id">S41_C01</data><data key="edge_json_path">None</data><data key="edge_evidence">An attacker can leverage CVE-2026-63520 to execute arbitrary code on a vulnerable SharePoint server with the privileges of the SharePoint Site’s service account</data><data key="edge_extraction_method">minie</data><data key="edge_polarity">positive</data><data key="edge_modality">possible</data></edge><edge id="oe_013f141ec43a74fa" source="e_dbd1ba0cc63988dc" target="e_2d31e1284f8f402d"><data key="edge_predicate_raw">is due to</data><data key="edge_assertion_id">a_fb8e5c7fcb320e0b</data><data key="edge_source_id">S41</data><data key="edge_source_url">https://www.rapid7.com/blog/post/etr-cve-2026-63520-microsoft-sharepoint-remote-code-execution-fixed/</data><data key="edge_chunk_id">S41_C01</data><data key="edge_json_path">None</data><data key="edge_evidence">The vulnerability is due to an unsafe .NET type instantiation issue within the Business Connectivity Services</data><data key="edge_extraction_method">minie</data><data key="edge_polarity">positive</data><data key="edge_modality">asserted</data></edge><edge id="oe_986d79c4f3c11176" source="e_2a2853641087ea0c" target="e_4ec908d775864dbb"><data key="edge_predicate_raw">exploit</data><data key="edge_assertion_id">a_fadccd5d5e0c8d99</data><data key="edge_source_id">S41</data><data key="edge_source_url">https://www.rapid7.com/blog/post/etr-cve-2026-63520-microsoft-sharepoint-remote-code-execution-fixed/</data><data key="edge_chunk_id">S41_C01</data><data key="edge_json_path">None</data><data key="edge_evidence">While the severity of the RCE is described as high, chained together with CVE-2026-55040 it becomes part of a critical unauthenticated RCE exploit chain against SharePoint</data><data key="edge_extraction_method">heuristic</data><data key="edge_polarity">positive</data><data key="edge_modality">asserted</data></edge><edge id="oe_a34ba41fea3f6ccb" source="e_79e97526fe049cc1" target="e_c69d823c1803b35a"><data key="edge_predicate_raw">was developed as entry for</data><data key="edge_assertion_id">a_60df3160d242cb53</data><data key="edge_source_id">S41</data><data key="edge_source_url">https://www.rapid7.com/blog/post/etr-cve-2026-63520-microsoft-sharepoint-remote-code-execution-fixed/</data><data key="edge_chunk_id">S41_C01</data><data key="edge_json_path">None</data><data key="edge_evidence">The exploit chain was developed as an entry for this year's Pwn2Own Berlin hacking competition; while our entry was unsuccessful on the day of the competition, this research highlights Rapid7 Labs' continued effort to raise the bar in Vulnerability Intelligence and our commitment to the preemptive protection of our customers through original vulnerability research</data><data key="edge_extraction_method">minie</data><data key="edge_polarity">positive</data><data key="edge_modality">asserted</data></edge><edge id="oe_1d8c09e6ddd64c8a" source="e_4f708a5efc3c1b7f" target="e_27e501b530a044e2"><data key="edge_predicate_raw">was unsuccessful on the day of</data><data key="edge_assertion_id">a_a631417b986d9683</data><data key="edge_source_id">S41</data><data key="edge_source_url">https://www.rapid7.com/blog/post/etr-cve-2026-63520-microsoft-sharepoint-remote-code-execution-fixed/</data><data key="edge_chunk_id">S41_C01</data><data key="edge_json_path">None</data><data key="edge_evidence">The exploit chain was developed as an entry for this year's Pwn2Own Berlin hacking competition; while our entry was unsuccessful on the day of the competition, this research highlights Rapid7 Labs' continued effort to raise the bar in Vulnerability Intelligence and our commitment to the preemptive protection of our customers through original vulnerability research</data><data key="edge_extraction_method">minie</data><data key="edge_polarity">positive</data><data key="edge_modality">asserted</data></edge><edge id="oe_9c249c04b8ad717b" source="e_f9cdf5b96222dc10" target="e_68d56bc6976682a6"><data key="edge_predicate_raw">highlights</data><data key="edge_assertion_id">a_ff46576f351c3ef9</data><data key="edge_source_id">S41</data><data key="edge_source_url">https://www.rapid7.com/blog/post/etr-cve-2026-63520-microsoft-sharepoint-remote-code-execution-fixed/</data><data key="edge_chunk_id">S41_C01</data><data key="edge_json_path">None</data><data key="edge_evidence">The exploit chain was developed as an entry for this year's Pwn2Own Berlin hacking competition; while our entry was unsuccessful on the day of the competition, this research highlights Rapid7 Labs' continued effort to raise the bar in Vulnerability Intelligence and our commitment to the preemptive protection of our customers through original vulnerability research</data><data key="edge_extraction_method">minie</data><data key="edge_polarity">positive</data><data key="edge_modality">asserted</data></edge><edge id="oe_a988ea6949efa1cf" source="e_a46852212f0950f8" target="e_eaac4a62d949ee42"><data key="edge_predicate_raw">be raise bar in</data><data key="edge_assertion_id">a_f66cb219e0c7c9b8</data><data key="edge_source_id">S41</data><data key="edge_source_url">https://www.rapid7.com/blog/post/etr-cve-2026-63520-microsoft-sharepoint-remote-code-execution-fixed/</data><data key="edge_chunk_id">S41_C01</data><data key="edge_json_path">None</data><data key="edge_evidence">The exploit chain was developed as an entry for this year's Pwn2Own Berlin hacking competition; while our entry was unsuccessful on the day of the competition, this research highlights Rapid7 Labs' continued effort to raise the bar in Vulnerability Intelligence and our commitment to the preemptive protection of our customers through original vulnerability research</data><data key="edge_extraction_method">minie</data><data key="edge_polarity">positive</data><data key="edge_modality">asserted</data></edge><edge id="oe_7e3a00c5711e4c8a" source="e_2fdd3b92e2cb08b5" target="e_85560bc21b6976ab"><data key="edge_predicate_raw">assist in</data><data key="edge_assertion_id">a_c59896b4cd6a52e8</data><data key="edge_source_id">S41</data><data key="edge_source_url">https://www.rapid7.com/blog/post/etr-cve-2026-63520-microsoft-sharepoint-remote-code-execution-fixed/</data><data key="edge_chunk_id">S41_C01</data><data key="edge_json_path">None</data><data key="edge_evidence">Our research methodology focused on understanding how publicly available AI models can assist in the discovery of significant vulnerabilities against proprietary enterprise targets</data><data key="edge_extraction_method">minie</data><data key="edge_polarity">positive</data><data key="edge_modality">possible</data></edge><edge id="oe_e0d7fbe4f484e9d3" source="e_016d96cb50ca7314" target="e_66b67e8882cde816"><data key="edge_predicate_raw">is accelerating</data><data key="edge_assertion_id">a_47cc124171eee89b</data><data key="edge_source_id">S41</data><data key="edge_source_url">https://www.rapid7.com/blog/post/etr-cve-2026-63520-microsoft-sharepoint-remote-code-execution-fixed/</data><data key