e_id">S41</data><data key="edge_source_url">https://www.rapid7.com/blog/post/etr-cve-2026-63520-microsoft-sharepoint-remote-code-execution-fixed/</data><data key="edge_chunk_id">S41_C03</data><data key="edge_json_path">None</data><data key="edge_evidence">Because SharePoint acts as a critical bridge between internal users, active directories, and cloud infrastructure, vulnerabilities within its architecture present a high-risk attack surface</data><data key="edge_extraction_method">minie</data><data key="edge_polarity">positive</data><data key="edge_modality">asserted</data></edge><edge id="oe_eebd2b1514107e39" source="e_791de43fccfd7f2f" target="e_e6e90eb94c09e808"><data key="edge_predicate_raw">acts as critical bridge between</data><data key="edge_assertion_id">a_112a3ea932b90e8e</data><data key="edge_source_id">S41</data><data key="edge_source_url">https://www.rapid7.com/blog/post/etr-cve-2026-63520-microsoft-sharepoint-remote-code-execution-fixed/</data><data key="edge_chunk_id">S41_C03</data><data key="edge_json_path">None</data><data key="edge_evidence">Because SharePoint acts as a critical bridge between internal users, active directories, and cloud infrastructure, vulnerabilities within its architecture present a high-risk attack surface</data><data key="edge_extraction_method">minie</data><data key="edge_polarity">positive</data><data key="edge_modality">asserted</data></edge><edge id="oe_2627463f924dea14" source="e_fbfb70a00355d68e" target="e_265d1c58ed249684"><data key="edge_predicate_raw">allows attacker to execute arbitrary code on</data><data key="edge_assertion_id">a_2e26afcc51480f51</data><data key="edge_source_id">S41</data><data key="edge_source_url">https://www.rapid7.com/blog/post/etr-cve-2026-63520-microsoft-sharepoint-remote-code-execution-fixed/</data><data key="edge_chunk_id">S41_C03</data><data key="edge_json_path">None</data><data key="edge_evidence">CVE-2026-63520 allows an attacker to execute arbitrary code on an affected server</data><data key="edge_extraction_method">minie</data><data key="edge_polarity">positive</data><data key="edge_modality">asserted</data></edge><edge id="oe_d96cdea5824c4f5f" source="e_fbfb70a00355d68e" target="e_ac2a710687d20f0f"><data key="edge_predicate_raw">allows attacker to execute</data><data key="edge_assertion_id">a_cc9e3339765c2a05</data><data key="edge_source_id">S41</data><data key="edge_source_url">https://www.rapid7.com/blog/post/etr-cve-2026-63520-microsoft-sharepoint-remote-code-execution-fixed/</data><data key="edge_chunk_id">S41_C03</data><data key="edge_json_path">None</data><data key="edge_evidence">CVE-2026-63520 allows an attacker to execute arbitrary code on an affected server</data><data key="edge_extraction_method">minie</data><data key="edge_polarity">positive</data><data key="edge_modality">asserted</data></edge><edge id="oe_b3566e74844a6423" source="e_05efe0da27589031" target="e_83f09256e9e71bb6"><data key="edge_predicate_raw">perform arbitrary operations such as</data><data key="edge_assertion_id">a_6f68092e7f9660d7</data><data key="edge_source_id">S41</data><data key="edge_source_url">https://www.rapid7.com/blog/post/etr-cve-2026-63520-microsoft-sharepoint-remote-code-execution-fixed/</data><data key="edge_chunk_id">S41_C03</data><data key="edge_json_path">None</data><data key="edge_evidence">By crafting a custom .NET gadget chain, an attacker can perform arbitrary operations such as executing an attacker-controlled OS command</data><data key="edge_extraction_method">minie</data><data key="edge_polarity">positive</data><data key="edge_modality">possible</data></edge><edge id="oe_21883de8bda5315e" source="e_17d9e7d2f2eada95" target="e_b1d71ecff3a572ce"><data key="edge_predicate_raw">is executed with permission of Windows service</data><data key="edge_assertion_id">a_6b0a5fd245bc2034</data><data key="edge_source_id">S41</data><data key="edge_source_url">https://www.rapid7.com/blog/post/etr-cve-2026-63520-microsoft-sharepoint-remote-code-execution-fixed/</data><data key="edge_chunk_id">S41_C03</data><data key="edge_json_path">None</data><data key="edge_evidence">The attacker's arbitrary code is executed with the permission of the Windows service account running the SharePoint Site instance</data><data key="edge_extraction_method">minie</data><data key="edge_polarity">positive</data><data key="edge_modality">asserted</data></edge><edge id="oe_aa88222b88415897" source="e_17d9e7d2f2eada95" target="e_b1d71ecff3a572ce"><data key="edge_predicate_raw">is executed</data><data key="edge_assertion_id">a_07b690e1e5697644</data><data key="edge_source_id">S41</data><data key="edge_source_url">https://www.rapid7.com/blog/post/etr-cve-2026-63520-microsoft-sharepoint-remote-code-execution-fixed/</data><data key="edge_chunk_id">S41_C03</data><data key="edge_json_path">None</data><data key="edge_evidence">The attacker's arbitrary code is executed with the permission of the Windows service account running the SharePoint Site instance</data><data key="edge_extraction_method">minie</data><data key="edge_polarity">positive</data><data key="edge_modality">asserted</data></edge><edge id="oe_f7ccb82b84f7330e" source="e_fbfb70a00355d68e" target="e_056762b3f0d13b70"><data key="edge_predicate_raw">be chained to</data><data key="edge_assertion_id">a_696a8c8782537dca</data><data key="edge_source_id">S41</data><data key="edge_source_url">https://www.rapid7.com/blog/post/etr-cve-2026-63520-microsoft-sharepoint-remote-code-execution-fixed/</data><data key="edge_chunk_id">S41_C03</data><data key="edge_json_path">None</data><data key="edge_evidence">As CVE-2026-63520 can be chained to the authentication bypass vulnerability, CVE-2026-55040, the resulting exploit chain allows for unauthenticated RCE against a vulnerable server</data><data key="edge_extraction_method">minie</data><data key="edge_polarity">positive</data><data key="edge_modality">possible</data></edge><edge id="oe_2c72af814e4294ba" source="e_df8fab3acbb5e0a1" target="e_a93ecc5884a81ad6"><data key="edge_predicate_raw">allows for unauthenticated RCE against</data><data key="edge_assertion_id">a_af452296f3124217</data><data key="edge_source_id">S41</data><data key="edge_source_url">https://www.rapid7.com/blog/post/etr-cve-2026-63520-microsoft-sharepoint-remote-code-execution-fixed/</data><data key="edge_chunk_id">S41_C03</data><data key="edge_json_path">None</data><data key="edge_evidence">As CVE-2026-63520 can be chained to the authentication bypass vulnerability, CVE-2026-55040, the resulting exploit chain allows for unauthenticated RCE against a vulnerable server</data><data key="edge_extraction_method">minie</data><data key="edge_polarity">positive</data><data key="edge_modality">possible</data></edge><edge id="oe_d4abb524694ca2b5" source="e_dbd1ba0cc63988dc" target="e_92755c59eb5d2a5b"><data key="edge_predicate_raw">was discovered by</data><data key="edge_assertion_id">a_1d23d764690fde94</data><data key="edge_source_id">S41</data><data key="edge_source_url">https://www.rapid7.com/blog/post/etr-cve-2026-63520-microsoft-sharepoint-remote-code-execution-fixed/</data><data key="edge_chunk_id">S41_C03</data><data key="edge_json_path">None</data><data key="edge_evidence">This vulnerability was discovered by Stephen Fewer, Senior Principal Security Researcher at Rapid7 and is being disclosed in accordance with Rapid7's vulnerability disclosure policy</data><data key="edge_extraction_method">minie</data><data key="edge_polarity">positive</data><data key="edge_modality">asserted</data></edge><edge id="oe_5ff0e0a339468371" source="e_dbd1ba0cc63988dc" target="e_6f86ae8844c3ae87"><data key="edge_predicate_raw">was discovered by Senior Principal Security Researcher at</data><data key="edge_assertion_id">a_dab9ca22fcbc6afd</data><data key="edge_source_id">S41</data><data key="edge_source_url">https://www.rapid7.com/blog/post/etr-cve-2026-63520-microsoft-sharepoint-remote-code-execution-fixed/</data><data key="edge_chunk_id">S41_C03</data><data key="edge_