</data><data key="edge_polarity">negative</data><data key="edge_modality">possible</data></edge><edge id="oe_a177539fa7368fe3" source="e_537e6ab50e8f2e44" target="e_c7fbbe2b7d7f160a"><data key="edge_predicate_raw">prevent</data><data key="edge_assertion_id">a_19a5f0180e2e6993</data><data key="edge_source_id">S42</data><data key="edge_source_url">https://msrc.microsoft.com/update-guide/vulnerability/CVE-2026-63520</data><data key="edge_chunk_id">S42_C02</data><data key="edge_json_path">None</data><data key="edge_evidence">Alternatively, the attacker has the ability to deny some availability, but the loss of availability presents a direct, serious consequence to the impacted component (e.g., the attacker cannot disrupt existing connections, but can prevent new connections; the attacker can repeatedly exploit a vulnerability that, in each instance of a successful attack, leaks a only small amount of memory, but after repeated exploitation causes a service to become completely unavailable)</data><data key="edge_extraction_method">minie</data><data key="edge_polarity">negative</data><data key="edge_modality">possible</data></edge><edge id="oe_b118ac1fcf9b6844" source="e_db6268d6f310949e" target="e_b082256680928c6b"><data key="edge_predicate_raw">causes service to become</data><data key="edge_assertion_id">a_fd34a4da0d4448fe</data><data key="edge_source_id">S42</data><data key="edge_source_url">https://msrc.microsoft.com/update-guide/vulnerability/CVE-2026-63520</data><data key="edge_chunk_id">S42_C03</data><data key="edge_json_path">None</data><data key="edge_evidence">of a successful attack, leaks a only small amount of memory, but after repeated exploitation causes a service to become completely unavailable)</data><data key="edge_extraction_method">minie</data><data key="edge_polarity">positive</data><data key="edge_modality">asserted</data></edge><edge id="oe_5607f081fd9568f7" source="e_db6268d6f310949e" target="e_9111a79bb0a0398b"><data key="edge_predicate_raw">causes</data><data key="edge_assertion_id">a_e745ace0e99706ce</data><data key="edge_source_id">S42</data><data key="edge_source_url">https://msrc.microsoft.com/update-guide/vulnerability/CVE-2026-63520</data><data key="edge_chunk_id">S42_C03</data><data key="edge_json_path">None</data><data key="edge_evidence">of a successful attack, leaks a only small amount of memory, but after repeated exploitation causes a service to become completely unavailable)</data><data key="edge_extraction_method">minie</data><data key="edge_polarity">positive</data><data key="edge_modality">asserted</data></edge><edge id="oe_d23312affeaa925a" source="e_db6268d6f310949e" target="e_b082256680928c6b"><data key="edge_predicate_raw">be become</data><data key="edge_assertion_id">a_c4952499e9230e67</data><data key="edge_source_id">S42</data><data key="edge_source_url">https://msrc.microsoft.com/update-guide/vulnerability/CVE-2026-63520</data><data key="edge_chunk_id">S42_C03</data><data key="edge_json_path">None</data><data key="edge_evidence">of a successful attack, leaks a only small amount of memory, but after repeated exploitation causes a service to become completely unavailable)</data><data key="edge_extraction_method">minie</data><data key="edge_polarity">positive</data><data key="edge_modality">asserted</data></edge><edge id="oe_ffa6cc9ef25d9a6b" source="e_dd256f5f1485834f" target="e_7adbd4ff7f080bab"><data key="edge_predicate_raw">exploit</data><data key="edge_assertion_id">a_d977a19f6d792ddd</data><data key="edge_source_id">S42</data><data key="edge_source_url">https://msrc.microsoft.com/update-guide/vulnerability/CVE-2026-63520</data><data key="edge_chunk_id">S42_C03</data><data key="edge_json_path">None</data><data key="edge_evidence">This metric measures the likelihood of the vulnerability being attacked, and is typically based on the current state of exploit techniques, public availability of exploit code, or active, 'in-the-wild' exploitation</data><data key="edge_extraction_method">heuristic</data><data key="edge_polarity">positive</data><data key="edge_modality">asserted</data></edge><edge id="oe_94772fae67689dab" source="e_527c56c7674a26dd" target="e_904da0b4f3960fb3"><data key="edge_predicate_raw">is important factor for</data><data key="edge_assertion_id">a_ce8d9bca095ca822</data><data key="edge_source_id">S42</data><data key="edge_source_url">https://msrc.microsoft.com/update-guide/vulnerability/CVE-2026-63520</data><data key="edge_chunk_id">S42_C03</data><data key="edge_json_path">None</data><data key="edge_evidence">The Remediation Level of a vulnerability is an important factor for prioritization</data><data key="edge_extraction_method">minie</data><data key="edge_polarity">positive</data><data key="edge_modality">asserted</data></edge><edge id="oe_297b86311faf4f81" source="e_4228490cbf8a6d91" target="e_98c110f1e21aa4eb"><data key="edge_predicate_raw">is unpatched when</data><data key="edge_assertion_id">a_c054950d94ae3b86</data><data key="edge_source_id">S42</data><data key="edge_source_url">https://msrc.microsoft.com/update-guide/vulnerability/CVE-2026-63520</data><data key="edge_chunk_id">S42_C03</data><data key="edge_json_path">None</data><data key="edge_evidence">The typical vulnerability is unpatched when initially published</data><data key="edge_extraction_method">minie</data><data key="edge_polarity">positive</data><data key="edge_modality">asserted</data></edge><edge id="oe_391a313e03597056" source="e_791715a2772f6f50" target="e_ccb9c0114a2220f3"><data key="edge_predicate_raw">patch</data><data key="edge_assertion_id">a_767822d914a7949b</data><data key="edge_source_id">S42</data><data key="edge_source_url">https://msrc.microsoft.com/update-guide/vulnerability/CVE-2026-63520</data><data key="edge_chunk_id">S42_C03</data><data key="edge_json_path">None</data><data key="edge_evidence">Workarounds or hotfixes may offer interim remediation until an official patch or upgrade is issued</data><data key="edge_extraction_method">heuristic</data><data key="edge_polarity">positive</data><data key="edge_modality">possible</data></edge><edge id="oe_b7f113b6d3804a5c" source="e_edf56b768b8904e2" target="e_a568574ebde0ab4b"><data key="edge_predicate_raw">becomes</data><data key="edge_assertion_id">a_e4a4b1aba7631936</data><data key="edge_source_id">S42</data><data key="edge_source_url">https://msrc.microsoft.com/update-guide/vulnerability/CVE-2026-63520</data><data key="edge_chunk_id">S42_C03</data><data key="edge_json_path">None</data><data key="edge_evidence">Each of these respective stages adjusts the temporal score downwards, reflecting the decreasing urgency as remediation becomes final</data><data key="edge_extraction_method">minie</data><data key="edge_polarity">positive</data><data key="edge_modality">asserted</data></edge><edge id="oe_1f2d04b3e6ca2182" source="e_298a9593b67b7b1f" target="e_34cf20183f45e324"><data key="edge_predicate_raw">has issued</data><data key="edge_assertion_id">a_a17d72146e1d168a</data><data key="edge_source_id">S42</data><data key="edge_source_url">https://msrc.microsoft.com/update-guide/vulnerability/CVE-2026-63520</data><data key="edge_chunk_id">S42_C03</data><data key="edge_json_path">None</data><data key="edge_evidence">Either the vendor has issued an official patch, or an upgrade is available</data><data key="edge_extraction_method">minie</data><data key="edge_polarity">positive</data><data key="edge_modality">asserted</data></edge><edge id="oe_43cb1722d64480ab" source="e_298a9593b67b7b1f" target="e_d068a0aa82ac3043"><data key="edge_predicate_raw">has issued</data><data key="edge_assertion_id">a_1edb5ae154636901</data><data key="edge_source_id">S42</data><data key="edge_source_url">https://msrc.microsoft.com/update-guide/vulnerability/CVE-2026-63520</data><data key="edge_chunk_id">S42_C03</data><data key="edge_json_path">None</data><data key="edge_evidence">Either the vendor has issued an official patch, or an upgrade is available</data><data key="edge_extraction_method">minie</data><data key="edge_polarity">positive</data><data key="edge_modality">asserted</data></edge><edge id="oe_44aa61e2ad60310b" source="e_66e4de79357567de" target="e_e916c75e8e43cbaf"><data key="edge_predicate_raw">cause</data><data key="edge_assertion_id">a_72e8ae886647116e</data><data key="edge_source_id">S42</data><data key="edge_source_url">https://msrc.microsoft.com/update-guide/vulnerability/CVE-2026-63520</data><data key="edge_chunk_id">S42_C03</data><data key="edge_json_path">None</data><data key="edge_evidence">For example, an impact may be recognized as undesirable, but the root cause may not be known</data><data key="edge_extraction_method">heuristic</data><data key="edge_polarity">negative</data><data key="edge_modality">possible</data></edge><edge id="oe_0b8ab82a5be3b8e1" source="e_dbd1ba0cc63988dc" target="e_33214aeb432b738b"><data key="edge_predicate_raw">be confirmed through</data><data key="edge_assertion_id">a_f7a8e295117182f6</data><data key="edge_source_id">S42</data><data key="edge_source_url">https://msrc.microsoft.com/update-guide/vulnerability/CVE-2026-63520</data><data key="edge_chunk_id">S42_C03</data><data key="edge_json_path">None</data><data key="edge_evidence">Finally, a vulnerability may be confirmed through acknowledgement by the author or vendor of the affected technology</data><data key="edge_extraction_method">minie</data><data key="edge_polarity">positive</data><data key="edge_modality">possible</data></edge><edge id="oe_7d6fa64d4660082a" source="e_dbd1ba0cc63988dc" target="e_298a9593b67b7b1f"><data key="edge_predicate_raw">be confirmed through acknowledgement by</data><data key="edge_assertion_id">a_c888e0c28f362066</data><data key="edge_source_id">S42</data><data key="edge_source_url">https://msrc.microsoft.com/update-guide/vulnerability/CVE-2026-63520</data><data key="edge_chunk_id">S42_C03</data><data key="edge_json_path">None</data><data key="edge_evidence">Finally, a vulnerability may be confirmed through acknowledgement by the author or vendor of the affected technology</data><data key="edge_extraction_method">minie</data><data key="edge_polarity">positive</data><data key="edge_modality">possible</data></edge><edge id="oe_68c7f7e6159cbae3" source="e_dbd1ba0cc63988dc" target="e_cf4606d100a09d0c"><data key="edge_predicate_raw">is known to exist with</data><data key="edge_assertion_id">a_bb8b0c7cedd99d1c</data><data key="edge_source_id">S42</data><data key="edge_source_url">https://msrc.microsoft.com/update-guide/vulnerability/CVE-2026-63520</data><data key="edge_chunk_id">S42_C03</data><data key="edge_json_path">None</data><data key="edge_evidence">The urgency of a vulnerability is higher when a vulnerability is known to exist with certainty</data><data key="edge_extraction_method">minie</data><data key="edge_polarity">positive</data><data key="edge_modality">asserted</data></edge><edge id="oe_1f1748c862e294c5" source="e_4676679afd99eed0" target="e_3655237b10b88be1"><data key="edge_predicate_raw">suggests</data><data key="edge_assertion_id">a_a9131ddaf9abae65</data><data key="edge_source_id">S42</data><data key="edge_source_url">https://msrc.microsoft.com/update-guide/vulnerability/CVE-2026-63520</data><data key="edge_chunk_id">S42_C03</data><data key="edge_json_path">None</data><data key="edge_evidence">This metric also suggests the level of technical knowledge available to would-be attackers</data><data key="edge_extraction_method">minie</data><data key="edge_polarity">positive</data><data key="edge_modality">asserted</data></edge><edge id="oe_c4a31cf097d5df87" source="e_08068329a4aeab79" target="e_44d2eca1baada6ea"><data key="edge_predicate_raw">exploits</data><data key="edge_assertion_id">a_8831144703ab3a75</data><data key="edge_source_id">S42</data><data key="edge_source_url">https://msrc.microsoft.com/update-guide/vulnerability/CVE-2026-63520</data><data key="edge_chunk_id">S42_C03</data><data key="edge_json_path">None</data><data key="edge_evidence">Detailed reports exist