ime and across user environments</data><data key="edge_extraction_method">minie</data><data key="edge_polarity">positive</data><data key="edge_modality">asserted</data></edge><edge id="oe_55a0a47d7e9c9ec6" source="e_dbd1ba0cc63988dc" target="e_3d75e6dbcbfb5033"><data key="edge_predicate_raw">are across</data><data key="edge_assertion_id">a_6f454d032b93a3d3</data><data key="edge_source_id">S50</data><data key="edge_source_url">https://www.first.org/cvss/v4.0/specification-document</data><data key="edge_chunk_id">S50_C03</data><data key="edge_json_path">None</data><data key="edge_evidence">the intrinsic characteristics of a vulnerability that are constant over time and across user environments</data><data key="edge_extraction_method">minie</data><data key="edge_polarity">positive</data><data key="edge_modality">asserted</data></edge><edge id="oe_6b1a76e4f088962c" source="e_c00a4051d0530e03" target="e_4e259ac87c6dfb68"><data key="edge_predicate_raw">reflect</data><data key="edge_assertion_id">a_33fa831db347c392</data><data key="edge_source_id">S50</data><data key="edge_source_url">https://www.first.org/cvss/v4.0/specification-document</data><data key="edge_chunk_id">S50_C03</data><data key="edge_json_path">None</data><data key="edge_evidence">The Exploitability metrics reflect the ease and technical means by which the vulnerability can be exploited</data><data key="edge_extraction_method">minie</data><data key="edge_polarity">positive</data><data key="edge_modality">possible</data></edge><edge id="oe_191f1c974fa05a38" source="e_c00a4051d0530e03" target="e_5460670fc143394a"><data key="edge_predicate_raw">reflect</data><data key="edge_assertion_id">a_dcc302623fb8a1c5</data><data key="edge_source_id">S50</data><data key="edge_source_url">https://www.first.org/cvss/v4.0/specification-document</data><data key="edge_chunk_id">S50_C03</data><data key="edge_json_path">None</data><data key="edge_evidence">The Exploitability metrics reflect the ease and technical means by which the vulnerability can be exploited</data><data key="edge_extraction_method">minie</data><data key="edge_polarity">positive</data><data key="edge_modality">possible</data></edge><edge id="oe_a0afc0aebf4795ea" source="e_dbd1ba0cc63988dc" target="e_4e259ac87c6dfb68"><data key="edge_predicate_raw">be exploited</data><data key="edge_assertion_id">a_60393fd165a889ee</data><data key="edge_source_id">S50</data><data key="edge_source_url">https://www.first.org/cvss/v4.0/specification-document</data><data key="edge_chunk_id">S50_C03</data><data key="edge_json_path">None</data><data key="edge_evidence">The Exploitability metrics reflect the ease and technical means by which the vulnerability can be exploited</data><data key="edge_extraction_method">minie</data><data key="edge_polarity">positive</data><data key="edge_modality">possible</data></edge><edge id="oe_e5e05fda4f3524dd" source="e_dbd1ba0cc63988dc" target="e_5460670fc143394a"><data key="edge_predicate_raw">be exploited</data><data key="edge_assertion_id">a_4d41a7b94bbbdee2</data><data key="edge_source_id">S50</data><data key="edge_source_url">https://www.first.org/cvss/v4.0/specification-document</data><data key="edge_chunk_id">S50_C03</data><data key="edge_json_path">None</data><data key="edge_evidence">The Exploitability metrics reflect the ease and technical means by which the vulnerability can be exploited</data><data key="edge_extraction_method">minie</data><data key="edge_polarity">positive</data><data key="edge_modality">possible</data></edge><edge id="oe_a7c5f75888ad7e74" source="e_290d8da624d84fb0" target="e_2f5c3d09f4bbc7c9"><data key="edge_predicate_raw">represent characteristics of</data><data key="edge_assertion_id">a_f1c3ebddfbd268a1</data><data key="edge_source_id">S50</data><data key="edge_source_url">https://www.first.org/cvss/v4.0/specification-document</data><data key="edge_chunk_id">S50_C03</data><data key="edge_json_path">None</data><data key="edge_evidence">That is, they represent characteristics of the “thing that is vulnerable”, which we refer to formally as the “vulnerable system”</data><data key="edge_extraction_method">minie</data><data key="edge_polarity">positive</data><data key="edge_modality">asserted</data></edge><edge id="oe_4fb821a6f7c7a7d9" source="e_be74ffef073dc8d3" target="e_7ee1ff4a70457dd7"><data key="edge_predicate_raw">refer thing to formally as</data><data key="edge_assertion_id">a_065b58dac1c7ca3b</data><data key="edge_source_id">S50</data><data key="edge_source_url">https://www.first.org/cvss/v4.0/specification-document</data><data key="edge_chunk_id">S50_C03</data><data key="edge_json_path">None</data><data key="edge_evidence">That is, they represent characteristics of the “thing that is vulnerable”, which we refer to formally as the “vulnerable system”</data><data key="edge_extraction_method">minie</data><data key="edge_polarity">positive</data><data key="edge_modality">asserted</data></edge><edge id="oe_7461608eba34c403" source="e_be74ffef073dc8d3" target="e_2f5c3d09f4bbc7c9"><data key="edge_predicate_raw">refer</data><data key="edge_assertion_id">a_6a2247e085f47e45</data><data key="edge_source_id">S50</data><data key="edge_source_url">https://www.first.org/cvss/v4.0/specification-document</data><data key="edge_chunk_id">S50_C03</data><data key="edge_json_path">None</data><data key="edge_evidence">That is, they represent characteristics of the “thing that is vulnerable”, which we refer to formally as the “vulnerable system”</data><data key="edge_extraction_method">minie</data><data key="edge_polarity">positive</data><data key="edge_modality">asserted</data></edge><edge id="oe_43b790491aa83e09" source="e_546996a8b2a435a8" target="e_e4537cb8e78c8b83"><data key="edge_predicate_raw">includes</data><data key="edge_assertion_id">a_ca84448d562063e8</data><data key="edge_source_id">S50</data><data key="edge_source_url">https://www.first.org/cvss/v4.0/specification-document</data><data key="edge_chunk_id">S50_C03</data><data key="edge_json_path">None</data><data key="edge_evidence">While the vulnerable system is typically a software application, operating system, module, driver, etc. (or possibly a hardware device), the subsequent system could be any of those examples but also includes human safety</data><data key="edge_extraction_method">minie</data><data key="edge_polarity">positive</data><data key="edge_modality">possible</data></edge><edge id="oe_d42fa4c60296e748" source="e_44bf90b131770ea6" target="e_b052dff516692230"><data key="edge_predicate_raw">is captured by</data><data key="edge_assertion_id">a_902a6cb566633921</data><data key="edge_source_id">S50</data><data key="edge_source_url">https://www.first.org/cvss/v4.0/specification-document</data><data key="edge_chunk_id">S50_C03</data><data key="edge_json_path">None</data><data key="edge_evidence">This property (formerly known as “Scope”), is captured by the separation of impacts to the vulnerable system and to subsequent systems, discussed later</data><data key="edge_extraction_method">minie</data><data key="edge_polarity">positive</data><data key="edge_modality">asserted</data></edge><edge id="oe_23295a63c843d303" source="e_44bf90b131770ea6" target="e_fc867da4c8e552a2"><data key="edge_predicate_raw">discussed to</data><data key="edge_assertion_id">a_59d1889ecad4b8de</data><data key="edge_source_id">S50</data><data key="edge_source_url">https://www.first.org/cvss/v4.0/specification-document</data><data key="edge_chunk_id">S50_C03</data><data key="edge_json_path">None</data><data key="edge_evidence">This property (formerly known as “Scope”), is captured by the separation of impacts to the vulnerable system and to subsequent systems, discussed later</data><data key="edge_extraction_method">minie</data><data key="edge_polarity">positive</data><data key="edge_modality">asserted</data></edge><edge id="oe_1fa47d9e8c50e19e" source="e_44bf90b131770ea6" target="e_d760c680924b2e91"><data key="edge_predicate_raw">discussed</data><data key="edge_assertion_id">a_19b0daf03335874b</data><data key="edge_source_id">S50</data><data key="edge_source_url">https://www.first.org/cvss/v4.0/specification-document</data><data key="edge_chunk_id">S50_C03</data><data key="edge_json_path">None</data><data key="edge_evidence">This property (formerly known as “Scope”), is captured by the separation of impacts to the vulnerable system and to subsequent systems, discussed later</data><data key="edge_extraction_method">minie</data><data key="edge_polarity">positive</data><data key="edge_modality">asserted</data></edge><edge id="oe_d22da7b2ed280ddd" source="e_838a95b0b63fa880" target="e_ca335c133f4134dc"><data key="edge_predicate_raw">change over</data><data key="edge_assertion_id">a_32c6e65d031eba6d</data><data key="edge_source_id">S50</data><data key="edge_source_url">https://www.first.org/cvss/v4.0/specification-document</data><data key="edge_chunk_id">S50_C03</data><data key="edge_json_path">None</data><data key="edge_evidence">The Threat metric group reflects the characteristics of a vulnerability related to threat that may change over time but not necessarily across user environments</data><data key="edge_extraction_method">minie</data><data key="edge_polarity">negative</data><data key="edge_modality">possible</data></edge><edge id="oe_3fa7cbd9d2b4a273" source="e_dd6ba352a6ceacc1" target="e_11d5ad81b4113afc"><data key="edge_predicate_raw">reflects</data><data key="edge_assertion_id">a_2a07885517d25493</data><data key="edge_source_id">S50</data><data key="edge_source_url">https://www.first.org/cvss/v4.0/specification-document</data><data key="edge_chunk_id">S50_C03</data><data key="edge_json_path">None</data><data key="edge_evidence">The Threat metric group reflects the characteristics of a vulnerability related to threat that may change over time but not necessarily across user environments</data><data key="edge_extraction_method">minie</data><data key="edge_polarity">negative</data><data key="edge_modality">possible</data></edge><edge id="oe_9496de97484b308d" source="e_2d838504a5f30d17" target="e_2ef59271821753f8"><data key="edge_predicate_raw">exploited</data><data key="edge_assertion_id">a_4ed59195161d78de</data><data key="edge_source_id">S50</data><data key="edge_source_url">https://www.first.org/cvss/v4.0/specification-document</data><data key="edge_chunk_id">S50_C03</data><data key="edge_json_path">None</data><data key="edge_evidence">For example, confirmation that the vulnerability has neither been exploited nor has any proof-of-concept exploit code or instructions publicly available will lower the resulting CVSS score</data><data key="edge_extraction_method">heuristic</data><data key="edge_polarity">positive</data><data key="edge_modality">asserted</data></edge><edge id="oe_26355fcb48ac2bc9" source="e_a9ed604eb1323e31" target="e_3b12bec043d26c18"><data key="edge_predicate_raw">be found in</data><data key="edge_assertion_id">a_af0c3438b2f53b1b</data><data key="edge_source_id">S50</data><data key="edge_source_url">https://www.first.org/cvss/v4.0/specification-document</data><data key="edge_chunk_id">S50_C03</data><data key="edge_json_path">None</data><data key="edge_evidence">The values found in this metric group may change over time</data><data key="edge_extraction_method">minie</data><data key="edge_polarity">positive</data><data key="edge_modality">possible</data></edge><edge id="oe_5f9d04d641b90767" source="e_abe69e34c599411a" target="e_ca335c133f4134dc"><data key="edge_predicate_raw">change over</data><data key="edge_assertion_id">a_72e1a5c4efa81ddf</data><data key="edge_source_id">S50</data><data key="edge_source_url">https://www.first.org/cvss/v4.0/specification-document</data><data key="edge_chunk_id">S50_C03</data><data key="edge_json_path">None</data><data key="edge_evidence">The values found in this metric group may change over time</data><data key="edge_extraction_method">minie</data><data key="edge_polarity">positive</data><data key="edge_modality">possible</data></edge><edge id="oe_c2c41a0cc19e9876" source="e_b84ee762ce82df1d" target="e_dbd1ba0cc63988dc"><data key="edge_predicate_raw">represents characteristics of</data><data key="edge_assertion_id">a_928ec0ed3048c5a8</data><data key="edge_source_id">S50</data><data key="edge_source_url">https://www.first.org/cvss/v4.0/specification-document</data><data key="edge_chunk_id">S50_C03</data><data key="edge_json_path">None</data><data key="edge_evidence">The Environmental metric group represents the characteristics of a vulnerability that are relevant and unique to a particular consumers’ environment</data><data key="edge_extraction_method">minie</data><data key="edge_polarity">positive</data><data key="edge_modality">asserted</data></edge><edge id="oe_46cbed2e136bb674" source="e_dbd1ba0cc63988dc" target="e_c8dcccc9a9dca201"><data key="edge_predicate_raw">are relevant to</data><data key="edge_assertion_id">a_f379fc3a766047d7</data><data key="edge_source_id">S50</data><data key="edge_source_url">https://www.first.org/cvss/v4.0/specification-document</data><data key="edge_chunk_id">S50_C03</data><data key="edge_json_path">None</data><data key="edge_evidence">The Environmental metric group represents the characteristics of a vulnerability that are relevant and unique to a particular consumers’ environment</data><data key="edge_extraction_method">minie</data><data key="edge_polarity">positive</data><data key="edge_modality">asserted</data></edge><edge id="oe_2179565c50186d27" source="e_dbd1ba0cc63988dc" target="e_c8dcccc9a9dca201"><data key="edge_predicate_raw">are unique to</data><data key="edge_assertion_id">a_35ab713e2ef6167f</data><data key="edge_source_id">S50</data><data key="edge_source_url">https://www.first.org/cvss/v4.0/specification-document</data><data key="edge_chunk_id">S50_C03</data><data key="edge_json_path">None</data><data key="edge_evidence">The Environmental metric group represents the characteristics of a vulnerability that are relevant and unique to a particular consumers’ environment</data><data key="edge_extraction_method">minie</data><data key="edge_polarity">positive</data><data key="edge_modality">asserted</data></edge><edge id="oe_45375e5e6caf56a6" source="e_1e8ea1b42ca055ae" target="e_3709b11f96009c9b"><data key="edge_predicate_raw">include presence of</data><data key="edge_assertion_id">a_4aa9b685e4841452</data><data key="edge_source_id">S50</data><data key="edge_source_url">https://www.first.org/cvss/v4.0/specification-document</data><data key="edge_chunk_id">S50_C03</data><data key="edge_json_path">None</data><data key="edge_evidence">Considerations include the presence of security controls which may mitigate some or all consequences of a successful attack, and the relative importance of a vulnerable system within a technology infrastructure</data><data key="edge_extraction_method">minie</data><data key="edge_polarity">positive</data><data key="edge_modality">possible</data></edge><edge id="oe_f607b3041f27c257" source="e_1e8ea1b42ca055ae" target="e_ecedfcb33ae54209"><data key="edge_predicate_raw">include</data><data key="edge_assertion_id">a_2980cda20963ef44</data><data key="edge_source_id">S50</data><data key="edge_source_url">https://www.first.org/cvss/v4.0/specification-document</data><data key="edge_chunk_id">S50_C03</data><data key="edge_json_path">None</data><data key="edge_evidence">Considerations include the presence of security controls which may mitigate some or all consequences of a successful attack, and the relative importance of a vulnerable system within a technology infrastructure</data><data key="edge_extraction_method">minie</data><data key="edge_polarity">positive</data><data key="edge_modality">possible</data></edge><edge id="oe_d42f67fcf2d68acb" source="e_371e2a8932c3cb22" target="e_768bf52735c34131"><data key="edge_predicate_raw">includes</data><data key="edge_assertion_id">a_03b35db034b6e3d0</data><data key="edge_source_id">S50</data><data key="edge_source_url">https://www.first.org/cvss/v4.0/specification-document</data><data key="edge_chunk_id">S50_C03</data><data key="edge_json_path">None</data><data key="edge_evidence">The Supplemental metric group includes metrics that provide context as well as describe and measure additional extrinsic attributes of a vulnerability</data><data key="edge_extraction_method">minie</data><data key="edge_polarity">positive</data><data key="edge_modality">asserted</data></edge><edge id="oe_f2f1aacdba4ee8d8" source="e_768bf52735c34131" target="e_466e6377cc3c1257"><data key="edge_predicate_raw">provide</data><data key="edge_assertion_id">a_eec295cbbcc677f0</data><data key="edge_source_id">S50</data><data key="edge_source_url">https://www.first.org/cvss/v4.0/specification-document</data><data key="edge_chunk_id">S50_C03</data><data key="edge_json_path">None</data><data key="edge_evidence">The Supplemental metric group includes metrics that provide context as well as describe and measure additional extrinsic attributes of a vulnerability</data><data key="edge_extraction_method">minie</data><data key="edge_polarity">positive</data><data key="edge_modality">asserted</data></edge><edge id="oe_d464395b4d7eef17" source="e_768bf52735c34131" target="e_5baf2218d93c33be"><data key="edge_predicate_raw">provide</data><data key="edge_assertion_id">a_80a93b60b8fc78af</data><data key="edge_source_id">S50</data><data key="edge_source_url">https://www.first.org/cvss/v4.0/specification-document</data><data key="edge_chunk_id">S50_C03</data><data key="edge_json_path">None</data><data key="edge_evidence">The Supplemental metric group includes metrics that provide context as well as describe and measure additional extrinsic attributes of a vulnerability</data><data key="edge_extraction_method">minie</data><data key="edge_polarity">positive</data><data key="edge_modality">asserted</data></edge><edge id="oe_032384b56bcae078" source="e_768bf52735c34131" target="e_dbd1ba0cc63988dc"><data key="edge_predicate_raw">measure additional extrinsic attributes of</data><data key="edge_assertion_id">a_ef16fee7b79d629a</data><data key="edge_source_id">S50</data><data key="edge_source_url">https://www.first.org/cvss/v4.0/specification-document</data><data key="edge_chunk_id">S50_C03</data><data key="edge_json_path">None</data><data key="edge_evidence">The Supplemental metric group includes metrics that provide context as well as describe and measure additional extrinsic attributes of a vulnerability</data><data key="edge_extraction_method">minie</data><data key="edge_polarity">positive</data><data key="edge_modality">asserted</data></edge><edge id="oe_3f57efd65e57341b" source="e_12024175e2291ad7" target="e_768bf52735c34131"><data key="edge_predicate_raw">be apply significant severity to</data><data key="edge_assertion_id">a_32f5b27869e5f4a1</data><data key="edge_source_id">S50</data><data key="edge_source_url">https://www.first.org/cvss/v4.0/specification-document</data><data key="edge_chunk_id">S50_C03</data><data key="edge_json_path">None</data><data key="edge_evidence">The response to each metric within the Supplemental metric group is to be determined by the CVSS consumer, allowing the usage of an end-user risk analysis system to apply locally significant severity to the metrics and values</data><data key="edge_extraction_method">minie</data><data key="edge_polarity">positive</data><data key="edge_modality">asserted</data></edge><edge id="oe_60382de961a3ba68" source="e_12024175e2291ad7" target="e_a9ed604eb1323e31"><data key="edge_predicate_raw">be apply significant severity to</data><data key="edge_assertion_id">a_5dc558895a55145f</data><data key="edge_source_id">S50</data><data key="edge_source_url">https://www.first.org/cvss/v4.0/specification-document</data><data key="edge_chunk_id">S50_C03</data><data key="edge_json_path">None</data><data key="edge_evidence">The response to each metric within the Supplemental metric group is to be determined by the CVSS consumer, allowing the usage of an end-user risk analysis system to apply locally significant severity to the metrics and values</data><data key="edge_extraction_method">minie</data><data key="edge_polarity">positive</data><data key="edge_modality">asserted</data></edge><edge id="oe_1f821bdad46200ab" source="e_88dcd2dc4051eb38" target="e_b0f6dca86eea0917"><data key="edge_predicate_raw">assign</data><data key="edge_assertion_id">a_c2200ea61a92a747</data><data key="edge_source_id">S50</data><data key="edge_source_url">https://www.first.org/cvss/v4.0/specification-document</data><data key="edge_chunk_id">S50_C03</data><data key="edge_json_path">None</data><data key="edge_evidence">Consumer organizations may then assign importance and/or effective impact of each metric, or set/combination of metrics, giving them more, less, or absolutely no effect on the categorization, prioritization, and assessment of the vulnerability</data><data key="edge_extraction_method">minie</data><data key="edge_polarity">negative</data><data key="edge_modality">possible</data></edge><edge id="oe_ce1c6a33cb115ccb" source="e_768bf52735c34131" target="e_660f4f640dd0931a"><data key="edge_predicate_raw">convey additional extrinsic characteristics of</data><data key="edge_assertion_id">a_6021e7d181941a7a</data><data key="edge_source_id">S50</data><data key="edge_source_url">https://www.first.org/cvss/v4.0/specification-document</data><data key="edge_chunk_id">S50_C03</data><data key="edge_json_path">None</data><data key="edge_evidence">Metrics and values will simply convey additional extrinsic characteristics of the vulnerability itself</data><data key="edge_extraction_method">minie</data><data key="edge_polarity">positive</data><data key="edge_modality">asserted</data></edge><edge id="oe_97b764b5aa8a25b0" source="e_a9ed604eb1323e31" target="e_660f4f640dd0931a"><data key="edge_predicate_raw">convey additional extrinsic characteristics of</data><data key="edge_assertion_id">a_151f8f7fe0f378bb</data><data key="edge_source_id">S50</data><data key="edge_source_url">https://www.first.org/cvss/v4.0/specification-document</data><data key="edge_chunk_id">S50_C03</data><data key="edge_json_path">None</data><data key="edge_evidence">Metrics and values will simply convey additional extrinsic characteristics of the vulnerability itself</data><data key="edge_extraction_method">minie</data><data key="edge_polarity">positive</data><data key="edge_modality">asserted</data></edge><edge id="oe_0a049f1c8c94f155" source="e_9db8f043050fbea7" target="e_80b852b98e6b518c"><data key="edge_predicate_raw">contains scoring rubrics for</data><data key="edge_assertion_id">a_a74768be71c7193d</data><data key="edge_source_id">S50</data><data key="edge_source_url">https://www.first.org/cvss/v4.0/specification-document</data><data key="edge_chunk_id">S50_C03</data><data key="edge_json_path">None</data><data key="edge_evidence">The User Guide contains scoring rubrics for the Base Metrics that may be useful when scoring</data><data key="edge_extraction_method">minie</data><data key="edge_polarity">positive</data><data key="edge_modality">possible</data></edge><edge id="oe_a521f0c773051391" source="e_80b852b98e6b518c" target="e_cd0a45b2a1788da0"><data key="edge_predicate_raw">be useful when</data><data key="edge_assertion_id">a_b763a44b0571ff5f</data><data key="edge_source_id">S50</data><data key="edge_source_url">https://www.first.org/cvss/v4.0/specification-document</data><data key="edge_chunk_id">S50_C03</data><data key="edge_json_path">None</data><data key="edge_evidence">The User Guide contains scoring rubrics for the Base Metrics that may be useful when scoring</data><data key="edge_extraction_method">minie</data><data key="edge_polarity">positive</data><data key="edge_modality">possible</data></edge><edge id="oe_726e9f1f1cb158ca" source="e_80b852b98e6b518c" target="e_f6498126c94c6f96"><data key="edge_predicate_raw">are assigned values by</data><data key="edge_assertion_id">a_51f2fa0877ad2519</data><data key="edge_source_id">S50</data><data key="edge_source_url">https://www.first.org/cvss/v4.0/specification-document</data><data key="edge_chunk_id">S50_C04</data><data key="edge_json_path">None</data><data key="edge_evidence">When the Base metrics are assigned values by an analyst, the Base metrics assessment results in a score ranging from 0.0 to 10.0</data><data key="edge_extraction_method">minie</data><data key="edge_polarity">positive</data><data key="edge_modality">asserted</data></edge><edge id="oe_5749898184c12bef" source="e_80b852b98e6b518c" target="e_a9ed604eb1323e31"><data key="edge_predicate_raw">are assigned</data><data key="edge_assertion_id">a_053f7952e253b5a0</data><data key="edge_source_id">S50</data><data key="edge_source_url">https://www.first.org/cvss/v4.0/specification-document</data><data key="edge_chunk_id">S50_C04</data><data key="edge_json_path">None</data><data key="edge_evidence">When the Base metrics are assigned values by an analyst, the Base metrics assessment results in a score ranging from 0.0 to 10.0</data><data key="edge_extraction_method">minie</data><data key="edge_polarity">positive</data><data key="edge_modality">asserted</data></edge><edge id="oe_177bfed395432d73" source="e_966561fb8ee48e35" target="e_26b4ac68b3f366a0"><data key="edge_predicate_raw">be refined by</data><data key="edge_assertion_id">a_6f2964dd6804640b</data><data key="edge_source_id">S50</data><data key="edge_source_url">https://www.first.org/cvss/v4.0/specification-document</data><data key="edge_chunk_id">S50_C04</data><data key="edge_json_path">None</data><data key="edge_evidence">The Base metrics assessment can then be further refined by assessing the Threat and Environmental metrics in order to more accurately reflect the relative severity posed by a vulnerability to a user’s environment at a specific point in time</data><data key="edge_extraction_method">minie</data><data key="edge_polarity">positive</data><data key="edge_modality">possible</data></edge><edge id="oe_360a91a0e3c83e46" source="e_966561fb8ee48e35" target="e_ee9c01563d9ca7b2"><data key="edge_predicate_raw">be refined by</data><data key="edge_assertion_id">a_c37825ad77ecd178</data><data key="edge_source_id">S50</data><data key="edge_source_url">https://www.first.org/cvss/v4.0/specification-document</data><data key="edge_chunk_id">S50_C04</data><data key="edge_json_path">None</data><data key="edge_evidence">The Base metrics assessment can then be further refined by assessing the Threat and Environmental metrics in order to more accurately reflect the relative severity posed by a vulnerability to a user’s environment at a specific point in time</data><data key="edge_extraction_method">minie</data><data key="edge_polarity">positive</data><data key="edge_modality">possible</data></edge><edge id="oe_57d15cff1ba1e894" source="e_d15e9e1afe2a9d2f" target="e_491a87f4c4b335f8"><data key="edge_predicate_raw">be posed by</data><data key="edge_assertion_id">a_d4552025a03d2301</data><data key="edge_source_id">S50</data><data key="edge_source_url">https://www.first.org/cvss/v4.0/specification-document</data><data key="edge_chunk_id">S50_C04</data><data key="edge_json_path">None</data><data key="edge_evidence">The Base metrics assessment can then be further refined by assessing the Threat and Environmental metrics in order to more accurately reflect the relative severity posed by a vulnerability to a user’s environment at a specific point in time</data><data key="edge_extraction_method">minie</data><data key="edge_polarity">positive</data><data key="edge_modality">possible</data></edge><edge id="oe_8a1e7520a96e377d" source="e_290d8da624d84fb0" target="e_a0ef75f1f1ee68c4"><data key="edge_predicate_raw">possess</data><data key="edge_assertion_id">a_743fe19665302c94</data><data key="edge_source_id">S50</data><data key="edge_source_url">https://www.first.org/cvss/v4.0/specification-document</data><data key="edge_chunk_id">S50_C04</data><data key="edge_json_path">None</data><data key="edge_evidence">Generally, the Base metrics are specified by vulnerability bulletin analysts, product vendors, or application vendors because they typically possess the most accurate information about the characteristics of a vulnerability</data><data key="edge_extraction_method">minie</data><data key="edge_polarity">positive</data><data key="edge_modality">asserted</data></edge><edge id="oe_1aa3f5e89511be74" source="e_80b852b98e6b518c" target="e_80cb9bff13d34e0c"><data key="edge_predicate_raw">are specified by</data><data key="edge_assertion_id">a_cf963e6fa4ba2d87</data><data key="edge_source_id">S50</data><data key="edge_source_url">https://www.first.org/cvss/v4.0/specification-document</data><data key="edge_chunk_id">S50_C04</data><data key="edge_json_path">None</data><data key="edge_evidence">Generally, the Base metrics are specified by vulnerability bulletin analysts, product vendors, or application vendors because they typically possess the most accurate information about the characteristics of a vulnerability</data><data key="edge_extraction_method">minie</data><data key="edge_polarity">positive</data><data key="edge_modality">asserted</data></edge><edge id="oe_d3fcb228ccd549be" source="e_80b852b98e6b518c" target="e_1a6f16aa777ea059"><data key="edge_predicate_raw">are specified by</data><data key="edge_assertion_id">a_ef45300edb19139b</data><data key="edge_source_id">S50</data><data key="edge_source_url">https://www.first.org/cvss/v4.0/specification-document</data><data key="edge_chunk_id">S50_C04</data><data key="edge_json_path">None</data><data key="edge_evidence">Generally, the Base metrics are specified by vulnerability bulletin analysts, product vendors, or application vendors because they typically possess the most accurate information about the characteristics of a vulnerability</data><data key="edge_extraction_method">minie</data><data key="edge_polarity">positive</data><data key="edge_modality">asserted</data></edge><edge id="oe_1ea922bf852e0fb0" source="e_80b852b98e6b518c" target="e_54d5f84d2fd12cc2"><data key="edge_predicate_raw">are specified by</data><data key="edge_assertion_id">a_6e06664940aeffbe</data><data key="edge_source_id">S50</data><data key="edge_source_url">https://www.first.org/cvss/v4.0/specification-document</data><data key="edge_chunk_id">S50_C04</data><data key="edge_json_path">None</data><data key="edge_evidence">Generally, the Base metrics are specified by vulnerability bulletin analysts, product vendors, or application vendors because they typically possess the most accurate information about the characteristics of a vulnerability</data><data key="edge_extraction_method">minie</data><data key="edge_polarity">positive</data><data key="edge_modality">asserted</data></edge><edge id="oe_4941c9122fe8c82f" source="e_838a95b0b63fa880" target="e_88dcd2dc4051eb38"><data key="edge_predicate_raw">are specified by</data><data key="edge_assertion_id">a_97c44024efe96f70</data><data key="edge_source_id">S50</data><data key="edge_source_url">https://www.first.org/cvss/v4.0/specification-document</data><data key="edge_chunk_id">S50_C04</data><data key="edge_json_path">None</data><data key="edge_evidence">The Threat and Environmental metrics are specified by consumer organizations because they are best able to assess the potential impact of a vulnerability within their own computing environment, at a given point in time</data><data key="edge_extraction_method">minie</data><data key="edge_polarity">positive</data><data key="edge_modality">asserted</data></edge><edge id="oe_0516850ce2cc2e73" source="e_b54a46ece8e786db" target="e_88dcd2dc4051eb38"><data key="edge_predicate_raw">are specified by</data><data key="edge_assertion_id">a_26bda14486e285fa</data><data key="edge_source_id">S50</data><data key="edge_source_url">https://www.first.org/cvss/v4.0/specification-document</data><data key="edge_chunk_id">S50_C04</data><data key="edge_json_path">None</data><data key="edge_evidence">The Threat and Environmental metrics are specified by consumer organizations because they are best able to assess the potential impact of a vulnerability within their own computing environment, at a given point in time</data><data key="edge_extraction_method">minie</data><data key="edge_polarity">positive</data><data key="edge_modality">asserted</data></edge><edge id="oe_6ac7a3d12a5d7b4b" source="e_a1963641021a625a" target="e_97d5b9fcbb9ac78b"><data key="edge_predicate_raw">produces</data><data key="edge_assertion_id">a_66be8957c080b294</data><data key="edge_source_id">S50</data><data key="edge_source_url">https://www.first.org/cvss/v4.0/specification-document</data><data key="edge_chunk_id">S50_C04</data><data key="edge_json_path">None</data><data key="edge_evidence">Assessing CVSS metrics also produces a vector string, a textual representation of the metric values used to derive a quantitative score and qualitative rating for the vulnerability</data><data key="edge_extraction_method">minie</data><data key="edge_polarity">positive</data><data key="edge_modality">asserted</data></edge><edge id="oe_7d6bb761048c494e" source="e_45b3e78147f50a23" target="e_dbd1ba0cc63988dc"><data key="edge_predicate_raw">be used to derive quantitative score for</data><data key="edge_assertion_id">a_d6b1c72e5111adc4</data><data key="edge_source_id">S50</data><data key="edge_source_url">https://www.first.org/cvss/v4.0/specification-document</data><data key="edge_chunk_id">S50_C04</data><data key="edge_json_path">None</data><data key="edge_evidence">Assessing CVSS metrics also produces a vector string, a textual representation of the metric values used to derive a quantitative score and qualitative rating for the vulnerability</data><data key="edge_extraction_method">minie</data><data key="edge_polarity">positive</data><data key="edge_modality">asserted</data></edge><edge id="oe_4019db096ff5e240" source="e_45b3e78147f50a23" target="e_ea4e8774919b4516"><data key="edge_predicate_raw">be used to derive</data><data key="edge_assertion_id">a_8ab184504e894ea2</data><data key="edge_source_id">S50</data><data key="edge_source_url">https://www.first.org/cvss/v4.0/specification-document</data><data key="edge_chunk_id">S50_C04</data><data key="edge_json_path">None</data><data key="edge_evidence">Assessing CVSS metrics also produces a vector string, a textual representation of the metric values used to derive a quantitative score and qualitative rating for the vulnerability</data><data key="edge_extraction_method">minie</data><data key="edge_polarity">positive</data><data key="edge_modality">asserted</data></edge><edge id="oe_2386c14dd9cd6990" source="e_97d5b9fcbb9ac78b" target="e_b77bee5b354b9d96"><data key="edge_predicate_raw">be displayed with</data><data key="edge_assertion_id">a_553c8609d2e19dae</data><data key="edge_source_id">S50</data><data key="edge_source_url">https://www.first.org/cvss/v4.0/specification-document</data><data key="edge_chunk_id">S50_C04</data><data key="edge_json_path">None</data><data key="edge_evidence">This vector string is a specifically formatted text string that contains each value assigned to each metric, and should be displayed with the vulnerability score</data><data key="edge_extraction_method">minie</data><data key="edge_polarity">positive</data><data key="edge_modality">asserted</data></edge><edge id="oe_9048eb7a4b288d8e" source="e_537e6ab50e8f2e44" target="e_dbd1ba0cc63988dc"><data key="edge_predicate_raw">has perfect knowledge of</data><data key="edge_assertion_id">a_43bad9961b38fabb</data><data key="edge_source_id">S50</data><data key="edge_source_url">https://www.first.org/cvss/v4.0/specification-document</data><data key="edge_chunk_id">S50_C04</data><data key="edge_json_path">None</data><data key="edge_evidence">Note that all metrics should be assessed under the assumption that the attacker has perfect knowledge of the vulnerability</data><data key="edge_extraction_method">minie</data><data key="edge_polarity">positive</data><data key="edge_modality">asserted</data></edge><edge id="oe_935e5ff68154f315" source="e_768bf52735c34131" target="e_f8b520c0a0b6460f"><data key="edge_predicate_raw">be used to calculate</data><data key="edge_assertion_id">a_341f07e3f45f1d16</data><data key="edge_source_id">S50</data><data key="edge_source_url">https://www.first.org/cvss/v4.0/specification-document</data><data key="edge_chunk_id">S50_C04</data><data key="edge_json_path">None</data><data key="edge_evidence">Numerical CVSS Scores have very different meanings based on the metrics used to calculate them</data><data key="edge_extraction_method">minie</data><data key="edge_polarity">positive</data><data key="edge_modality">asserted</data></edge><edge id="oe_6c9d634a70a1fdab" source="e_f6a7ad56b5ba29ba" target="e_4364e67a28b13c95"><data key="edge_predicate_raw">be leveraged to generate that</data><data key="edge_assertion_id">a_96e0358ebc99f6cd</data><data key="edge_source_id">S50</data><data key="edge_source_url">https://www.first.org/cvss/v4.0/specification-document</data><data key="edge_chunk_id">S50_C04</data><data key="edge_json_path">None</data><data key="edge_evidence">Regarding prioritization, the usefulness of a numerical CVSS score is directly proportional to the CVSS metrics leveraged to generate that score</data><data key="edge_extraction_method">minie</data><data key="edge_polarity">positive</data><data key="edge_modality">asserted</data></edge><edge id="oe_86f363582215cc19" source="e_105cc5cf493c670f" target="e_904da0b4f3960fb3"><data key="edge_predicate_raw">be Regarding</data><data key="edge_assertion_id">a_ac5a8678c2021ea8</data><data key="edge_source_id">S50</data><data key="edge_source_url">https://www.first.org/cvss/v4.0/specification-document</data><data key="edge_chunk_id">S50_C04</data><data key="edge_json_path">None</data><data key="edge_evidence">Regarding prioritization, the usefulness of a numerical CVSS score is directly proportional to the CVSS metrics leveraged to generate that score</data><data key="edge_extraction_method">minie</data><data key="edge_polarity">positive</data><data key="edge_modality">asserted</data></edge><edge id="oe_a9e17020558dec2c" source="e_af47c659804da2a9" target="e_c92a80f863b1c7d6"><data key="edge_predicate_raw">is proportional</data><data key="edge_assertion_id">a_a9f093df163f7aec</data><data key="edge_source_id">S50</data><data key="edge_source_url">https://www.first.org/cvss/v4.0/specification-document</data><data key="edge_chunk_id">S50_C04</data><data key="edge_json_path">None</data><data key="edge_evidence">Regarding prioritization, the usefulness of a numerical CVSS score is directly proportional to the CVSS metrics leveraged to generate that score</data><data key="edge_extraction_method">minie</data><data key="edge_polarity">positive</data><data key="edge_modality">asserted</data></edge><edge id="oe_5838c8c524e30df9" source="e_af47c659804da2a9" target="e_86cd872f75c203db"><data key="edge_predicate_raw">is proportional to</data><data key="edge_assertion_id">a_050a585b05aa6cf2</data><data key="edge_source_id">S50</data><data key="edge_source_url">https://www.first.org/cvss/v4.0/specification-document</data><data key="edge_chunk_id">S50_C04</data><data key="edge_json_path">None</data><data key="edge_evidence">Regarding prioritization, the usefulness of a numerical CVSS score is directly proportional to the CVSS metrics leveraged to generate that score</data><data key="edge_extraction_method">minie</data><data key="edge_polarity">positive</data><data key="edge_modality">asserted</data></edge><edge id="oe_bae80e9c1a3baee3" source="e_b189ba3fb7ef7706" target="e_1af6c78accf2e433"><data key="edge_predicate_raw">be labeled</data><data key="edge_assertion_id">a_7abe7d1a7ca90cb9</data><data key="edge_source_id">S50</data><data key="edge_source_url">https://www.first.org/cvss/v4.0/specification-document</data><data key="edge_chunk_id">S50_C04</data><data key="edge_json_path">None</data><data key="edge_evidence">Therefore, numerical CVSS scores should be labeled using nomenclature that communicates the metrics used in its generation</data><data key="edge_extraction_method">minie</data><data key="edge_polarity">positive</data><data key="edge_modality">asserted</data></edge><edge id="oe_6aa304aadb081a21" source="e_7d27fcc704b7bc10" target="e_bbcb8ea999353380"><data key="edge_predicate_raw">communicates metrics used in</data><data key="edge_assertion_id">a_3617cb8cc5c9bc00</data><data key="edge_source_id">S50</data><data key="edge_source_url">https://www.first.org/cvss/v4.0/specification-document</data><data key="edge_chunk_id">S50_C04</data><data key="edge_json_path">None</data><data key="edge_evidence">Therefore, numerical CVSS scores should be labeled using nomenclature that communicates the metrics used in its generation</data><data key="edge_extraction_method">minie</data><data key="edge_polarity">positive</data><data key="edge_modality">asserted</data></edge><edge id="oe_f2d4b794a77834ae" source="e_768bf52735c34131" target="e_bbcb8ea999353380"><data key="edge_predicate_raw">be used in</data><data key="edge_assertion_id">a_f453ecc2d64b2b48</data><data key="edge_source_id">S50</data><data key="edge_source_url">https://www.first.org/cvss/v4.0/specification-document</data><data key="edge_chunk_id">S50_C04</data><data key="edge_json_path">None</data><data key="edge_evidence">Therefore, numerical CVSS scores should be labeled using nomenclature that communicates the metrics used in its generation</data><data key="edge_extraction_method">minie</data><data key="edge_polarity">positive</data><data key="edge_modality">asserted</data></edge><edge id="oe_5e6c88f2c2b92808" source="e_2919d15188358d3d" target="e_a2e8a6e6d35412fe"><data key="edge_predicate_raw">used</data><data key="edge_assertion_id">a_d65a90aa44a51419</data><data key="edge_source_id">S50</data><data key="edge_source_url">https://www.first.org/cvss/v4.0/specification-document</data><data key="edge_chunk_id">S50_C04</data><data key="edge_json_path">None</data><data key="edge_evidence">This nomenclature should be used wherever a numerical CVSS value is displayed or communicated</data><data key="edge_extraction_method">heuristic</data><data key="edge_polarity">positive</data><data key="edge_modality">asserted</data></edge><edge id="oe_2717ea0337667154" source="e_9e3f8e0349f649b1" target="e_d800caf744b5709e"><data key="edge_predicate_raw">is responsibility of</data><data key="edge_assertion_id">a_e44ec34543a72f51</data><data key="edge_source_id">S50</data><data key="edge_source_url">https://www.first.org/cvss/v4.0/specification-document</data><data key="edge_chunk_id">S50_C05</data><data key="edge_json_path">None</data><data key="edge_evidence">The application of Environmental and Threat metrics is the responsibility of the CVSS consumer</data><data key="edge_extraction_method">minie</data><data key="edge_polarity">positive</data><data key="edge_modality">asserted</data></edge><edge id="oe_d3c78c5bae4d9002" source="e_845db19a5f318ea7" target="e_d800caf744b5709e"><data key="edge_predicate_raw">is responsibility of</data><data key="edge_assertion_id">a_6e7d4d62f793ae32</data><data key="edge_source_id">S50</data><data key="edge_source_url">https://www.first.org/cvss/v4.0/specification-document</data><data key="edge_chunk_id">S50_C05</data><data key="edge_json_path">None</data><data key="edge_evidence">The application of Environmental and Threat metrics is the responsibility of the CVSS consumer</data><data key="edge_extraction_method">minie</data><data key="edge_polarity">positive</data><data key="edge_modality">asserted</data></edge><edge id="oe_5a4d60b5f4d83f51" source="e_7563cb4baa21b7ab" target="e_51321b750147cbd0"><data key="edge_predicate_raw">provide Base Scores enumerated as</data><data key="edge_assertion_id">a_8adc1fc6686fab8c</data><data key="edge_source_id">S50</data><data key="edge_source_url">https://www.first.org/cvss/v4.0/specification-document</data><data key="edge_chunk_id">S50_C05</data><data key="edge_json_path">None</data><data key="edge_evidence">Assessment providers such as product maintainers and other public/private entities such as the National Vulnerability Database (NVD) typically provide only the Base Scores enumerated as CVSS-B</data><data key="edge_extraction_method">minie</data><data key="edge_polarity">positive</data><data key="edge_modality">asserted</data></edge><edge id="oe_9a7a37f7211f3f24" source="e_817fb241c4f3fb8a" target="e_51321b750147cbd0"><data key="edge_predicate_raw">provide Base Scores enumerated as</data><data key="edge_assertion_id">a_ac1da520f8663592</data><data key="edge_source_id">S50</data><data key="edge_source_url">https://www.first.org/cvss/v4.0/specification-document</data><data key="edge_chunk_id">S50_C05</data><data key="edge_json_path">None</data><data key="edge_evidence">Assessment providers such as product maintainers and other public/private entities such as the National Vulnerability Database (NVD) typically provide only the Base Scores enumerated as CVSS-B</data><data key="edge_extraction_method">minie</data><data key="edge_polarity">positive</data><data key="edge_modality">asserted</data></edge><edge id="oe_3a22d92b757eadb7" source="e_0aeb5fdf6effbdc8" target="e_51321b750147cbd0"><data key="edge_predicate_raw">be enumerated as</data><data key="edge_assertion_id">a_282c4f68ac056184</data><data key="edge_source_id">S50</data><data key="edge_source_url">https://www.first.org/cvss/v4.0/specification-document</data><data key="edge_chunk_id">S50_C05</data><data key="edge_json_path">None</data><data key="edge_evidence">Assessment providers such as product maintainers and other public/private entities such as the National Vulnerability Database (NVD) typically provide only the Base Scores enumerated as CVSS-B</data><data key="edge_extraction_method">minie</data><data key="edge_polarity">positive</data><data key="edge_modality">asserted</data></edge><edge id="oe_e8d9e725ccf5190d" source="e_3bca66551d1e30df" target="e_6fb05c788d94028e"><data key="edge_predicate_raw">are considered in calculation of</data><data key="edge_assertion_id">a_cc936b253cf97cc0</data><data key="edge_source_id">S50</data><data key="edge_source_url">https://www.first.org/cvss/v4.0/specification-document</data><data key="edge_chunk_id">S50_C05</data><data key="edge_json_path">None</data><data key="edge_evidence">In CVSS v4.0, Base, Threat, and Environmental metric values are always considered in the calculation of the final score</data><data key="edge_extraction_method">minie</data><data key="edge_polarity">positive</data><data key="edge_modality">asserted</data></edge><edge id="oe_3083b3f153327f2b" source="e_838a95b0b63fa880" target="e_6fb05c788d94028e"><data key="edge_predicate_raw">are considered in calculation of</data><data key="edge_assertion_id">a_1b71a8e807ac7be0</data><data key="edge_source_id">S50</data><data key="edge_source_url">https://www.first.org/cvss/v4.0/specification-document</data><data key="edge_chunk_id">S50_C05</data><data key="edge_json_path">None</data><data key="edge_evidence">In CVSS v4.0, Base, Threat, and Environmental metric values are always considered in the calculation of the final score</data><data key="edge_extraction_method">minie</data><data key="edge_polarity">positive</data><data key="edge_modality">asserted</data></edge><edge id="oe_bb6c4438f8d019c9" source="e_84c5fb779fc835d7" target="e_6fb05c788d94028e"><data key="edge_predicate_raw">are considered in calculation of</data><data key="edge_assertion_id">a_667250b8eee1171f</data><data key="edge_source_id">S50</data><data key="edge_source_url">https://www.first.org/cvss/v4.0/specification-document</data><data key="edge_chunk_id">S50_C05</data><data key="edge_json_path">None</data><data key="edge_evidence">In CVSS v4.0, Base, Threat, and Environmental metric values are always considered in the calculation of the final score</data><data key="edge_extraction_method">minie</data><data key="edge_polarity">positive</data><data key="edge_modality">asserted</data></edge><edge id="oe_60e6850a6e101d04" source="e_ba6a59ae6b0db851" target="e_5e3014756335417a"><data key="edge_predicate_raw">result in</data><data key="edge_assertion_id">a_0fc74000ea7ae8fc</data><data key="edge_source_id">S50</data><data key="edge_source_url">https://www.first.org/cvss/v4.0/specification-document</data><data key="edge_chunk_id">S50_C05</data><data key="edge_json_path">None</data><data key="edge_evidence">The absence of explicit Threat and/or Environmental metric selections will still result in a complete score using default (“Not Defined”) values</data><data key="edge_extraction_method">minie</data><data key="edge_polarity">negative</data><data key="edge_modality">asserted</data></edge><edge id="oe_7b97a9eb6218cb80" source="e_0b1f826002e28a94" target="e_5e3014756335417a"><data key="edge_predicate_raw">result in</data><data key="edge_assertion_id">a_4fc1f9170278144d</data><data key="edge_source_id">S50</data><data key="edge_source_url">https://www.first.org/cvss/v4.0/specification-document</data><data key="edge_chunk_id">S50_C05</data><data key="edge_json_path">None</data><data key="edge_evidence">The absence of explicit Threat and/or Environmental metric selections will still result in a complete score using default (“Not Defined”) values</data><data key="edge_extraction_method">minie</data><data key="edge_polarity">negative</data><data key="edge_modality">asserted</data></edge><edge id="oe_d8939caf3b488eda" source="e_1738e7185e9abbb3" target="e_44ac22faaa9a633f"><data key="edge_predicate_raw">be using</data><data key="edge_assertion_id">a_58dace037de49fe9</data><data key="edge_source_id">S50</data><data key="edge_source_url">https://www.first.org/cvss/v4.0/specification-document</data><data key="edge_chunk_id">S50_C05</data><data key="edge_json_path">None</data><data key="edge_evidence">The absence of explicit Threat and/or Environmental metric selections will still result in a complete score using default (“Not Defined”) values</data><data key="edge_extraction_method">minie</data><data key="edge_polarity">negative</data><data key="edge_modality">asserted</data></edge><edge id="oe_f0b2a90a3748eeef" source="e_c00a4051d0530e03" target="e_7105a374c44c5518"><data key="edge_predicate_raw">reflect characteristics of thing As</data><data key="edge_assertion_id">a_d539788c49e910ed</data><data key="edge_source_id">S50</data><data key="edge_source_url">https://www.first.org/cvss/v4.0/specification-document</data><data key="edge_chunk_id">S50_C05</data><data key="edge_json_path">None</data><data key="edge_evidence">As previously mentioned, the Exploitability metrics reflect the characteristics of the “thing that is vulnerable”, which we refer to formally as the vulnerable system</data><data key="edge_extraction_method">minie</data><data key="edge_polarity">positive</data><data key="edge_modality">asserted</data></edge><edge id="oe_91d4714dc55c2e8f" source="e_c00a4051d0530e03" target="e_2f5c3d09f4bbc7c9"><data key="edge_predicate_raw">reflect characteristics of</data><data key="edge_assertion_id">a_cd02e53f40dce747</data><data key="edge_source_id">S50</data><data key="edge_source_url">https://www.first.org/cvss/v4.0/specification-document</data><data key="edge_chunk_id">S50_C05</data><data key="edge_json_path">None</data><data key="edge_evidence">As previously mentioned, the Exploitability metrics reflect the characteristics of the “thing that is vulnerable”, which we refer to formally as the vulnerable system</data><data key="edge_extraction_method">minie</data><data key="edge_polarity">positive</data><data key="edge_modality">asserted</data></edge><edge id="oe_f0d868b429f31aba" source="e_be74ffef073dc8d3" target="e_7ee1ff4a70457dd7"><data key="edge_predicate_raw">refer thing to formally as</data><data key="edge_assertion_id">a_bf46cd7996c6b2b7</data><data key="edge_source_id">S50</data><data key="edge_source_url">https://www.first.org/cvss/v4.0/specification-document</data><data key="edge_chunk_id">S50_C05</data><data key="edge_json_path">None</data><data key="edge_evidence">As previously mentioned, the Exploitability metrics reflect the characteristics of the “thing that is vulnerable”, which we refer to formally as the vulnerable system</data><data key="edge_extraction_method">minie</data><data key="edge_polarity">positive</data><data key="edge_modality">asserted</data></edge><edge id="oe_2b98ef7890082e8f" source="e_be74ffef073dc8d3" target="e_2f5c3d09f4bbc7c9"><data key="edge_predicate_raw">refer</data><data key="edge_assertion_id">a_646382e0afda05fc</data><data key="edge_source_id">S50</data><data key="edge_source_url">https://www.first.org/cvss/v4.0/specification-document</data><data key="edge_chunk_id">S50_C05</data><data key="edge_json_path">None</data><data key="edge_evidence">As previously mentioned, the Exploitability metrics reflect the characteristics of the “thing that is vulnerable”, which we refer to formally as the vulnerable system</data><data key="edge_extraction_method">minie</data><data key="edge_polarity">positive</data><data key="edge_modality">asserted</data></edge><edge id="oe_c6453e4c5a5c6c9b" source="e_dbd1ba0cc63988dc" target="e_2676df0405400172"><data key="edge_predicate_raw">lead to</data><data key="edge_assertion_id">a_47a452a2deb43c50</data><data key="edge_source_id">S50</data><data key="edge_source_url">https://www.first.org/cvss/v4.0/specification-document</data><data key="edge_chunk_id">S50_C05</data><data key="edge_json_path">None</data><data key="edge_evidence">Therefore, each of the Exploitability metrics listed below should be assessed relative to the vulnerable system, and reflect the properties of the vulnerability that lead to a successful attack</data><data key="edge_extraction_method">minie</data><data key="edge_polarity">positive</data><data key="edge_modality">asserted</data></edge><edge id="oe_5ee5041c8c8a7f08" source="e_ad16450d4d7b98f8" target="e_80b852b98e6b518c"><data key="edge_predicate_raw">be assessing</data><data key="edge_assertion_id">a_e7ff37ba8a0e0928</data><data key="edge_source_id">S50</data><data key="edge_source_url">https://www.first.org/cvss/v4.0/specification-document</data><data key="edge_chunk_id">S50_C05</data><data key="edge_json_path">None</data><data key="edge_evidence">When assessing Base metrics, it should be assumed that the attacker has advanced knowledge of the target system, including general configuration and default defense mechanisms (e.g., built-in firewalls, rate limits, traffic policing)</data><data key="edge_extraction_method">minie</data><data key="edge_polarity">positive</data><data key="edge_modality">asserted</data></edge><edge id="oe_f5a6b767a5c260f7" source="e_537e6ab50e8f2e44" target="e_ebc645c43237e0bf"><data key="edge_predicate_raw">has advanced knowledge of target system</data><data key="edge_assertion_id">a_3effd521fc38258e</data><data key="edge_source_id">S50</data><data key="edge_source_url">https://www.first.org/cvss/v4.0/specification-document</data><data key="edge_chunk_id">S50_C05</data><data key="edge_json_path">None</data><data key="edge_evidence">When assessing Base metrics, it should be assumed that the attacker has advanced knowledge of the target system, including general configuration and default defense mechanisms (e.g., built-in firewalls, rate limits, traffic policing)</data><data key="edge_extraction_method">minie</data><data key="edge_polarity">positive</data><data key="edge_modality">asserted</data></edge><edge id="oe_49406750cdbb4f40" source="e_537e6ab50e8f2e44" target="e_606ef83eb3f75a72"><data key="edge_predicate_raw">has advanced knowledge of target system</data><data key="edge_assertion_id">a_08a9d9d5c7c0306d</data><data key="edge_source_id">S50</data><data key="edge_source_url">https://www.first.org/cvss/v4.0/specification-document</data><data key="edge_chunk_id">S50_C05</data><data key="edge_json_path">None</data><data key="edge_evidence">When assessing Base metrics, it should be assumed that the attacker has advanced knowledge of the target system, including general configuration and default defense mechanisms (e.g., built-in firewalls, rate limits, traffic policing)</data><data key="edge_extraction_method">minie</data><data key="edge_polarity">positive</data><data key="edge_modality">asserted</data></edge><edge id="oe_77977bafbcd78085" source="e_537e6ab50e8f2e44" target="e_277f0117c004b170"><data key="edge_predicate_raw">has advanced knowledge of</data><data key="edge_assertion_id">a_f2bf619a5f5996b4</data><data key="edge_source_id">S50</data><data key="edge_source_url">https://www.first.org/cvss/v4.0/specification-document</data><data key="edge_chunk_id">S50_C05</data><data key="edge_json_path">None</data><data key="edge_evidence">When assessing Base metrics, it should be assumed that the attacker has advanced knowledge of the target system, including general configuration and default defense mechanisms (e.g., built-in firewalls, rate limits, traffic policing)</data><data key="edge_extraction_method">minie</data><data key="edge_polarity">positive</data><data key="edge_modality">asserted</data></edge><edge id="oe_6dee226c23268977" source="e_dbd1ba0cc63988dc" target="e_b8ee2c28df4dc72b"><data key="edge_predicate_raw">results in</data><data key="edge_assertion_id">a_799cf20d2e1b094d</data><data key="edge_source_id">S50</data><data key="edge_source_url">https://www.first.org/cvss/v4.0/specification-document</data><data key="edge_chunk_id">S50_C05</data><data key="edge_json_path">None</data><data key="edge_evidence">For example, exploiting a vulnerability that results in repeatable, deterministic success should still be considered a Low value for Attack Complexity, independent of the attacker's knowledge or capabilities</data><data key="edge_extraction_method">minie</data><data key="edge_polarity">positive</data><data key="edge_modality">asserted</data></edge><edge id="oe_0773f12f4e7801e8" source="e_d76f0b71c9538da5" target="e_5ad6c123e5abaf11"><data key="edge_predicate_raw">be considered Low value for Attack Complexity independent of attacker 's knowledge For</data><data key="edge_assertion_id">a_968673285294a355</data><data key="edge_source_id">S50</data><data key="edge_source_url">https://www.first.org/cvss/v4.0/specification-document</data><data key="edge_chunk_id">S50_C05</data><data key="edge_json_path">None</data><data key="edge_evidence">For example, exploiting a vulnerability that results in repeatable, deterministic success should still be considered a Low value for Attack Complexity, independent of the attacker's knowledge or capabilities</data><data key="edge_extraction_method">minie</data><data key="edge_polarity">positive</data><data key="edge_modality">asserted</data></edge><edge id="oe_88e0025805648ffa" source="e_d76f0b71c9538da5" target="e_5ad6c123e5abaf11"><data key="edge_predicate_raw">be considered Low value for Attack Complexity independent of capabilities For</data><data key="edge_assertion_id">a_7f7e47a2d897751a</data><data key="edge_source_id">S50</data><data key="edge_source_url">https://www.first.org/cvss/v4.0/specification-document</data><data key="edge_chunk_id">S50_C05</data><data key="edge_json_path">None</data><data key="edge_evidence">For example, exploiting a vulnerability that results in repeatable, deterministic success should still be considered a Low value for Attack Complexity, independent of the attacker's knowledge or capabilities</data><data key="edge_extraction_method">minie</data><data key="edge_polarity">positive</data><data key="edge_modality">asserted</data></edge><edge id="oe_36a9f8493d1c18a8" source="e_d76f0b71c9538da5" target="e_fcae9732e4e96feb"><data key="edge_predicate_raw">be considered</data><data key="edge_assertion_id">a_5a8d928865aaa114</data><data key="edge_source_id">S50</data><data key="edge_source_url">https://www.first.org/cvss/v4.0/specification-document</data><data key="edge_chunk_id">S50_C05</data><data key="edge_json_path">None</data><data key="edge_evidence">For example, exploiting a vulnerability that results in repeatable, deterministic success should still be considered a Low value for Attack Complexity, independent of the attacker's knowledge or capabilities</data><data key="edge_extraction_method">minie</data><data key="edge_polarity">positive</data><data key="edge_modality">asserted</data></edge><edge id="oe_32c861909192e522" source="e_d76f0b71c9538da5" target="e_454f93ad983bcfc4"><data key="edge_predicate_raw">be considered</data><data key="edge_assertion_id">a_0de5c44f045ae568</data><data key="edge_source_id">S50</data><data key="edge_source_url">https://www.first.org/cvss/v4.0/specification-document</data><data key="edge_chunk_id">S50_C05</data><data key="edge_json_path">None</data><data key="edge_evidence">For example, exploiting a vulnerability that results in repeatable, deterministic success should still be considered a Low value for Attack Complexity, independent of the attacker's knowledge or capabilities</data><data key="edge_extraction_method">minie</data><data key="edge_polarity">positive</data><data key="edge_modality">asserted</data></edge><edge id="oe_b9ae46f1c79006f1" source="e_311023198a64814b" target="e_c00ecbf5fe9852a6"><data key="edge_predicate_raw">be reflected in Environmental metric scoring group</data><data key="edge_assertion_id">a_ae8fc9817e96bbf1</data><data key="edge_source_id">S50</data><data key="edge_source_url">https://www.first.org/cvss/v4.0/specification-document</data><data key="edge_chunk_id">S50_C05</data><data key="edge_json_path">None</data><data key="edge_evidence">Furthermore, target-specific attack mitigation (e.g., custom firewall filters, access lists) should instead be reflected in the Environmental metric scoring group</data><data key="edge_extraction_method">minie</data><data key="edge_polarity">positive</data><data key="edge_modality">asserted</data></edge><edge id="oe_9d778625591410c6" source="e_311023198a64814b" target="e_0aef75c4b33ae9e2"><data key="edge_predicate_raw">be reflected in</data><data key="edge_assertion_id">a_05c7037858057fd0</data><data key="edge_source_id">S50</data><data key="edge_source_url">https://www.first.org/cvss/v4.0/specification-document</data><data key="edge_chunk_id">S50_C05</data><data key="edge_json_path">None</data><data key="edge_evidence">Furthermore, target-specific attack mitigation (e.g., custom firewall filters, access lists) should instead be reflected in the Environmental metric scoring group</data><data key="edge_extraction_method">minie</data><data key="edge_polarity">positive</data><data key="edge_modality">asserted</data></edge><edge id="oe_16111ff37a9e75e7" source="e_df25c9975e563a89" target="e_c00ecbf5fe9852a6"><data key="edge_predicate_raw">be reflected</data><data key="edge_assertion_id">a_144ad7d42f99fa83</data><data key="edge_source_id">S50</data><data key="edge_source_url">https://www.first.org/cvss/v4.0/specification-document</data><data key="edge_chunk_id">S50_C05</data><data key="edge_json_path">None</data><data key="edge_evidence">Furthermore, target-specific attack mitigation (e.g., custom firewall filters, access lists) should instead be reflected in the Environmental metric scoring group</data><data key="edge_extraction_method">minie</data><data key="edge_polarity">positive</data><data key="edge_modality">asserted</data></edge><edge id="oe_7f6c3805143a5122" source="e_df25c9975e563a89" target="e_0aef75c4b33ae9e2"><data key="edge_predicate_raw">be reflected e.g. in</data><data key="edge_assertion_id">a_c4e37ebb4eb451c9</data><data key="edge_source_id">S50</data><data key="edge_source_url">https://www.first.org/cvss/v4.0/specification-document</data><data key="edge_chunk_id">S50_C05</data><data key="edge_json_path">None</data><data key="edge_evidence">Furthermore, target-specific attack mitigation (e.g., custom firewall filters, access lists) should instead be reflected in the Environmental metric scoring group</data><data key="edge_extraction_method">minie</data><data key="edge_polarity">positive</data><data key="edge_modality">asserted</data></edge><edge id="oe_305218d5bdd405e8" source="e_213a633d7417fc58" target="e_d1e2297d852c9556"><data key="edge_predicate_raw">is required</data><data key="edge_assertion_id">a_ec279f646a89eb0e</data><data key="edge_source_id">S50</data><data key="edge_source_url">https://www.first.org/cvss/v4.0/specification-document</data><data key="edge_chunk_id">S50_C05</data><data key="edge_json_path">None</data><data key="edge_evidence">Specific configurations should not impact any attribute contributing to the CVSS Base metric assessment , i.e., if a specific configuration is required for an attack to succeed, the vulnerable system should be assessed assuming it is in that configuration</data><data key="edge_extraction_method">heuristic</data><data key="edge_polarity">negative</data><data key="edge_modality">asserted</data></edge><edge id="oe_3aa64b4a196f5d22" source="e_4676679afd99eed0" target="e_466e6377cc3c1257"><data key="edge_predicate_raw">reflects</data><data key="edge_assertion_id">a_9b5168a9efb863cc</data><data key="edge_source_id">S50</data><data key="edge_source_url">https://www.first.org/cvss/v4.0/specification-document</data><data key="edge_chunk_id">S50_C05</data><data key="edge_json_path">None</data><data key="edge_evidence">This metric reflects the context by which vulnerability exploitation is possible</data><data key="edge_extraction_method">minie</data><data key="edge_polarity">positive</data><data key="edge_modality">possible</data></edge><edge id="oe_84d5bee160ca26b4" source="e_0704f64e3b0446e8" target="e_7ee1ff4a70457dd7"><data key="edge_predicate_raw">be in to exploit</data><data key="edge_assertion_id">a_a0a98b9bcfdbf533</data><data key="edge_source_id">S50</data><data key="edge_source_url">https://www.first.org/cvss/v4.0/specification-document</data><data key="edge_chunk_id">S50_C05</data><data key="edge_json_path">None</data><data key="edge_evidence">This metric value (and consequently the resulting severity) will be larger the more remote (logically, and physically) an attacker can be in order to exploit the vulnerable system</data><data key="edge_extraction_method">minie</data><data key="edge_polarity">positive</data><data key="edge_modality">possible</data></edge><edge id="oe_a8209bf9d7fdf013" source="e_dbd1ba0cc63988dc" target="e_571bc10d653316b8"><data key="edge_predicate_raw">be exploited from across</data><data key="edge_assertion_id">a_b85fcf0b271bcef5</data><data key="edge_source_id">S50</data><data key="edge_source_url">https://www.first.org/cvss/v4.0/specification-document</data><data key="edge_chunk_id">S50_C05</data><data key="edge_json_path">None</data><data key="edge_evidence">The assumption is that the number of potential attackers for a vulnerability that could be exploited from across a network is larger than the number of potential attackers that could exploit a vulnerability requiring physical access to a device, and therefore warrants a greater severity</data><data key="edge_extraction_method">minie</data><data key="edge_polarity">positive</data><data key="edge_modality">possible</data></edge><edge id="oe_fb28401171dd0881" source="e_6c929bb8a42a9b8c" target="e_b4e364ab91d013d5"><data key="edge_predicate_raw">is larger than number of</data><data key="edge_assertion_id">a_ca641f74ab50df45</data><data key="edge_source_id">S50</data><data key="edge_source_url">https://www.first.org/cvss/v4.0/specification-document</data><data key="edge_chunk_id">S50_C05</data><data key="edge_json_path">None</data><data key="edge_evidence">The assumption is that the number of potential attackers for a vulnerability that could be exploited from across a network is larger than the number of potential attackers that could exploit a vulnerability requiring physical access to a device, and therefore warrants a greater severity</data><data key="edge_extraction_method">minie</data><data key="edge_polarity">positive</data><data key="edge_modality">possible</data></edge><edge id="oe_61b62031b0d7da87" source="e_6c929bb8a42a9b8c" target="e_ae066f9e822bdfbf"><data key="edge_predicate_raw">warrants</data><data key="edge_assertion_id">a_190778958749f230</data><data key="edge_source_id">S50</data><data key="edge_source_url">https://www.first.org/cvss/v4.0/specification-document</data><data key="edge_chunk_id">S50_C05</data><data key="edge_json_path">None</data><data key="edge_evidence">The assumption is that the number of potential attackers for a vulnerability that could be exploited from across a network is larger than the number of potential attackers that could exploit a vulnerability requiring physical access to a device, and therefore warrants a greater severity</data><data key="edge_extraction_method">minie</data><data key="edge_polarity">positive</data><data key="edge_modality">possible</data></edge><edge id="oe_a12e88225b84cfec" source="e_b4e364ab91d013d5" target="e_684abf44c2980220"><data key="edge_predicate_raw">exploit</data><data key="edge_assertion_id">a_544aada0102bbc6c</data><data key="edge_source_id">S50</data><data key="edge_source_url">https://www.first.org/cvss/v4.0/specification-document</data><data key="edge_chunk_id">S50_C05</data><data key="edge_json_path">None</data><data key="edge_evidence">The assumption is that the number of potential attackers for a vulnerability that could be exploited from across a network is larger than the number of potential attackers that could exploit a vulnerability requiring physical access to a device, and therefore warrants a greater severity</data><data key="edge_extraction_method">minie</data><data key="edge_polarity">positive</data><data key="edge_modality">possible</data></edge><edge id="oe_15ed7476074dc4c1" source="e_dbd1ba0cc63988dc" target="e_99963bce824a5b88"><data key="edge_predicate_raw">be requiring</data><data key="edge_assertion_id">a_73e88f90dc5ff419</data><data key="edge_source_id">S50</data><data key="edge_source_url">https://www.first.org/cvss/v4.0/specification-document</data><data key="edge_chunk_id">S50_C05</data><data key="edge_json_path">None</data><data key="edge_evidence">The assumption is that the number of potential attackers for a vulnerability that could be exploited from across a network is larger than the number of potential attackers that could exploit a vulnerability requiring physical access to a device, and therefore warrants a greater severity</data><data key="edge_extraction_method">minie</data><data key="edge_polarity">positive</data><data key="edge_modality">possible</data></edge><edge id="oe_2547b9c89ab5ea8d" source="e_0dd1994901856e68" target="e_684abf44c2980220"><data key="edge_predicate_raw">exploit</data><data key="edge_assertion_id">a_b88617d28f88dfd9</data><data key="edge_source_id">S50</data><data key="edge_source_url">https://www.first.org/cvss/v4.0/specification-document</data><data key="edge_chunk_id">S50_C06</data><data key="edge_json_path">None</data><data key="edge_evidence">that could exploit a vulnerability requiring physical access to a device, and therefore warrants a greater severity</data><data key="edge_extraction_method">minie</data><data key="edge_polarity">positive</data><data key="edge_modality">possible</data></edge><edge id="oe_ca126e1f62249bbc" source="e_0dd1994901856e68" target="e_ae066f9e822bdfbf"><data key="edge_predicate_raw">warrants</data><data key="edge_assertion_id">a_d57a4bbd1e3afbda</data><data key="edge_source_id">S50</data><data key="edge_source_url">https://www.first.org/cvss/v4.0/specification-document</data><data key="edge_chunk_id">S50_C06</data><data key="edge_json_path">None</data><data key="edge_evidence">that could exploit a vulnerability requiring physical access to a device, and therefore warrants a greater severity</data><data key="edge_extraction_method">minie</data><data key="edge_polarity">positive</data><data key="edge_modality">possible</data></edge><edge id="oe_9fe09ad3f2ad747f" source="e_dbd1ba0cc63988dc" target="e_99963bce824a5b88"><data key="edge_predicate_raw">be requiring</data><data key="edge_assertion_id">a_d313881037a74931</data><data key="edge_source_id">S50</data><data key="edge_source_url">https://www.first.org/cvss/v4.0/specification-document</data><data key="edge_chunk_id">S50_C06</data><data key="edge_json_path">None</data><data key="edge_evidence">that could exploit a vulnerability requiring physical access to a device, and therefore warrants a greater severity</data><data key="edge_extraction_method">minie</data><data key="edge_polarity">positive</data><data key="edge_modality">possible</data></edge><edge id="oe_bf14e07a83287a01" source="e_114131fbf07bd451" target="e_04bc7314d5e166d8"><data key="edge_predicate_raw">is secure VPN within</data><data key="edge_assertion_id">a_24dc893432079f6e</data><data key="edge_source_id">S50</data><data key="edge_source_url">https://www.first.org/cvss/v4.0/specification-document</data><data key="edge_chunk_id">S50_C06</data><data key="edge_json_path">None</data><data key="edge_evidence">This can mean an attack must be launched from the same shared proximity (e.g., Bluetooth, NFC, or IEEE 802.11) or logical network (e.g., local IP subnet), or from within a secure or otherwise limited administrative domain (e.g., MPLS, secure VPN within an administrative network zone)</data><data key="edge_extraction_method">minie</data><data key="edge_polarity">positive</data><data key="edge_modality">possible</data></edge><edge id="oe_7b18e7d1a0ec7f7d" source="e_9bf6ead54114b2ce" target="e_9ce8b4e12489cfb0"><data key="edge_predicate_raw">be launched from</data><data key="edge_assertion_id">a_e2a8976ddcb12d29</data><data key="edge_source_id">S50</data><data key="edge_source_url">https://www.first.org/cvss/v4.0/specification-document</data><data key="edge_chunk_id">S50_C06</data><data key="edge_json_path">None</data><data key="edge_evidence">This can mean an attack must be launched from the same shared proximity (e.g., Bluetooth, NFC, or IEEE 802.11) or logical network (e.g., local IP subnet), or from within a secure or otherwise limited administrative domain (e.g., MPLS, secure VPN within an administrative network zone)</data><data key="edge_extraction_method">minie</data><data key="edge_polarity">positive</data><data key="edge_modality">possible</data></edge><edge id="oe_0bbb0bd155ae4b3b" source="e_9bf6ead54114b2ce" target="e_d492cfe3ad61e27e"><data key="edge_predicate_raw">be launched over</data><data key="edge_assertion_id">a_b25a43eb45247535</data><data key="edge_source_id">S50</data><data key="edge_source_url">https://www.first.org/cvss/v4.0/specification-document</data><data key="edge_chunk_id">S50_C06</data><data key="edge_json_path">None</data><data key="edge_evidence">Assessment Guidance: When deciding between Network and Adjacent, if an attack can be launched over a wide area network or from outside the logically adjacent administrative network domain, use Network</data><data key="edge_extraction_method">minie</data><data key="edge_polarity">positive</data><data key="edge_modality">possible</data></edge><edge id="oe_993b6dcba61dd98b" source="e_9bf6ead54114b2ce" target="e_e299850b57d85a43"><data key="edge_predicate_raw">be launched from outside</data><data key="edge_assertion_id">a_743ff12683900bcf</data><data key="edge_source_id">S50</data><data key="edge_source_url">https://www.first.org/cvss/v4.0/specification-document</data><data key="edge_chunk_id">S50_C06</data><data key="edge_json_path">None</data><data key="edge_evidence">Assessment Guidance: When deciding between Network and Adjacent, if an attack can be launched over a wide area network or from outside the logically adjacent administrative network domain, use Network</data><data key="edge_extraction_method">minie</data><data key="edge_polarity">positive</data><data key="edge_modality">possible</data></edge><edge id="oe_4d58e941650274e2" source="e_9bf6ead54114b2ce" target="e_d492cfe3ad61e27e"><data key="edge_predicate_raw">be launched over</data><data key="edge_assertion_id">a_9b158117bbccc8c6</data><data key="edge_source_id">S50</data><data key="edge_source_url">https://www.first.org/cvss/v4.0/specification-document</data><data key="edge_chunk_id">S50_C07</data><data key="edge_json_path">None</data><data key="edge_evidence">Guidance: When deciding between Network and Adjacent, if an attack can be launched over a wide area network or from outside the logically adjacent administrative network domain, use Network</data><data key="edge_extraction_method">minie</data><data key="edge_polarity">positive</data><data key="edge_modality">possible</data></edge><edge id="oe_c2f7d48d8a8d6285" source="e_9bf6ead54114b2ce" target="e_e299850b57d85a43"><data key="edge_predicate_raw">be launched from outside</data><data key="edge_assertion_id">a_e6e4c4a9662ea077</data><data key="edge_source_id">S50</data><data key="edge_source_url">https://www.first.org/cvss/v4.0/specification-document</data><data key="edge_chunk_id">S50_C07</data><data key="edge_json_path">None</data><data key="edge_evidence">Guidance: When deciding between Network and Adjacent, if an attack can be launched over a wide area network or from outside the logically adjacent administrative network domain, use Network</data><data key="edge_extraction_method">minie</data><data key="edge_polarity">positive</data><data key="edge_modality">possible</data></edge><edge id="oe_4df3b0cf506a5d6f" source="e_29c65a5cd23e4757" target="e_a8467b3b679857f9"><data key="edge_predicate_raw">is to increase</data><data key="edge_assertion_id">a_4335d62576769e91</data><data key="edge_source_id">S50</data><data key="edge_source_url">https://www.first.org/cvss/v4.0/specification-document</data><data key="edge_chunk_id">S50_C07</data><data key="edge_json_path">None</data><data key="edge_evidence">These are conditions whose primary purpose is to increase security and/or increase exploit engineering complexity</data><data key="edge_extraction_method">minie</data><data key="edge_polarity">positive</data><data key="edge_modality">asserted</data></edge><edge id="oe_eb615be7b39a77a1" source="e_29c65a5cd23e4757" target="e_c48cbd28d55ae3b5"><data key="edge_predicate_raw">is to increase</data><data key="edge_assertion_id">a_2be8656b3911d8e2</data><data key="edge_source_id">S50</data><data key="edge_source_url">https://www.first.org/cvss/v4.0/specification-document</data><data key="edge_chunk_id">S50_C07</data><data key="edge_json_path">None</data><data key="edge_evidence">These are conditions whose primary purpose is to increase security and/or increase exploit engineering complexity</data><data key="edge_extraction_method">minie</data><data key="edge_polarity">positive</data><data key="edge_modality">asserted</data></edge><edge id="oe_0532196153eaef64" source="e_dbd1ba0cc63988dc" target="e_8ac7dc38bfec7b49"><data key="edge_predicate_raw">require</data><data key="edge_assertion_id">a_b0630b7938698d02</data><data key="edge_source_id">S50</data><data key="edge_source_url">https://www.first.org/cvss/v4.0/specification-document</data><data key="edge_chunk_id">S50_C07</data><data key="edge_json_path">None</data><data key="edge_evidence">A vulnerability exploitable without a target-specific variable has a lower complexity than a vulnerability that would require non-trivial customization</data><data key="edge_extraction_method">minie</data><data key="edge_polarity">negative</data><data key="edge_modality">asserted</data></edge><edge id="oe_00b3f501e69f2f97" source="e_70cd09994cdc1f89" target="e_dbd1ba0cc63988dc"><data key="edge_predicate_raw">has lower complexity than</data><data key="edge_assertion_id">a_6df3d92c3d929b50</data><data key="edge_source_id">S50</data><data key="edge_source_url">https://www.first.org/cvss/v4.0/specification-document</data><data key="edge_chunk_id">S50_C07</data><data key="edge_json_path">None</data><data key="edge_evidence">A vulnerability exploitable without a target-specific variable has a lower complexity than a vulnerability that would require non-trivial customization</data><data key="edge_extraction_method">minie</data><data key="edge_polarity">negative</data><data key="edge_modality">asserted</data></edge><edge id="oe_d5e9d5b4d7168914" source="e_9d2aaa3fb666ce00" target="e_634f512d013908ef"><data key="edge_predicate_raw">is included in</data><data key="edge_assertion_id">a_f73ff323d19d7d4b</data><data key="edge_source_id">S50</data><data key="edge_source_url">https://www.first.org/cvss/v4.0/specification-document</data><data key="edge_chunk_id">S50_C07</data><data key="edge_json_path">None</data><data key="edge_evidence">The evasion or satisfaction of authentication mechanisms or requisites is included in the Privileges Required assessment and is not considered here as a factor of relevance for Attack Complexity</data><data key="edge_extraction_method">minie</data><data key="edge_polarity">negative</data><data key="edge_modality">asserted</data></edge><edge id="oe_dc8a172039ea1666" source="e_9d2aaa3fb666ce00" target="e_36ca5f7151d21469"><data key="edge_predicate_raw">is included</data><data key="edge_assertion_id">a_5225e52dc69827b5</data><data key="edge_source_id">S50</data><data key="edge_source_url">https://www.first.org/cvss/v4.0/specification-document</data><data key="edge_chunk_id">S50_C07</data><data key="edge_json_path">None</data><data key="edge_evidence">The evasion or satisfaction of authentication mechanisms or requisites is included in the Privileges Required assessment and is not considered here as a factor of relevance for Attack Complexity</data><data key="edge_extraction_method">minie</data><data key="edge_polarity">negative</data><data key="edge_modality">asserted</data></edge><edge id="oe_3bd6126b3b7336b2" source="e_7b303bd7f4eb490a" target="e_634f512d013908ef"><data key="edge_predicate_raw">is included in</data><data key="edge_assertion_id">a_e846cc9e08914fe7</data><data key="edge_source_id">S50</data><data key="edge_source_url">https://www.first.org/cvss/v4.0/specification-document</data><data key="edg