data key="edge_modality">asserted</data></edge><edge id="oe_da5c960c2489fb53" source="e_b1213156f02f477b" target="e_8326d4872ea42324"><data key="edge_predicate_raw">are to define</data><data key="edge_assertion_id">a_b5c753f62b50328f</data><data key="edge_source_id">S50</data><data key="edge_source_url">https://www.first.org/cvss/v4.0/specification-document</data><data key="edge_chunk_id">S50_C17</data><data key="edge_json_path">None</data><data key="edge_evidence">The intent of these metrics are to define the mitigations and compensating controls that are in place for a given environment</data><data key="edge_extraction_method">minie</data><data key="edge_polarity">positive</data><data key="edge_modality">asserted</data></edge><edge id="oe_6a1acc1284a51d29" source="e_596a3f18c38132af" target="e_db5858cf6e7acd99"><data key="edge_predicate_raw">be represent</data><data key="edge_assertion_id">a_2c0217abc14306d8</data><data key="edge_source_id">S50</data><data key="edge_source_url">https://www.first.org/cvss/v4.0/specification-document</data><data key="edge_chunk_id">S50_C17</data><data key="edge_json_path">None</data><data key="edge_evidence">It is acceptable to use the modified metrics to represent situations that increase the resulting score</data><data key="edge_extraction_method">minie</data><data key="edge_polarity">positive</data><data key="edge_modality">asserted</data></edge><edge id="oe_48bbc336fef1a9ac" source="e_db5858cf6e7acd99" target="e_754fa75553fa09be"><data key="edge_predicate_raw">increase</data><data key="edge_assertion_id">a_0858144ce9ba8616</data><data key="edge_source_id">S50</data><data key="edge_source_url">https://www.first.org/cvss/v4.0/specification-document</data><data key="edge_chunk_id">S50_C17</data><data key="edge_json_path">None</data><data key="edge_evidence">It is acceptable to use the modified metrics to represent situations that increase the resulting score</data><data key="edge_extraction_method">minie</data><data key="edge_polarity">positive</data><data key="edge_modality">asserted</data></edge><edge id="oe_5a8d5ae91a584e00" source="e_9b8d436553ded0d6" target="e_9299086080c4accc"><data key="edge_predicate_raw">be granted by</data><data key="edge_assertion_id">a_05220323cf69f6e5</data><data key="edge_source_id">S50</data><data key="edge_source_url">https://www.first.org/cvss/v4.0/specification-document</data><data key="edge_chunk_id">S50_C17</data><data key="edge_json_path">None</data><data key="edge_evidence">However, in the consumer analyst’s environment, administrative privileges might be granted by default without authenticating the user</data><data key="edge_extraction_method">minie</data><data key="edge_polarity">negative</data><data key="edge_modality">possible</data></edge><edge id="oe_fc9a6ef2fa495f60" source="e_9b8d436553ded0d6" target="e_2b564a610fc97c2c"><data key="edge_predicate_raw">be granted by default in</data><data key="edge_assertion_id">a_c6265ac0af3c2637</data><data key="edge_source_id">S50</data><data key="edge_source_url">https://www.first.org/cvss/v4.0/specification-document</data><data key="edge_chunk_id">S50_C17</data><data key="edge_json_path">None</data><data key="edge_evidence">However, in the consumer analyst’s environment, administrative privileges might be granted by default without authenticating the user</data><data key="edge_extraction_method">minie</data><data key="edge_polarity">negative</data><data key="edge_modality">possible</data></edge><edge id="oe_42747a23d14fff0f" source="e_9b8d436553ded0d6" target="e_e4f2a12429d15623"><data key="edge_predicate_raw">be granted by default without</data><data key="edge_assertion_id">a_c5fd395017d4d531</data><data key="edge_source_id">S50</data><data key="edge_source_url">https://www.first.org/cvss/v4.0/specification-document</data><data key="edge_chunk_id">S50_C17</data><data key="edge_json_path">None</data><data key="edge_evidence">However, in the consumer analyst’s environment, administrative privileges might be granted by default without authenticating the user</data><data key="edge_extraction_method">minie</data><data key="edge_polarity">negative</data><data key="edge_modality">possible</data></edge><edge id="oe_c781f141f0c3ffca" source="e_f6498126c94c6f96" target="e_506193cfefade053"><data key="edge_predicate_raw">set</data><data key="edge_assertion_id">a_7a0dd07abbdd1d36</data><data key="edge_source_id">S50</data><data key="edge_source_url">https://www.first.org/cvss/v4.0/specification-document</data><data key="edge_chunk_id">S50_C17</data><data key="edge_json_path">None</data><data key="edge_evidence">The analyst can set Privileges Required to High and Modified Privileges Required to None to reflect this more serious condition in their particular environment</data><data key="edge_extraction_method">minie</data><data key="edge_polarity">positive</data><data key="edge_modality">possible</data></edge><edge id="oe_c99506b013721a39" source="e_f6498126c94c6f96" target="e_8baba9b928c90883"><data key="edge_predicate_raw">set</data><data key="edge_assertion_id">a_c0848489badee2e8</data><data key="edge_source_id">S50</data><data key="edge_source_url">https://www.first.org/cvss/v4.0/specification-document</data><data key="edge_chunk_id">S50_C17</data><data key="edge_json_path">None</data><data key="edge_evidence">The analyst can set Privileges Required to High and Modified Privileges Required to None to reflect this more serious condition in their particular environment</data><data key="edge_extraction_method">minie</data><data key="edge_polarity">positive</data><data key="edge_modality">possible</data></edge><edge id="oe_9bea3a227e8a299d" source="e_1b50c049dec6c218" target="e_b084bc0ae581622f"><data key="edge_predicate_raw">be Required to High Privileges Required to None to reflect more serious condition in</data><data key="edge_assertion_id">a_c6f15da12e120f45</data><data key="edge_source_id">S50</data><data key="edge_source_url">https://www.first.org/cvss/v4.0/specification-document</data><data key="edge_chunk_id">S50_C17</data><data key="edge_json_path">None</data><data key="edge_evidence">The analyst can set Privileges Required to High and Modified Privileges Required to None to reflect this more serious condition in their particular environment</data><data key="edge_extraction_method">minie</data><data key="edge_polarity">positive</data><data key="edge_modality">possible</data></edge><edge id="oe_f0050ab0397b4bc8" source="e_1b50c049dec6c218" target="e_b084bc0ae581622f"><data key="edge_predicate_raw">be Required to Modified Privileges Required to None to reflect more serious condition in</data><data key="edge_assertion_id">a_7b76606012f52114</data><data key="edge_source_id">S50</data><data key="edge_source_url">https://www.first.org/cvss/v4.0/specification-document</data><data key="edge_chunk_id">S50_C17</data><data key="edge_json_path">None</data><data key="edge_evidence">The analyst can set Privileges Required to High and Modified Privileges Required to None to reflect this more serious condition in their particular environment</data><data key="edge_extraction_method">minie</data><data key="edge_polarity">positive</data><data key="edge_modality">possible</data></edge><edge id="oe_b09532e0581ab610" source="e_6cb481a83536ac29" target="e_f90f01579634abed"><data key="edge_predicate_raw">be Required to</data><data key="edge_assertion_id">a_d193a02456c510ec</data><data key="edge_source_id">S50</data><data key="edge_source_url">https://www.first.org/cvss/v4.0/specification-document</data><data key="edge_chunk_id">S50_C17</data><data key="edge_json_path">None</data><data key="edge_evidence">The analyst can set Privileges Required to High and Modified Privileges Required to None to reflect this more serious condition in their particular environment</data><data key="edge_extraction_method">minie</data><data key="edge_polarity">positive</data><data key="edge_modality">possible</data></edge><edge id="oe_2528a9a1c76c6011" source="e_cbda6adb410f4617" target="e_f90f01579634abed"><data key="edge_predicate_raw">be Required to</data><data key="edge_assertion_id">a_b29c6b78acb56f43</data><data key="edge_source_id">S50</data><data key="edge_source_url">https://www.first.org/cvss/v4.0/specification-document</data><data key="edge_chunk_id">S50_C17</data><data key="edge_json_path">None</data><data key="edge_evidence">The analyst can set Privileges Required to High and Modified Privileges Required to None to reflect this more serious condition in their particular environment</data><data key="edge_extraction_method">minie</data><data key="edge_polarity">positive</data><data key="edge_modality">possible</data></edge><edge id="oe_86d0a0cc3b6c946a" source="e_d45a29c5219856c1" target="e_24724c67123f239d"><data key="edge_predicate_raw">be to run listening service with</data><data key="edge_assertion_id">a_db32ab40eb771690</data><data key="edge_source_id">S50</data><data key="edge_source_url">https://www.first.org/cvss/v4.0/specification-document</data><data key="edge_chunk_id">S50_C17</data><data key="edge_json_path">None</data><data key="edge_evidence">Example 2: The default configuration for a vulnerable system may be to run a listening service with administrator privileges, for which a compromise might grant an attacker Confidentiality, Integrity, and Availability impacts that are all High</data><data key="edge_extraction_method">minie</data><data key="edge_polarity">positive</data><data key="edge_modality">possible</data></edge><edge id="oe_9c9c2f9695feb2d2" source="e_d45a29c5219856c1" target="e_349144947774f114"><data key="edge_predicate_raw">be to run</data><data key="edge_assertion_id">a_4eea76259d22783f</data><data key="edge_source_id">S50</data><data key="edge_source_url">https://www.first.org/cvss/v4.0/specification-document</data><data key="edge_chunk_id">S50_C17</data><data key="edge_json_path">None</data><data key="edge_evidence">Example 2: The default configuration for a vulnerable system may be to run a listening service with administrator privileges, for which a compromise might grant an attacker Confidentiality, Integrity, and Availability impacts that are all High</data><data key="edge_extraction_method">minie</data><data key="edge_polarity">positive</data><data key="edge_modality">possible</data></edge><edge id="oe_0c08d204b0952ef3" source="e_2777340d458412d6" target="e_24724c67123f239d"><data key="edge_predicate_raw">grant attacker Confidentiality listening service with</data><data key="edge_assertion_id">a_110095d42457583d</data><data key="edge_source_id">S50</data><data key="edge_source_url">https://www.first.org/cvss/v4.0/specification-document</data><data key="edge_chunk_id">S50_C17</data><data key="edge_json_path">None</data><data key="edge_evidence">Example 2: The default configuration for a vulnerable system may be to run a listening service with administrator privileges, for which a compromise might grant an attacker Confidentiality, Integrity, and Availability impacts that are all High</data><data key="edge_extraction_method">minie</data><data key="edge_polarity">positive</data><data key="edge_modality">possible</data></edge><edge id="oe_f79cedb1d9de7417" source="e_2777340d458412d6" target="e_349144947774f114"><data key="edge_predicate_raw">grant attacker Confidentiality</data><data key="edge_assertion_id">a_e6812a99763259c6</data><data key="edge_source_id">S50</data><data key="edge_source_url">https://www.first.org/cvss/v4.0/specification-document</data><data key="edge_chunk_id">S50_C17</data><data key="edge_json_path">None</data><data key="edge_evidence">Example 2: The default configuration for a vulnerable system may be to run a listening service with administrator privileges, for which a compromise might grant an attacker Confidentiality, Integrity, and Availability impacts that are all High</data><data key="edge_extraction_method">minie</data><data key="edge_polarity">positive</data><data key="edge_modality">possible</data></edge><edge id="oe_5f0c2e35be99a6d7" source="e_2cbef1015e8443fb" target="e_040dc8c7ec38f443"><data key="edge_predicate_raw">be running with</data><data key="edge_assertion_id">a_f84dcfd54de1b504</data><data key="edge_source_id">S50</data><data key="edge_source_url">https://www.first.org/cvss/v4.0/specification-document</data><data key="edge_chunk_id">S50_C17</data><data key="edge_json_path">None</data><data key="edge_evidence">Yet, in the consumer analyst’s environment, that same Internet service might be running with reduced privileges; in that case, the Modified Confidentiality, Modified Integrity, and Modified Availability might each be set to Low</data><data key="edge_extraction_method">minie</data><data key="edge_polarity">positive</data><data key="edge_modality">possible</data></edge><edge id="oe_f31baf5f2c4c9f96" source="e_2cbef1015e8443fb" target="e_2b564a610fc97c2c"><data key="edge_predicate_raw">be running with reduced privileges in</data><data key="edge_assertion_id">a_92e0fdfd3d3fa6a1</data><data key="edge_source_id">S50</data><data key="edge_source_url">https://www.first.org/cvss/v4.0/specification-document</data><data key="edge_chunk_id">S50_C17</data><data key="edge_json_path">None</data><data key="edge_evidence">Yet, in the consumer analyst’s environment, that same Internet service might be running with reduced privileges; in that case, the Modified Confidentiality, Modified Integrity, and Modified Availability might each be set to Low</data><data key="edge_extraction_method">minie</data><data key="edge_polarity">positive</data><data key="edge_modality">possible</data></edge><edge id="oe_db1b59976594da08" source="e_0103ceb496288738" target="e_acf7de49bb06f2fb"><data key="edge_predicate_raw">be reduced to</data><data key="edge_assertion_id">a_1436cf35cb146d1e</data><data key="edge_source_id">S50</data><data key="edge_source_url">https://www.first.org/cvss/v4.0/specification-document</data><data key="edge_chunk_id">S50_C17</data><data key="edge_json_path">None</data><data key="edge_evidence">All vulnerabilities found on those systems may have the Attack Vector (AV) values of “Network” reduced to “Adjacent”</data><data key="edge_extraction_method">minie</data><data key="edge_polarity">positive</data><data key="edge_modality">possible</data></edge><edge id="oe_d792f2fda4b5fdf0" source="e_3194ef0752b4dc4c" target="e_afccd7a4fc5871a9"><data key="edge_predicate_raw">has corresponding Base values of</data><data key="edge_assertion_id">a_914f3ccbfba9262b</data><data key="edge_source_id">S50</data><data key="edge_source_url">https://www.first.org/cvss/v4.0/specification-document</data><data key="edge_chunk_id">S50_C17</data><data key="edge_json_path">None</data><data key="edge_evidence">Each Modified Environmental metric has the same values as its corresponding Base metric, plus values of Not Defined and Safety</data><data key="edge_extraction_method">minie</data><data key="edge_polarity">negative</data><data key="edge_modality">asserted</data></edge><edge id="oe_28ac410314ff2571" source="e_3194ef0752b4dc4c" target="e_d999ddd1227d98cb"><data key="edge_predicate_raw">has corresponding Base values of</data><data key="edge_assertion_id">a_76e3ee1823f78b53</data><data key="edge_source_id">S50</data><data key="edge_source_url">https://www.first.org/cvss/v4.0/specification-document</data><data key="edge_chunk_id">S50_C17</data><data key="edge_json_path">None</data><data key="edge_evidence">Each Modified Environmental metric has the same values as its corresponding Base metric, plus values of Not Defined and Safety</data><data key="edge_extraction_method">minie</data><data key="edge_polarity">negative</data><data key="edge_modality">asserted</data></edge><edge id="oe_3bc1e9b2b0cbea52" source="e_a00feff6fcb1c982" target="e_b35718531dfb7863"><data key="edge_predicate_raw">uses</data><data key="edge_assertion_id">a_c80eef9512a5e8d5</data><data key="edge_source_id">S50</data><data key="edge_source_url">https://www.first.org/cvss/v4.0/specification-document</data><data key="edge_chunk_id">S50_C17</data><data key="edge_json_path">None</data><data key="edge_evidence">Not Defined is the default and uses the metric value of the associated Base metric</data><data key="edge_extraction_method">heuristic</data><data key="edge_polarity">negative</data><data key="edge_modality">asserted</data></edge><edge id="oe_5c55c09460bae12c" source="e_3194ef0752b4dc4c" target="e_afccd7a4fc5871a9"><data key="edge_predicate_raw">has corresponding Base values of</data><data key="edge_assertion_id">a_8cf63fcc8abd8db0</data><data key="edge_source_id">S50</data><data key="edge_source_url">https://www.first.org/cvss/v4.0/specification-document</data><data key="edge_chunk_id">S50_C18</data><data key="edge_json_path">None</data><data key="edge_evidence">as its corresponding Base metric, plus values of Not Defined and Safety</data><data key="edge_extraction_method">minie</data><data key="edge_polarity">negative</data><data key="edge_modality">asserted</data></edge><edge id="oe_e4ac8d89b9a0c1fa" source="e_3194ef0752b4dc4c" target="e_d999ddd1227d98cb"><data key="edge_predicate_raw">has corresponding Base values of</data><data key="edge_assertion_id">a_36e721876959ddb0</data><data key="edge_source_id">S50</data><data key="edge_source_url">https://www.first.org/cvss/v4.0/specification-document</data><data key="edge_chunk_id">S50_C18</data><data key="edge_json_path">None</data><data key="edge_evidence">as its corresponding Base metric, plus values of Not Defined and Safety</data><data key="edge_extraction_method">minie</data><data key="edge_polarity">negative</data><data key="edge_modality">asserted</data></edge><edge id="oe_64a06d3f7f63027d" source="e_e98177f81dbc3f16" target="e_368b2018bd5fc92e"><data key="edge_predicate_raw">exploiting</data><data key="edge_assertion_id">a_7a45f33f020a11e1</data><data key="edge_source_id">S50</data><data key="edge_source_url">https://www.first.org/cvss/v4.0/specification-document</data><data key="edge_chunk_id">S50_C18</data><data key="edge_json_path">None</data><data key="edge_evidence">When a system may have safety implications as a matter of how or where it is deployed, it is possible that exploiting a vulnerability within that system may have safety impact(s) which can be represented in the Environmental Metrics group</data><data key="edge_extraction_method">heuristic</data><data key="edge_polarity">positive</data><data key="edge_modality">possible</data></edge><edge id="oe_2b2a29b01881f68e" source="e_d04dc3e9ac82fc8c" target="e_0c881b4882d0a383"><data key="edge_predicate_raw">used</data><data key="edge_assertion_id">a_63ddf955a88e65d2</data><data key="edge_source_id">S50</data><data key="edge_source_url">https://www.first.org/cvss/v4.0/specification-document</data><data key="edge_chunk_id">S50_C18</data><data key="edge_json_path">None</data><data key="edge_evidence">If the exploitation of a technical vulnerability (with impact to either the availability or integrity of the vulnerable system) has the potential to impact human safety, the modified subsequent system impact of Safety (s) should be used (i.e., MSI:S/MSA/S)</data><data key="edge_extraction_method">heuristic</data><data key="edge_polarity">positive</data><data key="edge_modality">asserted</data></edge><edge id="oe_edfb3ac1a477e8cd" source="e_87a35caaa98faf5a" target="e_cd7fcb8a4781c41f"><data key="edge_predicate_raw">result in injuries categorized as</data><data key="edge_assertion_id">a_0b35fa4f4e7b137e</data><data key="edge_source_id">S50</data><data key="edge_source_url">https://www.first.org/cvss/v4.0/specification-document</data><data key="edge_chunk_id">S50_C18</data><data key="edge_json_path">None</data><data key="edge_evidence">Safety impact is applicable when it is predictable that an exploited vulnerability may result in injuries categorized as Marginal or worse using the IEC 61508 definitions outlined in the chart below</data><data key="edge_extraction_method">minie</data><data key="edge_polarity">positive</data><data key="edge_modality">possible</data></edge><edge id="oe_fa00f6e3ce900a86" source="e_87a35caaa98faf5a" target="e_8a528e0b3c3195da"><data key="edge_predicate_raw">result in injuries categorized as</data><data key="edge_assertion_id">a_b3a8980acc459963</data><data key="edge_source_id">S50</data><data key="edge_source_url">https://www.first.org/cvss/v4.0/specification-document</data><data key="edge_chunk_id">S50_C18</data><data key="edge_json_path">None</data><data key="edge_evidence">Safety impact is applicable when it is predictable that an exploited vulnerability may result in injuries categorized as Marginal or worse using the IEC 61508 definitions outlined in the chart below</data><data key="edge_extraction_method">minie</data><data key="edge_polarity">positive</data><data key="edge_modality">possible</data></edge><edge id="oe_3b6e584c224e58de" source="e_d5f0963a1e0287ed" target="e_cd7fcb8a4781c41f"><data key="edge_predicate_raw">be categorized as</data><data key="edge_assertion_id">a_a77df8b802f6a2f7</data><data key="edge_source_id">S50</data><data key="edge_source_url">https://www.first.org/cvss/v4.0/specification-document</data><data key="edge_chunk_id">S50_C18</data><data key="edge_json_path">None</data><data key="edge_evidence">Safety impact is applicable when it is predictable that an exploited vulnerability may result in injuries categorized as Marginal or worse using the IEC 61508 definitions outlined in the chart below</data><data key="edge_extraction_method">minie</data><data key="edge_polarity">positive</data><data key="edge_modality">possible</data></edge><edge id="oe_83b6eb4f60476a6e" source="e_d5f0963a1e0287ed" target="e_8a528e0b3c3195da"><data key="edge_predicate_raw">be categorized as</data><data key="edge_assertion_id">a_6b20a7a5a00053dd</data><data key="edge_source_id">S50</data><data key="edge_source_url">https://www.first.org/cvss/v4.0/specification-document</data><data key="edge_chunk_id">S50_C18</data><data key="edge_json_path">None</data><data key="edge_evidence">Safety impact is applicable when it is predictable that an exploited vulnerability may result in injuries categorized as Marginal or worse using the IEC 61508 definitions outlined in the chart below</data><data key="edge_extraction_method">minie</data><data key="edge_polarity">positive</data><data key="edge_modality">possible</data></edge><edge id="oe_1dda2edbfa1354ba" source="e_469e1f0a792f149b" target="e_371e2a8932c3cb22"><data key="edge_predicate_raw">are leveraged in</data><data key="edge_assertion_id">a_7c756b772b673633</data><data key="edge_source_id">S50</data><data key="edge_source_url">https://www.first.org/cvss/v4.0/specification-document</data><data key="edge_chunk_id">S50_C18</data><data key="edge_json_path">None</data><data key="edge_evidence">Note: Safety metric values are leveraged in both the Supplemental Metric Group (provided by the assessment providers) and the Environmental Metric Group (provided by the consumer analyst)</data><data key="edge_extraction_method">minie</data><data key="edge_polarity">positive</data><data key="edge_modality">asserted</data></edge><edge id="oe_01d1ab6d651a9e91" source="e_469e1f0a792f149b" target="e_b84ee762ce82df1d"><data key="edge_predicate_raw">are leveraged in</data><data key="edge_assertion_id">a_b0af087854a3d016</data><data key="edge_source_id">S50</data><data key="edge_source_url">https://www.first.org/cvss/v4.0/specification-document</data><data key="edge_chunk_id">S50_C18</data><data key="edge_json_path">None</data><data key="edge_evidence">Note: Safety metric values are leveraged in both the Supplemental Metric Group (provided by the assessment providers) and the Environmental Metric Group (provided by the consumer analyst)</data><data key="edge_extraction_method">minie</data><data key="edge_polarity">positive</data><data key="edge_modality">asserted</data></edge><edge id="oe_6fe5bb4cf354564f" source="e_54b478dcf9b37c22" target="e_1e8070a280814846"><data key="edge_predicate_raw">provides</data><data key="edge_assertion_id">a_1e4e5c9ff3122f22</data><data key="edge_source_id">S50</data><data key="edge_source_url">https://www.first.org/cvss/v4.0/specification-document</data><data key="edge_chunk_id">S50_C19</data><data key="edge_json_path">None</data><data key="edge_evidence">A new, optional metric group called the Supplemental metric group provides new metrics that describe and measure additional extrinsic attributes of a vulnerability</data><data key="edge_extraction_method">heuristic</data><data key="edge_polarity">positive</data><data key="edge_modality">asserted</data></edge><edge id="oe_03f149faf62b18f6" source="e_4b31ac02f1eb6833" target="e_b0b8500294aa8ce2"><data key="edge_predicate_raw">is provisioned by</data><data key="edge_assertion_id">a_db80797d2b0b0392</data><data key="edge_source_id">S50</data><data key="edge_source_url">https://www.first.org/cvss/v4.0/specification-document</data><data key="edge_chunk_id">S50_C19</data><data key="edge_json_path">None</data><data key="edge_evidence">While the assessment of Supplemental metrics is provisioned by the provider, the usage and response plan of each metric within the Supplemental metric group is determined by the consumer</data><data key="edge_extraction_method">minie</data><data key="edge_polarity">positive</data><data key="edge_modality">asserted</data></edge><edge id="oe_323e14fa0cb38bf3" source="e_586e3102a6ab682b" target="e_9a5ad6de08ab74ad"><data key="edge_predicate_raw">be employed</data><data key="edge_assertion_id">a_d8511ab2cabe5a24</data><data key="edge_source_id">S50</data><data key="edge_source_url">https://www.first.org/cvss/v4.0/specification-document</data><data key="edge_chunk_id">S50_C19</data><data key="edge_json_path">None</data><data key="edge_evidence">This contextual information may be employed differently in each consumer’s environment</data><data key="edge_extraction_method">minie</data><data key="edge_polarity">positive</data><data key="edge_modality">possible</data></edge><edge id="oe_a195d7e18d876755" source="e_f5258b70cd9cc35b" target="e_90b91b7c7673d09a"><data key="edge_predicate_raw">assign</data><data key="edge_assertion_id">a_8a7f939f2ec864c7</data><data key="edge_source_id">S50</data><data key="edge_source_url">https://www.first.org/cvss/v4.0/specification-document</data><data key="edge_chunk_id">S50_C19</data><data key="edge_json_path">None</data><data key="edge_evidence">Organizations may then assign importance and/or effective impact of each metric, or set/combination of metrics, giving them more, less, or absolutely no effect on the final risk analysis</data><data key="edge_extraction_method">minie</data><data key="edge_polarity">negative</data><data key="edge_modality">possible</data></edge><edge id="oe_6d4980859b5b2714" source="e_290d8da624d84fb0" target="e_9ab722c5f7b8353b"><data key="edge_predicate_raw">see</data><data key="edge_assertion_id">a_b87c8601faa34b2b</data><data key="edge_source_id">S50</data><data key="edge_source_url">https://www.first.org/cvss/v4.0/specification-document</data><data key="edge_chunk_id">S50_C19</data><data key="edge_json_path">None</data><data key="edge_evidence">Suppliers and vendors (AKA: scoring providers) may or may not provide Safety as a Supplemental Metric as they see fit</data><data key="edge_extraction_method">minie</data><data key="edge_polarity">negative</data><data key="edge_modality">possible</data></edge><edge id="oe_bd8620287f01416a" source="e_cbfc4c20d6f87cc5" target="e_c58642aeeaa4024e"><data key="edge_predicate_raw">be as</data><data key="edge_assertion_id">a_36ed922bcd15a606</data><data key="edge_source_id">S50</data><data key="edge_source_url">https://www.first.org/cvss/v4.0/specification-document</data><data key="edge_chunk_id">S50_C19</data><data key="edge_json_path">None</data><data key="edge_evidence">Suppliers and vendors (AKA: scoring providers) may or may not provide Safety as a Supplemental Metric as they see fit</data><data key="edge_extraction_method">minie</data><data key="edge_polarity">negative</data><data key="edge_modality">possible</data></edge><edge id="oe_5af193f5aeb619fc" source="e_ff4e6c2759cc3eb9" target="e_c58642aeeaa4024e"><data key="edge_predicate_raw">be as</data><data key="edge_assertion_id">a_1c0a2e6e2a1c8ee6</data><data key="edge_source_id">S50</data><data key="edge_source_url">https://www.first.org/cvss/v4.0/specification-document</data><data key="edge_chunk_id">S50_C19</data><data key="edge_json_path">None</data><data key="edge_evidence">Suppliers and vendors (AKA: scoring providers) may or may not provide Safety as a Supplemental Metric as they see fit</data><data key="edge_extraction_method">minie</data><data key="edge_polarity">negative</data><data key="edge_modality">possible</data></edge><edge id="oe_5d461acc07cba05a" source="e_9cf9e67a33f313e5" target="e_d999ddd1227d98cb"><data key="edge_predicate_raw">be aligned to</data><data key="edge_assertion_id">a_36a452fbfa9ef650</data><data key="edge_source_id">S50</data><data key="edge_source_url">https://www.first.org/cvss/v4.0/specification-document</data><data key="edge_chunk_id">S50_C19</data><data key="edge_json_path">None</data><data key="edge_evidence">When a system does have an intended use or fitness of purpose aligned to safety, it is possible that exploiting a vulnerability within that system may have Safety impact which can be represented in the Supplemental Metrics group</data><data key="edge_extraction_method">minie</data><data key="edge_polarity">positive</data><data key="edge_modality">possible</data></edge><edge id="oe_83e335e87638eab5" source="e_fb8ea41b8705c2d6" target="e_8fc389924516130b"><data key="edge_predicate_raw">be represented in</data><data key="edge_assertion_id">a_14de90c77e147f2d</data><data key="edge_source_id">S50</data><data key="edge_source_url">https://www.first.org/cvss/v4.0/specification-document</data><data key="edge_chunk_id">S50_C19</data><data key="edge_json_path">None</data><data key="edge_evidence">When a system does have an intended use or fitness of purpose aligned to safety, it is possible that exploiting a vulnerability within that system may have Safety impact which can be represented in the Supplemental Metrics group</data><data key="edge_extraction_method">minie</data><data key="edge_polarity">positive</data><data key="edge_modality">possible</data></edge><edge id="oe_2872700f18657803" source="e_35187791756c46dc" target="e_79a5b245db4e61f6"><data key="edge_predicate_raw">are as</data><data key="edge_assertion_id">a_9cec10eca500f4ee</data><data key="edge_source_id">S50</data><data key="edge_source_url">https://www.first.org/cvss/v4.0/specification-document</data><data key="edge_chunk_id">S50_C19</data><data key="edge_json_path">None</data><data key="edge_evidence">The possible values for the Safety Supplemental Metric are as follows:</data><data key="edge_extraction_method">minie</data><data key="edge_polarity">positive</data><data key="edge_modality">possible</data></edge><edge id="oe_0a110d14785e3d37" source="e_c6ed82b4ae70d76d" target="e_fd0c05ce2ddb775e"><data key="edge_predicate_raw">indicates</data><data key="edge_assertion_id">a_240beea787ab107a</data><data key="edge_source_id">S50</data><data key="edge_source_url">https://www.first.org/cvss/v4.0/specification-document</data><data key="edge_chunk_id">S50_C19</data><data key="edge_json_path">None</data><data key="edge_evidence">The Safety supplemental metric value indicates the degree of impact to the Safety of a human actor or participant that can be predictably injured as a result of the vulnerability being exploited</data><data key="edge_extraction_method">minie</data><data key="edge_polarity">positive</data><data key="edge_modality">possible</data></edge><edge id="oe_f5d9c5a4145538e7" source="e_c6ed82b4ae70d76d" target="e_a928ebd1914cd302"><data key="edge_predicate_raw">indicates</data><data key="edge_assertion_id">a_821a21593eb4f0eb</data><data key="edge_source_id">S50</data><data key="edge_source_url">https://www.first.org/cvss/v4.0/specification-document</data><data key="edge_chunk_id">S50_C19</data><data key="edge_json_path">None</data><data key="edge_evidence">The Safety supplemental metric value indicates the degree of impact to the Safety of a human actor or participant that can be predictably injured as a result of the vulnerability being exploited</data><data key="edge_extraction_method">minie</data><data key="edge_polarity">positive</data><data key="edge_modality">possible</data></edge><edge id="oe_f0a5a231d826f462" source="e_5af327031642cd80" target="e_690ae055b2fa02d6"><data key="edge_predicate_raw">be injured as result of</data><data key="edge_assertion_id">a_a47a7c00ec02e924</data><data key="edge_source_id">S50</data><data key="edge_source_url">https://www.first.org/cvss/v4.0/specification-document</data><data key="edge_chunk_id">S50_C19</data><data key="edge_json_path">None</data><data key="edge_evidence">The Safety supplemental metric value indicates the degree of impact to the Safety of a human actor or participant that can be predictably injured as a result of the vulnerability being exploited</data><data key="edge_extraction_method">minie</data><data key="edge_polarity">positive</data><data key="edge_modality">possible</data></edge><edge id="oe_99e0bbe31004da23" source="e_ab337f11e7d28d47" target="e_690ae055b2fa02d6"><data key="edge_predicate_raw">be injured as result of</data><data key="edge_assertion_id">a_f2232a1d4e3e6a63</data><data key="edge_source_id">S50</data><data key="edge_source_url">https://www.first.org/cvss/v4.0/specification-document</data><data key="edge_chunk_id">S50_C19</data><data key="edge_json_path">None</data><data key="edge_evidence">The Safety supplemental metric value indicates the degree of impact to the Safety of a human actor or participant that can be predictably injured as a result of the vulnerability being exploited</data><data key="edge_extraction_method">minie</data><data key="edge_polarity">positive</data><data key="edge_modality">possible</data></edge><edge id="oe_12e1bbe334a48f52" source="e_d999ddd1227d98cb" target="e_c58642aeeaa4024e"><data key="edge_predicate_raw">be described</data><data key="edge_assertion_id">a_331d80fee366ef35</data><data key="edge_source_id">S50</data><data key="edge_source_url">https://www.first.org/cvss/v4.0/specification-document</data><data key="edge_chunk_id">S50_C19</data><data key="edge_json_path">None</data><data key="edge_evidence">As a Supplemental metric, and consistent with the above table, Safety can be described with metric values of S:X, S:P, or S:N</data><data key="edge_extraction_method">minie</data><data key="edge_polarity">positive</data><data key="edge_modality">possible</data></edge><edge id="oe_e0df4fc6cba6fcfc" source="e_d999ddd1227d98cb" target="e_000918bc13dd8c22"><data key="edge_predicate_raw">be described consistent with</data><data key="edge_assertion_id">a_4369732790b01ea2</data><data key="edge_source_id">S50</data><data key="edge_source_url">https://www.first.org/cvss/v4.0/specification-document</data><data key="edge_chunk_id">S50_C19</data><data key="edge_json_path">None</data><data key="edge_evidence">As a Supplemental metric, and consistent with the above table, Safety can be described with metric values of S:X, S:P, or S:N</data><data key="edge_extraction_method">minie</data><data key="edge_polarity">positive</data><data key="edge_modality">possible</data></edge><edge id="oe_f0d43a830b796f0b" source="e_d1a2cdb8457da1b4" target="e_2e115427b410e854"><data key="edge_predicate_raw">captures answer to</data><data key="edge_assertion_id">a_019c067ad7761f1f</data><data key="edge_source_id">S50</data><data key="edge_source_url">https://www.first.org/cvss/v4.0/specification-document</data><data key="edge_chunk_id">S50_C19</data><data key="edge_json_path">None</data><data key="edge_evidence">The “Automatable” metric captures the answer to the question ”Can an attacker automate exploitation events for this vulnerability across multiple targets?” based on steps 1-4 of the kill chain2 [Hutchins et al., 2011]</data><data key="edge_extraction_method">minie</data><data key="edge_polarity">positive</data><data key="edge_modality">possible</data></edge><edge id="oe_69c5d8f85c05ba3c" source="e_d1a2cdb8457da1b4" target="e_29d07767f4a7edf1"><data key="edge_predicate_raw">captures</data><data key="edge_assertion_id">a_0184f4e452b708ef</data><data key="edge_source_id">S50</data><data key="edge_source_url">https://www.first.org/cvss/v4.0/specification-document</data><data key="edge_chunk_id">S50_C19</data><data key="edge_json_path">None</data><data key="edge_evidence">The “Automatable” metric captures the answer to the question ”Can an attacker automate exploitation events for this vulnerability across multiple targets?” based on steps 1-4 of the kill chain2 [Hutchins et al., 2011]</data><data key="edge_extraction_method">minie</data><data key="edge_polarity">positive</data><data key="edge_modality">possible</data></edge><edge id="oe_fc0d9627a3589064" source="e_537e6ab50e8f2e44" target="e_3c092a597518507c"><data key="edge_predicate_raw">automate exploitation events for vulnerability across</data><data key="edge_assertion_id">a_1f61b31aefedbc29</data><data key="edge_source_id">S50</data><data key="edge_source_url">https://www.first.org/cvss/v4.0/specification-document</data><data key="edge_chunk_id">S50_C19</data><data key="edge_json_path">None</data><data key="edge_evidence">The “Automatable” metric captures the answer to the question ”Can an attacker automate exploitation events for this vulnerability across multiple targets?” based on steps 1-4 of the kill chain2 [Hutchins et al., 2011]</data><data key="edge_extraction_method">minie</data><data key="edge_polarity">positive</data><data key="edge_modality">possible</data></edge><edge id="oe_fcaaa508fe19987e" source="e_537e6ab50e8f2e44" target="e_cd0eecf6d03be185"><data key="edge_predicate_raw">automate</data><data key="edge_assertion_id">a_120b193e2d0bb1b7</data><data key="edge_source_id">S50</data><data key="edge_source_url">https://www.first.org/cvss/v4.0/specification-document</data><data key="edge_chunk_id">S50_C19</data><data key="edge_json_path">None</data><data key="edge_evidence">The “Automatable” metric captures the answer to the question ”Can an attacker automate exploitation events for this vulnerability across multiple targets?” based on steps 1-4 of the kill chain2 [Hutchins et al., 2011]</data><data key="edge_extraction_method">minie</data><data key="edge_polarity">positive</data><data key="edge_modality">possible</data></edge><edge id="oe_a9c186490eb3fb0c" source="e_d1a2cdb8457da1b4" target="e_635799eb1edf6a5b"><data key="edge_predicate_raw">take values If</data><data key="edge_assertion_id">a_abd45a775e2b2446</data><data key="edge_source_id">S50</data><data key="edge_source_url">https://www.first.org/cvss/v4.0/specification-document</data><data key="edge_chunk_id">S50_C19</data><data key="edge_json_path">None</data><data key="edge_evidence">If evaluated, the metric can take the values no or yes:</data><data key="edge_extraction_method">minie</data><data key="edge_polarity">negative</data><data key="edge_modality">possible</data></edge><edge id="oe_753b3e93f8605661" source="e_d1a2cdb8457da1b4" target="e_a9ed604eb1323e31"><data key="edge_predicate_raw">take</data><data key="edge_assertion_id">a_9fd6493742523d3a</data><data key="edge_source_id">S50</data><data key="edge_source_url">https://www.first.org/cvss/v4.0/specification-document</data><data key="edge_chunk_id">S50_C19</data><data key="edge_json_path">None</data><data key="edge_evidence">If evaluated, the metric can take the values no or yes:</data><data key="edge_extraction_method">minie</data><data key="edge_polarity">negative</data><data key="edge_modality">possible</data></edge><edge id="oe_e5d2104c114a7c1c" source="e_11ec9ccc1fc96285" target="e_228b54a1a94571c6"><data key="edge_predicate_raw">publish Qualitative Severity Ratings from</data><data key="edge_assertion_id">a_414c6495a1aedee3</data><data key="edge_source_id">S50</data><data key="edge_source_url">https://www.first.org/cvss/v4.0/specification-document</data><data key="edge_chunk_id">S50_C20</data><data key="edge_json_path">None</data><data key="edge_evidence">Other vendors publish Qualitative Severity Ratings from the CVSS Specification Document in their advisories</data><data key="edge_extraction_method">minie</data><data key="edge_polarity">positive</data><data key="edge_modality">asserted</data></edge><edge id="oe_1172c0d549e88926" source="e_11ec9ccc1fc96285" target="e_835140d8fc9de36c"><data key="edge_predicate_raw">publish Qualitative Severity Ratings in</data><data key="edge_assertion_id">a_fdabcd03c1214a6a</data><data key="edge_source_id">S50</data><data key="edge_source_url">https://www.first.org/cvss/v4.0/specification-document</data><data key="edge_chunk_id">S50_C20</data><data key="edge_json_path">None</data><data key="edge_evidence">Other vendors publish Qualitative Severity Ratings from the CVSS Specification Document in their advisories</data><data key="edge_extraction_method">minie</data><data key="edge_polarity">positive</data><data key="edge_modality">asserted</data></edge><edge id="oe_4a07af71a2072df1" source="e_11ec9ccc1fc96285" target="e_6d50e79cbe0c218e"><data key="edge_predicate_raw">publish</data><data key="edge_assertion_id">a_134a7d3629eb8982</data><data key="edge_source_id">S50</data><data key="edge_source_url">https://www.first.org/cvss/v4.0/specification-document</data><data key="edge_chunk_id">S50_C20</data><data key="edge_json_path">None</data><data key="edge_evidence">Other vendors publish Qualitative Severity Ratings from the CVSS Specification Document in their advisories</data><data key="edge_extraction_method">minie</data><data key="edge_polarity">positive</data><data key="edge_modality">asserted</data></edge><edge id="oe_e1c9808e57776f12" source="e_bb192ae9e03fa1fb" target="e_4a17d33b79767a98"><data key="edge_predicate_raw">be incorporate</data><data key="edge_assertion_id">a_b432f097951ed828</data><data key="edge_source_id">S50</data><data key="edge_source_url">https://www.first.org/cvss/v4.0/specification-document</data><data key="edge_chunk_id">S50_C20</data><data key="edge_json_path">None</data><data key="edge_evidence">To facilitate a standardized method to incorporate additional provider-supplied assessment, an optional “pass-through” Supplemental Metric called Provider Urgency is available</data><data key="edge_extraction_method">minie</data><data key="edge_polarity">positive</data><data key="edge_modality">asserted</data></edge><edge id="oe_96d23c4130861a28" source="e_537e6ab50e8f2e44" target="e_d9b1236e8a068718"><data key="edge_predicate_raw">gain control over with</data><data key="edge_assertion_id">a_094e0eae180d408f</data><data key="edge_source_id">S50</data><data key="edge_source_url">https://www.first.org/cvss/v4.0/specification-document</data><data key="edge_chunk_id">S50_C20</data><data key="edge_json_path">None</data><data key="edge_evidence">Value Density describes the resources that the attacker will gain control over with a single exploitation event</data><data key="edge_extraction_method">minie</data><data key="edge_polarity">positive</data><data key="edge_modality">asserted</data></edge><edge id="oe_f7b35ec8bcfdc266" source="e_537e6ab50e8f2e44" target="e_ba719f9de4e00ae9"><data key="edge_predicate_raw">gain</data><data key="edge_assertion_id">a_9de81cf5d094c2d5</data><data key="edge_source_id">S50</data><data key="edge_source_url">https://www.first.org/cvss/v4.0/specification-document</data><data key="edge_chunk_id">S50_C20</data><data key="edge_json_path">None</data><data key="edge_evidence">Value Density describes the resources that the attacker will gain control over with a single exploitation event</data><data key="edge_extraction_method">minie</data><data key="edge_polarity">positive</data><data key="edge_modality">asserted</data></edge><edge id="oe_d5e44918572ac2e1" source="e_a2795c20852a50cd" target="e_c9e58d685e4a9f95"><data key="edge_predicate_raw">are direct responsibility of</data><data key="edge_assertion_id">a_caa076a93354189f</data><data key="edge_source_id">S50</data><data key="edge_source_url">https://www.first.org/cvss/v4.0/specification-document</data><data key="edge_chunk_id">S50_C21</data><data key="edge_json_path">None</data><data key="edge_evidence">Heuristically, such systems are often the direct responsibility of “system operators” rather than users</data><data key="edge_extraction_method">minie</data><data key="edge_polarity">positive</data><data key="edge_modality">asserted</data></edge><edge id="oe_badab63fb83744cf" source="e_a2795c20852a50cd" target="e_54cb474a80af0e69"><data key="edge_predicate_raw">are direct responsibility than</data><data key="edge_assertion_id">a_f824ac27784d958e</data><data key="edge_source_id">S50</data><data key="edge_source_url">https://www.first.org/cvss/v4.0/specification-document</data><data key="edge_chunk_id">S50_C21</data><data key="edge_json_path">None</data><data key="edge_evidence">Heuristically, such systems are often the direct responsibility of “system operators” rather than users</data><data key="edge_extraction_method">minie</data><data key="edge_polarity">positive</data><data key="edge_modality">asserted</data></edge><edge id="oe_8ff267e21199ec5d" source="e_f7f0082982beecc7" target="e_fd676437ab51b484"><data key="edge_predicate_raw">to provide</data><data key="edge_assertion_id">a_74cc442fc46ddd3a</data><data key="edge_source_id">S50</data><data key="edge_source_url">https://www.first.org/cvss/v4.0/specification-document</data><data key="edge_chunk_id">S50_C21</data><data key="edge_json_path">None</data><data key="edge_evidence">The intention of the Vulnerability Response Effort metric is to provide supplemental information on how difficult it is for consumers to provide an initial response to the impact of vulnerabilities for deployed products and services in their infrastructure</data><data key="edge_extraction_method">minie</data><data key="edge_polarity">positive</data><data key="edge_modality">asserted</data></edge><edge id="oe_1a1645ec4263d533" source="e_f7f0082982beecc7" target="e_fa83bcbab886e89f"><data key="edge_predicate_raw">to provide</data><data key="edge_assertion_id">a_5b7755d83264abb3</data><data key="edge_source_id">S50</data><data key="edge_source_url">https://www.first.org/cvss/v4.0/specification-document</data><data key="edge_chunk_id">S50_C21</data><data key="edge_json_path">None</data><data key="edge_evidence">The intention of the Vulnerability Response Effort metric is to provide supplemental information on how difficult it is for consumers to provide an initial response to the impact of vulnerabilities for deployed products and services in their infrastructure</data><data key="edge_extraction_method">minie</data><data key="edge_polarity">positive</data><data key="edge_modality">asserted</data></edge><edge id="oe_c33103a61adcb1d2" source="e_70973f0fc94d31c9" target="e_7f765772ac6c1cb7"><data key="edge_predicate_raw">be required into consideration when</data><data key="edge_assertion_id">a_8b404bd3336768ff</data><data key="edge_source_id">S50</data><data key="edge_source_url">https://www.first.org/cvss/v4.0/specification-document</data><data key="edge_chunk_id">S50_C21</data><data key="edge_json_path">None</data><data key="edge_evidence">The consumer can then take this additional information on effort required into consideration when applying mitigations and/or scheduling remediation</data><data key="edge_extraction_method">minie</data><data key="edge_polarity">positive</data><data key="edge_modality">possible</data></edge><edge id="oe_f48b39394244274f" source="e_70973f0fc94d31c9" target="e_301ab130bb3a8852"><data key="edge_predicate_raw">be required into consideration when</data><data key="edge_assertion_id">a_9883aad3607bba30</data><data key="edge_source_id">S50</data><data key="edge_source_url">https://www.first.org/cvss/v4.0/specification-document</data><data key="edge_chunk_id">S50_C21</data><data key="edge_json_path">None</data><data key="edge_evidence">The consumer can then take this additional information on effort required into consideration when applying mitigations and/or scheduling remediation</data><data key="edge_extraction_method">minie</data><data key="edge_polarity">positive</data><data key="edge_modality">possible</data></edge><edge id="oe_df2781848461b0e6" source="e_70973f0fc94d31c9" target="e_d93d3f2293801306"><data key="edge_predicate_raw">be required into</data><data key="edge_assertion_id">a_4959632157eb961e</data><data key="edge_source_id">S50</data><data key="edge_source_url">https://www.first.org/cvss/v4.0/specification-document</data><data key="edge_chunk_id">S50_C21</data><data key="edge_json_path">None</data><data key="edge_evidence">The consumer can then take this additional information on effort required into consideration when applying mitigations and/or scheduling remediation</data><data key="edge_extraction_method">minie</data><data key="edge_polarity">positive</data><data key="edge_modality">possible</data></edge><edge id="oe_cf9272c2150d7b89" source="e_a4d6f98a0fb303d3" target="e_0da99a133597d918"><data key="edge_predicate_raw">take additional information on effort required into</data><data key="edge_assertion_id">a_6b7ab659f2d23022</data><data key="edge_source_id">S50</data><data key="edge_source_url">https://www.first.org/cvss/v4.0/specification-document</data><data key="edge_chunk_id">S50_C21</data><data key="edge_json_path">None</data><data key="edge_evidence">The consumer can then take this additional information on effort required into consideration when applying mitigations and/or scheduling remediation</data><data key="edge_extraction_method">minie</data><data key="edge_polarity">positive</data><data key="edge_modality">possible</data></edge><edge id="oe_ba76ac73944a6ac4" source="e_a4d6f98a0fb303d3" target="e_ac1d0f6b26b25574"><data key="edge_predicate_raw">take additional information on effort required into</data><data key="edge_assertion_id">a_ca9f920d5537de92</data><data key="edge_source_id">S50</data><data key="edge_source_url">https://www.first.org/cvss/v4.0/specification-document</data><data key="edge_chunk_id">S50_C21</data><data key="edge_json_path">None</data><data key="edge_evidence">The consumer can then take this additional information on effort required into consideration when applying mitigations and/or scheduling remediation</data><data key="edge_extraction_method">minie</data><data key="edge_polarity">positive</data><data key="edge_modality">possible</data></edge><edge id="oe_61535f705fd67d5e" source="e_d5c915872f1063a4" target="e_1ff9ff52fcffcf3a"><data key="edge_predicate_raw">required</data><data key="edge_assertion_id">a_74f4ed24365dcc8b</data><data key="edge_source_id">S50</data><data key="edge_source_url">https://www.first.org/cvss/v4.0/specification-document</data><data key="edge_chunk_id">S50_C21</data><data key="edge_json_path">None</data><data key="edge_evidence">When calculating Vulnerability Response Effort, the effort required to deploy the quickest available response should be considered</data><data key="edge_extraction_method">heuristic</data><data key="edge_polarity">positive</data><data key="edge_modality">asserted</data></edge><edge id="oe_6c3a9875f58a17f6" source="e_23ea030c6b50d6f1" target="e_d7deb00ec419ff44"><data key="edge_predicate_raw">involves</data><data key="edge_assertion_id">a_89ee9f27239da5c5</data><data key="edge_source_id">S50</data><data key="edge_source_url">https://www.first.org/cvss/v4.0/specification-document</data><data key="edge_chunk_id">S50_C22</data><data key="edge_json_path">None</data><data key="edge_evidence">The only resolution to the vulnerability involves physical replacement (e.g. units deployed would have to be recalled for a depot level repair or replacement)</data><data key="edge_extraction_method">minie</data><data key="edge_polarity">positive</data><data key="edge_modality">asserted</data></edge><edge id="oe_2cba2fc509e6ebb2" source="e_47eab5f20c539cdb" target="e_ac4fee6dcc702b89"><data key="edge_predicate_raw">have to be recalled for</data><data key="edge_assertion_id">a_61f99f39994284c1</data><data key="edge_source_id">S50</data><data key="edge_source_url">https://www.first.org/cvss/v4.0/specification-document</data><data key="edge_chunk_id">S50_C22</data><data key="edge_json_path">None</data><data key="edge_evidence">The only resolution to the vulnerability involves physical replacement (e.g. units deployed would have to be recalled for a depot level repair or replacement)</data><data key="edge_extraction_method">minie</data><data key="edge_polarity">positive</data><data key="edge_modality">asserted</data></edge><edge id="oe_7cfcd66d4b71e910" source="e_47eab5f20c539cdb" target="e_524736485bb389af"><data key="edge_predicate_raw">have to be recalled for</data><data key="edge_assertion_id">a_4af8dac6f2f16a69</data><data key="edge_source_id">S50</data><data key="edge_source_url">https://www.first.org/cvss/v4.0/specification-document</data><data key="edge_chunk_id">S50_C22</data><data key="edge_json_path">None</data><data key="edge_evidence">The only resolution to the vulnerability involves physical replacement (e.g. units deployed would have to be recalled for a depot level repair or replacement)</data><data key="edge_extraction_method">minie</data><data key="edge_polarity">positive</data><data key="edge_modality">asserted</data></edge><edge id="oe_fe151382e4f71905" source="e_5ddf9ee4443e80dd" target="e_ace64742206fb24b"><data key="edge_predicate_raw">publishing</data><data key="edge_assertion_id">a_d252a678cbbc8bdc</data><data key="edge_source_id">S50</data><data key="edge_source_url">https://www.first.org/cvss/v4.0/specification-document</data><data key="edge_chunk_id">S50_C22</data><data key="edge_json_path">None</data><data key="edge_evidence">The use of these qualitative severity ratings is optional, and there is no requirement to include them when publishing CVSS scores</data><data key="edge_extraction_method">heuristic</data><data key="edge_polarity">negative</data><data key="edge_modality">asserted</data></edge><edge id="oe_f40d7e6b95c04ed6" source="e_290d8da624d84fb0" target="e_2e1496c46b0c67cc"><data key="edge_predicate_raw">help</data><data key="edge_assertion_id">a_2211c1215b9efe4e</data><data key="edge_source_id">S50</data><data key="edge_source_url">https://www.first.org/cvss/v4.0/specification-document</data><data key="edge_chunk_id">S50_C22</data><data key="edge_json_path">None</data><data key="edge_evidence">They are intended to help organizations properly assess and prioritize their vulnerability management processes</data><data key="edge_extraction_method">minie</data><data key="edge_polarity">positive</data><data key="edge_modality">asserted</data></edge><edge id="oe_bca6c30b99714661" source="e_290d8da624d84fb0" target="e_40e21c1bf87487d6"><data key="edge_predicate_raw">help</data><data key="edge_assertion_id">a_b7eb153ce241f478</data><data key="edge_source_id">S50</data><data key="edge_source_url">https://www.first.org/cvss/v4.0/specification-document</data><data key="edge_chunk_id">S50_C22</data><data key="edge_json_path">None</data><data key="edge_evidence">They are intended to help organizations properly assess and prioritize their vulnerability management processes</data><data key="edge_extraction_method">minie</data><data key="edge_polarity">positive</data><data key="edge_modality">asserted</data></edge><edge id="oe_e092d53b0d634a8c" source="e_ad16450d4d7b98f8" target="e_3871d9a29382ae85"><data key="edge_predicate_raw">is used to record CVSS metric information in</data><data key="edge_assertion_id">a_396f564b9d894e0b</data><data key="edge_source_id">S50</data><data key="edge_source_url">https://www.first.org/cvss/v4.0/specification-document</data><data key="edge_chunk_id">S50_C22</data><data key="edge_json_path">None</data><data key="edge_evidence">It is commonly used to record or transfer CVSS metric information in a concise and machine-readable form</data><data key="edge_extraction_method">minie</data><data key="edge_polarity">positive</data><data key="edge_modality">asserted</data></edge><edge id="oe_ed98e8e7667774d8" source="e_ad16450d4d7b98f8" target="e_c3091b917bf6c37c"><data key="edge_predicate_raw">is used to record CVSS metric information in</data><data key="edge_assertion_id">a_5022ded5f576f588</data><data key="edge_source_id">S50</data><data key="edge_source_url">https://www.first.org/cvss/v4.0/specification-document</data><data key="edge_chunk_id">S50_C22</data><data key="edge_json_path">None</data><data key="edge_evidence">It is commonly used to record or transfer CVSS metric information in a concise and machine-readable form</data><data key="edge_extraction_method">minie</data><data key="edge_polarity">positive</data><data key="edge_modality">asserted</data></edge><edge id="oe_97bed250d0a2b286" source="e_ad16450d4d7b98f8" target="e_11d9e0f2a7ae327b"><data key="edge_predicate_raw">is used to record</data><data key="edge_assertion_id">a_24041d413fab48b3</data><data key="edge_source_id">S50</data><data key="edge_source_url">https://www.first.org/cvss/v4.0/specification-document</data><data key="edge_chunk_id">S50_C22</data><data key="edge_json_path">None</data><data key="edge_evidence">It is commonly used to record or transfer CVSS metric information in a concise and machine-readable form</data><data key="edge_extraction_method">minie</data><data key="edge_polarity">positive</data><data key="edge_modality">asserted</data></edge><edge id="oe_9229babe3833f735" source="e_ad16450d4d7b98f8" target="e_69d96ed34aa1dab2"><data key="edge_predicate_raw">is used</data><data key="edge_assertion_id">a_58b88c4ecd3a2f02</data><data key="edge_source_id">S50</data><data key="edge_source_url">https://www.first.org/cvss/v4.0/specification-document</data><data key="edge_chunk_id">S50_C22</data><data key="edge_json_path">None</data><data key="edge_evidence">It is commonly used to record or transfer CVSS metric information in a concise and machine-readable form</data><data key="edge_extraction_method">minie</data><data key="edge_polarity">positive</data><data key="edge_modality">asserted</data></edge><edge id="oe_e129d6831cf206aa" source="e_ceef12725e7b8b39" target="e_6ab7b09e08984b56"><data key="edge_predicate_raw">follows in</data><data key="edge_assertion_id">a_c1f50b4deb70389f</data><data key="edge_source_id">S50</data><data key="edge_source_url">https://www.first.org/cvss/v4.0/specification-document</data><data key="edge_chunk_id">S50_C22</data><data key="edge_json_path">None</data><data key="edge_evidence">Metric information follows in the form of a set of metrics, each preceded by a forward slash, “/”, acting as a delimiter</data><data key="edge_extraction_method">minie</data><data key="edge_polarity">positive</data><data key="edge_modality">asserted</data></edge><edge id="oe_1585dcfe3be3612c" source="e_3194ef0752b4dc4c" target="e_84e82b5a59c3f406"><data key="edge_predicate_raw">has associated metric value in</data><data key="edge_assertion_id">a_e4f67125589227c1</data><data key="edge_source_id">S50</data><data key="edge_source_url">https://www.first.org/cvss/v4.0/specification-document</data><data key="edge_chunk_id">S50_C22</data><data key="edge_json_path">None</data><data key="edge_evidence">Each metric is a metric name in abbreviated form, a colon (“:”), and its associated metric value in abbreviated form</data><data key="edge_extraction_method">minie</data><data key="edge_polarity">positive</data><data key="edge_modality">asserted</data></edge><edge id="oe_93fec82945d85930" source="e_9e8758f7636f5ca5" target="e_1132648fd32b5522"><data key="edge_predicate_raw">are defined earlier in</data><data key="edge_assertion_id">a_dc1cc336dacbe2e7</data><data key="edge_source_id">S50</data><data key="edge_source_url">https://www.first.org/cvss/v4.0/specification-document</data><data key="edge_chunk_id">S50_C22</data><data key="edge_json_path">None</data><data key="edge_evidence">The abbreviated forms are defined earlier in this specification (in parentheses after each metric name and metric value, case sensitive), and are summarized in the table below</data><data key="edge_extraction_method">minie</data><data key="edge_polarity">positive</data><data key="edge_modality">asserted</data></edge><edge id="oe_913d3c7441987fbb" source="e_9e8758f7636f5ca5" target="e_534c943c598a31b3"><data key="edge_predicate_raw">are defined</data><data key="edge_assertion_id">a_4b6308422efdc0d9</data><data key="edge_source_id">S50</data><data key="edge_source_url">https://www.first.org/cvss/v4.0/specification-document</data><data key="edge_chunk_id">S50_C22</data><data key="edge_json_path">None</data><data key="edge_evidence">The abbreviated forms are defined earlier in this specification (in parentheses after each metric name and metric value, case sensitive), and are summarized in the table below</data><data key="edge_extraction_method">minie</data><data key="edge_polarity">positive</data><data key="edge_modality">asserted</data></edge><edge id="oe_58e49d296838f8ef" source="e_075097bc32ffa89f" target="e_afccd7a4fc5871a9"><data key="edge_predicate_raw">are considered to have value of</data><data key="edge_assertion_id">a_4cd9ecef4a3f2bfd</data><data key="edge_source_id">S50</data><data key="edge_source_url">https://www.first.org/cvss/v4.0/specification-document</data><data key="edge_chunk_id">S50_C23</data><data key="edge_json_path">None</data><data key="edge_evidence">Threat, Environmental, and Supplemental metrics are optional, and omitted metrics are considered to have the value of Not Defined (X)</data><data key="edge_extraction_method">minie</data><data key="edge_polarity">negative</data><data key="edge_modality">asserted</data></edge><edge id="oe_112cb932feb9809f" source="e_8c5bdfed19c88e1e" target="e_97d5b9fcbb9ac78b"><data key="edge_predicate_raw">be included in</data><data key="edge_assertion_id">a_14cd379067b847bf</data><data key="edge_source_id">S50</data><data key="edge_source_url">https://www.first.org/cvss/v4.0/specification-document</data><data key="edge_chunk_id">S50_C23</data><data key="edge_json_path">None</data><data key="edge_evidence">Metrics with a value of Not Defined can be explicitly included in a vector string if desired</data><data key="edge_extraction_method">minie</data><data key="edge_polarity">negative</data><data key="edge_modality">possible</data></edge><edge id="oe_493afc544024eb9d" source="e_8c5bdfed19c88e1e" target="e_5480893a3a1bed54"><data key="edge_predicate_raw">be included in vector string if</data><data key="edge_assertion_id">a_8c4f703ad6e55694</data><data key="edge_source_id">S50</data><data key="edge_source_url">https://www.first.org/cvss/v4.0/specification-document</data><data key="edge_chunk_id">S50_C23</data><data key="edge_json_path">None</data><data key="edge_evidence">Metrics with a value of Not Defined can be explicitly included in a vector string if desired</data><data key="edge_extraction_method">minie</data><data key="edge_polarity">negative</data><data key="edge_modality">possible</data></edge><edge id="oe_285688e5eaaba3f6" source="e_97d5b9fcbb9ac78b" target="e_942533ab55bfaf74"><data key="edge_predicate_raw">include same metric more than</data><data key="edge_assertion_id">a_def3c0a3d3c01fa4</data><data key="edge_source_id">S50</data><data key="edge_source_url">https://www.first.org/cvss/v4.0/specification-document</data><data key="edge_chunk_id">S50_C23</data><data key="edge_json_path">None</data><data key="edge_evidence">A vector string must not include the same metric more than once</data><data key="edge_extraction_method">minie</data><data key="edge_polarity">negative</data><data key="edge_modality">asserted</data></edge><edge id="oe_a681677396a7da10" source="e_e75f2414678a9f10" target="e_c4864c06dd486dbc"><data key="edge_predicate_raw">produce</data><data key="edge_assertion_id">a_84045182a1994c08</data><data key="edge_source_id">S50</data><data key="edge_source_url">https://www.first.org/cvss/v4.0/specification-document</data><data key="edge_chunk_id">S50_C24</data><data key="edge_json_path">None</data><data key="edge_evidence">and no specified Threat or Environmental metrics would produce the following vector:</data><data key="edge_extraction_method">minie</data><data key="edge_polarity">negative</data><data key="edge_modality">asserted</data></edge><edge id="oe_095816d70fec2561" source="e_8ba068c252e9939e" target="e_c4864c06dd486dbc"><data key="edge_predicate_raw">produce</data><data key="edge_assertion_id">a_03f1a68aedcd8159</data><data key="edge_source_id">S50</data><data key="edge_source_url">https://www.first.org/cvss/v4.0/specification-document</data><data key="edge_chunk_id">S50_C24</data><data key="edge_json_path">None</data><data key="edge_evidence">and no specified Threat or Environmental metrics would produce the following vector:</data><data key="edge_extraction_method">minie</data><data key="edge_polarity">negative</data><data key="edge_modality">asserted</data></edge><edge id="oe_6901a801d3a4cbdf" source="e_624143ab76175e34" target="e_c4864c06dd486dbc"><data key="edge_predicate_raw">produce</data><data key="edge_assertion_id">a_e1e45c1fd221709c</data><data key="edge_source_id">S50</data><data key="edge_source_url">https://www.first.org/cvss/v4.0/specification-document</data><data key="edge_chunk_id">S50_C24</data><data key="edge_json_path">None</data><data key="edge_evidence">The same example with the addition of Exploit Maturity: Attacked would produce the following vector:</data><data key="edge_extraction_method">minie</data><data key="edge_polarity">positive</data><data key="edge_modality">asserted</data></edge><edge id="oe_ecc82e8b03ac0053" source="e_ba98b64a1f19b637" target="e_930e4ac4ed729c4b"><data key="edge_predicate_raw">are provided along</data><data key="edge_assertion_id">a_848b1a45b9c67aab</data><data key="edge_source_id">S50</data><data key="edge_source_url">https://www.first.org/cvss/v4.0/specification-document</data><data key="edge_chunk_id">S50_C24</data><data key="edge_json_path">None</data><data key="edge_evidence">The following vectors are invalid and are provided along a short explanation:</data><data key="edge_extraction_method">minie</data><data key="edge_polarity">positive</data><data key="edge_modality">asserted</data></edge><edge id="oe_828dd68c7a12e932" source="e_d1a2cdb8457da1b4" target="e_942533ab55bfaf74"><data key="edge_predicate_raw">is defined more than</data><data key="edge_assertion_id">a_be04ab411bbd3cd0</data><data key="edge_source_id">S50</data><data key="edge_source_url">https://www.first.org/cvss/v4.0/specification-document</data><data key="edge_chunk_id">S50_C24</data><data key="edge_json_path">None</data><data key="edge_evidence">“E” metric is defined more than once</data><data key="edge_extraction_method">minie</data><data key="edge_polarity">positive</data><data key="edge_modality">asserted</data></edge><edge id="oe_861e7c92e6712f98" source="e_9c9b729429186233" target="e_835cd7b766648fa2"><data key="edge_predicate_raw">be calculate order of vectors from</data><data key="edge_assertion_id">a_3494d83edcc68d50</data><data key="edge_source_id">S50</data><data key="edge_source_url">https://www.first.org/cvss/v4.0/specification-document</data><data key="edge_chunk_id">S50_C24</data><data key="edge_json_path">None</data><data key="edge_evidence">Use the expert comparison data to calculate an order of vectors from least severe to most severe</data><data key="edge_extraction_method">minie</data><data key="edge_polarity">positive</data><data key="edge_modality">asserted</data></edge><edge id="oe_73eb5481e9107f97" source="e_5f88e862f178ae99" target="e_e7e4cc3411114886"><data key="edge_predicate_raw">represents boundary between qualitative severity scores to be</data><data key="edge_assertion_id">a_18d9e22138d6dc8c</data><data key="edge_source_id">S50</data><data key="edge_source_url">https://www.first.org/cvss/v4.0/specification-document</data><data key="edge_chunk_id">S50_C24</data><data key="edge_json_path">None</data><data key="edge_evidence">Solicit expert opinion to decide which equivalence set of vectors p in the ordering of vectors represents the boundary between qualitative severity scores to be backwards compatible with qualitative severity score boundaries from CVSS v3.x</data><data key="edge_extraction_method">minie</data><data key="edge_polarity">positive</data><data key="edge_modality">asserted</data></edge><edge id="oe_8c3661fc9df52e2c" source="e_5f88e862f178ae99" target="e_81f749c9c181f2c3"><data key="edge_predicate_raw">represents boundary between qualitative severity scores to be</data><data key="edge_assertion_id">a_05c8772d759405a1</data><data key="edge_source_id">S50</data><data key="edge_source_url">https://www.first.org/cvss/v4.0/specification-document</data><data key="edge_chunk_id">S50_C24</data><data key="edge_json_path">None</data><data key="edge_evidence">Solicit expert opinion to decide which equivalence set of vectors p in the ordering of vectors represents the boundary between qualitative severity scores to be backwards compatible with qualitative severity score boundaries from CVSS v3.x</data><data key="edge_extraction_method">minie</data><data key="edge_polarity">positive</data><data key="edge_modality">asserted</data></edge><edge id="oe_218c943605a75d22" source="e_5f88e862f178ae99" target="e_1276ee29f118b2a1"><data key="edge_predicate_raw">represents boundary between qualitative severity scores to be</data><data key="edge_assertion_id">a_6ca519b7734c5549</data><data key="edge_source_id">S50</data><data key="edge_source_url">https://www.first.org/cvss/v4.0/specification-document</data><data key="edge_chunk_id">S50_C24</data><data key="edge_json_path">None</data><data key="edge_evidence">Solicit expert opinion to decide which equivalence set of vectors p in the ordering of vectors represents the boundary between qualitative severity scores to be backwards compatible with qualitative severity score boundaries from CVSS v3.x</data><data key="edge_extraction_method">minie</data><data key="edge_polarity">positive</data><data key="edge_modality">asserted</data></edge><edge id="oe_253aff6541ca2bbd" source="e_bfaf17725bfcbe42" target="e_b52de94b00055efe"><data key="edge_predicate_raw">adjusts scores of vectors within qualitatively equivalent set of</data><data key="edge_assertion_id">a_a7315629c4a616e9</data><data key="edge_source_id">S50</data><data key="edge_source_url">https://www.first.org/cvss/v4.0/specification-document</data><data key="edge_chunk_id">S50_C24</data><data key="edge_json_path">None</data><data key="edge_evidence">Create a small score modification factor that adjusts the scores of vectors within a qualitatively equivalent set of vectors so that a change of any metric value results in a resulting score change, where possible</data><data key="edge_extraction_method">minie</data><data key="edge_polarity">positive</data><data key="edge_modality">possible</data></edge><edge id="oe_3172acb396c6e8cb" source="e_bfaf17725bfcbe42" target="e_b52de94b00055efe"><data key="edge_predicate_raw">adjusts scores of</data><data key="edge_assertion_id">a_9aecaeb373d3e386</data><data key="edge_source_id">S50</data><data key="edge_source_url">https://www.first.org/cvss/v4.0/specification-document</data><data key="edge_chunk_id">S50_C24</data><data key="edge_json_path">None</data><data key="edge_evidence">Create a small score modification factor that adjusts the scores of vectors within a qualitatively equivalent set of vectors so that a change of any metric value results in a resulting score change, where possible</data><data key="edge_extraction_method">minie</data><data key="edge_polarity">positive</data><data key="edge_modality">possible</data></edge><edge id="oe_83eaa6ee6f8d28e5" source="e_9bdb10fbcabccec2" target="e_4909cad877ba4cb8"><data key="edge_predicate_raw">is larger than</data><data key="edge_assertion_id">a_e15fd416cff6f51b</data><data key="edge_source_id">S50</data><data key="edge_source_url">https://www.first.org/cvss/v4.0/specification-document</data><data key="edge_chunk_id">S50_C24</data><data key="edge_json_path">None</data><data key="edge_evidence">The intent is that the score change is not larger than the uncertainty in the ranking of the vector groups as collected from the expert comparison data in step 2</data><data key="edge_extraction_method">minie</data><data key="edge_polarity">negative</data><data key="edge_modality">asserted</data></edge><edge id="oe_bba3c7f9de4bdd3c" source="e_87304ba0c995dfd8" target="e_a1855c7c1104c724"><data key="edge_predicate_raw">provides</data><data key="edge_assertion_id">a_0e9ffb9ec87073c6</data><data key="edge_source_id">S50</data><data key="edge_source_url">https://www.first.org/cvss/v4.0/specification-document</data><data key="edge_chunk_id">S50_C25</data><data key="edge_json_path">None</data><data key="edge_evidence">The CVSS v4.0 formula provides a mathematical approximation of all possible metric combinations ranked in order of severity where vectors are clustered in sets called MacroVectors</data><data key="edge_extraction_method">heuristic</data><data key="edge_polarity">positive</data><data key="edge_modality">possible</data></edge><edge id="oe_4409c3f5f1a83c13" source="e_db2d7cefcd44a623" target="e_487f2d8360640345"><data key="edge_predicate_raw">is defined by</data><data key="edge_assertion_id">a_0e4fe178007e840a</data><data key="edge_source_id">S50</data><data key="edge_source_url">https://www.first.org/cvss/v4.0/specification-document</data><data key="edge_chunk_id">S50_C25</data><data key="edge_json_path">None</data><data key="edge_evidence">The score of a MacroVector is defined by a lookup table as defined by the subject matter expert process mentioned above and is specified in Section 8.3</data><data key="edge_extraction_method">minie</data><data key="edge_polarity">positive</data><data key="edge_modality">asserted</data></edge><edge id="oe_54e14aa520ffa544" source="e_3c6f55c088fab9eb" target="e_b61076f91213a657"><data key="edge_predicate_raw">determined following preliminary metrics subgroups</data><data key="edge_assertion_id">a_c68f8797d9e68c67</data><data key="edge_source_id">S50</data><data key="edge_source_url">https://www.first.org/cvss/v4.0/specification-document</data><data key="edge_chunk_id">S50_C25</data><data key="edge_json_path">None</data><data key="edge_evidence">To determine a preliminary set of relevant MacroVectors, The SIG determined the following preliminary metrics subgroups</data><data key="edge_extraction_method">minie</data><data key="edge_polarity">positive</data><data key="edge_modality">asserted</data></edge><edge id="oe_bf541b23fb0fdcf5" source="e_9c20693240fd4aec" target="e_8cd932ab3b8bee55"><data key="edge_predicate_raw">be determined for</data><data key="edge_assertion_id">a_c231a0b3e7543c0f</data><data key="edge_source_id">S50</data><data key="edge_source_url">https://www.first.org/cvss/v4.0/specification-document</data><data key="edge_chunk_id">S50_C25</data><data key="edge_json_path">None</data><data key="edge_evidence">Additional EQs or levels can be determined for a finer resolution</data><data key="edge_extraction_method">minie</data><data key="edge_polarity">positive</data><data key="edge_modality">possible</data></edge><edge id="oe_76969fe3e987cad2" source="e_85f16cdced276a7c" target="e_8cd932ab3b8bee55"><data key="edge_predicate_raw">be determined for</data><data key="edge_assertion_id">a_0f23e3643bdc9fef</data><data key="edge_source_id">S50</data><data key="edge_source_url">https://www.first.org/cvss/v4.0/specification-document</data><data key="edge_chunk_id">S50_C25</data><data key="edge_json_path">None</data><data key="edge_evidence">Additional EQs or levels can be determined for a finer resolution</data><data key="edge_extraction_method">minie</data><data key="edge_polarity">positive</data><data key="edge_modality">possible</data></edge><edge id="oe_8b3f2c2e400a6781" source="e_290d8da624d84fb0" target="e_31a170fd27f47b65"><data key="edge_predicate_raw">be considered Since</data><data key="edge_assertion_id">a_567c995344c5e45f</data><data key="edge_source_id">S50</data><data key="edge_source_url">https://www.first.org/cvss/v4.0/specification-document</data><data key="edge_chunk_id">S50_C25</data><data key="edge_json_path">None</data><data key="edge_evidence">Since EQ3 and EQ6 are not independent they must be considered together</data><data key="edge_extraction_method">minie</data><data key="edge_polarity">negative</data><data key="edge_modality">asserted</data></edge><edge id="oe_7025a7a153304b55" source="e_290d8da624d84fb0" target="e_e376508129b912c3"><data key="edge_predicate_raw">be considered</data><data key="edge_assertion_id">a_fba25b2bf6294211</data><data key="edge_source_id">S50</data><data key="edge_source_url">https://www.first.org/cvss/v4.0/specification-document</data><data key="edge_chunk_id">S50_C25</data><data key="edge_json_path">None</data><data key="edge_evidence">Since EQ3 and EQ6 are not independent they must be considered together</data><data key="edge_extraction_method">minie</data><data key="edge_polarity">negative</data><data key="edge_modality">asserted</data></edge><edge id="oe_4d2893ab518ccd28" source="e_894b4c64e481e401" target="e_1e1f53c63d70d46a"><data key="edge_predicate_raw">is determined in</data><data key="edge_assertion_id">a_130be3af661afb73</data><data key="edge_source_id">S50</data><data key="edge_source_url">https://www.first.org/cvss/v4.0/specification-document</data><data key="edge_chunk_id">S50_C25</data><data key="edge_json_path">None</data><data key="edge_evidence">The lowest severity vector of a MacroVector is determined in a similar way</data><data key="edge_extraction_method">minie</data><data key="edge_polarity">positive</data><data key="edge_modality">asserted</data></edge><edge id="oe_9f337b7de204725a" source="e_43ffce3506ce7430" target="e_f244b68cb5567ebc"><data key="edge_predicate_raw">satisfy</data><data key="edge_assertion_id">a_2cc8e2a2481bddd7</data><data key="edge_source_id">S50</data><data key="edge_source_url">https://www.first.org/cvss/v4.0/specification-document</data><data key="edge_chunk_id">S50_C25</data><data key="edge_json_path">None</data><data key="edge_evidence">For example the MacroVectors which satisfy EQ1 at level 1 shown in Table 24 have as highest severity vectors all vectors with</data><data key="edge_extraction_method">minie</data><data key="edge_polarity">positive</data><data key="edge_modality">asserted</data></edge><edge id="oe_b4cf6e6c9e30ad06" source="e_c8f717f0d3936747" target="e_2690d2241b8551ec"><data key="edge_predicate_raw">default to</data><data key="edge_assertion_id">a_c04610c35b0609d9</data><data key="edge_source_id">S50</data><data key="edge_source_url">https://www.first.org/cvss/v4.0/specification-document</data><data key="edge_chunk_id">S50_C26</data><data key="edge_json_path">None</data><data key="edge_evidence">If E=X it will default to the worst case (i.e., E=A)</data><data key="edge_extraction_method">minie</data><data key="edge_polarity">positive</data><data key="edge_modality">asserted</data></edge><edge id="oe_47457a1b24aa253c" source="e_b6432506bf460085" target="e_d93ce20529fd6f28"><data key="edge_predicate_raw">contains</data><data key="edge_assertion_id">a_7f409676d5723b8b</data><data key="edge_source_id">S50</data><data key="edge_source_url">https://www.first.org/cvss/v4.0/specification-document</data><data key="edge_chunk_id">S50_C27</data><data key="edge_json_path">None</data><data key="edge_evidence">For example a Vector with VC:H/VI:H/VA:H has a severity distance of 3 from a vector that contains VC:H/VI:L/VA:N and is otherwise identical</data><data key="edge_extraction_method">minie</data><data key="edge_polarity">positive</data><data key="edge_modality">asserted</data></edge><edge id="oe_c992f3e85b0affe0" source="e_1db4f07f48300a97" target="e_9d702092532e5aae"><data key="edge_predicate_raw">is maximum severity distance between highest severity vector and lowest severity vector of</data><data key="edge_assertion_id">a_25d517c2d26cadc3</data><data key="edge_source_id">S50</data><data key="edge_source_url">https://www.first.org/cvss/v4.0/specification-document</data><data key="edge_chunk_id">S50_C27</data><data key="edge_json_path">None</data><data key="edge_evidence">The depth of a MacroVector is the maximum severity distance between the highest severity vector(s) and the lowest severity vector(s) of the MacroVector</data><data key="edge_extraction_method">minie</data><data key="edge_polarity">positive</data><data key="edge_modality">asserted</data></edge><edge id="oe_57d4df25ca5f987a" source="e_60df10c29cc61ee5" target="e_ff79bfdd10f203bb"><data key="edge_predicate_raw">be understood by</data><data key="edge_assertion_id">a_95bb1c6debab3c9c</data><data key="edge_source_id">S50</data><data key="edge_source_url">https://www.first.org/cvss/v4.0/specification-document</data><data key="edge_chunk_id">S50_C27</data><data key="edge_json_path">None</data><data key="edge_evidence">The notion of depth can be better understood by a graphical visualization</data><data key="edge_extraction_method">minie</data><data key="edge_polarity">positive</data><data key="edge_modality">possible</data></edge><edge id="oe_cccc716f58eb5149" source="e_c0ce3e1fa2075260" target="e_9d702092532e5aae"><data key="edge_predicate_raw">is assigned score of</data><data key="edge_assertion_id">a_a716aae400fc58f9</data><data key="edge_source_id">S50</data><data key="edge_source_url">https://www.first.org/cvss/v4.0/specification-document</data><data key="edge_chunk_id">S50_C27</data><data key="edge_json_path">None</data><data key="edge_evidence">The highest severity vector of a MacroVector is always assigned the score of the MacroVector from the cvss_lookup.js file within the CVSS v4.0 calculator reference implementation available on GitHub (see Section 8.3)</data><data key="edge_extraction_method">minie</data><data key="edge_polarity">positive</data><data key="edge_modality">asserted</data></edge><edge id="oe_6452b42d91ca66ab" source="e_c0ce3e1fa2075260" target="e_3bfabacd58fbea1f"><data key="edge_predicate_raw">is assigned score of MacroVector from</data><data key="edge_assertion_id">a_fb3b32c9cecdce8e</data><data key="edge_source_id">S50</data><data key="edge_source_url">https://www.first.org/cvss/v4.0/specification-document</data><data key="edge_chunk_id">S50_C27</data><data key="edge_json_path">None</data><data key="edge_evidence">The highest severity vector of a MacroVector is always assigned the score of the MacroVector from the cvss_lookup.js file within the CVSS v4.0 calculator reference implementation available on GitHub (see Section 8.3)</data><data key="edge_extraction_method">minie</data><data key="edge_polarity">positive</data><data key="edge_modality">asserted</data></edge><edge id="oe_b32e06bed694764e" source="e_7804ea78a2dd85ac" target="e_6f24582c11bc5129"><data key="edge_predicate_raw">is assigned</data><data key="edge_assertion_id">a_549e19b0a369fe61</data><data key="edge_source_id">S50</data><data key="edge_source_url">https://www.first.org/cvss/v4.0/specification-document</data><data key="edge_chunk_id">S50_C27</data><data key="edge_json_path">None</data><data key="edge_evidence">A vector within a MacroVector is assigned the score of the highest severity vector in the MacroVector minus the mean proportional distance from the MacroVectors below it</data><data key="edge_extraction_method">minie</data><data key="edge_polarity">positive</data><data key="edge_modality">asserted</data></edge><edge id="oe_3c6d54259de8eab1" source="e_7804ea78a2dd85ac" target="e_598bc482aa88ac26"><data key="edge_predicate_raw">is assigned</data><data key="edge_assertion_id">a_81e7015d943993ff</data><data key="edge_source_id">S50</data><data key="edge_source_url">https://www.first.org/cvss/v4.0/specification-document</data><data key="edge_chunk_id">S50_C27</data><data key="edge_json_path">None</data><data key="edge_evidence">A vector within a MacroVector is assigned the score of the highest severity vector in the MacroVector minus the mean proportional distance from the MacroVectors below it</data><data key="edge_extraction_method">minie</data><data key="edge_polarity">positive</data><data key="edge_modality">asserted</data></edge><edge id="oe_9e6991779fd0a929" source="e_e163460c91338b08" target="e_5d30834cf9dabcd9"><data key="edge_predicate_raw">is obtained by</data><data key="edge_assertion_id">a_2f191c7c28a59700</data><data key="edge_source_id">S50</data><data key="edge_source_url">https://www.first.org/cvss/v4.0/specification-document</data><data key="edge_chunk_id">S50_C27</data><data key="edge_json_path">None</data><data key="edge_evidence">This is obtained by the following algorithm</data><data key="edge_extraction_method">minie</data><data key="edge_polarity">positive</data><data key="edge_modality">asserted</data></edge><edge id="oe_502dcc7e35324d9a" source="e_aea8700531f30f00" target="e_3366d0c8a6934f09"><data key="edge_predicate_raw">is determined as difference between</data><data key="edge_assertion_id">a_e4beec192b04b2a7</data><data key="edge_source_id">S50</data><data key="edge_source_url">https://www.first.org/cvss/v4.0/specification-document</data><data key="edge_chunk_id">S50_C27</data><data key="edge_json_path">None</data><data key="edge_evidence">The maximal scoring difference is determined as the difference between the current MacroVector and the lower MacroVector</data><data key="edge_extraction_method">minie</data><data key="edge_polarity">positive</data><data key="edge_modality">asserted</data></edge><edge id="oe_0bb9d40b397301a8" source="e_5ad2f2ffe7c97896" target="e_b8800f698321cdcb"><data key="edge_predicate_raw">is determined by</data><data key="edge_assertion_id">a_6957d0429bfcf77d</data><data key="edge_source_id">S50</data><data key="edge_source_url">https://www.first.org/cvss/v4.0/specification-document</data><data key="edge_chunk_id">S50_C27</data><data key="edge_json_path">None</data><data key="edge_evidence">The proportion of the distance is determined by dividing the severity distance of the to-be-scored vector by the depth of the MacroVector</data><data key="edge_extraction_method">minie</data><data key="edge_polarity">positive</data><data key="edge_modality">asserted</data></edge><edge id="oe_e68ad623698059e7" source="e_aea8700531f30f00" target="e_43db8c6b67ae0647"><data key="edge_predicate_raw">is multiplied by proportion of</data><data key="edge_assertion_id">a_da7b8e27f541237c</data><data key="edge_source_id">S50</data><data key="edge_source_url">https://www.first.org/cvss/v4.0/specification-document</data><data key="edge_chunk_id">S50_C27</data><data key="edge_json_path">None</data><data key="edge_evidence">The maximal scoring difference is multiplied by the proportion of distance</data><data key="edge_extraction_method">minie</data><data key="edge_polarity">positive</data><data key="edge_modality">asserted</data></edge><edge id="oe_dfd3979e8b5a8813" source="e_401168aab527b720" target="e_6332c5e3343e7bc8"><data key="edge_predicate_raw">is score of MacroVector i.e. score of</data><data key="edge_assertion_id">a_11173e9118c5023d</data><data key="edge_source_id">S50</data><data key="edge_source_url">https://www.first.org/cvss/v4.0/specification-document</data><data key="edge_chunk_id">S50_C27</data><data key="edge_json_path">None</data><data key="edge_evidence">The score of the vector is the score of the MacroVector (i.e. the score of the highest severity vector) minus the mean distance so computed</data><data key="edge_extraction_method">minie</data><data key="edge_polarity">positive</data><data key="edge_modality">asserted</data></edge><edge id="oe_f6ad44842ab4cb9f" source="e_401168aab527b720" target="e_e11b4ac40800bc7d"><data key="edge_predicate_raw">is score of</data><data key="edge_assertion_id">a_64e9a4bb581883a8</data><data key="edge_source_id">S50</data><data key="edge_source_url">https://www.first.org/cvss/v4.0/specification-document</data><data key="edge_chunk_id">S50_C27</data><data key="edge_json_path">None</data><data key="edge_evidence">The score of the vector is the score of the MacroVector (i.e. the score of the highest severity vector) minus the mean distance so computed</data><data key="edge_extraction_method">minie</data><data key="edge_polarity">positive</data><data key="edge_modality">asserted</data></edge><edge id="oe_fdd21eb424b3b4d8" source="e_877691bf2b1a5cb6" target="e_3bfabacd58fbea1f"><data key="edge_predicate_raw">be found in</data><data key="edge_assertion_id">a_1a2e24953462c518</data><data key="edge_source_id">S50</data><data key="edge_source_url">https://www.first.org/cvss/v4.0/specification-document</data><data key="edge_chunk_id">S50_C27</data><data key="edge_json_path">None</data><data key="edge_evidence">A complete list of all MacroVectors and associated scores can be found in the cvss_lookup.js file within the CVSS v4.0 calculator reference implementation available on GitHub:</data><data key="edge_extraction_method">minie</data><data key="edge_polarity">positive</data><data key="edge_modality">possible</data></edge><edge id="oe_86763fa547b92585" source="e_29f374d3ae492bbc" target="e_c723ab0906f292c2"><data key="edge_predicate_raw">recognizes</data><data key="edge_assertion_id">a_74106c87b7149e34</data><data key="edge_source_id">S50</data><data key="edge_source_url">https://www.first.org/cvss/v4.0/specification-document</data><data key="edge_chunk_id">S50_C27</data><data key="edge_json_path">None</data><data key="edge_evidence">FIRST sincerely recognizes the contributions of the following CVSS Special Interest Group (SIG) members, listed in alphabet