y compressed in the definition of “high” complexity</data><data key="edge_extraction_method">minie</data><data key="edge_polarity">negative</data><data key="edge_modality">asserted</data></edge><edge id="oe_c382b3e7fc7557ec" source="e_b1d0bba94bd2b15a" target="e_5cdaf25141e0f4a9"><data key="edge_predicate_raw">do reflect</data><data key="edge_assertion_id">a_056a55e846d66f7c</data><data key="edge_source_id">S51</data><data key="edge_source_url">https://www.first.org/cvss/v4.0/user-guide</data><data key="edge_chunk_id">S51_C03</data><data key="edge_json_path">None</data><data key="edge_evidence">In CVSS v3.1, the “low” and “high” Attack Complexity (AC) values do not reflect the significant differences between conditions currently compressed in the definition of “high” complexity</data><data key="edge_extraction_method">minie</data><data key="edge_polarity">negative</data><data key="edge_modality">asserted</data></edge><edge id="oe_31ff72272c73a83f" source="e_92078ff0ec595868" target="e_8aa85f1a9d8ff84a"><data key="edge_predicate_raw">be compressed in definition of</data><data key="edge_assertion_id">a_6afbf4e3160f51d3</data><data key="edge_source_id">S51</data><data key="edge_source_url">https://www.first.org/cvss/v4.0/user-guide</data><data key="edge_chunk_id">S51_C03</data><data key="edge_json_path">None</data><data key="edge_evidence">In CVSS v3.1, the “low” and “high” Attack Complexity (AC) values do not reflect the significant differences between conditions currently compressed in the definition of “high” complexity</data><data key="edge_extraction_method">minie</data><data key="edge_polarity">negative</data><data key="edge_modality">asserted</data></edge><edge id="oe_b33cd4952484747f" source="e_92078ff0ec595868" target="e_2773b32753cf9830"><data key="edge_predicate_raw">be compressed</data><data key="edge_assertion_id">a_00b94b98fd39bd6e</data><data key="edge_source_id">S51</data><data key="edge_source_url">https://www.first.org/cvss/v4.0/user-guide</data><data key="edge_chunk_id">S51_C03</data><data key="edge_json_path">None</data><data key="edge_evidence">In CVSS v3.1, the “low” and “high” Attack Complexity (AC) values do not reflect the significant differences between conditions currently compressed in the definition of “high” complexity</data><data key="edge_extraction_method">minie</data><data key="edge_polarity">negative</data><data key="edge_modality">asserted</data></edge><edge id="oe_0be180526a1abec3" source="e_3b9e06e9595c32e3" target="e_5ad6c123e5abaf11"><data key="edge_predicate_raw">require higher For</data><data key="edge_assertion_id">a_d6ef3af5681d72c1</data><data key="edge_source_id">S51</data><data key="edge_source_url">https://www.first.org/cvss/v4.0/user-guide</data><data key="edge_chunk_id">S51_C03</data><data key="edge_json_path">None</data><data key="edge_evidence">For example, the evasion of security mitigation techniques such as ASLR or crypto objectively require significantly higher exploit complexity than iterating an attack to win a race condition; yet both conditions currently result in the same “penalty” to the final severity score</data><data key="edge_extraction_method">minie</data><data key="edge_polarity">positive</data><data key="edge_modality">asserted</data></edge><edge id="oe_b9a27e3e2016fce7" source="e_92361880d43db116" target="e_5ad6c123e5abaf11"><data key="edge_predicate_raw">require higher For</data><data key="edge_assertion_id">a_910ed112f5a5122b</data><data key="edge_source_id">S51</data><data key="edge_source_url">https://www.first.org/cvss/v4.0/user-guide</data><data key="edge_chunk_id">S51_C03</data><data key="edge_json_path">None</data><data key="edge_evidence">For example, the evasion of security mitigation techniques such as ASLR or crypto objectively require significantly higher exploit complexity than iterating an attack to win a race condition; yet both conditions currently result in the same “penalty” to the final severity score</data><data key="edge_extraction_method">minie</data><data key="edge_polarity">positive</data><data key="edge_modality">asserted</data></edge><edge id="oe_5dbe6b63614d59b1" source="e_3b9e06e9595c32e3" target="e_b3995f1a6399589d"><data key="edge_predicate_raw">require</data><data key="edge_assertion_id">a_84a7088bf7eeb74c</data><data key="edge_source_id">S51</data><data key="edge_source_url">https://www.first.org/cvss/v4.0/user-guide</data><data key="edge_chunk_id">S51_C03</data><data key="edge_json_path">None</data><data key="edge_evidence">For example, the evasion of security mitigation techniques such as ASLR or crypto objectively require significantly higher exploit complexity than iterating an attack to win a race condition; yet both conditions currently result in the same “penalty” to the final severity score</data><data key="edge_extraction_method">minie</data><data key="edge_polarity">positive</data><data key="edge_modality">asserted</data></edge><edge id="oe_c3fce8b257bb26e8" source="e_92361880d43db116" target="e_b3995f1a6399589d"><data key="edge_predicate_raw">require</data><data key="edge_assertion_id">a_cae54ec6fe7eea28</data><data key="edge_source_id">S51</data><data key="edge_source_url">https://www.first.org/cvss/v4.0/user-guide</data><data key="edge_chunk_id">S51_C03</data><data key="edge_json_path">None</data><data key="edge_evidence">For example, the evasion of security mitigation techniques such as ASLR or crypto objectively require significantly higher exploit complexity than iterating an attack to win a race condition; yet both conditions currently result in the same “penalty” to the final severity score</data><data key="edge_extraction_method">minie</data><data key="edge_polarity">positive</data><data key="edge_modality">asserted</data></edge><edge id="oe_5b76f07c760ed470" source="e_9bf6ead54114b2ce" target="e_83add226da8c3bc6"><data key="edge_predicate_raw">be win</data><data key="edge_assertion_id">a_7410dc43914643ea</data><data key="edge_source_id">S51</data><data key="edge_source_url">https://www.first.org/cvss/v4.0/user-guide</data><data key="edge_chunk_id">S51_C03</data><data key="edge_json_path">None</data><data key="edge_evidence">For example, the evasion of security mitigation techniques such as ASLR or crypto objectively require significantly higher exploit complexity than iterating an attack to win a race condition; yet both conditions currently result in the same “penalty” to the final severity score</data><data key="edge_extraction_method">minie</data><data key="edge_polarity">positive</data><data key="edge_modality">asserted</data></edge><edge id="oe_3cc8f7e5dc591153" source="e_92078ff0ec595868" target="e_7b5f3e2f6cc8b78e"><data key="edge_predicate_raw">result in</data><data key="edge_assertion_id">a_c470909ecc76445b</data><data key="edge_source_id">S51</data><data key="edge_source_url">https://www.first.org/cvss/v4.0/user-guide</data><data key="edge_chunk_id">S51_C03</data><data key="edge_json_path">None</data><data key="edge_evidence">For example, the evasion of security mitigation techniques such as ASLR or crypto objectively require significantly higher exploit complexity than iterating an attack to win a race condition; yet both conditions currently result in the same “penalty” to the final severity score</data><data key="edge_extraction_method">minie</data><data key="edge_polarity">positive</data><data key="edge_modality">asserted</data></edge><edge id="oe_6d5046a945b897b8" source="e_0651ca14b1e582f2" target="e_4d02ffe55962422b"><data key="edge_predicate_raw">make</data><data key="edge_assertion_id">a_13c19d7f0373262c</data><data key="edge_source_id">S51</data><data key="edge_source_url">https://www.first.org/cvss/v4.0/user-guide</data><data key="edge_chunk_id">S51_C03</data><data key="edge_json_path">None</data><data key="edge_evidence">Attack Requirements - Reflect the prerequisite conditions of the vulnerable component that make the attack possible</data><data key="edge_extraction_method">minie</data><data key="edge_polarity">positive</data><data key="edge_modality">possible</data></edge><edge id="oe_663f07e402bf211c" source="e_162dedc06540de52" target="e_79a5b245db4e61f6"><data key="edge_predicate_raw">are as</data><data key="edge_assertion_id">a_6d01eb7041ba0605</data><data key="edge_source_id">S51</data><data key="edge_source_url">https://www.first.org/cvss/v4.0/user-guide</data><data key="edge_chunk_id">S51_C03</data><data key="edge_json_path">None</data><data key="edge_evidence">The User Interaction Base Metric has been updated to allow for additional granularity when considering the interaction of a user with a vulnerable component, and details are as follows:</data><data key="edge_extraction_method">minie</data><data key="edge_polarity">positive</data><data key="edge_modality">asserted</data></edge><edge id="oe_8df29010d7ad6286" source="e_ad0c638231a934e2" target="e_92429ed6b6eb4cd0"><data key="edge_predicate_raw">has been updated to allow for</data><data key="edge_assertion_id">a_95424d0785ee5597</data><data key="edge_source_id">S51</data><data key="edge_source_url">https://www.first.org/cvss/v4.0/user-guide</data><data key="edge_chunk_id">S51_C03</data><data key="edge_json_path">None</data><data key="edge_evidence">The User Interaction Base Metric has been updated to allow for additional granularity when considering the interaction of a user with a vulnerable component, and details are as follows:</data><data key="edge_extraction_method">minie</data><data key="edge_polarity">positive</data><data key="edge_modality">asserted</data></edge><edge id="oe_720b11d3a2471d80" source="e_ad0c638231a934e2" target="e_0b208ed37488970c"><data key="edge_predicate_raw">has been updated to allow for</data><data key="edge_assertion_id">a_ac6877607b945a88</data><data key="edge_source_id">S51</data><data key="edge_source_url">https://www.first.org/cvss/v4.0/user-guide</data><data key="edge_chunk_id">S51_C03</data><data key="edge_json_path">None</data><data key="edge_evidence">The User Interaction Base Metric has been updated to allow for additional granularity when considering the interaction of a user with a vulnerable component, and details are as follows:</data><data key="edge_extraction_method">minie</data><data key="edge_polarity">positive</data><data key="edge_modality">asserted</data></edge><edge id="oe_418072adee79b6f8" source="e_d10f040039249e07" target="e_3db3ed4cd13e756a"><data key="edge_predicate_raw">requires</data><data key="edge_assertion_id">a_6644d845c84be7dd</data><data key="edge_source_id">S51</data><data key="edge_source_url">https://www.first.org/cvss/v4.0/user-guide</data><data key="edge_chunk_id">S51_C03</data><data key="edge_json_path">None</data><data key="edge_evidence">Passive (P): Successful exploitation of this vulnerability requires limited interaction by the targeted user with the vulnerable component and the attacker’s payload</data><data key="edge_extraction_method">minie</data><data key="edge_polarity">positive</data><data key="edge_modality">asserted</data></edge><edge id="oe_267d5d95c1773678" source="e_d10f040039249e07" target="e_c496d6d1dd957f39"><data key="edge_predicate_raw">requires</data><data key="edge_assertion_id">a_b062c1894c249432</data><data key="edge_source_id">S51</data><data key="edge_source_url">https://www.first.org/cvss/v4.0/user-guide</data><data key="edge_chunk_id">S51_C03</data><data key="edge_json_path">None</data><data key="edge_evidence">Passive (P): Successful exploitation of this vulnerability requires limited interaction by the targeted user with the vulnerable component and the attacker’s payload</data><data key="edge_extraction_method">minie</data><data key="edge_polarity">positive</data><data key="edge_modality">asserted</data></edge><edge id="oe_a1e22b76d43fe340" source="e_b3c77c913f52e355" target="e_8913949ce3c45f5f"><data key="edge_predicate_raw">be considered</data><data key="edge_assertion_id">a_c8fab54fbe620ce8</data><data key="edge_source_id">S51</data><data key="edge_source_url">https