">asserted</data></edge><edge id="oe_18284cf0eaa34ec6" source="e_8e874df517877380" target="e_50b2ccaf2cca5963"><data key="edge_predicate_raw">are outside</data><data key="edge_assertion_id">a_4a18dd8f69f5eae9</data><data key="edge_source_id">S51</data><data key="edge_source_url">https://www.first.org/cvss/v4.0/user-guide</data><data key="edge_chunk_id">S51_C04</data><data key="edge_json_path">None</data><data key="edge_evidence">The additional metrics allow industry sectors such as privacy, automotive, etc., to assess factors that are outside the core CVSS standard</data><data key="edge_extraction_method">minie</data><data key="edge_polarity">positive</data><data key="edge_modality">asserted</data></edge><edge id="oe_ee52b661c8fc2c70" source="e_9c9b729429186233" target="e_835cd7b766648fa2"><data key="edge_predicate_raw">be calculate order of vectors from</data><data key="edge_assertion_id">a_c08535afde521a04</data><data key="edge_source_id">S51</data><data key="edge_source_url">https://www.first.org/cvss/v4.0/user-guide</data><data key="edge_chunk_id">S51_C04</data><data key="edge_json_path">None</data><data key="edge_evidence">Use the expert comparison data to calculate an order of vectors from least severe to most severe</data><data key="edge_extraction_method">minie</data><data key="edge_polarity">positive</data><data key="edge_modality">asserted</data></edge><edge id="oe_a78273ceec96f4f0" source="e_0c097f4d339f6496" target="e_b52de94b00055efe"><data key="edge_predicate_raw">be decide what vector group in ordering of</data><data key="edge_assertion_id">a_90daf3631592c618</data><data key="edge_source_id">S51</data><data key="edge_source_url">https://www.first.org/cvss/v4.0/user-guide</data><data key="edge_chunk_id">S51_C04</data><data key="edge_json_path">None</data><data key="edge_evidence">Solicit expert opinion to decide what vector group in the ordering of vectors represents the boundary between qualitative severity scores to be backwards compatible with qualitative severity score boundaries from CVSS v3.x</data><data key="edge_extraction_method">minie</data><data key="edge_polarity">positive</data><data key="edge_modality">asserted</data></edge><edge id="oe_5b904168ebe6b91c" source="e_3268c0d3caf6f382" target="e_e7e4cc3411114886"><data key="edge_predicate_raw">represents boundary between qualitative severity scores to be</data><data key="edge_assertion_id">a_f84e13f9c4ee9180</data><data key="edge_source_id">S51</data><data key="edge_source_url">https://www.first.org/cvss/v4.0/user-guide</data><data key="edge_chunk_id">S51_C04</data><data key="edge_json_path">None</data><data key="edge_evidence">Solicit expert opinion to decide what vector group in the ordering of vectors represents the boundary between qualitative severity scores to be backwards compatible with qualitative severity score boundaries from CVSS v3.x</data><data key="edge_extraction_method">minie</data><data key="edge_polarity">positive</data><data key="edge_modality">asserted</data></edge><edge id="oe_3957e8ed9e9d4010" source="e_3268c0d3caf6f382" target="e_81f749c9c181f2c3"><data key="edge_predicate_raw">represents boundary between qualitative severity scores to be</data><data key="edge_assertion_id">a_3cbbcaa7aff51f23</data><data key="edge_source_id">S51</data><data key="edge_source_url">https://www.first.org/cvss/v4.0/user-guide</data><data key="edge_chunk_id">S51_C04</data><data key="edge_json_path">None</data><data key="edge_evidence">Solicit expert opinion to decide what vector group in the ordering of vectors represents the boundary between qualitative severity scores to be backwards compatible with qualitative severity score boundaries from CVSS v3.x</data><data key="edge_extraction_method">minie</data><data key="edge_polarity">positive</data><data key="edge_modality">asserted</data></edge><edge id="oe_7ce40d9596c17c88" source="e_3268c0d3caf6f382" target="e_1276ee29f118b2a1"><data key="edge_predicate_raw">represents boundary between qualitative severity scores to be</data><data key="edge_assertion_id">a_dba0c3078943caf1</data><data key="edge_source_id">S51</data><data key="edge_source_url">https://www.first.org/cvss/v4.0/user-guide</data><data key="edge_chunk_id">S51_C04</data><data key="edge_json_path">None</data><data key="edge_evidence">Solicit expert opinion to decide what vector group in the ordering of vectors represents the boundary between qualitative severity scores to be backwards compatible with qualitative severity score boundaries from CVSS v3.x</data><data key="edge_extraction_method">minie</data><data key="edge_polarity">positive</data><data key="edge_modality">asserted</data></edge><edge id="oe_5d39aec1915e8fdb" source="e_bfaf17725bfcbe42" target="e_97a865b3178655c7"><data key="edge_predicate_raw">adjusts scores of vectors within</data><data key="edge_assertion_id">a_fbc4af3f01f93898</data><data key="edge_source_id">S51</data><data key="edge_source_url">https://www.first.org/cvss/v4.0/user-guide</data><data key="edge_chunk_id">S51_C04</data><data key="edge_json_path">None</data><data key="edge_evidence">Create a small score modification factor that adjusts the scores of vectors within a vector group so that a change of any metric value results in a score change</data><data key="edge_extraction_method">minie</data><data key="edge_polarity">positive</data><data key="edge_modality">asserted</data></edge><edge id="oe_f594eac825aec42a" source="e_bfaf17725bfcbe42" target="e_b52de94b00055efe"><data key="edge_predicate_raw">adjusts scores of</data><data key="edge_assertion_id">a_49ce8ac33f56ce93</data><data key="edge_source_id">S51</data><data key="edge_source_url">https://www.first.org/cvss/v4.0/user-guide</data><data key="edge_chunk_id">S51_C04</data><data key="edge_json_path">None</data><data key="edge_evidence">Create a small score modification factor that adjusts the scores of vectors within a vector group so that a change of any metric value results in a score change</data><data key="edge_extraction_method">minie</data><data key="edge_polarity">positive</data><data key="edge_modality">asserted</data></edge><edge id="oe_d383424a8f1a6cbe" source="e_9bdb10fbcabccec2" target="e_4909cad877ba4cb8"><data key="edge_predicate_raw">is larger than</data><data key="edge_assertion_id">a_4190390e1be90804</data><data key="edge_source_id">S51</data><data key="edge_source_url">https://www.first.org/cvss/v4.0/user-guide</data><data key="edge_chunk_id">S51_C04</data><data key="edge_json_path">None</data><data key="edge_evidence">The intent is that the score change is not larger than the uncertainty in the ranking of the vector groups as collected from the expert comparison data in step 2</data><data key="edge_extraction_method">minie</data><data key="edge_polarity">negative</data><data key="edge_modality">asserted</data></edge><edge id="oe_4f7f870531b8eebe" source="e_1a03684ddc3e6555" target="e_5895b8f6b5de9fe7"><data key="edge_predicate_raw">helps satisfy couple of</data><data key="edge_assertion_id">a_cab5023d88e71582</data><data key="edge_source_id">S51</data><data key="edge_source_url">https://www.first.org/cvss/v4.0/user-guide</data><data key="edge_chunk_id">S51_C05</data><data key="edge_json_path">None</data><data key="edge_evidence">This step helps satisfy a couple of design requirements</data><data key="edge_extraction_method">minie</data><data key="edge_polarity">positive</data><data key="edge_modality">asserted</data></edge><edge id="oe_81ba3202dabb4ab8" source="e_be74ffef073dc8d3" target="e_cc622ea1d8ed0118"><data key="edge_predicate_raw">have available on</data><data key="edge_assertion_id">a_37e45e04b7120dbc</data><data key="edge_source_id">S51</data><data key="edge_source_url">https://www.first.org/cvss/v4.0/user-guide</data><data key="edge_chunk_id">S51_C05</data><data key="edge_json_path">None</data><data key="edge_evidence">The second is that we create the scoring system using no more time from experts than we have available on a volunteer basis to the SIG</data><data key="edge_extraction_method">minie</data><data key="edge_polarity">negative</data><data key="edge_modality">asserted</data></edge><edge id="oe_6b6c369e4b6e0ee2" source="e_bc4f46201ff94f99" target="e_339c5d84140bf52d"><data key="edge_predicate_raw">be using more time from</data><data key="edge_assertion_id">a_232b43e88e92f77d</data><data key="edge_source_id">S51</data><data key="edge_source_url">https://www.first.org/cvss/v4.0/user-guide</data><data key="edge_chunk_id">S51_C05</data><data key="edge_json_path">None</data><data key="edge_evidence">The second is that we create the scoring system using no more time from experts than we have available on a volunteer basis to the SIG</data><data key="edge_extraction_method">minie</data><data key="edge_polarity">negative</data><data key="edge_modality">asserted</data></edge><edge id="oe_d48965f14608fa27" source="e_992d08d2e3f12151" target="e_93d8650fe6b85a54"><data key="edge_predicate_raw">reduces expert effort into</data><data key="edge_assertion_id">a_23ea3b6640986bfd</data><data key="edge_source_id">S51</data><data key="edge_source_url">https://www.first.org/cvss/v4.0/user-guide</data><data key="edge_chunk_id">S51_C05</data><data key="edge_json_path">None</data><data key="edge_evidence">How this step reduces expert effort into the system is less obvious, and will be more clear in step 2</data><data key="edge_extraction_method">minie</data><data key="edge_polarity">positive</data><data key="edge_modality">asserted</data></edge><edge id="oe_e7f71017c843d2b5" source="e_992d08d2e3f12151" target="e_280e31a98bb7b317"><data key="edge_predicate_raw">reduces</data><data key="edge_assertion_id">a_d2b56ac08cba28ee</data><data key="edge_source_id">S51</data><data key="edge_source_url">https://www.first.org/cvss/v4.0/user-guide</data><data key="edge_chunk_id">S51_C05</data><data key="edge_json_path">None</data><data key="edge_evidence">How this step reduces expert effort into the system is less obvious, and will be more clear in step 2</data><data key="edge_extraction_method">minie</data><data key="edge_polarity">positive</data><data key="edge_modality">asserted</data></edge><edge id="oe_9add3ac1aa30ed7a" source="e_7ff2f0b96b9585b1" target="e_95c4670a7c30b406"><data key="edge_predicate_raw">is less</data><data key="edge_assertion_id">a_e56bb37cf59a68a9</data><data key="edge_source_id">S51</data><data key="edge_source_url">https://www.first.org/cvss/v4.0/user-guide</data><data key="edge_chunk_id">S51_C05</data><data key="edge_json_path">None</data><data key="edge_evidence">How this step reduces expert effort into the system is less obvious, and will be more clear in step 2</data><data key="edge_extraction_method">minie</data><data key="edge_polarity">positive</data><data key="edge_modality">asserted</data></edge><edge id="oe_1c27823573c264af" source="e_7ff2f0b96b9585b1" target="e_6c885ff8e70e95bc"><data key="edge_predicate_raw">be more</data><data key="edge_assertion_id">a_0a77bf681b94120b</data><data key="edge_source_id">S51</data><data key="edge_source_url">https://www.first.org/cvss/v4.0/user-guide</data><data key="edge_chunk_id">S51_C05</data><data key="edge_json_path">None</data><data key="edge_evidence">How this step reduces expert effort into the system is less obvious, and will be more clear in step 2</data><data key="edge_extraction_method">minie</data><data key="edge_polarity">positive</data><data key="edge_modality">asserted</data></edge><edge id="oe_3658976138a2af51" source="e_1ca2c11440c1c7d8" target="e_f61a4a44c562b733"><data key="edge_predicate_raw">see Sorting algorithm in</data><data key="edge_assertion_id">a_1041d61d252313fc</data><data key="edge_source_id">S51</data><data key="edge_source_url">https://www.first.org/cvss/v4.0/user-guide</data><data key="edge_chunk_id">S51_C05</data><data key="edge_json_path">None</data><data key="edge_evidence">Usually, the work grows in an order faster than the list size (in computational terms, order nlog(n), see Sorting algorithm - Wikipedia)</data><data key="edge_extraction_method">minie</data><data key="edge_polarity">positive</data><data key="edge_modality">asserted</data></edge><edge id="oe_723d28d93688c6fd" source="e_1ca2c11440c1c7d8" target="e_ae73db6c6dc9038f"><data key="edge_predicate_raw">see</data><data key="edge_assertion_id">a_dcb472eb51b9f77d</data><data key="edge_source_id">S51</data><data key="edge_source_url">https://www.first.org/cvss/v4.0/user-guide</data><data key="edge_chunk_id">S51_C05</data><data key="edge_json_path">None</data><data key="edge_evidence">Usually, the work grows in an order faster than the list size (in computational terms, order nlog(n), see Sorting algorithm - Wikipedia)</data><data key="edge_extraction_method">minie</data><data key="edge_polarity">positive</data><data key="edge_modality">asserted</data></edge><edge id="oe_c21e8fcd80ad54a7" source="e_5a64cb80b239712e" target="e_a1a213b061e94231"><data key="edge_predicate_raw">grows in order faster than</data><data key="edge_assertion_id">a_5460dcbbf519b876</data><data key="edge_source_id">S51</data><data key="edge_source_url">https://www.first.org/cvss/v4.0/user-guide</data><data key="edge_chunk_id">S51_C05</data><data key="edge_json_path">None</data><data key="edge_evidence">Usually, the work grows in an order faster than the list size (in computational terms, order nlog(n), see Sorting algorithm - Wikipedia)</data><data key="edge_extraction_method">minie</data><data key="edge_polarity">positive</data><data key="edge_modality">asserted</data></edge><edge id="oe_5314e6af38d1f733" source="e_be74ffef073dc8d3" target="e_1831388cea5ccaee"><data key="edge_predicate_raw">get smart input about</data><data key="edge_assertion_id">a_d7bd3e66170f4d73</data><data key="edge_source_id">S51</data><data key="edge_source_url">https://www.first.org/cvss/v4.0/user-guide</data><data key="edge_chunk_id">S51_C05</data><data key="edge_json_path">None</data><data key="edge_evidence">The impact on scoring system design is that if we want to get smart input about the whole CVSS vector space we have to assert some rules about it that help us make structured use of the data we collect from the expert analysts</data><data key="edge_extraction_method">minie</data><data key="edge_polarity">positive</data><data key="edge_modality">asserted</data></edge><edge id="oe_8fca794b654b3908" source="e_a1dcdd289f57b065" target="e_61641163de7ce9bc"><data key="edge_predicate_raw">make structured use of</data><data key="edge_assertion_id">a_2c0ffe4f35e89a68</data><data key="edge_source_id">S51</data><data key="edge_source_url">https://www.first.org/cvss/v4.0/user-guide</data><data key="edge_chunk_id">S51_C05</data><data key="edge_json_path">None</data><data key="edge_evidence">The impact on scoring system design is that if we want to get smart input about the whole CVSS vector space we have to assert some rules about it that help us make structured use of the data we collect from the expert analysts</data><data key="edge_extraction_method">minie</data><data key="edge_polarity">positive</data><data key="edge_modality">asserted</data></edge><edge id="oe_dcddd0084528289e" source="e_be74ffef073dc8d3" target="e_61641163de7ce9bc"><data key="edge_predicate_raw">collect from expert analysts</data><data key="edge_assertion_id">a_7a64b9fb30cec144</data><data key="edge_source_id">S51</data><data key="edge_source_url">https://www.first.org/cvss/v4.0/user-guide</data><data key="edge_chunk_id">S51_C05</data><data key="edge_json_path">None</data><data key="edge_evidence">The impact on scoring system design is that if we want to get smart input about the whole CVSS vector space we have to assert some rules about it that help us make structured use of the data we collect from the expert analysts</data><data key="edge_extraction_method">minie</data><data key="edge_polarity">positive</data><data key="edge_modality">asserted</data></edge><edge id="oe_7d178fa8a7f54056" source="e_be74ffef073dc8d3" target="e_61641163de7ce9bc"><data key="edge_predicate_raw">collect</data><data key="edge_assertion_id">a_7810ffa166c336ac</data><data key="edge_source_id">S51</data><data key="edge_source_url">https://www.first.org/cvss/v4.0/user-guide</data><data key="edge_chunk_id">S51_C05</data><data key="edge_json_path">None</data><data key="edge_evidence">The impact on scoring system design is that if we want to get smart input about the whole CVSS vector space we have to assert some rules about it that help us make structured use of the data we collect from the expert analysts</data><data key="edge_extraction_method">minie</data><data key="edge_polarity">positive</data><data key="edge_modality">asserted</data></edge><edge id="oe_e00d1f733de769b3" source="e_98b5283953a5c25e" target="e_ded111b0b7ddf357"><data key="edge_predicate_raw">has membership in</data><data key="edge_assertion_id">a_ac19f5b91d006733</data><data key="edge_source_id">S51</data><data key="edge_source_url">https://www.first.org/cvss/v4.0/user-guide</data><data key="edge_chunk_id">S51_C05</data><data key="edge_json_path">None</data><data key="edge_evidence">That is, we could generate a score for each possible vector based on their membership in the metric-group-based qualitative sets and the relative severity of those sets</data><data key="edge_extraction_method">minie</data><data key="edge_polarity">positive</data><data key="edge_modality">possible</data></edge><edge id="oe_b1d1a3f99faf00f5" source="e_477c05cd9e15847d" target="e_0c150b2def074ef8"><data key="edge_predicate_raw">are competing in</data><data key="edge_assertion_id">a_9903b6acc52200a1</data><data key="edge_source_id">S51</data><data key="edge_source_url">https://www.first.org/cvss/v4.0/user-guide</data><data key="edge_chunk_id">S51_C06</data><data key="edge_json_path">None</data><data key="edge_evidence">The expert comparisons are used as if the metric-group-based vector sets are competing in a match, and we want to rank the vector sets from "best" to "worst"</data><data key="edge_extraction_method">minie</data><data key="edge_polarity">positive</data><data key="edge_modality">asserted</data></edge><edge id="oe_792dffa494d67d75" source="e_b6432506bf460085" target="e_796e7f2dcc4c54d2"><data key="edge_predicate_raw">sets from</data><data key="edge_assertion_id">a_5b537fb1cbfd1d08</data><data key="edge_source_id">S51</data><data key="edge_source_url">https://www.first.org/cvss/v4.0/user-guide</data><data key="edge_chunk_id">S51_C06</data><data key="edge_json_path">None</data><data key="edge_evidence">The expert comparisons are used as if the metric-group-based vector sets are competing in a match, and we want to rank the vector sets from "best" to "worst"</data><data key="edge_extraction_method">minie</data><data key="edge_polarity">positive</data><data key="edge_modality">asserted</data></edge><edge id="oe_4c87e2dd704a1674" source="e_003cde4671cc5bd6" target="e_3c2dbd040ea56547"><data key="edge_predicate_raw">be used to turn expert comparisons into</data><data key="edge_assertion_id">a_1d0ae1ce41c6639f</data><data key="edge_source_id">S51</data><data key="edge_source_url">https://www.first.org/cvss/v4.0/user-guide</data><data key="edge_chunk_id">S51_C06</data><data key="edge_json_path">None</data><data key="edge_evidence">The algorithm used to turn these expert comparisons into a ranking is the same as the algorithm used to take outcomes of chess matches (comparisons) to rank chess players from best to worst</data><data key="edge_extraction_method">minie</data><data key="edge_polarity">positive</data><data key="edge_modality">asserted</data></edge><edge id="oe_99a0b9cbae2c4c17" source="e_003cde4671cc5bd6" target="e_3aac6d76fc7c4bcd"><data key="edge_predicate_raw">be used to turn</data><data key="edge_assertion_id">a_0de5df2562664f79</data><data key="edge_source_id">S51</data><data key="edge_source_url">https://www.first.org/cvss/v4.0/user-guide</data><data key="edge_chunk_id">S51_C06</data><data key="edge_json_path">None</data><data key="edge_evidence">The algorithm used to turn these expert comparisons into a ranking is the same as the algorithm used to take outcomes of chess matches (comparisons) to rank chess players from best to worst</data><data key="edge_extraction_method">minie</data><data key="edge_polarity">positive</data><data key="edge_modality">asserted</data></edge><edge id="oe_46f0b9920ececfa5" source="e_cd471d217b944e23" target="e_68a886681a67085e"><data key="edge_predicate_raw">is same as</data><data key="edge_assertion_id">a_2fc1fffb18b5e9a2</data><data key="edge_source_id">S51</data><data key="edge_source_url">https://www.first.org/cvss/v4.0/user-guide</data><data key="edge_chunk_id">S51_C06</data><data key="edge_json_path">None</data><data key="edge_evidence">The algorithm used to turn these expert comparisons into a ranking is the same as the algorithm used to take outcomes of chess matches (comparisons) to rank chess players from best to worst</data><data key="edge_extraction_method">minie</data><data key="edge_polarity">positive</data><data key="edge_modality">asserted</data></edge><edge id="oe_e226344cb2de733b" source="e_003cde4671cc5bd6" target="e_51e771101c478fa6"><data key="edge_predicate_raw">be used to take</data><data key="edge_assertion_id">a_bfc1f8705f7e70a5</data><data key="edge_source_id">S51</data><data key="edge_source_url">https://www.first.org/cvss/v4.0/user-guide</data><data key="edge_chunk_id">S51_C06</data><data key="edge_json_path">None</data><data key="edge_evidence">The algorithm used to turn these expert comparisons into a ranking is the same as the algorithm used to take outcomes of chess matches (comparisons) to rank chess players from best to worst</data><data key="edge_extraction_method">minie</data><data key="edge_polarity">positive</data><data key="edge_modality">asserted</data></edge><edge id="oe_abc10c879a21a2c2" source="e_62aa3b194b245c0e" target="e_796e7f2dcc4c54d2"><data key="edge_predicate_raw">be rank chess players from</data><data key="edge_assertion_id">a_2e61bdb60df1cada</data><data key="edge_source_id">S51</data><data key="edge_source_url">https://www.first.org/cvss/v4.0/user-guide</data><data key="edge_chunk_id">S51_C06</data><data key="edge_json_path">None</data><data key="edge_evidence">The algorithm used to turn these expert comparisons into a ranking is the same as the algorithm used to take outcomes of chess matches (comparisons) to rank chess players from best to worst</data><data key="edge_extraction_method">minie</data><data key="edge_polarity">positive</data><data key="edge_modality">asserted</data></edge><edge id="oe_72b7961af55aac71" source="e_56ce7efdce4cc762" target="e_ca335c133f4134dc"><data key="edge_predicate_raw">rate higher-scored vector set as more severe certain percentage of</data><data key="edge_assertion_id">a_4905d4e914c4085e</data><data key="edge_source_id">S51</data><data key="edge_source_url">https://www.first.org/cvss/v4.0/user-guide</data><data key="edge_chunk_id">S51_C06</data><data key="edge_json_path">None</data><data key="edge_evidence">The interpretation of the point scores for each vector set is that if a vector-set has a score 100 points higher than another vector-set, then that score difference predicts that an expert would rate the higher-scored vector set as "more severe" a certain percentage of the time</data><data key="edge_extraction_method">minie</data><data key="edge_polarity">positive</data><data key="edge_modality">asserted</data></edge><edge id="oe_f32c2b1fd19c89fe" source="e_33dca876a41ad65c" target="e_97c75915fece259d"><data key="edge_predicate_raw">be set as</data><data key="edge_assertion_id">a_5529666dc06f4b3f</data><data key="edge_source_id">S51</data><data key="edge_source_url">https://www.first.org/cvss/v4.0/user-guide</data><data key="edge_chunk_id">S51_C06</data><data key="edge_json_path">None</data><data key="edge_evidence">The interpretation of the point scores for each vector set is that if a vector-set has a score 100 points higher than another vector-set, then that score difference predicts that an expert would rate the higher-scored vector set as "more severe" a certain percentage of the time</data><data key="edge_extraction_method">minie</data><data key="edge_polarity">positive</data><data key="edge_modality">asserted</data></edge><edge id="oe_b94082599bd1a5fb" source="e_33dca876a41ad65c" target="e_d7273f4e25365f2d"><data key="edge_predicate_raw">be rated as more severe</data><data key="edge_assertion_id">a_3dad7aca165e623b</data><data key="edge_source_id">S51</data><data key="edge_source_url">https://www.first.org/cvss/v4.0/user-guide</data><data key="edge_chunk_id">S51_C06</data><data key="edge_json_path">None</data><data key="edge_evidence">The bigger the point-score difference, the larger the chance the higher-scored vector would be rated as more severe</data><data key="edge_extraction_method">minie</data><data key="edge_polarity">positive</data><data key="edge_modality">asserted</data></edge><edge id="oe_3433fa5916fa2933" source="e_33dca876a41ad65c" target="e_d7273f4e25365f2d"><data key="edge_predicate_raw">be rated</data><data key="edge_assertion_id">a_10b5586dcd64fd7c</data><data key="edge_source_id">S51</data><data key="edge_source_url">https://www.first.org/cvss/v4.0/user-guide</data><data key="edge_chunk_id">S51_C06</data><data key="edge_json_path">None</data><data key="edge_evidence">The bigger the point-score difference, the larger the chance the higher-scored vector would be rated as more severe</data><data key="edge_extraction_method">minie</data><data key="edge_polarity">positive</data><data key="edge_modality">asserted</data></edge><edge id="oe_35a682a0f803bc6a" source="e_a9eeb3ef214a021e" target="e_8c64f55ff55206c3"><data key="edge_predicate_raw">represents</data><data key="edge_assertion_id">a_a62149e2cce240eb</data><data key="edge_source_id">S51</data><data key="edge_source_url">https://www.first.org/cvss/v4.0/user-guide</data><data key="edge_chunk_id">S51_C06</data><data key="edge_json_path">None</data><data key="edge_evidence">Therefore, we believe the Elo algorithm output is stable and represents a reliable transformation from the diverse expert opinion inputs to a single severity ordering of the metric-group-based vector sets</data><data key="edge_extraction_method">minie</data><data key="edge_polarity">positive</data><data key="edge_modality">asserted</data></edge><edge id="oe_d265a59c6388e7ae" source="e_c4c3d4910efe515f" target="e_477c05cd9e15847d"><data key="edge_predicate_raw">be ordering of</data><data key="edge_assertion_id">a_2139639fed9e7873</data><data key="edge_source_id">S51</data><data key="edge_source_url">https://www.first.org/cvss/v4.0/user-guide</data><data key="edge_chunk_id">S51_C06</data><data key="edge_json_path">None</data><data key="edge_evidence">Therefore, we believe the Elo algorithm output is stable and represents a reliable transformation from the diverse expert opinion inputs to a single severity ordering of the metric-group-based vector sets</data><data key="edge_extraction_method">minie</data><data key="edge_polarity">positive</data><data key="edge_modality">asserted</data></edge><edge id="oe_3a89576e9db11d50" source="e_be74ffef073dc8d3" target="e_25951c5d0a9e44bb"><data key="edge_predicate_raw">believe</data><data key="edge_assertion_id">a_085e2c484a48c8e6</data><data key="edge_source_id">S51</data><data key="edge_source_url">https://www.first.org/cvss/v4.0/user-guide</data><data key="edge_chunk_id">S51_C06</data><data key="edge_json_path">None</data><data key="edge_evidence">Therefore, we believe the Elo algorithm output is stable and represents a reliable transformation from the diverse expert opinion inputs to a single severity ordering of the metric-group-based vector sets</data><data key="edge_extraction_method">minie</data><data key="edge_polarity">positive</data><data key="edge_modality">asserted</data></edge><edge id="oe_53092888eb21536d" source="e_3c6f55c088fab9eb" target="e_2da51adaae4997fa"><data key="edge_predicate_raw">improve compatibility with</data><data key="edge_assertion_id">a_55d43d8576e66e5a</data><data key="edge_source_id">S51</data><data key="edge_source_url">https://www.first.org/cvss/v4.0/user-guide</data><data key="edge_chunk_id">S51_C06</data><data key="edge_json_path">None</data><data key="edge_evidence">Before mapping the 270 metric-group-based vector sets to scores between 0.0 and 10.0, the SIG wanted to improve backwards compatibility with CVSS v3 scores</data><data key="edge_extraction_method">minie</data><data key="edge_polarity">positive</data><data key="edge_modality">asserted</data></edge><edge id="oe_1a039f3dfa1e82b0" source="e_e13aa03d5edf67fb" target="e_7292e4cff7ad0e72"><data key="edge_predicate_raw">define</data><data key="edge_assertion_id">a_cd10730b5621c2d1</data><data key="edge_source_id">S51</data><data key="edge_source_url">https://www.first.org/cvss/v4.0/user-guide</data><data key="edge_chunk_id">S51_C06</data><data key="edge_json_path">None</data><data key="edge_evidence">To do this, the SIG wanted to decide which metric-group-based vector sets define the qualitative severity set boundaries</data><data key="edge_extraction_method">minie</data><data key="edge_polarity">positive</data><data key="edge_modality">asserted</data></edge><edge id="oe_1d75398658f9b5f8" source="e_3c6f55c088fab9eb" target="e_e163460c91338b08"><data key="edge_predicate_raw">decide which metric-group-based vector sets define qualitative severity To do</data><data key="edge_assertion_id">a_b8342cdcf3ced701</data><data key="edge_source_id">S51</data><data key="edge_source_url">https://www.first.org/cvss/v4.0/user-guide</data><data key="edge_chunk_id">S51_C06</data><data key="edge_json_path">None</data><data key="edge_evidence">To do this, the SIG wanted to decide which metric-group-based vector sets define the qualitative severity set boundaries</data><data key="edge_extraction_method">minie</data><data key="edge_polarity">positive</data><data key="edge_modality">asserted</data></edge><edge id="oe_1e758bac9773af81" source="e_e163460c91338b08" target="e_f99c5ad31f75d2bb"><data key="edge_predicate_raw">was determined by soliciting input from</data><data key="edge_assertion_id">a_fb2388d026af5b28</data><data key="edge_source_id">S51</data><data key="edge_source_url">https://www.first.org/cvss/v4.0/user-guide</data><data key="edge_chunk_id">S51_C06</data><data key="edge_json_path">None</data><data key="edge_evidence">This was determined by soliciting input from the 30+ member CVSS SIG</data><data key="edge_extraction_method">minie</data><data key="edge_polarity">positive</data><data key="edge_modality">asserted</data></edge><edge id="oe_fa0a990981d4f974" source="e_2e7f6508490301b8" target="e_a3f5a028c4073979"><data key="edge_predicate_raw">defined</data><data key="edge_assertion_id">a_b4d305f514c7d544</data><data key="edge_source_id">S51</data><data key="edge_source_url">https://www.first.org/cvss/v4.0/user-guide</data><data key="edge_chunk_id">S51_C06</data><data key="edge_json_path">None</data><data key="edge_evidence">The SIG's then defined the boundaries as the average of the 5 SIG members' selections</data><data key="edge_extraction_method">minie</data><data key="edge_polarity">positive</data><data key="edge_modality">asserted</data></edge><edge id="oe_6199847f4c2012da" source="e_3b9aab84428344fa" target="e_37bc44e6064f36ed"><data key="edge_predicate_raw">resulted in</data><data key="edge_assertion_id">a_38ee92ecd293ca26</data><data key="edge_source_id">S51</data><data key="edge_source_url">https://www.first.org/cvss/v4.0/user-guide</data><data key="edge_chunk_id">S51_C07</data><data key="edge_json_path">None</data><data key="edge_evidence">The result of the total ordering (step 3) and qualitative severity boundaries (step 4) resulted in the following number of metric-group-based vector sets in each qualitative severity value</data><data key="edge_extraction_method">heuristic</data><data key="edge_polarity">positive</data><data key="edge_modality">asserted</data></edge><edge id="oe_1d27a8a9fa15f38d" source="e_44c24d383b33debf" target="e_8e1bfccf115aedc6"><data key="edge_predicate_raw">be assess lumpiness of</data><data key="edge_assertion_id">a_6c39eac24ef0e677</data><data key="edge_source_id">S51</data><data key="edge_source_url">https://www.first.org/cvss/v4.0/user-guide</data><data key="edge_chunk_id">S51_C07</data><data key="edge_json_path">None</data><data key="edge_evidence">However, the SIG does not believe that counting total number of possible CVSS v4.0 BTE vectors is a relevant way to assess lumpiness of CVSS v4 BTE scores</data><data key="edge_extraction_method">minie</data><data key="edge_polarity">negative</data><data key="edge_modality">possible</data></edge><edge id="oe_5d1cd100677053d0" source="e_7a3dbeb1850aac11" target="e_3813a0fc17711012"><data key="edge_predicate_raw">have to be</data><data key="edge_assertion_id">a_548e01243a05386b</data><data key="edge_source_id">S51</data><data key="edge_source_url">https://www.first.org/cvss/v4.0/user-guide</data><data key="edge_chunk_id">S51_C07</data><data key="edge_json_path">None</data><data key="edge_evidence">A better assessment of the distribution of CVSS v4 BTE scores will have to be an empirical assessment of how many times a vector string actually recurs in actual CVE ID assessments</data><data key="edge_extraction_method">minie</data><data key="edge_polarity">positive</data><data key="edge_modality">asserted</data></edge><edge id="oe_eca7d3e94cc2f095" source="e_8ca3eb60be0618d3" target="e_d4e917125a7a8d5a"><data key="edge_predicate_raw">share</data><data key="edge_assertion_id">a_dbb15dc8ac671255</data><data key="edge_source_id">S51</data><data key="edge_source_url">https://www.first.org/cvss/v4.0/user-guide</data><data key="edge_chunk_id">S51_C07</data><data key="edge_json_path">None</data><data key="edge_evidence">That algorithm is agglomerative hierarchical clustering (Hierarchical clustering - Wikipedia), which makes sure that vector sets that share the same CVSS v4 BTE score also have the smallest difference between their Elo-point scores</data><data key="edge_extraction_method">minie</data><data key="edge_polarity">positive</data><data key="edge_modality">asserted</data></edge><edge id="oe_93729631d8944bd1" source="e_8ca3eb60be0618d3" target="e_1db59a152d1d2619"><data key="edge_predicate_raw">have smallest difference between</data><data key="edge_assertion_id">a_4c670a385f45aeaa</data><data key="edge_source_id">S51</data><data key="edge_source_url">https://www.first.org/cvss/v4.0/user-guide</data><data key="edge_chunk_id">S51_C07</data><data key="edge_json_path">None</data><data key="edge_evidence">That algorithm is agglomerative hierarchical clustering (Hierarchical clustering - Wikipedia), which makes sure that vector sets that share the same CVSS v4 BTE score also have the smallest difference between their Elo-point scores</data><data key="edge_extraction_method">minie</data><data key="edge_polarity">positive</data><data key="edge_modality">asserted</data></edge><edge id="oe_e2df7ad7c9449458" source="e_57973dca3393636d" target="e_a705103665e9ea94"><data key="edge_predicate_raw">be create</data><data key="edge_assertion_id">a_e16a477b1c8a7a70</data><data key="edge_source_id">S51</data><data key="edge_source_url">https://www.first.org/cvss/v4.0/user-guide</data><data key="edge_chunk_id">S51_C07</data><data key="edge_json_path">None</data><data key="edge_evidence">In order to meet a requirement that any change in a metric value result in at least a 0.1 change in the CVSS v4 BTE score, the SIG added an additional step to create a small change in the score based on metric value changes within metric-group-based vector sets</data><data key="edge_extraction_method">minie</data><data key="edge_polarity">positive</data><data key="edge_modality">asserted</data></edge><edge id="oe_4d86378f3ce15eed" source="e_091431c5d3752dbc" target="e_477c05cd9e15847d"><data key="edge_predicate_raw">be based on metric value changes within</data><data key="edge_assertion_id">a_64a8b31c994e0808</data><data key="edge_source_id">S51</data><data key="edge_source_url">https://www.first.org/cvss/v4.0/user-guide</data><data key="edge_chunk_id">S51_C07</data><data key="edge_json_path">None</data><data key="edge_evidence">In order to meet a requirement that any change in a metric value result in at least a 0.1 change in the CVSS v4 BTE score, the SIG added an additional step to create a small change in the score based on metric value changes within metric-group-based vector sets</data><data key="edge_extraction_method">minie</data><data key="edge_polarity">positive</data><data key="edge_modality">asserted</data></edge><edge id="oe_9c9189f0895a6178" source="e_153b7b32aeec27b5" target="e_8ca3eb60be0618d3"><data key="edge_predicate_raw">be based on metric values within</data><data key="edge_assertion_id">a_fddf002795219c96</data><data key="edge_source_id">S51</data><data key="edge_source_url">https://www.first.org/cvss/v4.0/user-guide</data><data key="edge_chunk_id">S51_C07</data><data key="edge_json_path">None</data><data key="edge_evidence">Providing a small change based on metric values within vector sets allows the slightly-more-severe metric strings within a vector set to overlap the slightly-less-severe metric strings from a nearby but slightly-more-severe metric-group-based vector set</data><data key="edge_extraction_method">minie</data><data key="edge_polarity">positive</data><data key="edge_modality">asserted</data></edge><edge id="oe_25a95d703625d33f" source="e_03f8af832810d578" target="e_e87b74231bec2a78"><data key="edge_predicate_raw">allows slightly-more-severe metric strings within</data><data key="edge_assertion_id">a_8830169bd97daea5</data><data key="edge_source_id">S51</data><data key="edge_source_url">https://www.first.org/cvss/v4.0/user-guide</data><data key="edge_chunk_id">S51_C07</data><data key="edge_json_path">None</data><data key="edge_evidence">Providing a small change based on metric values within vector sets allows the slightly-more-severe metric strings within a vector set to overlap the slightly-less-severe metric strings from a nearby but slightly-more-severe metric-group-based vector set</data><data key="edge_extraction_method">minie</data><data key="edge_polarity">positive</data><data key="edge_modality">asserted</data></edge><edge id="oe_4baed2948b82d20a" source="e_03f8af832810d578" target="e_f51ac84ee0a80ed7"><data key="edge_predicate_raw">allows slightly-more-severe metric strings within</data><data key="edge_assertion_id">a_cc90753f32093c7a</data><data key="edge_source_id">S51</data><data key="edge_source_url">https://www.first.org/cvss/v4.0/user-guide</data><data key="edge_chunk_id">S51_C07</data><data key="edge_json_path">None</data><data key="edge_evidence">Providing a small change based on metric values within vector sets allows the slightly-more-severe metric strings within a vector set to overlap the slightly-less-severe metric strings from a nearby but slightly-more-severe metric-group-based vector set</data><data key="edge_extraction_method">minie</data><data key="edge_polarity">positive</data><data key="edge_modality">asserted</data></edge><edge id="oe_eebc1298233a3274" source="e_03f8af832810d578" target="e_11efb235c0a78f11"><data key="edge_predicate_raw">allows</data><data key="edge_assertion_id">a_9bb796fede0ea1e3</data><data key="edge_source_id">S51</data><data key="edge_source_url">https://www.first.org/cvss/v4.0/user-guide</data><data key="edge_chunk_id">S51_C07</data><data key="edge_json_path">None</data><data key="edge_evidence">Providing a small change based on metric values within vector sets allows the slightly-more-severe metric strings within a vector set to overlap the slightly-less-severe metric strings from a nearby but slightly-more-severe metric-group-based vector set</data><data key="edge_extraction_method">minie</data><data key="edge_polarity">positive</data><data key="edge_modality">asserted</data></edge><edge id="oe_f80c7eabf92afa9d" source="e_b6432506bf460085" target="e_5306ae0ca1f1560b"><data key="edge_predicate_raw">be set to overlap slightly-less-severe metric strings from</data><data key="edge_assertion_id">a_d22a7bc697fb3774</data><data key="edge_source_id">S51</data><data key="edge_source_url">https://www.first.org/cvss/v4.0/user-guide</data><data key="edge_chunk_id">S51_C07</data><data key="edge_json_path">None</data><data key="edge_evidence">Providing a small change based on metric values within vector sets allows the slightly-more-severe metric strings within a vector set to overlap the slightly-less-severe metric strings from a nearby but slightly-more-severe metric-group-based vector set</data><data key="edge_extraction_method">minie</data><data key="edge_polarity">positive</data><data key="edge_modality">asserted</data></edge><edge id="oe_ba77edcb87dda1bd" source="e_b6432506bf460085" target="e_3c07490f33fcdb9b"><data key="edge_predicate_raw">be set to overlap slightly-less-severe metric strings from</data><data key="edge_assertion_id">a_1a72f135e056533c</data><data key="edge_source_id">S51</data><data key="edge_source_url">https://www.first.org/cvss/v4.0/user-guide</data><data key="edge_chunk_id">S51_C07</data><data key="edge_json_path">None</data><data key="edge_evidence">Providing a small change based on metric values within vector sets allows the slightly-more-severe metric strings within a vector set to overlap the slightly-less-severe metric strings from a nearby but slightly-more-severe metric-group-based vector set</data><data key="edge_extraction_method">minie</data><data key="edge_polarity">positive</data><data key="edge_modality">asserted</data></edge><edge id="oe_300f50f833241cc4" source="e_b6432506bf460085" target="e_62881d6e64bdb716"><data key="edge_predicate_raw">be set to overlap</data><data key="edge_assertion_id">a_2fc123893af90c13</data><data key="edge_source_id">S51</data><data key="edge_source_url">https://www.first.org/cvss/v4.0/user-guide</data><data key="edge_chunk_id">S51_C07</data><data key="edge_json_path">None</data><data key="edge_evidence">Providing a small change based on metric values within vector sets allows the slightly-more-severe metric strings within a vector set to overlap the slightly-less-severe metric strings from a nearby but slightly-more-severe metric-group-based vector set</data><data key="edge_extraction_method">minie</data><data key="edge_polarity">positive</data><data key="edge_modality">asserted</data></edge><edge id="oe_1e5db56c2247cbe4" source="e_0c097f4d339f6496" target="e_5d6109fb25e0fb75"><data key="edge_predicate_raw">be ranking to be</data><data key="edge_assertion_id">a_2c0d31c8e7428431</data><data key="edge_source_id">S51</data><data key="edge_source_url">https://www.first.org/cvss/v4.0/user-guide</data><data key="edge_chunk_id">S51_C07</data><data key="edge_json_path">None</data><data key="edge_evidence">These small shifts account for the fact that every vector within an equivalence set is not identical even if they are importantly and saliently equivalent enough to enable expert opinion ranking to be possible</data><data key="edge_extraction_method">minie</data><data key="edge_polarity">negative</data><data key="edge_modality">possible</data></edge><edge id="oe_b67de40449977408" source="e_0c097f4d339f6496" target="e_5d6109fb25e0fb75"><data key="edge_predicate_raw">be ranking to be</data><data key="edge_assertion_id">a_87015d2f1a34db73</data><data key="edge_source_id">S51</data><data key="edge_source_url">https://www.first.org/cvss/v4.0/user-guide</data><data key="edge_chunk_id">S51_C08</data><data key="edge_json_path">None</data><data key="edge_evidence">shifts account for the fact that every vector within an equivalence set is not identical even if they are importantly and saliently equivalent enough to enable expert opinion ranking to be possible</data><data key="edge_extraction_method">minie</data><data key="edge_polarity">negative</data><data key="edge_modality">possible</data></edge><edge id="oe_257a945873a3a857" source="e_c983c1a036f2d485" target="e_a09a3298b7a4d470"><data key="edge_predicate_raw">be based on</data><data key="edge_assertion_id">a_c09423d820a2bf81</data><data key="edge_source_id">S51</data><data key="edge_source_url">https://www.first.org/cvss/v4.0/user-guide</data><data key="edge_chunk_id">S51_C08</data><data key="edge_json_path">None</data><data key="edge_evidence">Therefore, it is plausible to algorithmically define a change in CVSS v4 BTE score based on this ordering</data><data key="edge_extraction_method">minie</data><data key="edge_polarity">positive</data><data key="edge_modality">asserted</data></edge><edge id="oe_7ebf3a9edadf42a7" source="e_0c097f4d339f6496" target="e_0fe865e6b0d11c6c"><data key="edge_predicate_raw">was used to sort big-picture ordering of</data><data key="edge_assertion_id">a_0169d5cc21c62d91</data><data key="edge_source_id">S51</data><data key="edge_source_url">https://www.first.org/cvss/v4.0/user-guide</data><data key="edge_chunk_id">S51_C08</data><data key="edge_json_path">None</data><data key="edge_evidence">That is, the expert opinion was used to sort the big-picture ordering of qualitatively important differences</data><data key="edge_extraction_method">minie</data><data key="edge_polarity">positive</data><data key="edge_modality">asserted</data></edge><edge id="oe_bf88c02702f49028" source="e_39d80c497ea15938" target="e_f922a5468724441b"><data key="edge_predicate_raw">are salient to</data><data key="edge_assertion_id">a_678b0666b666b468</data><data key="edge_source_id">S51</data><data key="edge_source_url">https://www.first.org/cvss/v4.0/user-guide</data><data key="edge_chunk_id">S51_C08</data><data key="edge_json_path">None</data><data key="edge_evidence">The small changes in metric value that are not salient to a metric-group-based equivalence set change can still be used to represent a small change in the score that is consistent with the Elo-point difference interpretation of how likely an expert is to rate one vector set as more severe than another</data><data key="edge_extraction_method">minie</data><data key="edge_polarity">negative</data><data key="edge_modality">possible</data></edge><edge id="oe_430c58280246dfcf" source="e_89a290d50a4ee417" target="e_4364e67a28b13c95"><data key="edge_predicate_raw">be used to represent small change in</data><data key="edge_assertion_id">a_321dbd752ea8aa18</data><data key="edge_source_id">S51</data><data key="edge_source_url">https://www.first.org/cvss/v4.0/user-guide</data><data key="edge_chunk_id">S51_C08</data><data key="edge_json_path">None</data><data key="edge_evidence">The small changes in metric value that are not salient to a metric-group-based equivalence set change can still be used to represent a small change in the score that is consistent with the Elo-point difference interpretation of how likely an expert is to rate one vector set as more severe than another</data><data key="edge_extraction_method">minie</data><data key="edge_polarity">negative</data><data key="edge_modality">possible</data></edge><edge id="oe_a17d89af8cbd86a7" source="e_43b908d08d2ede0c" target="e_f7f0082982beecc7"><data key="edge_predicate_raw">are number of recommendations for</data><data key="edge_assertion_id">a_e418ba26f35fa9c9</data><data key="edge_source_id">S51</data><data key="edge_source_url">https://www.first.org/cvss/v4.0/user-guide</data><data key="edge_chunk_id">S51_C08</data><data key="edge_json_path">None</data><data key="edge_evidence">Below are a number of recommendations for consumers when assessing vulnerabilities with CVSS v4.0</data><data key="edge_extraction_method">minie</data><data key="edge_polarity">positive</data><data key="edge_modality">asserted</data></edge><edge id="oe_e72598e9e7ee7519" source="e_ad16450d4d7b98f8" target="e_31d865c1327d86e7"><data key="edge_predicate_raw">is recommended to enrich</data><data key="edge_assertion_id">a_311602c9bb9f3d04</data><data key="edge_source_id">S51</data><data key="edge_source_url">https://www.first.org/cvss/v4.0/user-guide</data><data key="edge_chunk_id">S51_C08</data><data key="edge_json_path">None</data><data key="edge_evidence">It is highly recommended to enrich the results from vulnerability scanning solutions with asset data</data><data key="edge_extraction_method">minie</data><data key="edge_polarity">positive</data><data key="edge_modality">asserted</data></edge><edge id="oe_22dfc5491b1c7196" source="e_ad16450d4d7b98f8" target="e_c71e4952422c37b4"><data key="edge_predicate_raw">is recommended to enrich</data><data key="edge_assertion_id">a_1a0f2ad52a87e292</data><data key="edge_source_id">S51</data><data key="edge_source_url">https://www.first.org/cvss/v4.0/user-guide</data><data key="edge_chunk_id">S51_C08</data><data key="edge_json_path">None</data><data key="edge_evidence">It is highly recommended to enrich the results from vulnerability scanning solutions with asset data</data><data key="edge_extraction_method">minie</data><data key="edge_polarity">positive</data><data key="edge_modality">asserted</data></edge><edge id="oe_8c5908cbe9f1f6d9" source="e_4e942ef53cb87a39" target="e_57e6975d8ca79e1f"><data key="edge_predicate_raw">is kept in</data><data key="edge_assertion_id">a_5cc8b03403c05896</data><data key="edge_source_id">S51</data><data key="edge_source_url">https://www.first.org/cvss/v4.0/user-guide</data><data key="edge_chunk_id">S51_C08</data><data key="edge_json_path">None</data><data key="edge_evidence">Often, asset management data is kept in a database that can easily be integrated with vulnerability scan data</data><data key="edge_extraction_method">minie</data><data key="edge_polarity">positive</data><data key="edge_modality">possible</data></edge><edge id="oe_8fce2ae7fd0fd732" source="e_57e6975d8ca79e1f" target="e_dbd1ba0cc63988dc"><data key="edge_predicate_raw">be integrated with</data><data key="edge_assertion_id">a_544211315541fe6b</data><data key="edge_source_id">S51</data><data key="edge_source_url">https://www.first.org/cvss/v4.0/user-guide</data><data key="edge_chunk_id">S51_C08</data><data key="edge_json_path">None</data><data key="edge_evidence">Often, asset management data is kept in a database that can easily be integrated with vulnerability scan data</data><data key="edge_extraction_method">minie</data><data key="edge_polarity">positive</data><data key="edge_modality">possible</data></edge><edge id="oe_41ab24420805b77b" source="e_8df5ed6835bb03e8" target="e_84b1db4e585f1e60"><data key="edge_predicate_raw">be utilize Environmental Metric Group to improve quality of</data><data key="edge_assertion_id">a_d1c23edc60793de7</data><data key="edge_source_id">S51</data><data key="edge_source_url">https://www.first.org/cvss/v4.0/user-guide</data><data key="edge_chunk_id">S51_C08</data><data key="edge_json_path">None</data><data key="edge_evidence">Not only will this step enable a Vulnerability Management team to utilize the Environmental Metric Group to improve the quality of the resulting CVSS scores, the engineers responsible for remediating identified vulnerabilities will have more information at their disposal</data><data key="edge_extraction_method">minie</data><data key="edge_polarity">negative</data><data key="edge_modality">asserted</data></edge><edge id="oe_15457cdd2840b43d" source="e_addcf29e935e808a" target="e_497e42a6e3587a83"><data key="edge_predicate_raw">have more information</data><data key="edge_assertion_id">a_08a15137d418dfae</data><data key="edge_source_id">S51</data><data key="edge_source_url">https://www.first.org/cvss/v4.0/user-guide</data><data key="edge_chunk_id">S51_C08</data><data key="edge_json_path">None</data><data key="edge_evidence">Not only will this step enable a Vulnerability Management team to utilize the Environmental Metric Group to improve the quality of the resulting CVSS scores, the engineers responsible for remediating identified vulnerabilities will have more information at their disposal</data><data key="edge_extraction_method">minie</data><data key="edge_polarity">negative</data><data key="edge_modality">asserted</data></edge><edge id="oe_3c263515f4bda9f6" source="e_addcf29e935e808a" target="e_482da9ea87102d14"><data key="edge_predicate_raw">have more information at</data><data key="edge_assertion_id">a_6ade768e54b748b1</data><data key="edge_source_id">S51</data><data key="edge_source_url">https://www.first.org/cvss/v4.0/user-guide</data><data key="edge_chunk_id">S51_C08</data><data key="edge_json_path">None</data><data key="edge_evidence">Not only will this step enable a Vulnerability Management team to utilize the Environmental Metric Group to improve the quality of the resulting CVSS scores, the engineers responsible for remediating identified vulnerabilities will have more information at their disposal</data><data key="edge_extraction_method">minie</data><data key="edge_polarity">negative</data><data key="edge_modality">asserted</data></edge><edge id="oe_fd90304553194a1e" source="e_718734d165927d5b" target="e_d93d3f2293801306"><data key="edge_predicate_raw">takes environmental factors into</data><data key="edge_assertion_id">a_e5515131dbe9c05e</data><data key="edge_source_id">S51</data><data key="edge_source_url">https://www.first.org/cvss/v4.0/user-guide</data><data key="edge_chunk_id">S51_C08</data><data key="edge_json_path">None</data><data key="edge_evidence">Once this information is integrated using automation, the result is a CVSS-BE score that takes those environmental factors into consideration</data><data key="edge_extraction_method">minie</data><data key="edge_polarity">positive</data><data key="edge_modality">asserted</data></edge><edge id="oe_9e6bc7a512a7f0ed" source="e_2079f7f0585a6a0c" target="e_386270aba5ab2e70"><data key="edge_predicate_raw">is integrated</data><data key="edge_assertion_id">a_84a35f942e3e4899</data><data key="edge_source_id">S51</data><data key="edge_source_url">https://www.first.org/cvss/v4.0/user-guide</data><data key="edge_chunk_id">S51_C08</data><data key="edge_json_path">None</data><data key="edge_evidence">Once this information is integrated using automation, the result is a CVSS-BE score that takes those environmental factors into consideration</data><data key="edge_extraction_method">minie</data><data key="edge_polarity">positive</data><data key="edge_modality">asserted</data></edge><edge id="oe_3e0d19253072825d" source="e_5a0c30db9530a8c8" target="e_4e841e8f418f5ece"><data key="edge_predicate_raw">be used to get</data><data key="edge_assertion_id">a_1ab74ad8986406de</data><data key="edge_source_id">S51</data><data key="edge_source_url">https://www.first.org/cvss/v4.0/user-guide</data><data key="edge_chunk_id">S51_C08</data><data key="edge_json_path">None</data><data key="edge_evidence">Additionally, the Asset Class and similar information can be used to get the vulnerability to the right engineers for remediation</data><data key="edge_extraction_method">minie</data><data key="edge_polarity">positive</data><data key="edge_modality">possible</data></edge><edge id="oe_1268d3538dc15218" source="e_9fae45ed82c56355" target="e_4e841e8f418f5ece"><data key="edge_predicate_raw">be used to get</data><data key="edge_assertion_id">a_d4ca4aba313ac756</data><data key="edge_source_id">S51</data><data key="edge_source_url">https://www.first.org/cvss/v4.0/user-guide</data><data key="edge_chunk_id">S51_C08</data><data key="edge_json_path">None</data><data key="edge_evidence">Additionally, the Asset Class and similar information can be used to get the vulnerability to the right engineers for remediation</data><data key="edge_extraction_method">minie</data><data key="edge_polarity">positive</data><data key="edge_modality">possible</data></edge><edge id="oe_b400d27c506c64c2" source="e_9f4bc004f1ab89c0" target="e_b49174ea90f56347"><data key="edge_predicate_raw">have been exploited which in</data><data key="edge_assertion_id">a_fd6f7176817e3178</data><data key="edge_source_id">S51</data><data key="edge_source_url">https://www.first.org/cvss/v4.0/user-guide</data><data key="edge_chunk_id">S51_C08</data><data key="edge_json_path">None</data><data key="edge_evidence">Knowing which vulnerabilities have been exploited in the past should have a significant impact on the resulting score</data><data key="edge_extraction_method">minie</data><data key="edge_polarity">positive</data><data key="edge_modality">asserted</data></edge><edge id="oe_eb223e72f5f2fb72" source="e_ebf0ee816f3b1469" target="e_754fa75553fa09be"><data key="edge_predicate_raw">have significant impact on</data><data key="edge_assertion_id">a_04d62e5b2025965d</data><data key="edge_source_id">S51</data><data key="edge_source_url">https://www.first.org/cvss/v4.0/user-guide</data><data key="edge_chunk_id">S51_C08</data><data key="edge_json_path">None</data><data key="edge_evidence">Knowing which vulnerabilities have been exploited in the past should have a significant impact on the resulting score</data><data key="edge_extraction_method">minie</data><data key="edge_polarity">positive</data><data key="edge_modality">asserted</data></edge><edge id="oe_438608e5bd768162" source="e_5a0fedab9d05fa10" target="e_3f3b075acc698583"><data key="edge_predicate_raw">Exploit</data><data key="edge_assertion_id">a_116b721ec8fd24eb</data><data key="edge_source_id">S51</data><data key="edge_source_url">https://www.first.org/cvss/v4.0/user-guide</data><data key="edge_chunk_id">S51_C09</data><data key="edge_json_path">None</data><data key="edge_evidence">There are many sources that can provide threat intelligence regarding the Exploit Maturity of vulnerabilities</data><data key="edge_extraction_method">heuristic</data><data key="edge_polarity">positive</data><data key="edge_modality">possible</data></edge><edge id="oe_c29fcd6467fe0935" source="e_ad16450d4d7b98f8" target="e_1ee64bd510d4d512"><data key="edge_predicate_raw">is recommended to gather</data><data key="edge_assertion_id">a_522cd262e27c6bb7</data><data key="edge_source_id">S51</data><data key="edge_source_url">https://www.first.org/cvss/v4.0/user-guide</data><data key="edge_chunk_id">S51_C09</data><data key="edge_json_path">None</data><data key="edge_evidence">It is important to understand that none of these sources are perfect and it is highly recommended to gather multiple sources of threat intelligence to improve the comprehensiveness and fidelity of the information being used to enrich your vulnerability data</data><data key="edge_extraction_method">minie</data><data key="edge_polarity">positive</data><data key="edge_modality">asserted</data></edge><edge id="oe_b04de0c68b3965e7" source="e_ad16450d4d7b98f8" target="e_85409dcf567a6c20"><data key="edge_predicate_raw">is recommended to gather</data><data key="edge_assertion_id">a_c333aed85e1811f2</data><data key="edge_source_id">S51</data><data key="edge_source_url">https://www.first.org/cvss/v4.0/user-guide</data><data key="edge_chunk_id">S51_C09</data><data key="edge_json_path">None</data><data key="edge_evidence">It is important to understand that none of these sources are perfect and it is highly recommended to gather multiple sources of threat intelligence to improve the comprehensiveness and fidelity of the information being used to enrich your vulnerability data</data><data key="edge_extraction_method">minie</data><data key="edge_polarity">positive</data><data key="edge_modality">asserted</data></edge><edge id="oe_5733cb877f3b1352" source="e_2079f7f0585a6a0c" target="e_1c52e1decc7a5f1e"><data key="edge_predicate_raw">be used to enrich</data><data key="edge_assertion_id">a_8bf27e4fb09968b1</data><data key="edge_source_id">S51</data><data key="edge_source_url">https://www.first.org/cvss/v4.0/user-guide</data><data key="edge_chunk_id">S51_C09</data><data key="edge_json_path">None</data><data key="edge_evidence">It is important to understand that none of these sources are perfect and it is highly recommended to gather multiple sources of threat intelligence to improve the comprehensiveness and fidelity of the information being used to enrich your vulnerability data</data><data key="edge_extraction_method">minie</data><data key="edge_polarity">positive</data><data key="edge_modality">asserted</data></edge><edge id="oe_fa2a1f62b6a99e0b" source="e_73bf974d84bb49a2" target="e_dbd1ba0cc63988dc"><data key="edge_predicate_raw">be matched against</data><data key="edge_assertion_id">a_f10851082209002b</data><data key="edge_source_id">S51</data><data key="edge_source_url">https://www.first.org/cvss/v4.0/user-guide</data><data key="edge_chunk_id">S51_C09</data><data key="edge_json_path">None</data><data key="edge_evidence">The application of the threat intelligence should be matched against vulnerability scan data using automation</data><data key="edge_extraction_method">minie</data><data key="edge_polarity">positive</data><data key="edge_modality">asserted</data></edge><edge id="oe_e062c550e45d4ef7" source="e_61641163de7ce9bc" target="e_7c308622fb827a74"><data key="edge_predicate_raw">be using</data><data key="edge_assertion_id">a_6f5ef446299f4fa3</data><data key="edge_source_id">S51</data><data key="edge_source_url">https://www.first.org/cvss/v4.0/user-guide</data><data key="edge_chunk_id">S51_C09</data><data key="edge_json_path">None</data><data key="edge_evidence">The application of the threat intelligence should be matched against vulnerability scan data using automation</data><data key="edge_extraction_method">minie</data><data key="edge_polarity">positive</data><data key="edge_modality">asserted</data></edge><edge id="oe_b1511f838b66404f" source="e_d4cff6070f136c90" target="e_1fff5eac1bcbc74f"><data key="edge_predicate_raw">constrain impacts When</data><data key="edge_assertion_id">a_f3babdba7baf7923</data><data key="edge_source_id">S51</data><data key="edge_source_url">https://www.first.org/cvss/v4.0/user-guide</data><data key="edge_chunk_id">S51_C09</data><data key="edge_json_path">None</data><data key="edge_evidence">When understanding when to assess the impact of vulnerabilities, analysts should constrain impacts to a reasonable, final outcome which they are confident an attacker is able to achieve</data><data key="edge_extraction_method">minie</data><data key="edge_polarity">positive</data><data key="edge_modality">asserted</data></edge><edge id="oe_50e979b2d3baaede" source="e_d4cff6070f136c90" target="e_35b2194131dcbc9a"><data key="edge_predicate_raw">constrain impacts to</data><data key="edge_assertion_id">a_12e26522f9283bb8</data><data key="edge_source_id">S51</data><data key="edge_source_url">https://www.first.org/cvss/v4.0/user-guide</data><data key="edge_chunk_id">S51_C09</data><data key="edge_json_path">None</data><data key="edge_evidence">When understanding when to assess the impact of vulnerabilities, analysts should constrain impacts to a reasonable, final outcome which they are confident an attacker is able to achieve</data><data key="edge_extraction_method">minie</data><data key="edge_polarity">positive</data><data key="edge_modality">asserted</data></edge><edge id="oe_7c9ad5080d8bd5ff" source="e_d4cff6070f136c90" target="e_57598c70746601d2"><data key="edge_predicate_raw">constrain</data><data key="edge_assertion_id">a_ab04af7a8a532664</data><data key="edge_source_id">S51</data><data key="edge_source_url">https://www.first.org/cvss/v4.0/user-guide</data><data key="edge_chunk_id">S51_C09</data><data key="edge_json_path">None</data><data key="edge_evidence">When understanding when to assess the impact of vulnerabilities, analysts should constrain impacts to a reasonable, final outcome which they are confident an attacker is able to achieve</data><data key="edge_extraction_method">minie</data><data key="edge_polarity">positive</data><data key="edge_modality">asserted</data></edge><edge id="oe_0177677ee42de059" source="e_78240206089584ed" target="e_263de49d43bd1b14"><data key="edge_predicate_raw">send trivial crafted request to</data><data key="edge_assertion_id">a_49f1e062864555d8</data><data key="edge_source_id">S51</data><data key="edge_source_url">https://www.first.org/cvss/v4.0/user-guide</data><data key="edge_chunk_id">S51_C09</data><data key="edge_json_path">None</data><data key="edge_evidence">In vulnerability 1, a remote, unauthenticated attacker can send a trivial, crafted request to a web server which causes the web server to disclose the plaintext password of the root (administrator) account</data><data key="edge_extraction_method">minie</data><data key="edge_polarity">positive</data><data key="edge_modality">possible</data></edge><edge id="oe_96e609a0d387989d" source="e_78240206089584ed" target="e_1ea78944d607055b"><data key="edge_predicate_raw">send</data><data key="edge_assertion_id">a_4541a2116e7f9660</data><data key="edge_source_id">S51</data><data key="edge_source_url">https://www.first.org/cvss/v4.0/user-guide</data><data key="edge_chunk_id">S51_C09</data><data key="edge_json_path">None</data><data key="edge_evidence">In vulnerability 1, a remote, unauthenticated attacker can send a trivial, crafted request to a web server which causes the web server to disclose the plaintext password of the root (administrator) account</data><data key="edge_extraction_method">minie</data><data key="edge_polarity">positive</data><data key="edge_modality">possible</data></edge><edge id="oe_7492c3910ceb8420" source="e_263de49d43bd1b14" target="e_a5bf3049399cbfde"><data key="edge_predicate_raw">causes web server to disclose plaintext password of</data><data key="edge_assertion_id">a_e5a58ef399899e48</data><data key="edge_source_id">S51</data><data key="edge_source_url">https://www.first.org/cvss/v4.0/user-guide</data><data key="edge_chunk_id">S51_C09</data><data key="edge_json_path">None</data><data key="edge_evidence">In vulnerability 1, a remote, unauthenticated attacker can send a trivial, crafted request to a web server which causes the web server to disclose the plaintext password of the root (administrator) account</data><data key="edge_extraction_method">minie</data><data key="edge_polarity">positive</data><data key="edge_modality">possible</data></edge><edge id="oe_2d957173ea2ff3b8" source="e_f2dca16215b933e8" target="e_4577be1b0308aebb"><data key="edge_predicate_raw">be send crafted request to</data><data key="edge_assertion_id">a_ec64fd3690033285</data><data key="edge_source_id">S51</data><data key="edge_source_url">https://www.first.org/cvss/v4.0/user-guide</data><data key="edge_chunk_id">S51_C09</data><data key="edge_json_path">None</data><data key="edge_evidence">The analyst only knows from the vulnerability description that the attacker has access to send a crafted request to the web server in order to exploit the vulnerability</data><data key="edge_extraction_method">minie</data><data key="edge_polarity">positive</data><data key="edge_modality">asserted</data></edge><edge id="oe_cc5c71da7f839bf9" source="e_f2dca16215b933e8" target="e_263de49d43bd1b14"><data key="edge_predicate_raw">be send crafted request to</data><data key="edge_assertion_id">a_e6ca0672c97aaacc</data><data key="edge_source_id">S51</data><data key="edge_source_url">https://www.first.org/cvss/v4.0/user-guide</data><data key="edge_chunk_id">S51_C09</data><data key="edge_json_path">None</data><data key="edge_evidence">The analyst only knows from the vulnerability description that the attacker has access to send a crafted request to the web server in order to exploit the vulnerability</data><data key="edge_extraction_method">minie</data><data key="edge_polarity">positive</data><data key="edge_modality">asserted</data></edge><edge id="oe_50c2ae7291ac9b90" source="e_9ed9f9c2275e8e7e" target="e_d73ec488c2d81f5f"><data key="edge_predicate_raw">stop</data><data key="edge_assertion_id">a_9c8c7c1e9a0b8945</data><data key="edge_source_id">S51</data><data key="edge_source_url">https://www.first.org/cvss/v4.0/user-guide</data><data key="edge_chunk_id">S51_C09</data><data key="edge_json_path">None</data><data key="edge_evidence">Impact should stop there; while an attacker may be able to use these credentials to later execute code as the administrator, it is not known that the attacker has access to a login prompt or method to execute commands with those credentials</data><data key="edge_extraction_method">minie</data><data key="edge_polarity">negative</data><data key="edge_modality">possible</data></edge><edge id="oe_0f411108d125aa71" source="e_dd36d981d34aaf68" target="e_3b3d0e812f84d35c"><data key="edge_predicate_raw">be execute code as</data><data key="edge_assertion_id">a_60759f7fbe6bb876</data><data key="edge_source_id">S51</data><data key="edge_source_url">https://www.first.org/cvss/v4.0/user-guide</data><data key="edge_chunk_id">S51_C09</data><data key="edge_json_path">None</data><data key="edge_evidence">Impact should stop there; while an attacker may be able to use these credentials to later execute code as the administrator, it is not known that the attacker has access to a login prompt or method to execute commands with those credentials</data><data key="edge_extraction_method">minie</data><data key="edge_polarity">negative</data><data key="edge_modality">possible</data></edge><edge id="oe_23e7c17d0872f272" source="e_dd36d981d34aaf68" target="e_0a74ab6b8c124112"><data key="edge_predicate_raw">be execute</data><data key="edge_assertion_id">a_6eeaf5117c215352</data><data key="edge_source_id">S51</data><data key="edge_source_url">https://www.first.org/cvss/v4.0/user-guide</data><data key="edge_chunk_id">S51_C09</data><data key="edge_json_path">None</data><data key="edge_evidence">Impact should stop there; while an attacker may be able to use these credentials to later execute code as the administrator, it is not known that the attacker has access to a login prompt or method to execute commands with those credentials</data><data key="edge_extraction_method">minie</data><data key="edge_polarity">negative</data><data key="edge_modality">possible</data></edge><edge id="oe_511bd57662f69468" source="e_fbf88db92200997c" target="e_dfd2e098a96fa540"><data key="edge_predicate_raw">represents direct serious loss of</data><data key="edge_assertion_id">a_83b734ddc15a11ae</data><data key="edge_source_id">S51</data><data key="edge_source_url">https://www.first.org/cvss/v4.0/user-guide</data><data key="edge_chunk_id">S51_C09</data><data key="edge_json_path">None</data><data key="edge_evidence">Gaining access to this password represents a direct, serious loss of Confidentiality only:</data><data key="edge_extraction_method">minie</data><data key="edge_polarity">positive</data><data key="edge_modality">asserted</data></edge><edge id="oe_6c6be7a6df709b14" source="e_5962be0a3867e263" target="e_1ad4fa20584b7a30"><data key="edge_predicate_raw">send trivial crafted request to</data><data key="edge_assertion_id">a_5fa90c015db8af45</data><data key="edge_source_id">S51</data><data key="edge_source_url">https://www.first.org/cvss/v4.0/user-guide</data><data key="edge_chunk_id">S51_C09</data><data key="edge_json_path">None</data><data key="edge_evidence">In vulnerability 2, a local, low-privileged user can send a trivial, crafted request to the operating system which causes it to disclose the plaintext password of the root (administrator) account</data><data key="edge_extraction_method">minie</data><data key="edge_polarity">positive</data><data key="edge_modality">possible</data></edge><edge id="oe_feb93fd775b77344" source="e_5962be0a3867e263" target="e_1ea78944d607055b"><data key="edge_predicate_raw">send</data><data key="edge_assertion_id">a_90b56c23fc5bf26b</data><data key="edge_source_id">S51</data><data key="edge_source_url">https://www.first.org/cvss/v4.0/user-guide</data><data key="edge_chunk_id">S51_C09</data><data key="edge_json_path">None</data><data key="edge_evidence">In vulnerability 2, a local, low-privileged user can send a trivial, crafted request to the operating system which causes it to disclose the plaintext password of the root (administrator) account</data><data key="edge_extraction_method">minie</data><data key="edge_polarity">positive</data><data key="edge_modality">possible</data></edge><edge id="oe_02625d5004b8bc31" source="e_1ad4fa20584b7a30" target="e_a5bf3049399cbfde"><data key="edge_predicate_raw">causes it to disclose plaintext password of</data><data key="edge_assertion_id">a_e8c362f0e777a070</data><data key="edge_source_id">S51</data><data key="edge_source_url">https://www.first.org/cvss/v4.0/user-guide</data><data key="edge_chunk_id">S51_C09</data><data key="edge_json_path">None</data><data key="edge_evidence">In vulnerability 2, a local, low-privileged user can send a trivial, crafted request to the operating system which causes it to disclose the plaintext password of the root (administrator) account</data><data key="edge_extraction_method">minie</data><data key="edge_polarity">positive</data><data key="edge_modality">possible</data></edge><edge id="oe_c087081c73742875" source="e_f6498126c94c6f96" target="e_26e3fb5566d7e9dd"><data key="edge_predicate_raw">knows from</data><data key="edge_assertion_id">a_85752cc727d4b8c9</data><data key="edge_source_id">S51</data><data key="edge_source_url">https://www.first.org/cvss/v4.0/user-guide</data><data key="edge_chunk_id">S51_C09</data><data key="edge_json_path">None</data><data key="edge_evidence">The analyst knows from the vulnerability description that the attacker has access to the operating system, and can log in as a local, low privileged attacker</data><data key="edge_extraction_method">minie</data><data key="edge_polarity">positive</data><data key="edge_modality">possible</data></edge><edge id="oe_2a25f919115bd91e" source="e_537e6ab50e8f2e44" target="e_f77593ea2106ed6a"><data key="edge_predicate_raw">log in as</data><data key="edge_assertion_id">a_fa2b23a9f1cf315a</data><data key="edge_source_id">S51</data><data key="edge_source_url">https://www.first.org/cvss/v4.0/user-guide</data><data key="edge_chunk_id">S51_C09</data><data key="edge_json_path">None</data><data key="edge_evidence">The analyst knows from the vulnerability description that the attacker has access to the operating system, and can log in as a local, low privileged attacker</data><data key="edge_extraction_method">minie</data><data key="edge_polarity">positive</data><data key="edge_modality">possible</data></edge><edge id="oe_ad7b8921f7b02330" source="e_fbf88db92200997c" target="e_53dd9263602ab61d"><data key="edge_predicate_raw">represents direct serious loss of</data><data key="edge_assertion_id">a_7eb17076e4d24419</data><data key="edge_source_id">S51</data><data key="edge_source_url">https://www.first.org/cvss/v4.0/user-guide</data><data key="edge_chunk_id">S51_C09</data><data key="edge_json_path">None</data><data key="edge_evidence">Gaining access to this password represents a direct, serious loss of Confidentiality, Integrity, and Availability because the analyst can reasonably issue commands as the root / administrator account (assume that the attacker could log out from their own account and log back in as root):</data><data key="edge_extraction_method">minie</data><data key="edge_polarity">positive</data><data key="edge_modality">possible</data></edge><edge id="oe_668660380c634e02" source="e_fbf88db92200997c" target="e_e56e3d4771ca46d9"><data key="edge_predicate_raw">represents direct serious loss of</data><data key="edge_assertion_id">a_2264022a0075a135</data><data key="edge_source_id">S51</data><data key="edge_source_url">https://www.first.org/cvss/v4.0/user-guide</data><data key="edge_chunk_id">S51_C09</data><data key="edge_json_path">None</data><data key="edge_evidence">Gaining access to this password represents a direct, serious loss of Confidentiality, Integrity, and Availability because the analyst can reasonably issue commands as the root / administrator account (assume that the attacker could log out from their own account and log back in as root):</data><data key="edge_ex