ce">In a distributed environment, a vulnerability in a component providing connectivity, protection, or authentication services to components in a different security domain should include assessment for the Subsequent System(s) if a successful attack impacts these other components</data><data key="edge_extraction_method">minie</data><data key="edge_polarity">positive</data><data key="edge_modality">asserted</data></edge><edge id="oe_7ea608f54cd6f404" source="e_33a6d55650df3130" target="e_546996a8b2a435a8"><data key="edge_predicate_raw">include assessment for</data><data key="edge_assertion_id">a_d9de1833fd6d541d</data><data key="edge_source_id">S51</data><data key="edge_source_url">https://www.first.org/cvss/v4.0/user-guide</data><data key="edge_chunk_id">S51_C13</data><data key="edge_json_path">None</data><data key="edge_evidence">In a distributed environment, a vulnerability in a component providing connectivity, protection, or authentication services to components in a different security domain should include assessment for the Subsequent System(s) if a successful attack impacts these other components</data><data key="edge_extraction_method">minie</data><data key="edge_polarity">positive</data><data key="edge_modality">asserted</data></edge><edge id="oe_497ee65aea9ae416" source="e_c47b9b8ad4cbc4ea" target="e_307218c17d7454bd"><data key="edge_predicate_raw">affects primary availability of</data><data key="edge_assertion_id">a_a2dd3529f74ff1d9</data><data key="edge_source_id">S51</data><data key="edge_source_url">https://www.first.org/cvss/v4.0/user-guide</data><data key="edge_chunk_id">S51_C13</data><data key="edge_json_path">None</data><data key="edge_evidence">For example, a vulnerability in a component such as a router, firewall, or authentication manager that affects the primary availability of one or more downstream components can impact a Subsequent System</data><data key="edge_extraction_method">minie</data><data key="edge_polarity">positive</data><data key="edge_modality">possible</data></edge><edge id="oe_3c8c133f85698867" source="e_55774da456650e7f" target="e_5ad6c123e5abaf11"><data key="edge_predicate_raw">impact Subsequent System For</data><data key="edge_assertion_id">a_68d9241e52572602</data><data key="edge_source_id">S51</data><data key="edge_source_url">https://www.first.org/cvss/v4.0/user-guide</data><data key="edge_chunk_id">S51_C13</data><data key="edge_json_path">None</data><data key="edge_evidence">For example, a vulnerability in a component such as a router, firewall, or authentication manager that affects the primary availability of one or more downstream components can impact a Subsequent System</data><data key="edge_extraction_method">minie</data><data key="edge_polarity">positive</data><data key="edge_modality">possible</data></edge><edge id="oe_d881fe988ac2d2a0" source="e_c90bbf9358513439" target="e_5ad6c123e5abaf11"><data key="edge_predicate_raw">impact Subsequent System For</data><data key="edge_assertion_id">a_1fb73ede966d41a5</data><data key="edge_source_id">S51</data><data key="edge_source_url">https://www.first.org/cvss/v4.0/user-guide</data><data key="edge_chunk_id">S51_C13</data><data key="edge_json_path">None</data><data key="edge_evidence">For example, a vulnerability in a component such as a router, firewall, or authentication manager that affects the primary availability of one or more downstream components can impact a Subsequent System</data><data key="edge_extraction_method">minie</data><data key="edge_polarity">positive</data><data key="edge_modality">possible</data></edge><edge id="oe_2d9e1acfb6ecb38d" source="e_45fe1524d128e332" target="e_5ad6c123e5abaf11"><data key="edge_predicate_raw">impact Subsequent System For</data><data key="edge_assertion_id">a_2eb96ff00f7a06ab</data><data key="edge_source_id">S51</data><data key="edge_source_url">https://www.first.org/cvss/v4.0/user-guide</data><data key="edge_chunk_id">S51_C13</data><data key="edge_json_path">None</data><data key="edge_evidence">For example, a vulnerability in a component such as a router, firewall, or authentication manager that affects the primary availability of one or more downstream components can impact a Subsequent System</data><data key="edge_extraction_method">minie</data><data key="edge_polarity">positive</data><data key="edge_modality">possible</data></edge><edge id="oe_b25e4ad6013c4101" source="e_55774da456650e7f" target="e_546996a8b2a435a8"><data key="edge_predicate_raw">impact</data><data key="edge_assertion_id">a_935d94711aa36a3b</data><data key="edge_source_id">S51</data><data key="edge_source_url">https://www.first.org/cvss/v4.0/user-guide</data><data key="edge_chunk_id">S51_C13</data><data key="edge_json_path">None</data><data key="edge_evidence">For example, a vulnerability in a component such as a router, firewall, or authentication manager that affects the primary availability of one or more downstream components can impact a Subsequent System</data><data key="edge_extraction_method">minie</data><data key="edge_polarity">positive</data><data key="edge_modality">possible</data></edge><edge id="oe_9a904fa498499912" source="e_c90bbf9358513439" target="e_546996a8b2a435a8"><data key="edge_predicate_raw">impact</data><data key="edge_assertion_id">a_c093d3db80b46fea</data><data key="edge_source_id">S51</data><data key="edge_source_url">https://www.first.org/cvss/v4.0/user-guide</data><data key="edge_chunk_id">S51_C13</data><data key="edge_json_path">None</data><data key="edge_evidence">For example, a vulnerability in a component such as a router, firewall, or authentication manager that affects the primary availability of one or more downstream components can impact a Subsequent System</data><data key="edge_extraction_method">minie</data><data key="edge_polarity">positive</data><data key="edge_modality">possible</data></edge><edge id="oe_f5eaf40f2820c22a" source="e_45fe1524d128e332" target="e_546996a8b2a435a8"><data key="edge_predicate_raw">impact</data><data key="edge_assertion_id">a_03fa8a2ddccdb255</data><data key="edge_source_id">S51</data><data key="edge_source_url">https://www.first.org/cvss/v4.0/user-guide</data><data key="edge_chunk_id">S51_C13</data><data key="edge_json_path">None</data><data key="edge_evidence">For example, a vulnerability in a component such as a router, firewall, or authentication manager that affects the primary availability of one or more downstream components can impact a Subsequent System</data><data key="edge_extraction_method">minie</data><data key="edge_polarity">positive</data><data key="edge_modality">possible</data></edge><edge id="oe_580a4ab7ccd8d9db" source="e_2676df0405400172" target="e_dde1241d5b7a5aa8"><data key="edge_predicate_raw">causes</data><data key="edge_assertion_id">a_664033144c5cbc2d</data><data key="edge_source_id">S51</data><data key="edge_source_url">https://www.first.org/cvss/v4.0/user-guide</data><data key="edge_chunk_id">S51_C13</data><data key="edge_json_path">None</data><data key="edge_evidence">However, if a successful attack either does not affect at all, or causes only negligible impact to other components, the vulnerability should be assessed as having no impact to a Subsequent System</data><data key="edge_extraction_method">minie</data><data key="edge_polarity">negative</data><data key="edge_modality">asserted</data></edge><edge id="oe_578de98f376ab1b7" source="e_dbd1ba0cc63988dc" target="e_6ab9b97627d2f379"><data key="edge_predicate_raw">be assessed as having impact to Subsequent System</data><data key="edge_assertion_id">a_a1191ef7035813d3</data><data key="edge_source_id">S51</data><data key="edge_source_url">https://www.first.org/cvss/v4.0/user-guide</data><data key="edge_chunk_id">S51_C13</data><data key="edge_json_path">None</data><data key="edge_evidence">However, if a successful attack either does not affect at all, or causes only negligible impact to other components, the vulnerability should be assessed as having no impact to a Subsequent System</data><data key="edge_extraction_method">minie</data><data key="edge_polarity">negative</data><data key="edge_modality">asserted</data></edge><edge id="oe_ef0bd58e4ad9fb52" source="e_2676df0405400172" target="e_d33d35b1f0e869ff"><data key="edge_predicate_raw">does affect</data><data key="edge_assertion_id">a_4b4f5e03b8cee00f</data><data key="edge_source_id">S51</data><data key="edge_source_url">https://www.first.org/cvss/v4.0/user-guide</data><data key="edge_chunk_id">S51_C13</data><data key="edge_json_path">None</data><data key="edge_evidence">Additionally, a vulnerability in a component designed to be deployed as part of a larger fault-tolerant topology should not be assessed with a Subsequent System impact if the fault-tolerance means a successful attack does not affect other components</data><data key="edge_extraction_method">minie</data><data key="edge_polarity">negative</data><data key="edge_modality">asserted</data></edge><edge id="oe_394bdf4fb31320b2" source="e_7c78e1084fcc7cc8" target="e_46d56e71076f9b45"><data key="edge_predicate_raw">be designed to be deployed as part of</data><data key="edge_assertion_id">a_ef914f80c819b7bf</data><data key="edge_source_id">S51</data><data key="edge_source_url">https://www.first.org/cvss/v4.0/user-guide</data><data key="edge_chunk_id">S51_C13</data><data key="edge_json_path">None</data><data key="edge_evidence">Additionally, a vulnerability in a component designed to be deployed as part of a larger fault-tolerant topology should not be assessed with a Subsequent System impact if the fault-tolerance means a successful attack does not affect other components</data><data key="edge_extraction_method">minie</data><data key="edge_polarity">negative</data><data key="edge_modality">asserted</data></edge><edge id="oe_a9bb2e679d8dd220" source="e_9e0568711abea57e" target="e_7ee1ff4a70457dd7"><data key="edge_predicate_raw">be provided by</data><data key="edge_assertion_id">a_2aeb7d565e5a19e2</data><data key="edge_source_id">S51</data><data key="edge_source_url">https://www.first.org/cvss/v4.0/user-guide</data><data key="edge_chunk_id">S51_C13</data><data key="edge_json_path">None</data><data key="edge_evidence">Any effect on additional services provided by the Vulnerable System is considered a secondary impact and not a Subsequent System impact</data><data key="edge_extraction_method">minie</data><data key="edge_polarity">negative</data><data key="edge_modality">asserted</data></edge><edge id="oe_1787a57425ffc094" source="e_5309f8f497111306" target="e_b35bf6705878f607"><data key="edge_predicate_raw">allows attacker to compromise other files on</data><data key="edge_assertion_id">a_db00bf0154e39137</data><data key="edge_source_id">S51</data><data key="edge_source_url">https://www.first.org/cvss/v4.0/user-guide</data><data key="edge_chunk_id">S51_C13</data><data key="edge_json_path">None</data><data key="edge_evidence">A vulnerability in a simple Portable Document Format (PDF) reader that allows an attacker to compromise other files on the same operating system when a victim opens a malicious PDF document is assessed as having no impact to a Subsequent System</data><data key="edge_extraction_method">minie</data><data key="edge_polarity">negative</data><data key="edge_modality">asserted</data></edge><edge id="oe_7786b3900a962948" source="e_f9848de32419b8b0" target="e_ae88557804e6bd47"><data key="edge_predicate_raw">is considered as</data><data key="edge_assertion_id">a_05b26457184ddc68</data><data key="edge_source_id">S51</data><data key="edge_source_url">https://www.first.org/cvss/v4.0/user-guide</data><data key="edge_chunk_id">S51_C13</data><data key="edge_json_path">None</data><data key="edge_evidence">A SQL injection vulnerability in a web application is not usually considered as causing impact to a Subsequent System assuming that the credentials are shared between web application and impacted SQL database, and therefore they are part of the same security scope</data><data key="edge_extraction_method">minie</data><data key="edge_polarity">negative</data><data key="edge_modality">asserted</data></edge><edge id="oe_20763091edbdff97" source="e_761cc9bc3cf32e49" target="e_b0d5a2d00bf0a58e"><data key="edge_predicate_raw">are shared between</data><data key="edge_assertion_id">a_b3aa70e8db1afb8a</data><data key="edge_source_id">S51</data><data key="edge_source_url">https://www.first.org/cvss/v4.0/user-guide</data><data key="edge_chunk_id">S51_C13</data><data key="edge_json_path">None</data><data key="edge_evidence">A SQL injection vulnerability in a web application is not usually considered as causing impact to a Subsequent System assuming that the credentials are shared between web application and impacted SQL database, and therefore they are part of the same security scope</data><data key="edge_extraction_method">minie</data><data key="edge_polarity">negative</data><data key="edge_modality">asserted</data></edge><edge id="oe_56ceb17fe8b59cc0" source="e_290d8da624d84fb0" target="e_c01a240dd22b190d"><data key="edge_predicate_raw">are part of</data><data key="edge_assertion_id">a_5149fe577f0fc6aa</data><data key="edge_source_id">S51</data><data key="edge_source_url">https://www.first.org/cvss/v4.0/user-guide</data><data key="edge_chunk_id">S51_C13</data><data key="edge_json_path">None</data><data key="edge_evidence">A SQL injection vulnerability in a web application is not usually considered as causing impact to a Subsequent System assuming that the credentials are shared between web application and impacted SQL database, and therefore they are part of the same security scope</data><data key="edge_extraction_method">minie</data><data key="edge_polarity">negative</data><data key="edge_modality">asserted</data></edge><edge id="oe_95d99423926f8bb6" source="e_dbd1ba0cc63988dc" target="e_263de49d43bd1b14"><data key="edge_predicate_raw">crashes</data><data key="edge_assertion_id">a_acb4227c423380f2</data><data key="edge_source_id">S51</data><data key="edge_source_url">https://www.first.org/cvss/v4.0/user-guide</data><data key="edge_chunk_id">S51_C13</data><data key="edge_json_path">None</data><data key="edge_evidence">A vulnerability that crashes a web server or SSH server is not considered impact to a Subsequent System since the impact is limited only to the service provided by the affected server</data><data key="edge_extraction_method">minie</data><data key="edge_polarity">negative</data><data key="edge_modality">asserted</data></edge><edge id="oe_290d40b28a9ac274" source="e_dbd1ba0cc63988dc" target="e_64acae39e69439e5"><data key="edge_predicate_raw">crashes</data><data key="edge_assertion_id">a_0d7009d4c74f9d40</data><data key="edge_source_id">S51</data><data key="edge_source_url">https://www.first.org/cvss/v4.0/user-guide</data><data key="edge_chunk_id">S51_C13</data><data key="edge_json_path">None</data><data key="edge_evidence">A vulnerability that crashes a web server or SSH server is not considered impact to a Subsequent System since the impact is limited only to the service provided by the affected server</data><data key="edge_extraction_method">minie</data><data key="edge_polarity">negative</data><data key="edge_modality">asserted</data></edge><edge id="oe_1d4018b3dcc1bfc0" source="e_9ed9f9c2275e8e7e" target="e_265d1c58ed249684"><data key="edge_predicate_raw">is limited to service provided by</data><data key="edge_assertion_id">a_e7c98d7e5bc8c5a9</data><data key="edge_source_id">S51</data><data key="edge_source_url">https://www.first.org/cvss/v4.0/user-guide</data><data key="edge_chunk_id">S51_C13</data><data key="edge_json_path">None</data><data key="edge_evidence">A vulnerability that crashes a web server or SSH server is not considered impact to a Subsequent System since the impact is limited only to the service provided by the affected server</data><data key="edge_extraction_method">minie</data><data key="edge_polarity">negative</data><data key="edge_modality">asserted</data></edge><edge id="oe_ee64e49fd6c8b44f" source="e_9111a79bb0a0398b" target="e_265d1c58ed249684"><data key="edge_predicate_raw">be provided by</data><data key="edge_assertion_id">a_648efbec91db7db6</data><data key="edge_source_id">S51</data><data key="edge_source_url">https://www.first.org/cvss/v4.0/user-guide</data><data key="edge_chunk_id">S51_C13</data><data key="edge_json_path">None</data><data key="edge_evidence">A vulnerability that crashes a web server or SSH server is not considered impact to a Subsequent System since the impact is limited only to the service provided by the affected server</data><data key="edge_extraction_method">minie</data><data key="edge_polarity">negative</data><data key="edge_modality">asserted</data></edge><edge id="oe_162aff9924d8afa8" source="e_48b9de94f1a079e8" target="e_546996a8b2a435a8"><data key="edge_predicate_raw">are considered constituent elements of</data><data key="edge_assertion_id">a_5f45e8d0b13d7752</data><data key="edge_source_id">S51</data><data key="edge_source_url">https://www.first.org/cvss/v4.0/user-guide</data><data key="edge_chunk_id">S51_C13</data><data key="edge_json_path">None</data><data key="edge_evidence">The impact on users is secondary and is not considered as impact to a Subsequent System as users are not considered constituent elements of the Subsequent System</data><data key="edge_extraction_method">minie</data><data key="edge_polarity">negative</data><data key="edge_modality">asserted</data></edge><edge id="oe_ef070f9528b69ac0" source="e_c2f8092b3084f8b9" target="e_979de52c5d68a67b"><data key="edge_predicate_raw">is considered as</data><data key="edge_assertion_id">a_8353950db51f10c9</data><data key="edge_source_id">S51</data><data key="edge_source_url">https://www.first.org/cvss/v4.0/user-guide</data><data key="edge_chunk_id">S51_C13</data><data key="edge_json_path">None</data><data key="edge_evidence">The impact on users is secondary and is not considered as impact to a Subsequent System as users are not considered constituent elements of the Subsequent System</data><data key="edge_extraction_method">minie</data><data key="edge_polarity">negative</data><data key="edge_modality">asserted</data></edge><edge id="oe_4eabeff931b5928d" source="e_dbd1ba0cc63988dc" target="e_ac163e65d54540dc"><data key="edge_predicate_raw">permits attacker to exhaust shared system resource such as</data><data key="edge_assertion_id">a_b766b394c98283d2</data><data key="edge_source_id">S51</data><data key="edge_source_url">https://www.first.org/cvss/v4.0/user-guide</data><data key="edge_chunk_id">S51_C13</data><data key="edge_json_path">None</data><data key="edge_evidence">A vulnerability that permits an attacker to exhaust a shared system resource, such as filling up a file system, should not be considered as causing impact to a Subsequent System</data><data key="edge_extraction_method">minie</data><data key="edge_polarity">negative</data><data key="edge_modality">asserted</data></edge><edge id="oe_4873db600aeeae10" source="e_dbd1ba0cc63988dc" target="e_ae88557804e6bd47"><data key="edge_predicate_raw">be considered as</data><data key="edge_assertion_id">a_06120fdbd0c5d660</data><data key="edge_source_id">S51</data><data key="edge_source_url">https://www.first.org/cvss/v4.0/user-guide</data><data key="edge_chunk_id">S51_C13</data><data key="edge_json_path">None</data><data key="edge_evidence">A vulnerability that permits an attacker to exhaust a shared system resource, such as filling up a file system, should not be considered as causing impact to a Subsequent System</data><data key="edge_extraction_method">minie</data><data key="edge_polarity">negative</data><data key="edge_modality">asserted</data></edge><edge id="oe_bee8b4d18bc79090" source="e_537e6ab50e8f2e44" target="e_e9457e2b248d9c8e"><data key="edge_predicate_raw">is acting under usual capabilities of</data><data key="edge_assertion_id">a_2fc98daff343ce86</data><data key="edge_source_id">S51</data><data key="edge_source_url">https://www.first.org/cvss/v4.0/user-guide</data><data key="edge_chunk_id">S51_C13</data><data key="edge_json_path">None</data><data key="edge_evidence">The attacker is still acting under the usual capabilities of the application and not breaching any security boundary</data><data key="edge_extraction_method">minie</data><data key="edge_polarity">negative</data><data key="edge_modality">asserted</data></edge><edge id="oe_ed88940ed3af4c47" source="e_e9457e2b248d9c8e" target="e_9f701b5a024de6bc"><data key="edge_predicate_raw">allows</data><data key="edge_assertion_id">a_c2e04ed2cea60012</data><data key="edge_source_id">S51</data><data key="edge_source_url">https://www.first.org/cvss/v4.0/user-guide</data><data key="edge_chunk_id">S51_C13</data><data key="edge_json_path">None</data><data key="edge_evidence">By exploiting a vulnerability in an application that allows users restricted access to resources shared with other components across multiple security scopes (e.g., operating system resources such as system files), an attacker can access resources that they should not be able to access</data><data key="edge_extraction_method">minie</data><data key="edge_polarity">negative</data><data key="edge_modality">possible</data></edge><edge id="oe_9ed25431e29fd414" source="e_c4631f903e1159e5" target="e_2c6e3da5d40bff1e"><data key="edge_predicate_raw">be shared with other components across</data><data key="edge_assertion_id">a_19f6e92160702e23</data><data key="edge_source_id">S51</data><data key="edge_source_url">https://www.first.org/cvss/v4.0/user-guide</data><data key="edge_chunk_id">S51_C13</data><data key="edge_json_path">None</data><data key="edge_evidence">By exploiting a vulnerability in an application that allows users restricted access to resources shared with other components across multiple security scopes (e.g., operating system resources such as system files), an attacker can access resources that they should not be able to access</data><data key="edge_extraction_method">minie</data><data key="edge_polarity">negative</data><data key="edge_modality">possible</data></edge><edge id="oe_f2a93f379ada2311" source="e_537e6ab50e8f2e44" target="e_e9457e2b248d9c8e"><data key="edge_predicate_raw">access resources that they be able to access By exploiting vulnerability in</data><data key="edge_assertion_id">a_5c726ecc1acd46c2</data><data key="edge_source_id">S51</data><data key="edge_source_url">https://www.first.org/cvss/v4.0/user-guide</data><data key="edge_chunk_id">S51_C13</data><data key="edge_json_path">None</data><data key="edge_evidence">By exploiting a vulnerability in an application that allows users restricted access to resources shared with other components across multiple security scopes (e.g., operating system resources such as system files), an attacker can access resources that they should not be able to access</data><data key="edge_extraction_method">minie</data><data key="edge_polarity">negative</data><data key="edge_modality">possible</data></edge><edge id="oe_d199024d26083bce" source="e_290d8da624d84fb0" target="e_f2dca16215b933e8"><data key="edge_predicate_raw">be able to</data><data key="edge_assertion_id">a_b1b835a74c461836</data><data key="edge_source_id">S51</data><data key="edge_source_url">https://www.first.org/cvss/v4.0/user-guide</data><data key="edge_chunk_id">S51_C13</data><data key="edge_json_path">None</data><data key="edge_evidence">By exploiting a vulnerability in an application that allows users restricted access to resources shared with other components across multiple security scopes (e.g., operating system resources such as system files), an attacker can access resources that they should not be able to access</data><data key="edge_extraction_method">minie</data><data key="edge_polarity">negative</data><data key="edge_modality">possible</data></edge><edge id="oe_86afc0a20945d5ca" source="e_537e6ab50e8f2e44" target="e_241d976726cdd325"><data key="edge_predicate_raw">access resources that they be able to access such as</data><data key="edge_assertion_id">a_56ca5acc9eeaee2f</data><data key="edge_source_id">S51</data><data key="edge_source_url">https://www.first.org/cvss/v4.0/user-guide</data><data key="edge_chunk_id">S51_C14</data><data key="edge_json_path">None</data><data key="edge_evidence">such as system files), an attacker can access resources that they should not be able to access</data><data key="edge_extraction_method">minie</data><data key="edge_polarity">negative</data><data key="edge_modality">possible</data></edge><edge id="oe_af984907ea8474f6" source="e_290d8da624d84fb0" target="e_f2dca16215b933e8"><data key="edge_predicate_raw">be able to</data><data key="edge_assertion_id">a_3789cce5e4ff103d</data><data key="edge_source_id">S51</data><data key="edge_source_url">https://www.first.org/cvss/v4.0/user-guide</data><data key="edge_chunk_id">S51_C14</data><data key="edge_json_path">None</data><data key="edge_evidence">such as system files), an attacker can access resources that they should not be able to access</data><data key="edge_extraction_method">minie</data><data key="edge_polarity">negative</data><data key="edge_modality">possible</data></edge><edge id="oe_5d99a9ef9df89579" source="e_e9457e2b248d9c8e" target="e_067458e2fc3518b8"><data key="edge_predicate_raw">implements</data><data key="edge_assertion_id">a_d6533795b71721fe</data><data key="edge_source_id">S51</data><data key="edge_source_url">https://www.first.org/cvss/v4.0/user-guide</data><data key="edge_chunk_id">S51_C14</data><data key="edge_json_path">None</data><data key="edge_evidence">A vulnerability in an application that implements its own security domain which allows attackers to affect resources outside its security scope should be assessed as having Subsequent System impact</data><data key="edge_extraction_method">minie</data><data key="edge_polarity">positive</data><data key="edge_modality">asserted</data></edge><edge id="oe_17902dc4674fbeaa" source="e_067458e2fc3518b8" target="e_aa5c471d3ab8993a"><data key="edge_predicate_raw">allows attackers to affect resources outside</data><data key="edge_assertion_id">a_5e3d62965f16834c</data><data key="edge_source_id">S51</data><data key="edge_source_url">https://www.first.org/cvss/v4.0/user-guide</data><data key="edge_chunk_id">S51_C14</data><data key="edge_json_path">None</data><data key="edge_evidence">A vulnerability in an application that implements its own security domain which allows attackers to affect resources outside its security scope should be assessed as having Subsequent System impact</data><data key="edge_extraction_method">minie</data><data key="edge_polarity">positive</data><data key="edge_modality">asserted</data></edge><edge id="oe_54996194fa40eabf" source="e_067458e2fc3518b8" target="e_c4631f903e1159e5"><data key="edge_predicate_raw">allows attackers to affect</data><data key="edge_assertion_id">a_663483e621cd42b6</data><data key="edge_source_id">S51</data><data key="edge_source_url">https://www.first.org/cvss/v4.0/user-guide</data><data key="edge_chunk_id">S51_C14</data><data key="edge_json_path">None</data><data key="edge_evidence">A vulnerability in an application that implements its own security domain which allows attackers to affect resources outside its security scope should be assessed as having Subsequent System impact</data><data key="edge_extraction_method">minie</data><data key="edge_polarity">positive</data><data key="edge_modality">asserted</data></edge><edge id="oe_f59cfcab69cf3332" source="e_a906ea46569d27f0" target="e_d427909b481dc85e"><data key="edge_predicate_raw">be assessed as</data><data key="edge_assertion_id">a_79447e7af3054460</data><data key="edge_source_id">S51</data><data key="edge_source_url">https://www.first.org/cvss/v4.0/user-guide</data><data key="edge_chunk_id">S51_C14</data><data key="edge_json_path">None</data><data key="edge_evidence">A vulnerability in an application that implements its own security domain which allows attackers to affect resources outside its security scope should be assessed as having Subsequent System impact</data><data key="edge_extraction_method">minie</data><data key="edge_polarity">positive</data><data key="edge_modality">asserted</data></edge><edge id="oe_9c4eb39129530d48" source="e_830672f45c1d3680" target="e_cd3989223926eb75"><data key="edge_predicate_raw">be governed by</data><data key="edge_assertion_id">a_9335c83f32353923</data><data key="edge_source_id">S51</data><data key="edge_source_url">https://www.first.org/cvss/v4.0/user-guide</data><data key="edge_chunk_id">S51_C14</data><data key="edge_json_path">None</data><data key="edge_evidence">This assumes the application provides no features for users to access resources governed by a higher-level security domain shared with other components across multiple security scopes (e.g., the resources of the underlying operating system)</data><data key="edge_extraction_method">minie</data><data key="edge_polarity">negative</data><data key="edge_modality">asserted</data></edge><edge id="oe_60ab6b986583d3fc" source="e_5d179dc0effbd161" target="e_2c6e3da5d40bff1e"><data key="edge_predicate_raw">be shared with other components across</data><data key="edge_assertion_id">a_640f1513c9c958bc</data><data key="edge_source_id">S51</data><data key="edge_source_url">https://www.first.org/cvss/v4.0/user-guide</data><data key="edge_chunk_id">S51_C14</data><data key="edge_json_path">None</data><data key="edge_evidence">This assumes the application provides no features for users to access resources governed by a higher-level security domain shared with other components across multiple security scopes (e.g., the resources of the underlying operating system)</data><data key="edge_extraction_method">minie</data><data key="edge_polarity">negative</data><data key="edge_modality">asserted</data></edge><edge id="oe_30eab2b8d791c241" source="e_48b9de94f1a079e8" target="e_7a8de3a356ca250f"><data key="edge_predicate_raw">to interact beyond</data><data key="edge_assertion_id">a_c5ac093025047041</data><data key="edge_source_id">S51</data><data key="edge_source_url">https://www.first.org/cvss/v4.0/user-guide</data><data key="edge_chunk_id">S51_C14</data><data key="edge_json_path">None</data><data key="edge_evidence">One example would be a web application that allows users to read and modify web pages and files only under the web application’s installation paths, and provides no feature for users to interact beyond these paths</data><data key="edge_extraction_method">minie</data><data key="edge_polarity">negative</data><data key="edge_modality">asserted</data></edge><edge id="oe_54e697cc7f423141" source="e_b0d5a2d00bf0a58e" target="e_ccc766b713b4ea69"><data key="edge_predicate_raw">allows users to read web pages only under</data><data key="edge_assertion_id">a_1de17197b2f896d0</data><data key="edge_source_id">S51</data><data key="edge_source_url">https://www.first.org/cvss/v4.0/user-guide</data><data key="edge_chunk_id">S51_C14</data><data key="edge_json_path">None</data><data key="edge_evidence">One example would be a web application that allows users to read and modify web pages and files only under the web application’s installation paths, and provides no feature for users to interact beyond these paths</data><data key="edge_extraction_method">minie</data><data key="edge_polarity">negative</data><data key="edge_modality">asserted</data></edge><edge id="oe_6905b9fb4ca8da8b" source="e_b0d5a2d00bf0a58e" target="e_ccc766b713b4ea69"><data key="edge_predicate_raw">allows users to read files only under</data><data key="edge_assertion_id">a_b827b553353a8f7d</data><data key="edge_source_id">S51</data><data key="edge_source_url">https://www.first.org/cvss/v4.0/user-guide</data><data key="edge_chunk_id">S51_C14</data><data key="edge_json_path">None</data><data key="edge_evidence">One example would be a web application that allows users to read and modify web pages and files only under the web application’s installation paths, and provides no feature for users to interact beyond these paths</data><data key="edge_extraction_method">minie</data><data key="edge_polarity">negative</data><data key="edge_modality">asserted</data></edge><edge id="oe_25cd6a148bafcdfe" source="e_b0d5a2d00bf0a58e" target="e_27d46fe5356aa741"><data key="edge_predicate_raw">allows users to read</data><data key="edge_assertion_id">a_5fad82c7ae29f752</data><data key="edge_source_id">S51</data><data key="edge_source_url">https://www.first.org/cvss/v4.0/user-guide</data><data key="edge_chunk_id">S51_C14</data><data key="edge_json_path">None</data><data key="edge_evidence">One example would be a web application that allows users to read and modify web pages and files only under the web application’s installation paths, and provides no feature for users to interact beyond these paths</data><data key="edge_extraction_method">minie</data><data key="edge_polarity">negative</data><data key="edge_modality">asserted</data></edge><edge id="oe_bf3392f42139c381" source="e_b0d5a2d00bf0a58e" target="e_b08ea7e3d08237a2"><data key="edge_predicate_raw">allows users to read</data><data key="edge_assertion_id">a_94e6136a4d3aa854</data><data key="edge_source_id">S51</data><data key="edge_source_url">https://www.first.org/cvss/v4.0/user-guide</data><data key="edge_chunk_id">S51_C14</data><data key="edge_json_path">None</data><data key="edge_evidence">One example would be a web application that allows users to read and modify web pages and files only under the web application’s installation paths, and provides no feature for users to interact beyond these paths</data><data key="edge_extraction_method">minie</data><data key="edge_polarity">negative</data><data key="edge_modality">asserted</data></edge><edge id="oe_f54406d645ec46f3" source="e_b0d5a2d00bf0a58e" target="e_85e8f3bb29189db9"><data key="edge_predicate_raw">allows users</data><data key="edge_assertion_id">a_dc16f508141e6773</data><data key="edge_source_id">S51</data><data key="edge_source_url">https://www.first.org/cvss/v4.0/user-guide</data><data key="edge_chunk_id">S51_C14</data><data key="edge_json_path">None</data><data key="edge_evidence">One example would be a web application that allows users to read and modify web pages and files only under the web application’s installation paths, and provides no feature for users to interact beyond these paths</data><data key="edge_extraction_method">minie</data><data key="edge_polarity">negative</data><data key="edge_modality">asserted</data></edge><edge id="oe_4c71368af222940a" source="e_a906ea46569d27f0" target="e_25ed22a879cd36e2"><data key="edge_predicate_raw">be allowing malicious user to</data><data key="edge_assertion_id">a_b4160e8013c1af7e</data><data key="edge_source_id">S51</data><data key="edge_source_url">https://www.first.org/cvss/v4.0/user-guide</data><data key="edge_chunk_id">S51_C14</data><data key="edge_json_path">None</data><data key="edge_evidence">A vulnerability in this application allowing a malicious user to access operating system files unrelated to this application is considered impact to a Subsequent System</data><data key="edge_extraction_method">minie</data><data key="edge_polarity">positive</data><data key="edge_modality">asserted</data></edge><edge id="oe_543314478fcf0c88" source="e_3ab600ffc9f65c6a" target="e_5d8f863ffeae224e"><data key="edge_predicate_raw">files</data><data key="edge_assertion_id">a_d967f1203170b100</data><data key="edge_source_id">S51</data><data key="edge_source_url">https://www.first.org/cvss/v4.0/user-guide</data><data key="edge_chunk_id">S51_C14</data><data key="edge_json_path">None</data><data key="edge_evidence">A vulnerability in this application allowing a malicious user to access operating system files unrelated to this application is considered impact to a Subsequent System</data><data key="edge_extraction_method">minie</data><data key="edge_polarity">positive</data><data key="edge_modality">asserted</data></edge><edge id="oe_4801234b0dd20540" source="e_dbd1ba0cc63988dc" target="e_571bc10d653316b8"><data key="edge_predicate_raw">is assessed with Attack Vector of</data><data key="edge_assertion_id">a_4324f41b6d3e47df</data><data key="edge_source_id">S51</data><data key="edge_source_url">https://www.first.org/cvss/v4.0/user-guide</data><data key="edge_chunk_id">S51_C14</data><data key="edge_json_path">None</data><data key="edge_evidence">If a vulnerability is assessed with an Attack Vector (AV) of Network (N) and the analyst has high confidence that the vulnerable system is deployed on a secure network unavailable from the Internet, Modified Attack Vector (MAV) may be assessed as Adjacent, reducing the resulting severity score</data><data key="edge_extraction_method">minie</data><data key="edge_polarity">positive</data><data key="edge_modality">possible</data></edge><edge id="oe_032325b66c69699c" source="e_7ee1ff4a70457dd7" target="e_f26720649f642157"><data key="edge_predicate_raw">is deployed on secure network unavailable from</data><data key="edge_assertion_id">a_dbc09f4b5986edc8</data><data key="edge_source_id">S51</data><data key="edge_source_url">https://www.first.org/cvss/v4.0/user-guide</data><data key="edge_chunk_id">S51_C14</data><data key="edge_json_path">None</data><data key="edge_evidence">If a vulnerability is assessed with an Attack Vector (AV) of Network (N) and the analyst has high confidence that the vulnerable system is deployed on a secure network unavailable from the Internet, Modified Attack Vector (MAV) may be assessed as Adjacent, reducing the resulting severity score</data><data key="edge_extraction_method">minie</data><data key="edge_polarity">positive</data><data key="edge_modality">possible</data></edge><edge id="oe_ed9e35aabb9ec674" source="e_4dc239162c062c58" target="e_f1f0149335109bc6"><data key="edge_predicate_raw">be used</data><data key="edge_assertion_id">a_c2c63df5c086a7b7</data><data key="edge_source_id">S51</data><data key="edge_source_url">https://www.first.org/cvss/v4.0/user-guide</data><data key="edge_chunk_id">S51_C14</data><data key="edge_json_path">None</data><data key="edge_evidence">When assessing the impact of a vulnerability in a library, independent of any adopting program or implementation, the analyst will often be unable to take into account the ways in which the library might be used</data><data key="edge_extraction_method">minie</data><data key="edge_polarity">positive</data><data key="edge_modality">possible</data></edge><edge id="oe_b9edfe9e1234f1f7" source="e_e042c3358a8c88e7" target="e_cb9f483ceb3dfe87"><data key="edge_predicate_raw">requires</data><data key="edge_assertion_id">a_9ab9c7016dbfc0ba</data><data key="edge_source_id">S51</data><data key="edge_source_url">https://www.first.org/cvss/v4.0/user-guide</data><data key="edge_chunk_id">S51_C14</data><data key="edge_json_path">None</data><data key="edge_evidence">While specific products using the library should generate CVSS scores specific to how they use the library, assessing the library itself requires assumptions to be made</data><data key="edge_extraction_method">heuristic</data><data key="edge_polarity">positive</data><data key="edge_modality">asserted</data></edge><edge id="oe_9d6beefacec1f89e" source="e_f6498126c94c6f96" target="e_670573848fbf41cb"><data key="edge_predicate_raw">account for</data><data key="edge_assertion_id">a_ea09e6e9508f7df8</data><data key="edge_source_id">S51</data><data key="edge_source_url">https://www.first.org/cvss/v4.0/user-guide</data><data key="edge_chunk_id">S51_C14</data><data key="edge_json_path">None</data><data key="edge_evidence">The analyst should account for the reasonable worst-case scenario</data><data key="edge_extraction_method">minie</data><data key="edge_polarity">positive</data><data key="edge_modality">asserted</data></edge><edge id="oe_46e7f927ba76ebfb" source="e_4dc239162c062c58" target="e_82307ea50e8b2f0c"><data key="edge_predicate_raw">performs</data><data key="edge_assertion_id">a_9c498013d885c3ac</data><data key="edge_source_id">S51</data><data key="edge_source_url">https://www.first.org/cvss/v4.0/user-guide</data><data key="edge_chunk_id">S51_C14</data><data key="edge_json_path">None</data><data key="edge_evidence">For example, a library that performs image conversion would reasonably be used by programs that accept images from untrusted sources over a network</data><data key="edge_extraction_method">minie</data><data key="edge_polarity">positive</data><data key="edge_modality">asserted</data></edge><edge id="oe_0d5d78c7148b5042" source="e_4dc239162c062c58" target="e_5ad6c123e5abaf11"><data key="edge_predicate_raw">be used by programs For</data><data key="edge_assertion_id">a_e3bf713505a7f35c</data><data key="edge_source_id">S51</data><data key="edge_source_url">https://www.first.org/cvss/v4.0/user-guide</data><data key="edge_chunk_id">S51_C14</data><data key="edge_json_path">None</data><data key="edge_evidence">For example, a library that performs image conversion would reasonably be used by programs that accept images from untrusted sources over a network</data><data key="edge_extraction_method">minie</data><data key="edge_polarity">positive</data><data key="edge_modality">asserted</data></edge><edge id="oe_47992e350b234d1f" source="e_4dc239162c062c58" target="e_e380413965b09830"><data key="edge_predicate_raw">be used by</data><data key="edge_assertion_id">a_aedb99f8b93f4948</data><data key="edge_source_id">S51</data><data key="edge_source_url">https://www.first.org/cvss/v4.0/user-guide</data><data key="edge_chunk_id">S51_C14</data><data key="edge_json_path">None</data><data key="edge_evidence">For example, a library that performs image conversion would reasonably be used by programs that accept images from untrusted sources over a network</data><data key="edge_extraction_method">minie</data><data key="edge_polarity">positive</data><data key="edge_modality">asserted</data></edge><edge id="oe_41f6c5ccd4004692" source="e_e380413965b09830" target="e_28c249862a8f9c3e"><data key="edge_predicate_raw">accept images from</data><data key="edge_assertion_id">a_50c71b9b0538814b</data><data key="edge_source_id">S51</data><data key="edge_source_url">https://www.first.org/cvss/v4.0/user-guide</data><data key="edge_chunk_id">S51_C14</data><data key="edge_json_path">None</data><data key="edge_evidence">For example, a library that performs image conversion would reasonably be used by programs that accept images from untrusted sources over a network</data><data key="edge_extraction_method">minie</data><data key="edge_polarity">positive</data><data key="edge_modality">asserted</data></edge><edge id="oe_0ab965155ff4be56" source="e_e380413965b09830" target="e_571bc10d653316b8"><data key="edge_predicate_raw">accept images over</data><data key="edge_assertion_id">a_98ce5f7fc387632e</data><data key="edge_source_id">S51</data><data key="edge_source_url">https://www.first.org/cvss/v4.0/user-guide</data><data key="edge_chunk_id">S51_C14</data><data key="edge_json_path">None</data><data key="edge_evidence">For example, a library that performs image conversion would reasonably be used by programs that accept images from untrusted sources over a network</data><data key="edge_extraction_method">minie</data><data key="edge_polarity">positive</data><data key="edge_modality">asserted</data></edge><edge id="oe_a9eed7af742387a9" source="e_e380413965b09830" target="e_2bf2d33645237391"><data key="edge_predicate_raw">accept</data><data key="edge_assertion_id">a_f97a66460cdab5ef</data><data key="edge_source_id">S51</data><data key="edge_source_url">https://www.first.org/cvss/v4.0/user-guide</data><data key="edge_chunk_id">S51_C14</data><data key="edge_json_path">None</data><data key="edge_evidence">For example, a library that performs image conversion would reasonably be used by programs that accept images from untrusted sources over a network</data><data key="edge_extraction_method">minie</data><data key="edge_polarity">positive</data><data key="edge_modality">asserted</data></edge><edge id="oe_9a4bc41a03ccaeff" source="e_ad16450d4d7b98f8" target="e_9ba4118400b2b8a1"><data key="edge_predicate_raw">pass them In</data><data key="edge_assertion_id">a_71155d47d99a9d6a</data><data key="edge_source_id">S51</data><data key="edge_source_url">https://www.first.org/cvss/v4.0/user-guide</data><data key="edge_chunk_id">S51_C14</data><data key="edge_json_path">None</data><data key="edge_evidence">In the reasonable worst-case, it would pass them to the library without checking the validity of the images</data><data key="edge_extraction_method">minie</data><data key="edge_polarity">negative</data><data key="edge_modality">asserted</data></edge><edge id="oe_2b2fe468ddb8fae3" source="e_ad16450d4d7b98f8" target="e_4dc239162c062c58"><data key="edge_predicate_raw">pass them to</data><data key="edge_assertion_id">a_e8f3df3387836c6a</data><data key="edge_source_id">S51</data><data key="edge_source_url">https://www.first.org/cvss/v4.0/user-guide</data><data key="edge_chunk_id">S51_C14</data><data key="edge_json_path">None</data><data key="edge_evidence">In the reasonable worst-case, it would pass them to the library without checking the validity of the images</data><data key="edge_extraction_method">minie</data><data key="edge_polarity">negative</data><data key="edge_modality">asserted</data></edge><edge id="oe_cbd2d7038b92bb0c" source="e_ad16450d4d7b98f8" target="e_2bf2d33645237391"><data key="edge_predicate_raw">pass them without checking validity of</data><data key="edge_assertion_id">a_ada5478bddce3566</data><data key="edge_source_id">S51</data><data key="edge_source_url">https://www.first.org/cvss/v4.0/user-guide</data><data key="edge_chunk_id">S51_C14</data><data key="edge_json_path">None</data><data key="edge_evidence">In the reasonable worst-case, it would pass them to the library without checking the validity of the images</data><data key="edge_extraction_method">minie</data><data key="edge_polarity">negative</data><data key="edge_modality">asserted</data></edge><edge id="oe_989da9cb287