ction_method">minie</data><data key="edge_polarity">positive</data><data key="edge_modality">possible</data></edge><edge id="oe_c07f01d49817917f" source="e_bebdf23dc9b18acb" target="e_0a74ab6b8c124112"><data key="edge_predicate_raw">exploit</data><data key="edge_assertion_id">a_f3ecc3f5bb710e1c</data><data key="edge_source_id">S51</data><data key="edge_source_url">https://www.first.org/cvss/v4.0/user-guide</data><data key="edge_chunk_id">S51_C21</data><data key="edge_json_path">None</data><data key="edge_evidence">Proof-of-Concept exploit code: Software or sufficient technical details that can be used to demonstrate the existence of a vulnerability</data><data key="edge_extraction_method">minie</data><data key="edge_polarity">positive</data><data key="edge_modality">possible</data></edge><edge id="oe_f31163e2a95e0495" source="e_a9cafd81fad645c8" target="e_dbd1ba0cc63988dc"><data key="edge_predicate_raw">be targeting</data><data key="edge_assertion_id">a_a5bf48cab938399a</data><data key="edge_source_id">S51</data><data key="edge_source_url">https://www.first.org/cvss/v4.0/user-guide</data><data key="edge_chunk_id">S51_C21</data><data key="edge_json_path">None</data><data key="edge_evidence">Reported: Based on applicable threat intelligence, activity targeting the vulnerability is known by someone other than the attacker and the victim</data><data key="edge_extraction_method">minie</data><data key="edge_polarity">positive</data><data key="edge_modality">reported</data></edge><edge id="oe_f00647601d91ee86" source="e_de83c7ab7e48010a" target="e_537e6ab50e8f2e44"><data key="edge_predicate_raw">is known by someone other than</data><data key="edge_assertion_id">a_014a3347e19f9b1f</data><data key="edge_source_id">S51</data><data key="edge_source_url">https://www.first.org/cvss/v4.0/user-guide</data><data key="edge_chunk_id">S51_C21</data><data key="edge_json_path">None</data><data key="edge_evidence">Reported: Based on applicable threat intelligence, activity targeting the vulnerability is known by someone other than the attacker and the victim</data><data key="edge_extraction_method">minie</data><data key="edge_polarity">positive</data><data key="edge_modality">reported</data></edge><edge id="oe_1435b4b30c7e6afa" source="e_de83c7ab7e48010a" target="e_997847e8cee53e6b"><data key="edge_predicate_raw">is known by someone other than</data><data key="edge_assertion_id">a_734e73e8afc8b955</data><data key="edge_source_id">S51</data><data key="edge_source_url">https://www.first.org/cvss/v4.0/user-guide</data><data key="edge_chunk_id">S51_C21</data><data key="edge_json_path">None</data><data key="edge_evidence">Reported: Based on applicable threat intelligence, activity targeting the vulnerability is known by someone other than the attacker and the victim</data><data key="edge_extraction_method">minie</data><data key="edge_polarity">positive</data><data key="edge_modality">reported</data></edge><edge id="oe_34e1dc5031078e43" source="e_4bf310a0cf7b17dd" target="e_d5e564049d5c97e4"><data key="edge_predicate_raw">used</data><data key="edge_assertion_id">a_688fa9ab9f2be7c0</data><data key="edge_source_id">S51</data><data key="edge_source_url">https://www.first.org/cvss/v4.0/user-guide</data><data key="edge_chunk_id">S51_C22</data><data key="edge_json_path">None</data><data key="edge_evidence">Resource: Asset used or consumed during the execution of a process.9 Examples of resources include (but are not limited to) file contents, file identifiers, memory pointers, memory contents, CPU cycles, and network bandwidth</data><data key="edge_extraction_method">heuristic</data><data key="edge_polarity">negative</data><data key="edge_modality">asserted</data></edge><edge id="oe_3e9f9a9f95903683" source="e_f65918fd9e091c28" target="e_93d8650fe6b85a54"><data key="edge_predicate_raw">direct how</data><data key="edge_assertion_id">a_60d0bc3151d9151a</data><data key="edge_source_id">S51</data><data key="edge_source_url">https://www.first.org/cvss/v4.0/user-guide</data><data key="edge_chunk_id">S51_C22</data><data key="edge_json_path">None</data><data key="edge_evidence">Security policy: A set of policy rules (or principles) that direct how a system (or an organization) provides security services to protect sensitive and critical system resources.11</data><data key="edge_extraction_method">minie</data><data key="edge_polarity">positive</data><data key="edge_modality">asserted</data></edge><edge id="oe_a3729ea80f68678a" source="e_9a03a9aedb645c2d" target="e_7bc66a71c6cc9944"><data key="edge_predicate_raw">provides</data><data key="edge_assertion_id">a_f2bd9c7264c6cdc0</data><data key="edge_source_id">S51</data><data key="edge_source_url">https://www.first.org/cvss/v4.0/user-guide</data><data key="edge_chunk_id">S51_C22</data><data key="edge_json_path">None</data><data key="edge_evidence">Security policy: A set of policy rules (or principles) that direct how a system (or an organization) provides security services to protect sensitive and critical system resources.11</data><data key="edge_extraction_method">minie</data><data key="edge_polarity">positive</data><data key="edge_modality">asserted</data></edge><edge id="oe_73383c7377539d37" source="e_39103e9a67affb14" target="e_9b4a10d05a1f7a60"><data key="edge_predicate_raw">be simplify Software including exploit frameworks such as</data><data key="edge_assertion_id">a_c243397eed5503ee</data><data key="edge_source_id">S51</data><data key="edge_source_url">https://www.first.org/cvss/v4.0/user-guide</data><data key="edge_chunk_id">S51_C22</data><data key="edge_json_path">None</data><data key="edge_evidence">Solutions to simplify: Software that makes exploitation of the vulnerability trivial, including exploit frameworks, such as Metasploit or Cobalt Strike, or other tools that work reliably and against many different systems</data><data key="edge_extraction_method">minie</data><data key="edge_polarity">positive</data><data key="edge_modality">asserted</data></edge><edge id="oe_3ebecf0f25259997" source="e_39103e9a67affb14" target="e_a8b8d2b831403f96"><data key="edge_predicate_raw">be simplify Software including exploit frameworks such as</data><data key="edge_assertion_id">a_fc842394105bc219</data><data key="edge_source_id">S51</data><data key="edge_source_url">https://www.first.org/cvss/v4.0/user-guide</data><data key="edge_chunk_id">S51_C22</data><data key="edge_json_path">None</data><data key="edge_evidence">Solutions to simplify: Software that makes exploitation of the vulnerability trivial, including exploit frameworks, such as Metasploit or Cobalt Strike, or other tools that work reliably and against many different systems</data><data key="edge_extraction_method">minie</data><data key="edge_polarity">positive</data><data key="edge_modality">asserted</data></edge><edge id="oe_002cc90258b25ca6" source="e_39103e9a67affb14" target="e_39bc76bcef4afb1d"><data key="edge_predicate_raw">be simplify Software including exploit frameworks such as</data><data key="edge_assertion_id">a_6547919e0bdfb460</data><data key="edge_source_id">S51</data><data key="edge_source_url">https://www.first.org/cvss/v4.0/user-guide</data><data key="edge_chunk_id">S51_C22</data><data key="edge_json_path">None</data><data key="edge_evidence">Solutions to simplify: Software that makes exploitation of the vulnerability trivial, including exploit frameworks, such as Metasploit or Cobalt Strike, or other tools that work reliably and against many different systems</data><data key="edge_extraction_method">minie</data><data key="edge_polarity">positive</data><data key="edge_modality">asserted</data></edge><edge id="oe_0586c1c4aa57f908" source="e_fd14ed7ffb68c6c3" target="e_f81b7533e05fcef9"><data key="edge_predicate_raw">makes exploitation of</data><data key="edge_assertion_id">a_2c5bdfaf4c6e0290</data><data key="edge_source_id">S51</data><data key="edge_source_url">https://www.first.org/cvss/v4.0/user-guide</data><data key="edge_chunk_id">S51_C22</data><data key="edge_json_path">None</data><data key="edge_evidence">Solutions to simplify: Software that makes exploitation of the vulnerability trivial, including exploit frameworks, such as Metasploit or Cobalt Strike, or other tools that work reliably and against many different systems</data><data key="edge_extraction_method">minie</data><data key="edge_polarity">positive</data><data key="edge_modality">asserted</data></edge><edge id="oe_5e78507dc30b10e7" source="e_0afffd6dbd074e95" target="e_f81b7533e05fcef9"><data key="edge_predicate_raw">makes exploitation of</data><data key="edge_assertion_id">a_31dadb5886fecfae</data><data key="edge_source_id">S51</data><data key="edge_source_url">https://www.first.org/cvss/v4.0/user-guide</data><data key="edge_chunk_id">S51_C22</data><data key="edge_json_path">None</data><data key="edge_evidence">Solutions to simplify: Software that makes exploitation of the vulnerability trivial, including exploit frameworks, such as Metasploit or Cobalt Strike, or other tools that work reliably and against many different systems</data><data key="edge_extraction_method">minie</data><data key="edge_polarity">positive</data><data key="edge_modality">asserted</data></edge><edge id="oe_29e1a78348555d19" source="e_374712641fd0a636" target="e_f81b7533e05fcef9"><data key="edge_predicate_raw">makes exploitation of</data><data key="edge_assertion_id">a_48d143f1daa50340</data><data key="edge_source_id">S51</data><data key="edge_source_url">https://www.first.org/cvss/v4.0/user-guide</data><data key="edge_chunk_id">S51_C22</data><data key="edge_json_path">None</data><data key="edge_evidence">Solutions to simplify: Software that makes exploitation of the vulnerability trivial, including exploit frameworks, such as Metasploit or Cobalt Strike, or other tools that work reliably and against many different systems</data><data key="edge_extraction_method">minie</data><data key="edge_polarity">positive</data><data key="edge_modality">asserted</data></edge><edge id="oe_aa3570f04f95f6b9" source="e_39bc76bcef4afb1d" target="e_02047e928cd28b09"><data key="edge_predicate_raw">work</data><data key="edge_assertion_id">a_f6576d7a83b2e504</data><data key="edge_source_id">S51</data><data key="edge_source_url">https://www.first.org/cvss/v4.0/user-guide</data><data key="edge_chunk_id">S51_C22</data><data key="edge_json_path">None</data><data key="edge_evidence">Solutions to simplify: Software that makes exploitation of the vulnerability trivial, including exploit frameworks, such as Metasploit or Cobalt Strike, or other tools that work reliably and against many different systems</data><data key="edge_extraction_method">minie</data><data key="edge_polarity">positive</data><data key="edge_modality">asserted</data></edge><edge id="oe_95062ded20e285fe" source="e_aa5d4cdb8743a06c" target="e_ad16450d4d7b98f8"><data key="edge_predicate_raw">include for example</data><data key="edge_assertion_id">a_041e0f0fcbe7e8c7</data><data key="edge_source_id">S51</data><data key="edge_source_url">https://www.first.org/cvss/v4.0/user-guide</data><data key="edge_chunk_id">S51_C22</data><data key="edge_json_path">None</data><data key="edge_evidence">Information systems include, for example, IT systems, ICS systems, OT systems, computing hardware, and so on</data><data key="edge_extraction_method">minie</data><data key="edge_polarity">positive</data><data key="edge_modality">asserted</data></edge><edge id="oe_e2438d11e3059113" source="e_aa5d4cdb8743a06c" target="e_ad16450d4d7b98f8"><data key="edge_predicate_raw">include</data><data key="edge_assertion_id">a_621298d45c0a8b7d</data><data key="edge_source_id">S51</data><data key="edge_source_url">https://www.first.org/cvss/v4.0/user-guide</data><data key="edge_chunk_id">S51_C22</data><data key="edge_json_path">None</data><data key="edge_evidence">Information systems include, for example, IT systems, ICS systems, OT systems, computing hardware, and so on</data><data key="edge_extraction_method">minie</data><data key="edge_polarity">positive</data><data key="edge_modality">asserted</data></edge><edge id="oe_2efbabf326266aff" source="e_65a2bc8471f9273a" target="e_87a35caaa98faf5a"><data key="edge_predicate_raw">is violated as result of</data><data key="edge_assertion_id">a_7ac8bb07045fc752</data><data key="edge_source_id">S51</data><data key="edge_source_url">https://www.first.org/cvss/v4.0/user-guide</data><data key="edge_chunk_id">S51_C22</data><data key="edge_json_path">None</data><data key="edge_evidence">Subsequent System: A system whose security policy is violated as a result of the exploited vulnerability but that is not the Vulnerable System</data><data key="edge_extraction_method">minie</data><data key="edge_polarity">negative</data><data key="edge_modality">asserted</data></edge><edge id="oe_cc20813e81652b62" source="e_80403aa9bda2cfc7" target="e_87a35caaa98faf5a"><data key="edge_predicate_raw">is violated as result of</data><data key="edge_assertion_id">a_96c634e48c321e91</data><data key="edge_source_id">S51</data><data key="edge_source_url">https://www.first.org/cvss/v4.0/user-guide</data><data key="edge_chunk_id">S51_C22</data><data key="edge_json_path">None</data><data key="edge_evidence">Subsequent System: A system whose security policy is violated as a result of the exploited vulnerability but that is not the Vulnerable System</data><data key="edge_extraction_method">minie</data><data key="edge_polarity">negative</data><data key="edge_modality">asserted</data></edge><edge id="oe_4fbe2204a668b893" source="e_537e6ab50e8f2e44" target="e_8abf2bc157c8b84d"><data key="edge_predicate_raw">violates security policy of information system</data><data key="edge_assertion_id">a_4e60b88f0788ff55</data><data key="edge_source_id">S51</data><data key="edge_source_url">https://www.first.org/cvss/v4.0/user-guide</data><data key="edge_chunk_id">S51_C22</data><data key="edge_json_path">None</data><data key="edge_evidence">Successful attack: A successful attack (or successful exploit of a vulnerability) is a situation where an attacker violates the security policy of an information system</data><data key="edge_extraction_method">minie</data><data key="edge_polarity">positive</data><data key="edge_modality">asserted</data></edge><edge id="oe_73989a836b213a90" source="e_668be19210801bc1" target="e_adb86950277d31be"><data key="edge_predicate_raw">contribute to production of</data><data key="edge_assertion_id">a_baf3b0b231c1c195</data><data key="edge_source_id">S51</data><data key="edge_source_url">https://www.first.org/cvss/v4.0/user-guide</data><data key="edge_chunk_id">S51_C22</data><data key="edge_json_path">None</data><data key="edge_evidence">Supply Chain: A subset of industry members (often cutting across many industries) that contribute to the production of goods and services that an organization (industry, or geopolitical entity) consumes</data><data key="edge_extraction_method">minie</data><data key="edge_polarity">positive</data><data key="edge_modality">asserted</data></edge><edge id="oe_205bfdaf9263961e" source="e_668be19210801bc1" target="e_aedfa9daeec6ba5f"><data key="edge_predicate_raw">contribute to production of</data><data key="edge_assertion_id">a_70871f9153cf8427</data><data key="edge_source_id">S51</data><data key="edge_source_url">https://www.first.org/cvss/v4.0/user-guide</data><data key="edge_chunk_id">S51_C22</data><data key="edge_json_path">None</data><data key="edge_evidence">Supply Chain: A subset of industry members (often cutting across many industries) that contribute to the production of goods and services that an organization (industry, or geopolitical entity) consumes</data><data key="edge_extraction_method">minie</data><data key="edge_polarity">positive</data><data key="edge_modality">asserted</data></edge><edge id="oe_5796f579411633a6" source="e_e09999ff828efeef" target="e_3b3250fcd74bf447"><data key="edge_predicate_raw">affected</data><data key="edge_assertion_id">a_e5e6359c0d53b9f8</data><data key="edge_source_id">S51</data><data key="edge_source_url">https://www.first.org/cvss/v4.0/user-guide</data><data key="edge_chunk_id">S51_C22</data><data key="edge_json_path">None</data><data key="edge_evidence">For CVSS, usually said of a person authorized to access a vulnerable system affected by the vulnerability being scored</data><data key="edge_extraction_method">heuristic</data><data key="edge_polarity">positive</data><data key="edge_modality">reported</data></edge><edge id="oe_853655049d01e024" source="e_42d90d39b4d09371" target="e_ead7e2cc858e005e"><data key="edge_predicate_raw">requires successful completion of prior exploits</data><data key="edge_assertion_id">a_6b405238c6db797e</data><data key="edge_source_id">S51</data><data key="edge_source_url">https://www.first.org/cvss/v4.0/user-guide</data><data key="edge_chunk_id">S51_C22</data><data key="edge_json_path">None</data><data key="edge_evidence">Vulnerability chaining: The sequential exploitation of multiple vulnerabilities in order to attack an information system, where one or more exploits at the end of the chain requires the successful completion of prior exploits in order to be exploited.14</data><data key="edge_extraction_method">minie</data><data key="edge_polarity">positive</data><data key="edge_modality">asserted</data></edge><edge id="oe_519af1673b15e99e" source="e_4e5e7719d8de2720" target="e_ead7e2cc858e005e"><data key="edge_predicate_raw">be attack</data><data key="edge_assertion_id">a_8ee1f33226abe5d3</data><data key="edge_source_id">S51</data><data key="edge_source_url">https://www.first.org/cvss/v4.0/user-guide</data><data key="edge_chunk_id">S51_C23</data><data key="edge_json_path">None</data><data key="edge_evidence">multiple vulnerabilities in order to attack an information system, where one or more exploits at the end of the chain requires the successful completion of prior exploits in order to be exploited.14</data><data key="edge_extraction_method">minie</data><data key="edge_polarity">positive</data><data key="edge_modality">asserted</data></edge><edge id="oe_0fe019153f14462d" source="e_42d90d39b4d09371" target="e_ead7e2cc858e005e"><data key="edge_predicate_raw">requires successful completion of prior exploits</data><data key="edge_assertion_id">a_029275a63286a3b2</data><data key="edge_source_id">S51</data><data key="edge_source_url">https://www.first.org/cvss/v4.0/user-guide</data><data key="edge_chunk_id">S51_C23</data><data key="edge_json_path">None</data><data key="edge_evidence">multiple vulnerabilities in order to attack an information system, where one or more exploits at the end of the chain requires the successful completion of prior exploits in order to be exploited.14</data><data key="edge_extraction_method">minie</data><data key="edge_polarity">positive</data><data key="edge_modality">asserted</data></edge><edge id="oe_2d96db90d56810a2" source="e_65a2bc8471f9273a" target="e_87a35caaa98faf5a"><data key="edge_predicate_raw">is violated as result of</data><data key="edge_assertion_id">a_02a1a510934b1618</data><data key="edge_source_id">S51</data><data key="edge_source_url">https://www.first.org/cvss/v4.0/user-guide</data><data key="edge_chunk_id">S51_C23</data><data key="edge_json_path">None</data><data key="edge_evidence">Vulnerable System: A system whose security policy is violated as the result of an exploited vulnerability and which contains the vulnerability</data><data key="edge_extraction_method">minie</data><data key="edge_polarity">positive</data><data key="edge_modality">asserted</data></edge><edge id="oe_30959c13900fed07" source="e_b82be424e7d21f94" target="e_dbd1ba0cc63988dc"><data key="edge_predicate_raw">contains</data><data key="edge_assertion_id">a_b07b0bb4cdfee823</data><data key="edge_source_id">S51</data><data key="edge_source_url">https://www.first.org/cvss/v4.0/user-guide</data><data key="edge_chunk_id">S51_C23</data><data key="edge_json_path">None</data><data key="edge_evidence">Vulnerable System: A system whose security policy is violated as the result of an exploited vulnerability and which contains the vulnerability</data><data key="edge_extraction_method">minie</data><data key="edge_polarity">positive</data><data key="edge_modality">asserted</data></edge><edge id="oe_7a9190a2d84d56e2" source="e_06e725c9e9907cc0" target="e_5086ede60e614714"><data key="edge_predicate_raw">are aid to scoring</data><data key="edge_assertion_id">a_4b9fc6b84d7a4d3a</data><data key="edge_source_id">S51</data><data key="edge_source_url">https://www.first.org/cvss/v4.0/user-guide</data><data key="edge_chunk_id">S51_C23</data><data key="edge_json_path">None</data><data key="edge_evidence">The scoring rubrics are an aid to scoring vulnerabilities by supplementing the metric definitions in the Specification Document</data><data key="edge_extraction_method">minie</data><data key="edge_polarity">positive</data><data key="edge_modality">asserted</data></edge><edge id="oe_aab4daaaebe92eee" source="e_16c19720b709151a" target="e_83a4aec228a36ef4"><data key="edge_predicate_raw">is adapted from</data><data key="edge_assertion_id">a_01644b454d21c008</data><data key="edge_source_id">S51</data><data key="edge_source_url">https://www.first.org/cvss/v4.0/user-guide</data><data key="edge_chunk_id">S51_C23</data><data key="edge_json_path">None</data><data key="edge_evidence">This sourcing criteria is adapted from Spring JM, Illari P</data><data key="edge_extraction_method">minie</data><data key="edge_polarity">positive</data><data key="edge_modality">asserted</data></edge><edge id="oe_e19fc9701a0000bc" source="e_852ad9df33f7bf00" target="e_def246b038b6e247"><data key="edge_predicate_raw">are preferred / in certain contexts From</data><data key="edge_assertion_id">a_03b0908286cf0c43</data><data key="edge_source_id">S51</data><data key="edge_source_url">https://www.first.org/cvss/v4.0/user-guide</data><data key="edge_chunk_id">S51_C23</data><data key="edge_json_path">None</data><data key="edge_evidence">From RFC 4949 \$ authorization: Specific terms are preferred in certain contexts:</data><data key="edge_extraction_method">minie</data><data key="edge_polarity">positive</data><data key="edge_modality">asserted</data></edge><edge id="oe_5772cced95b90523" source="e_852ad9df33f7bf00" target="e_9eb62e90aacb93d5"><data key="edge_predicate_raw">are preferred / in</data><data key="edge_assertion_id">a_7f6220ed771d6f43</data><data key="edge_source_id">S51</data><data key="edge_source_url">https://www.first.org/cvss/v4.0/user-guide</data><data key="edge_chunk_id">S51_C23</data><data key="edge_json_path">None</data><data key="edge_evidence">From RFC 4949 \$ authorization: Specific terms are preferred in certain contexts:</data><data key="edge_extraction_method">minie</data><data key="edge_polarity">positive</data><data key="edge_modality">asserted</data></edge><edge id="oe_c38322be065b2a3c" source="e_40521ab18540bb62" target="e_958b05c1984d5a1e"><data key="edge_predicate_raw">be used to align with</data><data key="edge_assertion_id">a_5bf0afbc1d1c5d20</data><data key="edge_source_id">S51</data><data key="edge_source_url">https://www.first.org/cvss/v4.0/user-guide</data><data key="edge_chunk_id">S51_C23</data><data key="edge_json_path">None</data><data key="edge_evidence">- /PKI/ "Authorization" SHOULD be used, to align with "certification</data><data key="edge_extraction_method">minie</data><data key="edge_polarity">positive</data><data key="edge_modality">asserted</data></edge><edge id="oe_fc47f90b845a7a18" source="e_e163460c91338b08" target="e_a92e222452dc79d3"><data key="edge_predicate_raw">is consistent for</data><data key="edge_assertion_id">a_d18ef1053de98fd4</data><data key="edge_source_id">S51</data><data key="edge_source_url">https://www.first.org/cvss/v4.0/user-guide</data><data key="edge_chunk_id">S51_C23</data><data key="edge_json_path">None</data><data key="edge_evidence">NIST has [several different definitions]() for security policy, this is consistent with at least some of them. ↩</data><data key="edge_extraction_method">minie</data><data key="edge_polarity">positive</data><data key="edge_modality">asserted</data></edge><edge id="oe_01e5d39b777d0867" source="e_b585119b28a1d6c9" target="e_cf503d8a57cdc58d"><data key="edge_predicate_raw">is open framework for communicating characteristics of</data><data key="edge_assertion_id">a_484408a480f6e209</data><data key="edge_source_id">S52</data><data key="edge_source_url">https://www.first.org/cvss/v3.1/specification-document</data><data key="edge_chunk_id">S52_C01</data><data key="edge_json_path">None</data><data key="edge_evidence">The Common Vulnerability Scoring System (CVSS) is an open framework for communicating the characteristics and severity of software vulnerabilities</data><data key="edge_extraction_method">minie</data><data key="edge_polarity">positive</data><data key="edge_modality">asserted</data></edge><edge id="oe_aa09a6a0d03f6677" source="e_b585119b28a1d6c9" target="e_e6145aa9c0971bc2"><data key="edge_predicate_raw">is open framework for</data><data key="edge_assertion_id">a_08b2d9da9b94e0fc</data><data key="edge_source_id">S52</data><data key="edge_source_url">https://www.first.org/cvss/v3.1/specification-document</data><data key="edge_chunk_id">S52_C01</data><data key="edge_json_path">None</data><data key="edge_evidence">The Common Vulnerability Scoring System (CVSS) is an open framework for communicating the characteristics and severity of software vulnerabilities</data><data key="edge_extraction_method">minie</data><data key="edge_polarity">positive</data><data key="edge_modality">asserted</data></edge><edge id="oe_3d0eb1d6e16b0558" source="e_dbd1ba0cc63988dc" target="e_44fb585ec7e6699b"><data key="edge_predicate_raw">are unique to</data><data key="edge_assertion_id">a_0186308facaf1cb8</data><data key="edge_source_id">S52</data><data key="edge_source_url">https://www.first.org/cvss/v3.1/specification-document</data><data key="edge_chunk_id">S52_C01</data><data key="edge_json_path">None</data><data key="edge_evidence">The Base group represents the intrinsic qualities of a vulnerability that are constant over time and across user environments, the Temporal group reflects the characteristics of a vulnerability that change over time, and the Environmental group represents the characteristics of a vulnerability that are unique to a user's environment</data><data key="edge_extraction_method">minie</data><data key="edge_polarity">positive</data><data key="edge_modality">asserted</data></edge><edge id="oe_49574c7dc32e567c" source="e_38c8318b1fef3eff" target="e_dbd1ba0cc63988dc"><data key="edge_predicate_raw">represents intrinsic qualities of</data><data key="edge_assertion_id">a_ab13673c8bbf47bf</data><data key="edge_source_id">S52</data><data key="edge_source_url">https://www.first.org/cvss/v3.1/specification-document</data><data key="edge_chunk_id">S52_C01</data><data key="edge_json_path">None</data><data key="edge_evidence">The Base group represents the intrinsic qualities of a vulnerability that are constant over time and across user environments, the Temporal group reflects the characteristics of a vulnerability that change over time, and the Environmental group represents the characteristics of a vulnerability that are unique to a user's environment</data><data key="edge_extraction_method">minie</data><data key="edge_polarity">positive</data><data key="edge_modality">asserted</data></edge><edge id="oe_6ab2efc1bea48f9b" source="e_dbd1ba0cc63988dc" target="e_ca335c133f4134dc"><data key="edge_predicate_raw">are constant over</data><data key="edge_assertion_id">a_a00fb07f2cb4b543</data><data key="edge_source_id">S52</data><data key="edge_source_url">https://www.first.org/cvss/v3.1/specification-document</data><data key="edge_chunk_id">S52_C01</data><data key="edge_json_path">None</data><data key="edge_evidence">The Base group represents the intrinsic qualities of a vulnerability that are constant over time and across user environments, the Temporal group reflects the characteristics of a vulnerability that change over time, and the Environmental group represents the characteristics of a vulnerability that are unique to a user's environment</data><data key="edge_extraction_method">minie</data><data key="edge_polarity">positive</data><data key="edge_modality">asserted</data></edge><edge id="oe_cbc036aac586a11a" source="e_dbd1ba0cc63988dc" target="e_ca335c133f4134dc"><data key="edge_predicate_raw">are across user environments over</data><data key="edge_assertion_id">a_9d0c4156782336ca</data><data key="edge_source_id">S52</data><data key="edge_source_url">https://www.first.org/cvss/v3.1/specification-document</data><data key="edge_chunk_id">S52_C01</data><data key="edge_json_path">None</data><data key="edge_evidence">The Base group represents the intrinsic qualities of a vulnerability that are constant over time and across user environments, the Temporal group reflects the characteristics of a vulnerability that change over time, and the Environmental group represents the characteristics of a vulnerability that are unique to a user's environment</data><data key="edge_extraction_method">minie</data><data key="edge_polarity">positive</data><data key="edge_modality">asserted</data></edge><edge id="oe_0a242341ed695976" source="e_dbd1ba0cc63988dc" target="e_3d75e6dbcbfb5033"><data key="edge_predicate_raw">are across</data><data key="edge_assertion_id">a_8a7e711383cdbf1b</data><data key="edge_source_id">S52</data><data key="edge_source_url">https://www.first.org/cvss/v3.1/specification-document</data><data key="edge_chunk_id">S52_C01</data><data key="edge_json_path">None</data><data key="edge_evidence">The Base group represents the intrinsic qualities of a vulnerability that are constant over time and across user environments, the Temporal group reflects the characteristics of a vulnerability that change over time, and the Environmental group represents the characteristics of a vulnerability that are unique to a user's environment</data><d