ge_polarity">positive</data><data key="edge_modality">asserted</data></edge><edge id="oe_0c6767808c5a876f" source="e_be74ffef073dc8d3" target="e_2f5c3d09f4bbc7c9"><data key="edge_predicate_raw">refer</data><data key="edge_assertion_id">a_70f805808844c18b</data><data key="edge_source_id">S52</data><data key="edge_source_url">https://www.first.org/cvss/v3.1/specification-document</data><data key="edge_chunk_id">S52_C02</data><data key="edge_json_path">None</data><data key="edge_evidence">That is, they represent characteristics of the thing that is vulnerable, which we refer to formally as the vulnerable component</data><data key="edge_extraction_method">minie</data><data key="edge_polarity">positive</data><data key="edge_modality">asserted</data></edge><edge id="oe_2314296650ea2ab6" source="e_290d8da624d84fb0" target="e_2f5c3d09f4bbc7c9"><data key="edge_predicate_raw">represent characteristics of</data><data key="edge_assertion_id">a_44bff9bf2e3922f4</data><data key="edge_source_id">S52</data><data key="edge_source_url">https://www.first.org/cvss/v3.1/specification-document</data><data key="edge_chunk_id">S52_C02</data><data key="edge_json_path">None</data><data key="edge_evidence">That is, they represent characteristics of the thing that is vulnerable, which we refer to formally as the vulnerable component</data><data key="edge_extraction_method">minie</data><data key="edge_polarity">positive</data><data key="edge_modality">asserted</data></edge><edge id="oe_d98ca507bf585185" source="e_44d5b5c401e205a9" target="e_d760c680924b2e91"><data key="edge_predicate_raw">be discussed</data><data key="edge_assertion_id">a_18f3fd9455ed3765</data><data key="edge_source_id">S52</data><data key="edge_source_url">https://www.first.org/cvss/v3.1/specification-document</data><data key="edge_chunk_id">S52_C02</data><data key="edge_json_path">None</data><data key="edge_evidence">This property is captured by the Scope metric, discussed later</data><data key="edge_extraction_method">minie</data><data key="edge_polarity">positive</data><data key="edge_modality">asserted</data></edge><edge id="oe_9d5c8b673043b461" source="e_4d4fca7ad49e3fcf" target="e_dbd1ba0cc63988dc"><data key="edge_predicate_raw">reflects characteristics of</data><data key="edge_assertion_id">a_b3a983d61d9c8750</data><data key="edge_source_id">S52</data><data key="edge_source_url">https://www.first.org/cvss/v3.1/specification-document</data><data key="edge_chunk_id">S52_C02</data><data key="edge_json_path">None</data><data key="edge_evidence">The Temporal metric group reflects the characteristics of a vulnerability that may change over time but not across user environments</data><data key="edge_extraction_method">minie</data><data key="edge_polarity">negative</data><data key="edge_modality">possible</data></edge><edge id="oe_426a07f86e7eb49b" source="e_dbd1ba0cc63988dc" target="e_ca335c133f4134dc"><data key="edge_predicate_raw">change over</data><data key="edge_assertion_id">a_a1bd82d80a845e92</data><data key="edge_source_id">S52</data><data key="edge_source_url">https://www.first.org/cvss/v3.1/specification-document</data><data key="edge_chunk_id">S52_C02</data><data key="edge_json_path">None</data><data key="edge_evidence">The Temporal metric group reflects the characteristics of a vulnerability that may change over time but not across user environments</data><data key="edge_extraction_method">minie</data><data key="edge_polarity">negative</data><data key="edge_modality">possible</data></edge><edge id="oe_b7021341dc680faf" source="e_dbd1ba0cc63988dc" target="e_dbeb49618673aac7"><data key="edge_predicate_raw">change across</data><data key="edge_assertion_id">a_84dd08442e80cd8b</data><data key="edge_source_id">S52</data><data key="edge_source_url">https://www.first.org/cvss/v3.1/specification-document</data><data key="edge_chunk_id">S52_C02</data><data key="edge_json_path">None</data><data key="edge_evidence">The Temporal metric group reflects the characteristics of a vulnerability that may change over time but not across user environments</data><data key="edge_extraction_method">minie</data><data key="edge_polarity">negative</data><data key="edge_modality">possible</data></edge><edge id="oe_5e13b8be9d4ab832" source="e_0915479bc15411b6" target="e_b5dac192ab4acd82"><data key="edge_predicate_raw">increase</data><data key="edge_assertion_id">a_8121ee2a017edbcc</data><data key="edge_source_id">S52</data><data key="edge_source_url">https://www.first.org/cvss/v3.1/specification-document</data><data key="edge_chunk_id">S52_C02</data><data key="edge_json_path">None</data><data key="edge_evidence">For example, the presence of a simple-to-use exploit kit would increase the CVSS score, while the creation of an official patch would decrease it</data><data key="edge_extraction_method">minie</data><data key="edge_polarity">positive</data><data key="edge_modality">asserted</data></edge><edge id="oe_31d8b80e495bc0c6" source="e_ac011aa32b65a2e0" target="e_ad16450d4d7b98f8"><data key="edge_predicate_raw">decrease</data><data key="edge_assertion_id">a_030740d780079cee</data><data key="edge_source_id">S52</data><data key="edge_source_url">https://www.first.org/cvss/v3.1/specification-document</data><data key="edge_chunk_id">S52_C02</data><data key="edge_json_path">None</data><data key="edge_evidence">For example, the presence of a simple-to-use exploit kit would increase the CVSS score, while the creation of an official patch would decrease it</data><data key="edge_extraction_method">minie</data><data key="edge_polarity">positive</data><data key="edge_modality">asserted</data></edge><edge id="oe_f63c2c0f29990ca5" source="e_dbd1ba0cc63988dc" target="e_1649d73b65b2ed56"><data key="edge_predicate_raw">are relevant to</data><data key="edge_assertion_id">a_7dd359efc5416ff8</data><data key="edge_source_id">S52</data><data key="edge_source_url">https://www.first.org/cvss/v3.1/specification-document</data><data key="edge_chunk_id">S52_C03</data><data key="edge_json_path">None</data><data key="edge_evidence">The Environmental metric group represents the characteristics of a vulnerability that are relevant and unique to a particular user’s environment</data><data key="edge_extraction_method">minie</data><data key="edge_polarity">positive</data><data key="edge_modality">asserted</data></edge><edge id="oe_a2e1a2bb021c606b" source="e_dbd1ba0cc63988dc" target="e_1649d73b65b2ed56"><data key="edge_predicate_raw">are unique to</data><data key="edge_assertion_id">a_a7b2b68a2e939916</data><data key="edge_source_id">S52</data><data key="edge_source_url">https://www.first.org/cvss/v3.1/specification-document</data><data key="edge_chunk_id">S52_C03</data><data key="edge_json_path">None</data><data key="edge_evidence">The Environmental metric group represents the characteristics of a vulnerability that are relevant and unique to a particular user’s environment</data><data key="edge_extraction_method">minie</data><data key="edge_polarity">positive</data><data key="edge_modality">asserted</data></edge><edge id="oe_6256938355231db7" source="e_b84ee762ce82df1d" target="e_dbd1ba0cc63988dc"><data key="edge_predicate_raw">represents characteristics of</data><data key="edge_assertion_id">a_1d2639c54181eebd</data><data key="edge_source_id">S52</data><data key="edge_source_url">https://www.first.org/cvss/v3.1/specification-document</data><data key="edge_chunk_id">S52_C03</data><data key="edge_json_path">None</data><data key="edge_evidence">The Environmental metric group represents the characteristics of a vulnerability that are relevant and unique to a particular user’s environment</data><data key="edge_extraction_method">minie</data><data key="edge_polarity">positive</data><data key="edge_modality">asserted</data></edge><edge id="oe_5844da8de51e6362" source="e_1e8ea1b42ca055ae" target="e_3709b11f96009c9b"><data key="edge_predicate_raw">include presence of</data><data key="edge_assertion_id">a_c48db5b43d22f772</data><data key="edge_source_id">S52</data><data key="edge_source_url">https://www.first.org/cvss/v3.1/specification-document</data><data key="edge_chunk_id">S52_C03</data><data key="edge_json_path">None</data><data key="edge_evidence">Considerations include the presence of security controls which may mitigate some or all consequences of a successful attack, and the relative importance of a vulnerable system within a technology infrastructure</data><data key="edge_extraction_method">minie</data><data key="edge_polarity">positive</data><data key="edge_modality">possible</data></edge><edge id="oe_bcd92df22ee02e41" source="e_1e8ea1b42ca055ae" target="e_ecedfcb33ae54209"><data key="edge_predicate_raw">include</data><data key="edge_assertion_id">a_49929a2d7f7e9cf3</data><data key="edge_source_id">S52</data><data key="edge_source_url">https://www.first.org/cvss/v3.1/specification-document</data><data key="edge_chunk_id">S52_C03</data><data key="edge_json_path">None</data><data key="edge_evidence">Considerations include the presence of security controls which may mitigate some or all consequences of a successful attack, and the relative importance of a vulnerable system within a technology infrastructure</data><data key="edge_extraction_method">minie</data><data key="edge_polarity">positive</data><data key="edge_modality">possible</data></edge><edge id="oe_71903b08a6be33ec" source="e_9db8f043050fbea7" target="e_80b852b98e6b518c"><data key="edge_predicate_raw">contains scoring rubrics for</data><data key="edge_assertion_id">a_d9de8fe023d2bee8</data><data key="edge_source_id">S52</data><data key="edge_source_url">https://www.first.org/cvss/v3.1/specification-document</data><data key="edge_chunk_id">S52_C03</data><data key="edge_json_path">None</data><data key="edge_evidence">The User Guide contains scoring rubrics for the Base Metrics that may be useful when scoring</data><data key="edge_extraction_method">minie</data><data key="edge_polarity">positive</data><data key="edge_modality">possible</data></edge><edge id="oe_427cca1ead5df068" source="e_80b852b98e6b518c" target="e_cd0a45b2a1788da0"><data key="edge_predicate_raw">be useful when</data><data key="edge_assertion_id">a_d283bcb3c7fa03ab</data><data key="edge_source_id">S52</data><data key="edge_source_url">https://www.first.org/cvss/v3.1/specification-document</data><data key="edge_chunk_id">S52_C03</data><data key="edge_json_path">None</data><data key="edge_evidence">The User Guide contains scoring rubrics for the Base Metrics that may be useful when scoring</data><data key="edge_extraction_method">minie</data><data key="edge_polarity">positive</data><data key="edge_modality">possible</data></edge><edge id="oe_252b05434fed609f" source="e_80b852b98e6b518c" target="e_f6498126c94c6f96"><data key="edge_predicate_raw">are assigned values by</data><data key="edge_assertion_id">a_d7ced59d42550a0d</data><data key="edge_source_id">S52</data><data key="edge_source_url">https://www.first.org/cvss/v3.1/specification-document</data><data key="edge_chunk_id">S52_C03</data><data key="edge_json_path">None</data><data key="edge_evidence">When the Base metrics are assigned values by an analyst, the Base equation computes a score ranging from 0.0 to 10.0 as illustrated in Figure 2</data><data key="edge_extraction_method">minie</data><data key="edge_polarity">positive</data><data key="edge_modality">asserted</data></edge><edge id="oe_e47e6688375f0b7c" source="e_80b852b98e6b518c" target="e_a9ed604eb1323e31"><data key="edge_predicate_raw">are assigned</data><data key="edge_assertion_id">a_3dd3ce5875d00fa4</data><data key="edge_source_id">S52</data><data key="edge_source_url">https://www.first.org/cvss/v3.1/specification-document</data><data key="edge_chunk_id">S52_C03</data><data key="edge_json_path">None</data><data key="edge_evidence">When the Base metrics are assigned values by an analyst, the Base equation computes a score ranging from 0.0 to 10.0 as illustrated in Figure 2</data><data key="edge_extraction_method">minie</data><data key="edge_polarity">positive</data><data key="edge_modality">asserted</data></edge><edge id="oe_a74630251bf4ac08" source="e_4877b2bf1b130d1f" target="e_1f8b03b1f8c955c4"><data key="edge_predicate_raw">is derived from</data><data key="edge_assertion_id">a_9dac36e0b9f155db</data><data key="edge_source_id">S52</data><data key="edge_source_url">https://www.first.org/cvss/v3.1/specification-document</data><data key="edge_chunk_id">S52_C03</data><data key="edge_json_path">None</data><data key="edge_evidence">The Exploitability sub-score equation is derived from the Base Exploitability metrics, while the Impact sub-score equation is derived from the Base Impact metrics</data><data key="edge_extraction_method">minie</data><data key="edge_polarity">positive</data><data key="edge_modality">asserted</data></edge><edge id="oe_fd6a4360916966fb" source="e_42a7aeb6884747b3" target="e_31bc17d765a1a69b"><data key="edge_predicate_raw">is derived from</data><data key="edge_assertion_id">a_75b8f4fc914a24df</data><data key="edge_source_id">S52</data><data key="edge_source_url">https://www.first.org/cvss/v3.1/specification-document</data><data key="edge_chunk_id">S52_C03</data><data key="edge_json_path">None</data><data key="edge_evidence">The Exploitability sub-score equation is derived from the Base Exploitability metrics, while the Impact sub-score equation is derived from the Base Impact metrics</data><data key="edge_extraction_method">minie</data><data key="edge_polarity">positive</data><data key="edge_modality">asserted</data></edge><edge id="oe_ca282b08054e4668" source="e_5dd63c0e6e0c1501" target="e_3d46fbacae03f292"><data key="edge_predicate_raw">be refined by</data><data key="edge_assertion_id">a_dc31b7ff752bef80</data><data key="edge_source_id">S52</data><data key="edge_source_url">https://www.first.org/cvss/v3.1/specification-document</data><data key="edge_chunk_id">S52_C03</data><data key="edge_json_path">None</data><data key="edge_evidence">The Base Score can then be refined by scoring the Temporal and Environmental metrics in order to more accurately reflect the relative severity posed by a vulnerability to a user’s environment at a specific point in time</data><data key="edge_extraction_method">minie</data><data key="edge_polarity">positive</data><data key="edge_modality">possible</data></edge><edge id="oe_240ea81482f28df9" source="e_5dd63c0e6e0c1501" target="e_2e9974620e004f2f"><data key="edge_predicate_raw">be refined by</data><data key="edge_assertion_id">a_7efd636c35616e55</data><data key="edge_source_id">S52</data><data key="edge_source_url">https://www.first.org/cvss/v3.1/specification-document</data><data key="edge_chunk_id">S52_C03</data><data key="edge_json_path">None</data><data key="edge_evidence">The Base Score can then be refined by scoring the Temporal and Environmental metrics in order to more accurately reflect the relative severity posed by a vulnerability to a user’s environment at a specific point in time</data><data key="edge_extraction_method">minie</data><data key="edge_polarity">positive</data><data key="edge_modality">possible</data></edge><edge id="oe_e0e46f919baae796" source="e_3d4814f0d5e669ab" target="e_2a7ed2bff0cdae40"><data key="edge_predicate_raw">be reflect more</data><data key="edge_assertion_id">a_2425eb8937c15a91</data><data key="edge_source_id">S52</data><data key="edge_source_url">https://www.first.org/cvss/v3.1/specification-document</data><data key="edge_chunk_id">S52_C03</data><data key="edge_json_path">None</data><data key="edge_evidence">The Base Score can then be refined by scoring the Temporal and Environmental metrics in order to more accurately reflect the relative severity posed by a vulnerability to a user’s environment at a specific point in time</data><data key="edge_extraction_method">minie</data><data key="edge_polarity">positive</data><data key="edge_modality">possible</data></edge><edge id="oe_72e2be4c5e93c15c" source="e_3a9157715b31805c" target="e_2a7ed2bff0cdae40"><data key="edge_predicate_raw">be reflect more</data><data key="edge_assertion_id">a_de6869185d6c903e</data><data key="edge_source_id">S52</data><data key="edge_source_url">https://www.first.org/cvss/v3.1/specification-document</data><data key="edge_chunk_id">S52_C03</data><data key="edge_json_path">None</data><data key="edge_evidence">The Base Score can then be refined by scoring the Temporal and Environmental metrics in order to more accurately reflect the relative severity posed by a vulnerability to a user’s environment at a specific point in time</data><data key="edge_extraction_method">minie</data><data key="edge_polarity">positive</data><data key="edge_modality">possible</data></edge><edge id="oe_f0f9e77877e32640" source="e_d15e9e1afe2a9d2f" target="e_491a87f4c4b335f8"><data key="edge_predicate_raw">be posed by</data><data key="edge_assertion_id">a_b121b6243dc11bf4</data><data key="edge_source_id">S52</data><data key="edge_source_url">https://www.first.org/cvss/v3.1/specification-document</data><data key="edge_chunk_id">S52_C03</data><data key="edge_json_path">None</data><data key="edge_evidence">The Base Score can then be refined by scoring the Temporal and Environmental metrics in order to more accurately reflect the relative severity posed by a vulnerability to a user’s environment at a specific point in time</data><data key="edge_extraction_method">minie</data><data key="edge_polarity">positive</data><data key="edge_modality">possible</data></edge><edge id="oe_4251b39ab3cc24a5" source="e_3bca66551d1e30df" target="e_80cb9bff13d34e0c"><data key="edge_predicate_raw">are specified by</data><data key="edge_assertion_id">a_76b49b25c9126283</data><data key="edge_source_id">S52</data><data key="edge_source_url">https://www.first.org/cvss/v3.1/specification-document</data><data key="edge_chunk_id">S52_C03</data><data key="edge_json_path">None</data><data key="edge_evidence">Generally, the Base and Temporal metrics are specified by vulnerability bulletin analysts, security product vendors, or application vendors because they typically possess the most accurate information about the characteristics of a vulnerability</data><data key="edge_extraction_method">minie</data><data key="edge_polarity">positive</data><data key="edge_modality">asserted</data></edge><edge id="oe_ccf96ce77df2f943" source="e_3bca66551d1e30df" target="e_98088102bdb119ab"><data key="edge_predicate_raw">are specified by</data><data key="edge_assertion_id">a_46f62a1f7dd53a69</data><data key="edge_source_id">S52</data><data key="edge_source_url">https://www.first.org/cvss/v3.1/specification-document</data><data key="edge_chunk_id">S52_C03</data><data key="edge_json_path">None</data><data key="edge_evidence">Generally, the Base and Temporal metrics are specified by vulnerability bulletin analysts, security product vendors, or application vendors because they typically possess the most accurate information about the characteristics of a vulnerability</data><data key="edge_extraction_method">minie</data><data key="edge_polarity">positive</data><data key="edge_modality">asserted</data></edge><edge id="oe_7c6575014119131f" source="e_3bca66551d1e30df" target="e_54d5f84d2fd12cc2"><data key="edge_predicate_raw">are specified by</data><data key="edge_assertion_id">a_158b526efd2dbbb6</data><data key="edge_source_id">S52</data><data key="edge_source_url">https://www.first.org/cvss/v3.1/specification-document</data><data key="edge_chunk_id">S52_C03</data><data key="edge_json_path">None</data><data key="edge_evidence">Generally, the Base and Temporal metrics are specified by vulnerability bulletin analysts, security product vendors, or application vendors because they typically possess the most accurate information about the characteristics of a vulnerability</data><data key="edge_extraction_method">minie</data><data key="edge_polarity">positive</data><data key="edge_modality">asserted</data></edge><edge id="oe_cb2729c58b020110" source="e_d558a240751fca46" target="e_80cb9bff13d34e0c"><data key="edge_predicate_raw">are specified by</data><data key="edge_assertion_id">a_ae0b327b32a4bded</data><data key="edge_source_id">S52</data><data key="edge_source_url">https://www.first.org/cvss/v3.1/specification-document</data><data key="edge_chunk_id">S52_C03</data><data key="edge_json_path">None</data><data key="edge_evidence">Generally, the Base and Temporal metrics are specified by vulnerability bulletin analysts, security product vendors, or application vendors because they typically possess the most accurate information about the characteristics of a vulnerability</data><data key="edge_extraction_method">minie</data><data key="edge_polarity">positive</data><data key="edge_modality">asserted</data></edge><edge id="oe_83600610dfc84fcf" source="e_d558a240751fca46" target="e_98088102bdb119ab"><data key="edge_predicate_raw">are specified by</data><data key="edge_assertion_id">a_1a549452ac82fe63</data><data key="edge_source_id">S52</data><data key="edge_source_url">https://www.first.org/cvss/v3.1/specification-document</data><data key="edge_chunk_id">S52_C03</data><data key="edge_json_path">None</data><data key="edge_evidence">Generally, the Base and Temporal metrics are specified by vulnerability bulletin analysts, security product vendors, or application vendors because they typically possess the most accurate information about the characteristics of a vulnerability</data><data key="edge_extraction_method">minie</data><data key="edge_polarity">positive</data><data key="edge_modality">asserted</data></edge><edge id="oe_307202a5e649ee53" source="e_d558a240751fca46" target="e_54d5f84d2fd12cc2"><data key="edge_predicate_raw">are specified by</data><data key="edge_assertion_id">a_2ad2a3a88c393074</data><data key="edge_source_id">S52</data><data key="edge_source_url">https://www.first.org/cvss/v3.1/specification-document</data><data key="edge_chunk_id">S52_C03</data><data key="edge_json_path">None</data><data key="edge_evidence">Generally, the Base and Temporal metrics are specified by vulnerability bulletin analysts, security product vendors, or application vendors because they typically possess the most accurate information about the characteristics of a vulnerability</data><data key="edge_extraction_method">minie</data><data key="edge_polarity">positive</data><data key="edge_modality">asserted</data></edge><edge id="oe_6fdccdc55b9e850d" source="e_290d8da624d84fb0" target="e_a0ef75f1f1ee68c4"><data key="edge_predicate_raw">possess</data><data key="edge_assertion_id">a_552ca1215b4dd3d4</data><data key="edge_source_id">S52</data><data key="edge_source_url">https://www.first.org/cvss/v3.1/specification-document</data><data key="edge_chunk_id">S52_C03</data><data key="edge_json_path">None</data><data key="edge_evidence">Generally, the Base and Temporal metrics are specified by vulnerability bulletin analysts, security product vendors, or application vendors because they typically possess the most accurate information about the characteristics of a vulnerability</data><data key="edge_extraction_method">minie</data><data key="edge_polarity">positive</data><data key="edge_modality">asserted</data></edge><edge id="oe_11596754925858a3" source="e_b54a46ece8e786db" target="e_b5e10b330165a2fb"><data key="edge_predicate_raw">are specified by</data><data key="edge_assertion_id">a_48022e93e0743fc1</data><data key="edge_source_id">S52</data><data key="edge_source_url">https://www.first.org/cvss/v3.1/specification-document</data><data key="edge_chunk_id">S52_C03</data><data key="edge_json_path">None</data><data key="edge_evidence">The Environmental metrics are specified by end-user organizations because they are best able to assess the potential impact of a vulnerability within their own computing environment</data><data key="edge_extraction_method">minie</data><data key="edge_polarity">positive</data><data key="edge_modality">asserted</data></edge><edge id="oe_e592110ba660846f" source="e_45b3e78147f50a23" target="e_dbd1ba0cc63988dc"><data key="edge_predicate_raw">be used to score</data><data key="edge_assertion_id">a_dddef0c88900641b</data><data key="edge_source_id">S52</data><data key="edge_source_url">https://www.first.org/cvss/v3.1/specification-document</data><data key="edge_chunk_id">S52_C03</data><data key="edge_json_path">None</data><data key="edge_evidence">Scoring CVSS metrics also produces a vector string, a textual representation of the metric values used to score the vulnerability</data><data key="edge_extraction_method">minie</data><data key="edge_polarity">positive</data><data key="edge_modality">asserted</data></edge><edge id="oe_8101e5e45212c75f" source="e_fee39a19d8f3b06c" target="e_97d5b9fcbb9ac78b"><data key="edge_predicate_raw">produces</data><data key="edge_assertion_id">a_775d1de81db67c37</data><data key="edge_source_id">S52</data><data key="edge_source_url">https://www.first.org/cvss/v3.1/specification-document</data><data key="edge_chunk_id">S52_C03</data><data key="edge_json_path">None</data><data key="edge_evidence">Scoring CVSS metrics also produces a vector string, a textual representation of the metric values used to score the vulnerability</data><data key="edge_extraction_method">minie</data><data key="edge_polarity">positive</data><data key="edge_modality">asserted</data></edge><edge id="oe_11b633e8f79aa44f" source="e_97d5b9fcbb9ac78b" target="e_b77bee5b354b9d96"><data key="edge_predicate_raw">be displayed with</data><data key="edge_assertion_id">a_0e91beef2b5f0b03</data><data key="edge_source_id">S52</data><data key="edge_source_url">https://www.first.org/cvss/v3.1/specification-document</data><data key="edge_chunk_id">S52_C03</data><data key="edge_json_path">None</data><data key="edge_evidence">This vector string is a specifically formatted text string that contains each value assigned to each metric, and should always be displayed with the vulnerability score</data><data key="edge_extraction_method">minie</data><data key="edge_polarity">positive</data><data key="edge_modality">asserted</data></edge><edge id="oe_c3cc1b3decc7df32" source="e_be74ffef073dc8d3" target="e_0651ca14b1e582f2"><data key="edge_predicate_raw">refer thing to formally as</data><data key="edge_assertion_id">a_ddc6143e1fc6e0d7</data><data key="edge_source_id">S52</data><data key="edge_source_url">https://www.first.org/cvss/v3.1/specification-document</data><data key="edge_chunk_id">S52_C04</data><data key="edge_json_path">None</data><data key="edge_evidence">As previously mentioned, the Exploitability metrics reflect the characteristics of the thing that is vulnerable, which we refer to formally as the vulnerable component</data><data key="edge_extraction_method">minie</data><data key="edge_polarity">positive</data><data key="edge_modality">asserted</data></edge><edge id="oe_acc7901f6a02e895" source="e_be74ffef073dc8d3" target="e_2f5c3d09f4bbc7c9"><data key="edge_predicate_raw">refer</data><data key="edge_assertion_id">a_06a864f776f48c07</data><data key="edge_source_id">S52</data><data key="edge_source_url">https://www.first.org/cvss/v3.1/specification-document</data><data key="edge_chunk_id">S52_C04</data><data key="edge_json_path">None</data><data key="edge_evidence">As previously mentioned, the Exploitability metrics reflect the characteristics of the thing that is vulnerable, which we refer to formally as the vulnerable component</data><data key="edge_extraction_method">minie</data><data key="edge_polarity">positive</data><data key="edge_modality">asserted</data></edge><edge id="oe_f2ed13d75a16df3a" source="e_c00a4051d0530e03" target="e_7105a374c44c5518"><data key="edge_predicate_raw">reflect characteristics of thing As</data><data key="edge_assertion_id">a_579f6a321cd4dc08</data><data key="edge_source_id">S52</data><data key="edge_source_url">https://www.first.org/cvss/v3.1/specification-document</data><data key="edge_chunk_id">S52_C04</data><data key="edge_json_path">None</data><data key="edge_evidence">As previously mentioned, the Exploitability metrics reflect the characteristics of the thing that is vulnerable, which we refer to formally as the vulnerable component</data><data key="edge_extraction_method">minie</data><data key="edge_polarity">positive</data><data key="edge_modality">asserted</data></edge><edge id="oe_a4f4693053d90017" source="e_c00a4051d0530e03" target="e_2f5c3d09f4bbc7c9"><data key="edge_predicate_raw">reflect characteristics of</data><data key="edge_assertion_id">a_93027b9f02e70971</data><data key="edge_source_id">S52</data><data key="edge_source_url">https://www.first.org/cvss/v3.1/specification-document</data><data key="edge_chunk_id">S52_C04</data><data key="edge_json_path">None</data><data key="edge_evidence">As previously mentioned, the Exploitability metrics reflect the characteristics of the thing that is vulnerable, which we refer to formally as the vulnerable component</data><data key="edge_extraction_method">minie</data><data key="edge_polarity">positive</data><data key="edge_modality">asserted</data></edge><edge id="oe_92ec6bf662b4ce51" source="e_dbd1ba0cc63988dc" target="e_2676df0405400172"><data key="edge_predicate_raw">lead to</data><data key="edge_assertion_id">a_4e59ab24ff29bb43</data><data key="edge_source_id">S52</data><data key="edge_source_url">https://www.first.org/cvss/v3.1/specification-document</data><data key="edge_chunk_id">S52_C04</data><data key="edge_json_path">None</data><data key="edge_evidence">Therefore, each of the Exploitability metrics listed below should be scored relative to the vulnerable component, and reflect the properties of the vulnerability that lead to a successful attack</data><data key="edge_extraction_method">minie</data><data key="edge_polarity">positive</data><data key="edge_modality">asserted</data></edge><edge id="oe_0406cf442d36cd6b" source="e_ad16450d4d7b98f8" target="e_80b852b98e6b518c"><data key="edge_predicate_raw">be scoring</data><data key="edge_assertion_id">a_058555d48072c882</data><data key="edge_source_id">S52</data><data key="edge_source_url">https://www.first.org/cvss/v3.1/specification-document</data><data key="edge_chunk_id">S52_C04</data><data key="edge_json_path">None</data><data key="edge_evidence">When scoring Base metrics, it should be assumed that the attacker has advanced knowledge of the weaknesses of the target system, including general configuration and default defense mechanisms (e.g., built-in firewalls, rate limits, traffic policing)</data><data key="edge_extraction_method">minie</data><data key="edge_polarity">positive</data><data key="edge_modality">asserted</data></edge><edge id="oe_d3a269cc8d613c33" source="e_537e6ab50e8f2e44" target="e_f010684a824b5984"><data key="edge_predicate_raw">has advanced</data><data key="edge_assertion_id">a_2aab091fb2597abf</data><data key="edge_source_id">S52</data><data key="edge_source_url">https://www.first.org/cvss/v3.1/specification-document</data><data key="edge_chunk_id">S52_C04</data><data key="edge_json_path">None</data><data key="edge_evidence">When scoring Base metrics, it should be assumed that the attacker has advanced knowledge of the weaknesses of the target system, including general configuration and default defense mechanisms (e.g., built-in firewalls, rate limits, traffic policing)</data><data key="edge_extraction_method">minie</data><data key="edge_polarity">positive</data><data key="edge_modality">asserted</data></edge><edge id="oe_aa34aadd3def2757" source="e_537e6ab50e8f2e44" target="e_5b3274220e6c2888"><data key="edge_predicate_raw">has advanced</data><data key="edge_assertion_id">a_cf13e94b31fc0577</data><data key="edge_source_id">S52</data><data key="edge_source_url">https://www.first.org/cvss/v3.1/specification-document</data><data key="edge_chunk_id">S52_C04</data><data key="edge_json_path">None</data><data key="edge_evidence">When scoring Base metrics, it should be assumed that the attacker has advanced knowledge of the weaknesses of the target system, including general configuration and default defense mechanisms (e.g., built-in firewalls, rate limits, traffic policing)</data><data key="edge_extraction_method">minie</data><data key="edge_polarity">positive</data><data key="edge_modality">asserted</data></edge><edge id="oe_cdb00d74041d362d" source="e_dbd1ba0cc63988dc" target="e_b8ee2c28df4dc72b"><data key="edge_predicate_raw">results in</data><data key="edge_assertion_id">a_661247cda7ef1efc</data><data key="edge_source_id">S52</data><data key="edge_source_url">https://www.first.org/cvss/v3.1/specification-document</data><data key="edge_chunk_id">S52_C04</data><data key="edge_json_path">None</data><data key="edge_evidence">For example, exploiting a vulnerability that results in repeatable, deterministic success should still be considered a Low value for Attack Complexity, independent of the attacker's knowledge or capabilities</data><data key="edge_extraction_method">minie</data><data key="edge_polarity">positive</data><data key="edge_modality">asserted</data></edge><edge id="oe_7cecc8b4bdd5c608" source="e_d76f0b71c9538da5" target="e_5ad6c123e5abaf11"><data key="edge_predicate_raw">be considered Low value for Attack Complexity independent of attacker 's knowledge For</data><data key="edge_assertion_id">a_3be404dad8122c54</data><data key="edge_source_id">S52</data><data key="edge_source_url">https://www.first.org/cvss/v3.1/specification-document</data><data key="edge_chunk_id">S52_C04</data><data key="edge_json_path">None</data><data key="edge_evidence">For example, exploiting a vulnerability that results in repeatable, deterministic success should still be considered a Low value for Attack Complexity, independent of the attacker's knowledge or capabilities</data><data key="edge_extraction_method">minie</data><data key="edge_polarity">positive</data><data key="edge_modality">asserted</data></edge><edge id="oe_f2afae4c86bdc462" source="e_d76f0b71c9538da5" target="e_5ad6c123e5abaf11"><data key="edge_predicate_raw">be considered Low value for Attack Complexity independent of capabilities For</data><data key="edge_assertion_id">a_1dbf3dac167294f8</data><data key="edge_source_id">S52</data><data key="edge_source_url">https://www.first.org/cvss/v3.1/specification-document</data><data key="edge_chunk_id">S52_C04</data><data key="edge_json_path">None</data><data key="edge_evidence">For example, exploiting a vulnerability that results in repeatable, deterministic success should still be considered a Low value for Attack Complexity, independent of the attacker's knowledge or capabilities</data><data key="edge_extraction_method">minie</data><data key="edge_polarity">positive</data><data key="edge_modality">asserted</data></edge><edge id="oe_234ce8ddf027cc51" source="e_d76f0b71c9538da5" target="e_fcae9732e4e96feb"><data key="edge_predicate_raw">be considered</data><data key="edge_assertion_id">a_dbd79c570074492c</data><data key="edge_source_id">S52</data><data key="edge_source_url">https://www.first.org/cvss/v3.1/specification-document</data><data key="edge_chunk_id">S52_C04</data><data key="edge_json_path">None</data><data key="edge_evidence">For example, exploiting a vulnerability that results in repeatable, deterministic success should still be considered a Low value for Attack Complexity, independent of the attacker's knowledge or capabilities</data><data key="edge_extraction_method">minie</data><data key="edge_polarity">positive</data><data key="edge_modality">asserted</data></edge><edge id="oe_fa213a4d164e48b6" source="e_d76f0b71c9538da5" target="e_454f93ad983bcfc4"><data key="edge_predicate_raw">be considered</data><data key="edge_assertion_id">a_3175712753929313</data><data key="edge_source_id">S52</data><data key="edge_source_url">https://www.first.org/cvss/v3.1/specification-document</data><data key="edge_chunk_id">S52_C04</data><data key="edge_json_path">None</data><data key="edge_evidence">For example, exploiting a vulnerability that results in repeatable, deterministic success should still be considered a Low value for Attack Complexity, independent of the attacker's knowledge or capabilities</data><data key="edge_extraction_method">minie</data><data key="edge_polarity">positive</data><data key="edge_modality">asserted</data></edge><edge id="oe_5ad6679169a76f90" source="e_df25c9975e563a89" target="e_c00ecbf5fe9852a6"><data key="edge_predicate_raw">be reflected</data><data key="edge_assertion_id">a_2c851c364a11aabc</data><data key="edge_source_id">S52</data><data key="edge_source_url">https://www.first.org/cvss/v3.1/specification-document</data><data key="edge_chunk_id">S52_C04</data><data key="edge_json_path">None</data><data key="edge_evidence">Furthermore, target-specific attack mitigation (e.g., custom firewall filters, access lists) should instead be reflected in the Environmental metric scoring group</data><data key="edge_extraction_method">minie</data><data key="edge_polarity">positive</data><data key="edge_modality">asserted</data></edge><edge id="oe_389599e902ab1c84" source="e_df25c9975e563a89" target="e_0aef75c4b33ae9e2"><data key="edge_predicate_raw">be reflected e.g. in</data><data key="edge_assertion_id">a_5afcc6a3d1779a4b</data><data key="edge_source_id">S52</data><data key="edge_source_url">https://www.first.org/cvss/v3.1/specification-document</data><data key="edge_chunk_id">S52_C04</data><data key="edge_json_path">None</data><data key="edge_evidence">Furthermore, target-specific attack mitigation (e.g., custom firewall filters, access lists) should instead be reflected in the Environmental metric scoring group</data><data key="edge_extraction_method">minie</data><data key="edge_polarity">positive</data><data key="edge_modality">asserted</data></edge><edge id="oe_9adcc31e4685aee4" source="e_311023198a64814b" target="e_c00ecbf5fe9852a6"><data key="edge_predicate_raw">be reflected in Environmental metric scoring group</data><data key="edge_assertion_id">a_4747f522d8dd7cd4</data><data key="edge_source_id">S52</data><data key="edge_source_url">https://www.first.org/cvss/v3.1/specification-document</data><data key="edge_chunk_id">S52_C04</data><data key="edge_json_path">None</data><data key="edge_evidence">Furthermore, target-specific attack mitigation (e.g., custom firewall filters, access lists) should instead be reflected in the Environmental metric scoring group</data><data key="edge_extraction_method">minie</data><data key="edge_polarity">positive</data><data key="edge_modality">asserted</data></edge><edge id="oe_c0fc9e8b8a249c9f" source="e_311023198a64814b" target="e_0aef75c4b33ae9e2"><data key="edge_predicate_raw">be reflected in</data><data key="edge_assertion_id">a_314bc28f12d3bb5b</data><data key="edge_source_id">S52</data><data key="edge_source_url">https://www.first.org/cvss/v3.1/specification-document</data><data key="edge_chunk_id">S52_C04</data><data key="edge_json_path">None</data><data key="edge_evidence">Furthermore, target-specific attack mitigation (e.g., custom firewall filters, access lists) should instead be reflected in the Environmental metric scoring group</data><data key="edge_extraction_method">minie</data><data key="edge_polarity">positive</data><data key="edge_modality">asserted</data></edge><edge id="oe_a911ec61235f9716" source="e_213a633d7417fc58" target="e_5b24a8af5bcdf837"><data key="edge_predicate_raw">is required</data><data key="edge_assertion_id">a_badf88d8dfd21f98</data><data key="edge_source_id">S52</data><data key="edge_source_url">https://www.first.org/cvss/v3.1/specification-document</data><data key="edge_chunk_id">S52_C04</data><data key="edge_json_path">None</data><data key="edge_evidence">Specific configurations should not impact any attribute contributing to the CVSS Base Score, i.e., if a specific configuration is required for an attack to succeed, the vulnerable component should be scored assuming it is in that configuration</data><data key="edge_extraction_method">heuristic</data><data key="edge_polarity">negative</data><data key="edge_modality">asserted</data></edge><edge id="oe_1c05539d978ee3bb" source="e_4676679afd99eed0" target="e_466e6377cc3c1257"><data key="edge_predicate_raw">reflects</data><data key="edge_assertion_id">a_34079e02ba8aaa5c</data><data key="edge_source_id">S52</data><data key="edge_source_url">https://www.first.org/cvss/v3.1/specification-document</data><data key="edge_chunk_id">S52_C04</data><data key="edge_json_path">None</data><data key="edge_evidence">This metric reflects the context by which vulnerability exploitation is possible</data><data key="edge_extraction_method">minie</data><data key="edge_polarity">positive</data><data key="edge_modality">possible</data></edge><edge id="oe_6a7e5f9226f069c6" source="e_0704f64e3b0446e8" target="e_0651ca14b1e582f2"><data key="edge_predicate_raw">be in to exploit</data><data key="edge_assertion_id">a_1fc8b01a5eb47a9f</data><data key="edge_source_id">S52</data><data key="edge_source_url">https://www.first.org/cvss/v3.1/specification-document</data><data key="edge_chunk_id">S52_C04</data><data key="edge_json_path">None</data><data key="edge_evidence">This metric value (and consequently the Base Score) will be larger the more remote (logically, and physically) an attacker can be in order to exploit the vulnerable component</data><data key="edge_extraction_method">minie</data><data key="edge_polarity">positive</data><data key="edge_modality">possible</data></edge><edge id="oe_36574beeba739e7d" source="e_dbd1ba0cc63988dc" target="e_571bc10d653316b8"><data key="edge_predicate_raw">be exploited from across</data><data key="edge_assertion_id">a_5dd77c079a90b27e</data><data key="edge_source_id">S52</data><data key="edge_source_url">https://www.first.org/cvss/v3.1/specification-document</data><data key="edge_chunk_id">S52_C04</data><data key="edge_json_path">None</data><data key="edge_evidence">The assumption is that the number of potential attackers for a vulnerability that could be exploited from across a network is larger than the number of potential attackers that could exploit a vulnerability requiring physical access to a device, and therefore warrants a greater Base Score</data><data key="edge_extraction_method">minie</data><data key="edge_polarity">positive</data><data key="edge_modality">possible</data></edge><edge id="oe_aae49b0d752d3998" source="e_6c929bb8a42a9b8c" target="e_b4e364ab91d013d5"><data key="edge_predicate_raw">is larger than number of</data><data key="edge_assertion_id">a_7c29b4b77cb61b55</data><data key="edge_source_id">S52</data><data key="edge_source_url">https://www.first.org/cvss/v3.1/specification-document</data><data key="edge_chunk_id">S52_C04</data><data key="edge_json_path">None</data><data key="edge_evidence">The assumption is that the number of potential attackers for a vulnerability that could be exploited from across a network is larger than the number of potential attackers that could exploit a vulnerability requiring physical access to a device, and therefore warrants a greater Base Score</data><data key="edge_extraction_method">minie</data><data key="edge_polarity">positive</data><data key="edge_modality">possible</data></edge><edge id="oe_dba4daeb3124e887" source="e_6c929bb8a42a9b8c" target="e_1abffb155679e04c"><data key="edge_predicate_raw">warrants</data><data key="edge_assertion_id">a_64dffa10ad6dce44</data><data key="edge_source_id">S52</data><data key="edge_source_url">https://www.first.org/cvss/v3.1/specification-document</data><data key="edge_chunk_id">S52_C04</data><data key="edge_json_path">None</data><data key="edge_evidence">The assumption is that the number of potential attackers for a vulnerability that could be exploited from across a network is larger than the number of potential attackers that could exploit a vulnerability requiring physical access to a device, and therefore warrants a greater Base Score</data><data key="edge_extraction_method">minie</data><data key="edge_polarity">positive</data><data key="edge_modality">possible</data></edge><edge id="oe_3edf5cc4d18c1dd0" source="e_b4e364ab91d013d5" target="e_684abf44