dge_json_path">None</data><data key="edge_evidence">This can mean an attack must be launched from the same shared physical (e.g., Bluetooth or IEEE 802.11) or logical (e.g., local IP subnet) network, or from within a secure or otherwise limited administrative domain (e.g., MPLS, secure VPN to an administrative network zone)</data><data key="edge_extraction_method">minie</data><data key="edge_polarity">positive</data><data key="edge_modality">possible</data></edge><edge id="oe_7681928fc78da825" source="e_e163460c91338b08" target="e_6130283655ec203c"><data key="edge_predicate_raw">mean from within</data><data key="edge_assertion_id">a_5b42df66d0e436de</data><data key="edge_source_id">S52</data><data key="edge_source_url">https://www.first.org/cvss/v3.1/specification-document</data><data key="edge_chunk_id">S52_C05</data><data key="edge_json_path">None</data><data key="edge_evidence">This can mean an attack must be launched from the same shared physical (e.g., Bluetooth or IEEE 802.11) or logical (e.g., local IP subnet) network, or from within a secure or otherwise limited administrative domain (e.g., MPLS, secure VPN to an administrative network zone)</data><data key="edge_extraction_method">minie</data><data key="edge_polarity">positive</data><data key="edge_modality">possible</data></edge><edge id="oe_9d87bc3257369706" source="e_9bf6ead54114b2ce" target="e_32ac150c7b7e742f"><data key="edge_predicate_raw">be launched from</data><data key="edge_assertion_id">a_81b5e22a6eccd66a</data><data key="edge_source_id">S52</data><data key="edge_source_url">https://www.first.org/cvss/v3.1/specification-document</data><data key="edge_chunk_id">S52_C05</data><data key="edge_json_path">None</data><data key="edge_evidence">This can mean an attack must be launched from the same shared physical (e.g., Bluetooth or IEEE 802.11) or logical (e.g., local IP subnet) network, or from within a secure or otherwise limited administrative domain (e.g., MPLS, secure VPN to an administrative network zone)</data><data key="edge_extraction_method">minie</data><data key="edge_polarity">positive</data><data key="edge_modality">possible</data></edge><edge id="oe_14d8bcbf4e7f41a0" source="e_9bf6ead54114b2ce" target="e_fdc1a10ff63ad4b3"><data key="edge_predicate_raw">be launched from</data><data key="edge_assertion_id">a_a66eee96bd717df7</data><data key="edge_source_id">S52</data><data key="edge_source_url">https://www.first.org/cvss/v3.1/specification-document</data><data key="edge_chunk_id">S52_C05</data><data key="edge_json_path">None</data><data key="edge_evidence">This can mean an attack must be launched from the same shared physical (e.g., Bluetooth or IEEE 802.11) or logical (e.g., local IP subnet) network, or from within a secure or otherwise limited administrative domain (e.g., MPLS, secure VPN to an administrative network zone)</data><data key="edge_extraction_method">minie</data><data key="edge_polarity">positive</data><data key="edge_modality">possible</data></edge><edge id="oe_33c019c5832a509e" source="e_9bf6ead54114b2ce" target="e_e85c55da35560a77"><data key="edge_predicate_raw">be launched from</data><data key="edge_assertion_id">a_be54fc63a68c18ca</data><data key="edge_source_id">S52</data><data key="edge_source_url">https://www.first.org/cvss/v3.1/specification-document</data><data key="edge_chunk_id">S52_C05</data><data key="edge_json_path">None</data><data key="edge_evidence">This can mean an attack must be launched from the same shared physical (e.g., Bluetooth or IEEE 802.11) or logical (e.g., local IP subnet) network, or from within a secure or otherwise limited administrative domain (e.g., MPLS, secure VPN to an administrative network zone)</data><data key="edge_extraction_method">minie</data><data key="edge_polarity">positive</data><data key="edge_modality">possible</data></edge><edge id="oe_598124ed8c0ed793" source="e_9bf6ead54114b2ce" target="e_d492cfe3ad61e27e"><data key="edge_predicate_raw">be launched over</data><data key="edge_assertion_id">a_e1f1cbf19f2bf488</data><data key="edge_source_id">S52</data><data key="edge_source_url">https://www.first.org/cvss/v3.1/specification-document</data><data key="edge_chunk_id">S52_C05</data><data key="edge_json_path">None</data><data key="edge_evidence">Scoring Guidance: When deciding between Network and Adjacent, if an attack can be launched over a wide area network or from outside the logically adjacent administrative network domain, use Network</data><data key="edge_extraction_method">minie</data><data key="edge_polarity">positive</data><data key="edge_modality">possible</data></edge><edge id="oe_d6004173e1be9826" source="e_9bf6ead54114b2ce" target="e_e299850b57d85a43"><data key="edge_predicate_raw">be launched from outside</data><data key="edge_assertion_id">a_a153f3f570d82944</data><data key="edge_source_id">S52</data><data key="edge_source_url">https://www.first.org/cvss/v3.1/specification-document</data><data key="edge_chunk_id">S52_C05</data><data key="edge_json_path">None</data><data key="edge_evidence">Scoring Guidance: When deciding between Network and Adjacent, if an attack can be launched over a wide area network or from outside the logically adjacent administrative network domain, use Network</data><data key="edge_extraction_method">minie</data><data key="edge_polarity">positive</data><data key="edge_modality">possible</data></edge><edge id="oe_a362f88c56ea4a7d" source="e_537e6ab50e8f2e44" target="e_dbd1ba0cc63988dc"><data key="edge_predicate_raw">exploit</data><data key="edge_assertion_id">a_25602ff3927912ae</data><data key="edge_source_id">S52</data><data key="edge_source_url">https://www.first.org/cvss/v3.1/specification-document</data><data key="edge_chunk_id">S52_C05</data><data key="edge_json_path">None</data><data key="edge_evidence">Network should be used even if the attacker is required to be on the same intranet to exploit the vulnerable system (e.g., the attacker can only exploit the vulnerability from inside a corporate network)</data><data key="edge_extraction_method">minie</data><data key="edge_polarity">positive</data><data key="edge_modality">possible</data></edge><edge id="oe_8d007c5106eb378d" source="e_537e6ab50e8f2e44" target="e_f2cc395935e11daa"><data key="edge_predicate_raw">exploit vulnerability from inside</data><data key="edge_assertion_id">a_20186bbcf1ab4091</data><data key="edge_source_id">S52</data><data key="edge_source_url">https://www.first.org/cvss/v3.1/specification-document</data><data key="edge_chunk_id">S52_C05</data><data key="edge_json_path">None</data><data key="edge_evidence">Network should be used even if the attacker is required to be on the same intranet to exploit the vulnerable system (e.g., the attacker can only exploit the vulnerability from inside a corporate network)</data><data key="edge_extraction_method">minie</data><data key="edge_polarity">positive</data><data key="edge_modality">possible</data></edge><edge id="oe_9653a0cb3fe5d9b0" source="e_537e6ab50e8f2e44" target="e_604f9d94669df251"><data key="edge_predicate_raw">is required to be on</data><data key="edge_assertion_id">a_60f15575778dd32d</data><data key="edge_source_id">S52</data><data key="edge_source_url">https://www.first.org/cvss/v3.1/specification-document</data><data key="edge_chunk_id">S52_C05</data><data key="edge_json_path">None</data><data key="edge_evidence">Network should be used even if the attacker is required to be on the same intranet to exploit the vulnerable system (e.g., the attacker can only exploit the vulnerability from inside a corporate network)</data><data key="edge_extraction_method">minie</data><data key="edge_polarity">positive</data><data key="edge_modality">possible</data></edge><edge id="oe_ccf99fe1e8881dd3" source="e_537e6ab50e8f2e44" target="e_7ee1ff4a70457dd7"><data key="edge_predicate_raw">is required to be to exploit</data><data key="edge_assertion_id">a_50082d412b256d61</data><data key="edge_source_id">S52</data><data key="edge_source_url">https://www.first.org/cvss/v3.1/specification-document</data><data key="edge_chunk_id">S52_C05</data><data key="edge_json_path">None</data><data key="edge_evidence">Network should be used even if the attacker is required to be on the same intranet to exploit the vulnerable system (e.g., the attacker can only exploit the vulnerability from inside a corporate network)</data><data key="edge_extraction_method">minie</data><data key="edge_polarity">positive</data><data key="edge_modality">possible</data></edge><edge id="oe_3d759b97d1e51eee" source="e_4676679afd99eed0" target="e_6222cbe778251f55"><data key="edge_predicate_raw">describes conditions beyond</data><data key="edge_assertion_id">a_5650553ae884ceb3</data><data key="edge_source_id">S52</data><data key="edge_source_url">https://www.first.org/cvss/v3.1/specification-document</data><data key="edge_chunk_id">S52_C05</data><data key="edge_json_path">None</data><data key="edge_evidence">This metric describes the conditions beyond the attacker’s control that must exist in order to exploit the vulnerability</data><data key="edge_extraction_method">minie</data><data key="edge_polarity">positive</data><data key="edge_modality">asserted</data></edge><edge id="oe_106a0bbf4df9f41a" source="e_f18bdb19e94ba6dc" target="e_dbd1ba0cc63988dc"><data key="edge_predicate_raw">exist in to exploit</data><data key="edge_assertion_id">a_e96941bfc1578eec</data><data key="edge_source_id">S52</data><data key="edge_source_url">https://www.first.org/cvss/v3.1/specification-document</data><data key="edge_chunk_id">S52_C05</data><data key="edge_json_path">None</data><data key="edge_evidence">This metric describes the conditions beyond the attacker’s control that must exist in order to exploit the vulnerability</data><data key="edge_extraction_method">minie</data><data key="edge_polarity">positive</data><data key="edge_modality">asserted</data></edge><edge id="oe_c1ac619d75a1d645" source="e_67850df17ab6ea20" target="e_01558e47b2eef8dd"><data key="edge_predicate_raw">require</data><data key="edge_assertion_id">a_ac97c9151afc43f4</data><data key="edge_source_id">S52</data><data key="edge_source_url">https://www.first.org/cvss/v3.1/specification-document</data><data key="edge_chunk_id">S52_C05</data><data key="edge_json_path">None</data><data key="edge_evidence">As described below, such conditions may require the collection of more information about the target, or computational exceptions</data><data key="edge_extraction_method">minie</data><data key="edge_polarity">positive</data><data key="edge_modality">possible</data></edge><edge id="oe_8e525616a251f4c2" source="e_67850df17ab6ea20" target="e_7c2ea70eaaaaf7b7"><data key="edge_predicate_raw">require</data><data key="edge_assertion_id">a_c189476cb4151ec8</data><data key="edge_source_id">S52</data><data key="edge_source_url">https://www.first.org/cvss/v3.1/specification-document</data><data key="edge_chunk_id">S52_C05</data><data key="edge_json_path">None</data><data key="edge_evidence">As described below, such conditions may require the collection of more information about the target, or computational exceptions</data><data key="edge_extraction_method">minie</data><data key="edge_polarity">positive</data><data key="edge_modality">possible</data></edge><edge id="oe_157ce534290858b2" source="e_67850df17ab6ea20" target="e_45df5fa9df2f731e"><data key="edge_predicate_raw">are captured in</data><data key="edge_assertion_id">a_3d507751a6e2430b</data><data key="edge_source_id">S52</data><data key="edge_source_url">https://www.first.org/cvss/v3.1/specification-document</data><data key="edge_chunk_id">S52_C05</data><data key="edge_json_path">None</data><data key="edge_evidence">Importantly, the assessment of this metric excludes any requirements for user interaction in order to exploit the vulnerability (such conditions are captured in the User Interaction metric)</data><data key="edge_extraction_method">minie</data><data key="edge_polarity">positive</data><data key="edge_modality">asserted</data></edge><edge id="oe_bc492a3123919e1b" source="e_213a633d7417fc58" target="e_70d08b8077a5c72d"><data key="edge_predicate_raw">is required</data><data key="edge_assertion_id">a_925d534ac6cd1f9a</data><data key="edge_source_id">S52</data><data key="edge_source_url">https://www.first.org/cvss/v3.1/specification-document</data><data key="edge_chunk_id">S52_C05</data><data key="edge_json_path">None</data><data key="edge_evidence">If a specific configuration is required for an attack to succeed, the Base metrics should be scored assuming the vulnerable component is in that configuration</data><data key="edge_extraction_method">heuristic</data><data key="edge_polarity">positive</data><data key="edge_modality">asserted</data></edge><edge id="oe_8f80cda478214104" source="e_5dd63c0e6e0c1501" target="e_f3607712f3b4d57b"><data key="edge_predicate_raw">is greatest for</data><data key="edge_assertion_id">a_a9883cd151fa39f8</data><data key="edge_source_id">S52</data><data key="edge_source_url">https://www.first.org/cvss/v3.1/specification-document</data><data key="edge_chunk_id">S52_C05</data><data key="edge_json_path">None</data><data key="edge_evidence">The Base Score is greatest for the least complex attacks</data><data key="edge_extraction_method">minie</data><data key="edge_polarity">positive</data><data key="edge_modality">asserted</data></edge><edge id="oe_e51797fa9abb21af" source="e_4f92e23ebdc6fffe" target="e_76edc2bdd4022652"><data key="edge_predicate_raw">is outside scope of</data><data key="edge_assertion_id">a_19fb27acda5b7b37</data><data key="edge_source_id">S52</data><data key="edge_source_url">https://www.first.org/cvss/v3.1/specification-document</data><data key="edge_chunk_id">S52_C06</data><data key="edge_json_path">None</data><data key="edge_evidence">As described in Section 2.1, detailed knowledge of the vulnerable component is outside the scope of Attack Complexity</data><data key="edge_extraction_method">minie</data><data key="edge_polarity">positive</data><data key="edge_modality">asserted</data></edge><edge id="oe_4c825dad9ec94b0d" source="e_4676679afd99eed0" target="e_1b50c049dec6c218"><data key="edge_predicate_raw">describes level of</data><data key="edge_assertion_id">a_1d3b0821492c9f6c</data><data key="edge_source_id">S52</data><data key="edge_source_url">https://www.first.org/cvss/v3.1/specification-document</data><data key="edge_chunk_id">S52_C06</data><data key="edge_json_path">None</data><data key="edge_evidence">This metric describes the level of privileges an attacker must possess before successfully exploiting the vulnerability</data><data key="edge_extraction_method">minie</data><data key="edge_polarity">positive</data><data key="edge_modality">asserted</data></edge><edge id="oe_b964185c1615bc90" source="e_537e6ab50e8f2e44" target="e_1b50c049dec6c218"><data key="edge_predicate_raw">possess before exploiting vulnerability</data><data key="edge_assertion_id">a_36930d6dbbec82a5</data><data key="edge_source_id">S52</data><data key="edge_source_url">https://www.first.org/cvss/v3.1/specification-document</data><data key="edge_chunk_id">S52_C06</data><data key="edge_json_path">None</data><data key="edge_evidence">This metric describes the level of privileges an attacker must possess before successfully exploiting the vulnerability</data><data key="edge_extraction_method">minie</data><data key="edge_polarity">positive</data><data key="edge_modality">asserted</data></edge><edge id="oe_4dfdb1b9c5c82d00" source="e_537e6ab50e8f2e44" target="e_1b50c049dec6c218"><data key="edge_predicate_raw">possess</data><data key="edge_assertion_id">a_c742b971babba7b0</data><data key="edge_source_id">S52</data><data key="edge_source_url">https://www.first.org/cvss/v3.1/specification-document</data><data key="edge_chunk_id">S52_C06</data><data key="edge_json_path">None</data><data key="edge_evidence">This metric describes the level of privileges an attacker must possess before successfully exploiting the vulnerability</data><data key="edge_extraction_method">minie</data><data key="edge_polarity">positive</data><data key="edge_modality">asserted</data></edge><edge id="oe_a505c9976f7de08e" source="e_1b50c049dec6c218" target="e_4b32a6da9f7ed0c2"><data key="edge_predicate_raw">Required</data><data key="edge_assertion_id">a_fcb660cf81fa897a</data><data key="edge_source_id">S52</data><data key="edge_source_url">https://www.first.org/cvss/v3.1/specification-document</data><data key="edge_chunk_id">S52_C06</data><data key="edge_json_path">None</data><data key="edge_evidence">Scoring Guidance: Privileges Required is usually None for hard-coded credential vulnerabilities or vulnerabilities requiring social engineering (e.g., reflected cross-site scripting, cross-site request forgery, or file parsing vulnerability in a PDF reader)</data><data key="edge_extraction_method">heuristic</data><data key="edge_polarity">positive</data><data key="edge_modality">asserted</data></edge><edge id="oe_cdf403afc04d28a2" source="e_4676679afd99eed0" target="e_dec2edef719a5775"><data key="edge_predicate_raw">captures</data><data key="edge_assertion_id">a_a5cbf1d50550f373</data><data key="edge_source_id">S52</data><data key="edge_source_url">https://www.first.org/cvss/v3.1/specification-document</data><data key="edge_chunk_id">S52_C06</data><data key="edge_json_path">None</data><data key="edge_evidence">This metric captures the requirement for a human user, other than the attacker, to participate in the successful compromise of the vulnerable component</data><data key="edge_extraction_method">minie</data><data key="edge_polarity">positive</data><data key="edge_modality">asserted</data></edge><edge id="oe_11e6a0896b71a452" source="e_06cebb65494ded95" target="e_537e6ab50e8f2e44"><data key="edge_predicate_raw">is other than</data><data key="edge_assertion_id">a_533b6b2bce4d7e24</data><data key="edge_source_id">S52</data><data key="edge_source_url">https://www.first.org/cvss/v3.1/specification-document</data><data key="edge_chunk_id">S52_C06</data><data key="edge_json_path">None</data><data key="edge_evidence">This metric captures the requirement for a human user, other than the attacker, to participate in the successful compromise of the vulnerable component</data><data key="edge_extraction_method">minie</data><data key="edge_polarity">positive</data><data key="edge_modality">asserted</data></edge><edge id="oe_c84e0c6f353d1f0d" source="e_8bb0cd6b7b68cd93" target="e_0651ca14b1e582f2"><data key="edge_predicate_raw">be participate in successful compromise of</data><data key="edge_assertion_id">a_8260b9a530d802ce</data><data key="edge_source_id">S52</data><data key="edge_source_url">https://www.first.org/cvss/v3.1/specification-document</data><data key="edge_chunk_id">S52_C06</data><data key="edge_json_path">None</data><data key="edge_evidence">This metric captures the requirement for a human user, other than the attacker, to participate in the successful compromise of the vulnerable component</data><data key="edge_extraction_method">minie</data><data key="edge_polarity">positive</data><data key="edge_modality">asserted</data></edge><edge id="oe_85186c95841a1a8d" source="e_dbd1ba0cc63988dc" target="e_537e6ab50e8f2e44"><data key="edge_predicate_raw">be exploited at will of</data><data key="edge_assertion_id">a_8c66ff3005c30eb5</data><data key="edge_source_id">S52</data><data key="edge_source_url">https://www.first.org/cvss/v3.1/specification-document</data><data key="edge_chunk_id">S52_C06</data><data key="edge_json_path">None</data><data key="edge_evidence">This metric determines whether the vulnerability can be exploited solely at the will of the attacker, or whether a separate user (or user-initiated process) must participate in some manner</data><data key="edge_extraction_method">minie</data><data key="edge_polarity">positive</data><data key="edge_modality">possible</data></edge><edge id="oe_475158b0efd2e299" source="e_dbd1ba0cc63988dc" target="e_060bbd297383d5a7"><data key="edge_predicate_raw">be exploited</data><data key="edge_assertion_id">a_2420c9bb14066a34</data><data key="edge_source_id">S52</data><data key="edge_source_url">https://www.first.org/cvss/v3.1/specification-document</data><data key="edge_chunk_id">S52_C06</data><data key="edge_json_path">None</data><data key="edge_evidence">This metric determines whether the vulnerability can be exploited solely at the will of the attacker, or whether a separate user (or user-initiated process) must participate in some manner</data><data key="edge_extraction_method">minie</data><data key="edge_polarity">positive</data><data key="edge_modality">possible</data></edge><edge id="oe_f3b16e92b31d99f9" source="e_e9457e2b248d9c8e" target="e_5868de2faeea5cad"><data key="edge_predicate_raw">enforces</data><data key="edge_assertion_id">a_921db5dac18150b2</data><data key="edge_source_id">S52</data><data key="edge_source_url">https://www.first.org/cvss/v3.1/specification-document</data><data key="edge_chunk_id">S52_C07</data><data key="edge_json_path">None</data><data key="edge_evidence">Formally, a security authority is a mechanism (e.g., an application, an operating system, firmware, a sandbox environment) that defines and enforces access control in terms of how certain subjects/actors (e.g., human users, processes) can access certain restricted objects/resources (e.g., files, CPU, memory) in a controlled manner</data><data key="edge_extraction_method">minie</data><data key="edge_polarity">positive</data><data key="edge_modality">possible</data></edge><edge id="oe_a3e49eda21e0c210" source="e_b207b668cde495fa" target="e_aae86f4c23eebd84"><data key="edge_predicate_raw">access certain restricted objects/resources in</data><data key="edge_assertion_id">a_76e8ecb2d7624084</data><data key="edge_source_id">S52</data><data key="edge_source_url">https://www.first.org/cvss/v3.1/specification-document</data><data key="edge_chunk_id">S52_C07</data><data key="edge_json_path">None</data><data key="edge_evidence">Formally, a security authority is a mechanism (e.g., an application, an operating system, firmware, a sandbox environment) that defines and enforces access control in terms of how certain subjects/actors (e.g., human users, processes) can access certain restricted objects/resources (e.g., files, CPU, memory) in a controlled manner</data><data key="edge_extraction_method">minie</data><data key="edge_polarity">positive</data><data key="edge_modality">possible</data></edge><edge id="oe_48dbe8d0be6281e7" source="e_b207b668cde495fa" target="e_21679ea8f030a021"><data key="edge_predicate_raw">access</data><data key="edge_assertion_id">a_ae472d372ac9ee8c</data><data key="edge_source_id">S52</data><data key="edge_source_url">https://www.first.org/cvss/v3.1/specification-document</data><data key="edge_chunk_id">S52_C07</data><data key="edge_json_path">None</data><data key="edge_evidence">Formally, a security authority is a mechanism (e.g., an application, an operating system, firmware, a sandbox environment) that defines and enforces access control in terms of how certain subjects/actors (e.g., human users, processes) can access certain restricted objects/resources (e.g., files, CPU, memory) in a controlled manner</data><data key="edge_extraction_method">minie</data><data key="edge_polarity">positive</data><data key="edge_modality">possible</data></edge><edge id="oe_245e18b135cdc90d" source="e_a2d051a0c8b1e4c0" target="e_c6090a4ef9d48689"><data key="edge_predicate_raw">can affect</data><data key="edge_assertion_id">a_1f37876f325f3122</data><data key="edge_source_id">S52</data><data key="edge_source_url">https://www.first.org/cvss/v3.1/specification-document</data><data key="edge_chunk_id">S52_C07</data><data key="edge_json_path">None</data><data key="edge_evidence">If a vulnerability in a vulnerable component can affect a component which is in a different security scope than the vulnerable component, a Scope change occurs</data><data key="edge_extraction_method">heuristic</data><data key="edge_polarity">positive</data><data key="edge_modality">possible</data></edge><edge id="oe_6c968c0a2d052851" source="e_5a8afa4be03d6fa0" target="e_d33d35b1f0e869ff"><data key="edge_predicate_raw">encompasses</data><data key="edge_assertion_id">a_e98f4f242b505351</data><data key="edge_source_id">S52</data><data key="edge_source_url">https://www.first.org/cvss/v3.1/specification-document</data><data key="edge_chunk_id">S52_C07</data><data key="edge_json_path">None</data><data key="edge_evidence">The security scope of a component encompasses other components that provide functionality solely to that component, even if these other components have their own security authority</data><data key="edge_extraction_method">minie</data><data key="edge_polarity">positive</data><data key="edge_modality">asserted</data></edge><edge id="oe_7d6a271f1f36913b" source="e_d33d35b1f0e869ff" target="e_c9f7ebbebae4fbbf"><data key="edge_predicate_raw">provide</data><data key="edge_assertion_id">a_d8f3b1dd535699ff</data><data key="edge_source_id">S52</data><data key="edge_source_url">https://www.first.org/cvss/v3.1/specification-document</data><data key="edge_chunk_id">S52_C07</data><data key="edge_json_path">None</data><data key="edge_evidence">The security scope of a component encompasses other components that provide functionality solely to that component, even if these other components have their own security authority</data><data key="edge_extraction_method">minie</data><data key="edge_polarity">positive</data><data key="edge_modality">asserted</data></edge><edge id="oe_b2a7398a5e5d017b" source="e_d33d35b1f0e869ff" target="e_7c78e1084fcc7cc8"><data key="edge_predicate_raw">provide functionality to</data><data key="edge_assertion_id">a_2f19ddd449b1e812</data><data key="edge_source_id">S52</data><data key="edge_source_url">https://www.first.org/cvss/v3.1/specification-document</data><data key="edge_chunk_id">S52_C07</data><data key="edge_json_path">None</data><data key="edge_evidence">The security scope of a component encompasses other components that provide functionality solely to that component, even if these other components have their own security authority</data><data key="edge_extraction_method">minie</data><data key="edge_polarity">positive</data><data key="edge_modality">asserted</data></edge><edge id="oe_e9eb505c62e891fa" source="e_57e6975d8ca79e1f" target="e_1a1a19848ea641b6"><data key="edge_predicate_raw">has own security authority</data><data key="edge_assertion_id">a_5465f72735672dd8</data><data key="edge_source_id">S52</data><data key="edge_source_url">https://www.first.org/cvss/v3.1/specification-document</data><data key="edge_chunk_id">S52_C07</data><data key="edge_json_path">None</data><data key="edge_evidence">For example, a database used solely by one application is considered part of that application’s security scope even if the database has its own security authority, e.g., a mechanism controlling access to database records based on database users and associated database privileges</data><data key="edge_extraction_method">minie</data><data key="edge_polarity">positive</data><data key="edge_modality">asserted</data></edge><edge id="oe_25e901a014a46d3d" source="e_c28d390a51760d01" target="e_bf700d4cadb34682"><data key="edge_predicate_raw">be controlling</data><data key="edge_assertion_id">a_bfe95fffc2d83f3e</data><data key="edge_source_id">S52</data><data key="edge_source_url">https://www.first.org/cvss/v3.1/specification-document</data><data key="edge_chunk_id">S52_C07</data><data key="edge_json_path">None</data><data key="edge_evidence">For example, a database used solely by one application is considered part of that application’s security scope even if the database has its own security authority, e.g., a mechanism controlling access to database records based on database users and associated database privileges</data><data key="edge_extraction_method">minie</data><data key="edge_polarity">positive</data><data key="edge_modality">asserted</data></edge><edge id="oe_ef5b1a3fb21dbf89" source="e_57e6975d8ca79e1f" target="e_251515984e7513ef"><data key="edge_predicate_raw">has own security authority</data><data key="edge_assertion_id">a_15c877315d6399ae</data><data key="edge_source_id">S52</data><data key="edge_source_url">https://www.first.org/cvss/v3.1/specification-document</data><data key="edge_chunk_id">S52_C07</data><data key="edge_json_path">None</data><data key="edge_evidence">For example, a database used solely by one application is considered part of that application’s security scope even if the database has its own security authority, e.g., a mechanism controlling access to database records based on database users and associated database privileges</data><data key="edge_extraction_method">minie</data><data key="edge_polarity">positive</data><data key="edge_modality">asserted</data></edge><edge id="oe_87ba1abe2e374b4e" source="e_c28d390a51760d01" target="e_69773b75411107ba"><data key="edge_predicate_raw">be controlling</data><data key="edge_assertion_id">a_718a27f004658f3e</data><data key="edge_source_id">S52</data><data key="edge_source_url">https://www.first.org/cvss/v3.1/specification-document</data><data key="edge_chunk_id">S52_C07</data><data key="edge_json_path">None</data><data key="edge_evidence">For example, a database used solely by one application is considered part of that application’s security scope even if the database has its own security authority, e.g., a mechanism controlling access to database records based on database users and associated database privileges</data><data key="edge_extraction_method">minie</data><data key="edge_polarity">positive</data><data key="edge_modality">asserted</data></edge><edge id="oe_9b9a709d7fbd1f18" source="e_57e6975d8ca79e1f" target="e_060bbd297383d5a7"><data key="edge_predicate_raw">be used</data><data key="edge_assertion_id">a_7807f553478646d3</data><data key="edge_source_id">S52</data><data key="edge_source_url">https://www.first.org/cvss/v3.1/specification-document</data><data key="edge_chunk_id">S52_C07</data><data key="edge_json_path">None</data><data key="edge_evidence">For example, a database used solely by one application is considered part of that application’s security scope even if the database has its own security authority, e.g., a mechanism controlling access to database records based on database users and associated database privileges</data><data key="edge_extraction_method">minie</data><data key="edge_polarity">positive</data><data key="edge_modality">asserted</data></edge><edge id="oe_3687321b43671b03" source="e_75ac4e09b3f2b875" target="e_574f4eefb6751805"><data key="edge_predicate_raw">capture</data><data key="edge_assertion_id">a_920e75d2ddd9fe3d</data><data key="edge_source_id">S52</data><data key="edge_source_url">https://www.first.org/cvss/v3.1/specification-document</data><data key="edge_chunk_id">S52_C07</data><data key="edge_json_path">None</data><data key="edge_evidence">The Impact metrics capture the effects of a successfully exploited vulnerability on the component that suffers the worst outcome that is most directly and predictably associated with the attack</data><data key="edge_extraction_method">minie</data><data key="edge_polarity">positive</data><data key="edge_modality">asserted</data></edge><edge id="oe_eda3113e0afba225" source="e_7c78e1084fcc7cc8" target="e_f6a769ad9aaa74c7"><data key="edge_predicate_raw">suffers</data><data key="edge_assertion_id">a_e37f762d89c7f313</data><data key="edge_source_id">S52</data><data key="edge_source_url">https://www.first.org/cvss/v3.1/specification-document</data><data key="edge_chunk_id">S52_C07</data><data key="edge_json_path">None</data><data key="edge_evidence">The Impact metrics capture the effects of a successfully exploited vulnerability on the component that suffers the worst outcome that is most directly and predictably associated with the attack</data><data key="edge_extraction_method">minie</data><data key="edge_polarity">positive</data><data key="edge_modality">asserted</data></edge><edge id="oe_8fba3282e04129c4" source="e_f6a769ad9aaa74c7" target="e_4ac362a88316741a"><data key="edge_predicate_raw">is associated with attack</data><data key="edge_assertion_id">a_e68008fb18bb3c33</data><data key="edge_source_id">S52</data><data key="edge_source_url">https://www.first.org/cvss/v3.1/specification-document</data><data key="edge_chunk_id">S52_C07</data><data key="edge_json_path">None</data><data key="edge_evidence">The Impact metrics capture the effects of a successfully exploited vulnerability on the component that suffers the worst outcome that is most directly and predictably associated with the attack</data><data key="edge_extraction_method">minie</data><data key="edge_polarity">positive</data><data key="edge_modality">asserted</data></edge><edge id="oe_4aa31178ea85b708" source="e_f6a769ad9aaa74c7" target="e_9bf6ead54114b2ce"><data key="edge_predicate_raw">is associated with</data><data key="edge_assertion_id">a_37e466a26914c6c0</data><data key="edge_source_id">S52</data><data key="edge_source_url">https://www.first.org/cvss/v3.1/specification-document</data><data key="edge_chunk_id">S52_C07</data><data key="edge_json_path">None</data><data key="edge_evidence">The Impact metrics capture the effects of a successfully exploited vulnerability on the component that suffers the worst outcome that is most directly and predictably associated with the attack</data><data key="edge_extraction_method">minie</data><data key="edge_polarity">positive</data><data key="edge_modality">asserted</data></edge><edge id="oe_4deecb39424cd013" source="e_d4cff6070f136c90" target="e_35b2194131dcbc9a"><data key="edge_predicate_raw">constrain impacts to</data><data key="edge_assertion_id">a_d2f32d34ec718e99</data><data key="edge_source_id">S52</data><data key="edge_source_url">https://www.first.org/cvss/v3.1/specification-document</data><data key="edge_chunk_id">S52_C07</data><data key="edge_json_path">None</data><data key="edge_evidence">Analysts should constrain impacts to a reasonable, final outcome which they are confident an attacker is able to achieve</data><data key="edge_extraction_method">minie</data><data key="edge_polarity">positive</data><data key="edge_modality">asserted</data></edge><edge id="oe_e24cb4e38671b7d1" source="e_d4cff6070f136c90" target="e_57598c70746601d2"><data key="edge_predicate_raw">constrain</data><data key="edge_assertion_id">a_56e7d59c0eb9e2a4</data><data key="edge_source_id">S52</data><data key="edge_source_url">https://www.first.org/cvss/v3.1/specification-document</data><data key="edge_chunk_id">S52_C07</data><data key="edge_json_path">None</data><data key="edge_evidence">Analysts should constrain impacts to a reasonable, final outcome which they are confident an attacker is able to achieve</data><data key="edge_extraction_method">minie</data><data key="edge_polarity">positive</data><data key="edge_modality">asserted</data></edge><edge id="oe_0dcb52550696cb12" source="e_ee268ae1243d986c" target="e_4ac362a88316741a"><data key="edge_predicate_raw">is associated with attack</data><data key="edge_assertion_id">a_97b91f5addc04747</data><data key="edge_source_id">S52</data><data key="edge_source_url">https://www.first.org/cvss/v3.1/specification-document</data><data key="edge_chunk_id">S52_C08</data><data key="edge_json_path">None</data><data key="edge_evidence">outcome that is most directly and predictably associated with the attack</data><data key="edge_extraction_method">minie</data><data key="edge_polarity">positive</data><data key="edge_modality">asserted</data></edge><edge id="oe_f6362354eb94b295" source="e_ee268ae1243d986c" target="e_9bf6ead54114b2ce"><data key="edge_predicate_raw">is associated with</data><data key="edge_assertion_id">a_8e908eef68964530</data><data key="edge_source_id">S52</data><data key="edge_source_url">https://www.first.org/cvss/v3.1/specification-document</data><data key="edge_chunk_id">S52_C08</data><data key="edge_json_path">None</data><data key="edge_evidence">outcome that is most directly and predictably associated with the attack</data><data key="edge_extraction_method">minie</data><data key="edge_polarity">positive</data><data key="edge_modality">asserted</data></edge><edge id="oe_d1398652fdfc9395" source="e_5abf948c6bee4fdf" target="e_f3d00477181497a6"><data key="edge_predicate_raw">be able</data><data key="edge_assertion_id">a_ba55a813e31f2b89</data><data key="edge_source_id">S52</data><data key="edge_source_url">https://www.first.org/cvss/v3.1/specification-document</data><data key="edge_chunk_id">S52_C08</data><data key="edge_json_path">None</data><data key="edge_evidence">For example, consider a vulnerability that requires read-only permissions prior to being able to exploit the vulnerability</data><data key="edge_extraction_method">minie</data><data key="edge_polarity">positive</data><data key="edge_modality">asserted</data></edge><edge id="oe_ece9f2c177ff3afb" source="e_dbd1ba0cc63988dc" target="e_f3d00477181497a6"><data key="edge_predicate_raw">requires read-only permissions prior to being</data><data key="edge_assertion_id">a_8d38628e3d33faa5</data><data key="edge_source_id">S52</data><data key="edge_source_url">https://www.first.org/cvss/v3.1/specification-document</data><data key="edge_chunk_id">S52_C08</data><data key="edge_json_path">None</data><data key="edge_evidence">For example, consider a vulnerability that requires read-only permissions prior to being able to exploit the vulnerability</data><data key="edge_extraction_method">minie</data><data key="edge_polarity">positive</data><data key="edge_modality">asserted</data></edge><edge id="oe_09720066c3c4290c" source="e_dbd1ba0cc63988dc" target="e_abe5b5f78166cb31"><data key="edge_predicate_raw">requires</data><data key="edge_assertion_id">a_5b2ff9ce520b6120</data><data key="edge_source_id">S52</data><data key="edge_source_url">https://www.first.org/cvss/v3.1/specification-document</data><data key="edge_chunk_id">S52_C08</data><data key="edge_json_path">None</data><data key="edge_evidence">For example, consider a vulnerability that requires read-only permissions prior to being able to exploit the vulnerability</data><data key="edge_extraction_method">minie</data><data key="edge_polarity">positive</data><data key="edge_modality">asserted</data></edge><edge id="oe_53fadfb2f9235e85" source="e_8f5263a93ee3ad05" target="e_f2dca16215b933e8"><data key="edge_predicate_raw">write</data><data key="edge_assertion_id">a_94efb2a8db098f32</data><data key="edge_source_id">S52</data><data key="edge_source_url">https://www.first.org/cvss/v3.1/specification-document</data><data key="edge_chunk_id">S52_C08</data><data key="edge_json_path">None</data><data key="edge_evidence">After successful exploitation, the attacker maintains the same level of read access, and gains write access</data><data key="edge_extraction_method">minie</data><data key="edge_polarity">positive</data><data key="edge_modality">asserted</data></edge><edge id="oe_3ea19b32a7960841" source="e_29bb0e9d5a84c984" target="e_f2dca16215b933e8"><data key="edge_predicate_raw">write</data><data key="edge_assertion_id">a_62524b2fab530a8e</data><data key="edge_source_id">S52</data><data key="edge_source_url">https://www.first.org/cvss/v3.1/specification-document</data><data key="edge_chunk_id">S52_C08</data><data key="edge_json_path">None</data><data key="edge_evidence">After successful exploitation, the attacker maintains the same level of read access, and gains write access</data><data key="edge_extraction_method">minie</data><data key="edge_polarity">positive</data><data key="edge_modality">asserted</data></edge><edge id="oe_5ef1587e6e511409" source="e_537e6ab50e8f2e44" target="e_16ea76003b3fd67e"><data key="edge_predicate_raw">maintains gains write access After</data><data key="edge_assertion_id">a_0fdfb9b89ef38f7f</data><data key="edge_source_id">S52</data><data key="edge_source_url">https://www.first.org/cvss/v3.1/specification-document</data><data key="edge_chunk_id">S52_C08</data><data key="edge_json_path">None</data><data key="edge_evidence">After successful exploitation, the attacker maintains the same level of read access, and gains write access</data><data key="edge_extraction_method">minie</data><data key="edge_polarity">positive</data><data key="edge_modality">asserted</data></edge><edge id="oe_9869bddfb415a693" source="e_537e6ab50e8f2e44" target="e_d0456205cb01f7a0"><data key="edge_predicate_raw">maintains</data><data key="edge_assertion_id">a_a43f054c71ea1103</data><data key="edge_source_id">S52</data><data key="edge_source_url">https://www.first.org/cvss/v3.1/specification-document</data><data key="edge_chunk_id">S52_C08</data><data key="edge_json_path">None</data><data key="edge_evidence">After successful exploitation, the attacker maintains the same level of read access, and gains write access</data><data key="edge_extraction_method">minie</data><data key="edge_polarity">positive</data><data key="edge_modality">asserted</data></edge><edge id="oe_9fa18f8b835e2510" source="e_537e6ab50e8f2e44" target="e_5ad6c123e5abaf11"><data key="edge_predicate_raw">starts with partial access to restricted information For</data><data key="edge_assertion_id">a_8fbe14f0b622a7e2</data><data key="edge_source_id">S52</data><data key="edge_source_url">https://www.first.org/cvss/v3.1/specification-document</data><data key="edge_chunk_id">S52_C08</data><data key="edge_json_path">None</data><data key="edge_evidence">For example, if an attacker starts with partial access to restricted information (Confidentiality Low) and successful exploitation of the vulnerability results in complete loss in confidentiality (Confidentiality High), then the resultant CVSS Base Score should reference the “end game” Impact metric value (Confidentiality High)</data><data key="edge_extraction_method">minie</data><data key="edge_polarity">positive</data><data key="edge_modality">asserted</data></edge><edge id="oe_a4574ce5203cbf5b" source="e_537e6ab50e8f2e44" target="e_5ad6c123e5abaf11"><data key="edge_predicate_raw">starts with partial access to successful exploitation of vulnerability For</data><data key="edge_assertion_id">a_9b06ffef5cd425df</data><data key="edge_source_id">S52</data><data key="edge_source_url">https://www.first.org/cvss/v3.1/specification-document</data><data key="edge_chunk_id">S52_C08</data><data key="edge_json_path">None</data><data key="edge_evidence">For example, if an attacker starts with partial access to restricted information (Confidentiality Low) and successful exploitation of the vulnerability results in complete loss in confidentiality (Confidentiality High), then the resultant CVSS Base Score should reference the “end game” Impact metric value (Confidentiality High)</data><data key="edge_extraction_method">minie</data><data key="edge_polarity">positive</data><data key="edge_modality">asserted</data></edge><edge id="oe_7339da5d53485403" source="e_537e6ab50e8f2e44" target="e_7ec3a26547017318"><data key="edge_predicate_raw">starts with</data><data key="edge_assertion_id">a_d90a55e430e9a72b</data><data key="edge_source_id">S52</data><data key="edge_source_url">https://www.first.org/cvss/v3.1/specification-document</data><data key="edge_chunk_id">S52_C08</data><data key="edge_json_path">None</data><data key="edge_evidence">For example, if an attacker starts with partial access to restricted information (Confidentiality Low) and successful exploitation of the vulnerability results in complete loss in confidentiality (Confidentiality High), then the resultant CVSS Base Score should reference the “end game” Impact metric value (Confidentiality High)</data><data key="edge_extraction_method">minie</data><data key="edge_polarity">positive</data><data key="edge_modality">asserted</data></edge><edge id="oe_3d166ec13bb4714c" source="e_537e6ab50e8f2e44" target="e_0b036e5df064a6b7"><data key="edge_predicate_raw">starts with</data><data key="edge_assertion_id">a_77a06318522ec3d4</data><data key="edge_source_id">S52</data><data key="edge_source_url">https://www.first.org/cvss/v3.1/specification-document</data><data key="edge_chunk_id">S52_C08</data><data key="edge_json_path">None</data><data key="edge_evidence">For example, if an attacker starts with partial access to restricted information (Confidentiality Low) and successful exploitation of the vulnerability results in complete loss in confidentiality (Confidentiality High), then the resultant CVSS Base Score should reference the “end game” Impact metric value (Confidentiality High)</data><data key="edge_extraction_method">minie</data><data key="edge_polarity">positive</data><data key="edge_modality">asserted</data></edge><edge id="oe_93783ea92db9c0af" source="e_384266dea333f2df" target="e_d7268769fbad72a0"><data key="edge_predicate_raw">reference</data><data key="edge_assertion_id">a_ca77f0a73175a72c</data><data key="edge_source_id">S52</data><data key="edge_source_url">https://www.first.org/cvss/v3.1/specification-document</data><data key="edge_chunk_id">S52_C08</data><data key="edge_json_path">None</data><data key="edge_evidence">For example, if an attacker starts with partial access to restricted information (Confidentiality Low) and successful exploitation of the vulnerability results in complete loss in confidentiality (Confidentiality High), then the resultant CVSS Base Score should reference the “end game” Impact metric value (Confidentiality High)</data><data key="edge_extraction_method">minie</data><data key="edge_polarity">positive</data><data key="edge_modality">asserted</data></edge><edge id="oe_6335b76a4a6e6e73" source="e_841d5cae83210039" target="e_c1b8569aebaf6353"><data key="edge_predicate_raw">be managed by</data><data key="edge_assertion_id">a_c72cbe7abc6e571f</data><data key="edge_source_id">S52</data><data key="edge_source_url">https://www.first.org/cvss/v3.1/specification-document</data><data key="edge_chunk_id">S52_C08</data><data key="edge_json_path">None</data><data key="edge_evidence">This metric measures the impact to the confidentiality of the information resources managed by a software component due to a successfully exploited vulnerability</data><data key="edge_extraction_method">minie</data><data key="edge_polarity">positive</data><data key="edge_modality">asserted</data></edge><edge id="oe_ed826d27e8c820fb" source="e_dfd2e098a96fa540" target="e_6e5ec707cbc044ff"><data key="edge_predicate_raw">refers to limiting</data><data key="edge_assertion_id">a_93315b515300f614</data><data key="edge_source_id">S52</data><data key="edge_source_url">https://www.first.org/cvss/v3.1/specification-document</data><data key="edge_chunk_id">S52_C08</data><data key="edge_json_path">None</data><data key="edge_evidence">Confidentiality refers to limiting information access and disclosure to only authorized users, as well as preventing access by, or disclosure to, unauthorized ones</data><data key="edge_extraction_method">minie</data><data key="edge_polarity">positive</data><data key="edge_modality">asserted</data></edge><edge id="oe_7468d416068e7e92" source="e_dfd2e098a96fa540" target="e_8b2074bad160dde7"><data key="edge_predicate_raw">refers to limiting</data><data key="edge_assertion_id">a_bb19bbf259411cfb</data><data key="edge_source_id">S52</data><data key="edge_source_url">https://www.first.org/cvss/v3.1/specification-document</data><data key="edge_chunk_id">S52_C08</data><data key="edge_json_path">None</data><data key="edge_evidence">Confidentiality refers to limiting information access and disclosure to only authorized users, as well as preventing access by, or disclosure to, unauthorized ones</data><data key="edge_extraction_method">minie</data><data key="edge_polarity">positive</data><data key="edge_modality">asserted</data></edge><edge id="oe_5687ab6f51f04717" source="e_dfd2e098a96fa540" target="e_a15d5fd58349b1ad"><data key="edge_predicate_raw">refers to preventing</data><data key="edge_assertion_id">a_d9aae54190aa7438</data><data key="edge_source_id">S52</data><data key="edge_source_url">https://www.first.org/cvss/v3.1/specification-document</data><data key="edge_chunk_id">S52_C08</data><data key="edge_json_path">None</data><data key="edge_evidence">Confidentiality refers to limiting information access and disclosure to only authorized users, as well as preventing access by, or disclosure to, unauthorized ones</data><data key="edge_extraction_method">minie</data><data key="edge_polarity">positive</data><data key="edge_modality">asserted</data></edge><edge id="oe_ab7227b45a1fd318" source="e_fabb36a448bb30b7" target="e_eb1797b298a230c0"><data key="edge_predicate_raw">disclosed</data><data key="edge_assertion_id">a_79aac04c11b93fab</data><data key="edge_source_id">S52</data><data key="edge_source_url">https://www.first.org/cvss/v3.1/specification-document</data><data key="edge_chunk_id">S52_C08</data><data key="edge_json_path">None</data><data key="edge_evidence">Alternatively, access to only some restricted information is obtained, but the disclosed information presents a direct, serious impact</data><data key="edge_extraction_method">heuristic</data><data key="edge_polarity">positive</data><data key="edge_modality">asserted</data></edge><edge id="oe_2931889583a62a1a" source="e_53dd9263602ab61d" target="e_2079f7f0585a6a0c"><data key="edge_predicate_raw">refers to trustworthiness of</data><data key="edge_assertion_id">a_3cedd4031d4a6e90</data><data key="edge_source_id">S52</data><data key="edge_source_url">https://www.first.org/cvss/v3.1/specification-document</data><data key="edge_chunk_id">S52_C09</data><data key="edge_json_path">None</data><data key="edge_evidence">Integrity refers to the trustworthiness and veracity of information</data><data key="edge_extraction_method">minie</data><data key="edge_polarity">positive</data><data key="edge_modality">asserted</data></edge><edge id="oe_ad6a40c611a6d1d0" source="e_53dd9263602ab61d" target="e_edea54677a8d7d64"><data key="edge_predicate_raw">refers to</data><data key="edge_assertion_id">a_407c2962ef166580</data><data key="edge_source_id">S52</data><data key="edge_source_url">https://www.first.org/cvss/v3.1/specification-document</data><data key="edge_chunk_id">S52_C09</data><data key="edge_json_path">None</data><data key="edge_evidence">Integrity refers to the trustworthiness and veracity of information</data><data key="edge_extraction_method">minie</data><data key="edge_polarity">positive</data><data key="edge_modality">asserted</data></edge><edge id="oe_aca502fb70d29c1c" source="e_d2b630e61129d09b" target="e_26e0466f06957bd3"><data key="edge_predicate_raw">be protected by</data><data key="edge_assertion_id">a_9772b6971dcd5120</data><data key="edge_source_id">S52</data><data key="edge_source_url">https://www.first.org/cvss/v3.1/specification-document</data><data key="edge_chunk_id">S52_C09</data><data key="edge_json_path">None</data><data key="edge_evidence">For example, the attacker is able to modify any/all files protected by the impacted component</data><data key="edge_extraction_method">minie</data><data key="edge_polarity">positive</data><data key="edge_modality">asserted</data></edge><edge id="oe_98304a48fcca86d2" source="e_332fd4a216e1c401" target="e_2228b2b192c550b5"><data key="edge_predicate_raw">be resulting from</data><data key="edge_assertion_id">a_88f7212581ae2850</data><data key="edge_source_id">S52</data><data key="edge_source_url">https://www.first.org/cvss/v3.1/specification-document</data><data key="edge_chunk_id">S52_C09</data><data key="edge_json_path">None</data><data key="edge_evidence">This metric measures the impact to the availability of the impacted component resulting from a successfully exploited vulnerability</data><data key="edge_extraction_method">minie</data><data key="edge_polarity">positive</data><data key="edge_modality">asserted</data></edge><edge id="oe_ea71b32d3baad82a" source="e_dfd2e098a96fa540" target="e_751883363f9bc7cb"><data key="edge_predicate_raw">apply to</data><data key="edge_assertion_id">a_bc027f4648ccff80</data><data key="edge_source_id">S52</data><data key="edge_source_url">https://www.first.org/cvss/v3.1/specification-document</data><data key="edge_chunk_id">S52_C09</data><data key="edge_json_path">None</data><data key="edge_evidence">While the Confidentiality and Integrity impact metrics apply to the loss of confidentiality or integrity of data (e.g., information, files) used by the impacted component, this metric refers to the loss of availability of the impacted component itself, such as a networked service (e.g., web, database, email)</data><data key="edge_extraction_method">minie</data><data key="edge_polarity">positive</data><data key="edge_modality">asserted</data></edge><edge id="oe_4282e825329ae288" source="e_dfd2e098a96fa540" target="e_53dd9263602ab61d"><data key="edge_predicate_raw">apply to loss of</data><data key="edge_assertion_id">a_901592c1525b2cab</data><data key="edge_source_id">S52</data><data key="edge_source_url">https://www.first.org/cvss/v3.1/specification-document</data><data key="edge_chunk_id">S52_C09</data><data key="edge_json_path">None</data><data key="edge_evidence">While the Confidentiality and Integrity impact metrics apply to the loss of confidentiality or integrity of data (e.g., information, files) used by the impacted component, this metric refers to the loss of availability of the impacted component itself, such as a networked service (e.g., web, database, email)</data><data key="edge_extraction_method">minie</data><data key="edge_polarity">positive</data><data key="edge_modality">asserted</data></edge><edge id="oe_a9d68ee751fca4d7" source="e_09f091e141fb1fa3" target="e_751883363f9bc7cb"><data key="edge_predicate_raw">apply to</data><data key="edge_assertion_id">a_d25055a75b644c8d</data><data key="edge_source_id">S52</data><data key="edge_source_url">https://www.first.org/cvss/v3.1/specification-document</data><data key="edge_chunk_id">S52_C09</data><data key="edge_json_path">None</data><data key="edge_evidence">While the Confidentiality and Integrity impact metrics apply to the loss of confidentiality or integrity of data (e.g., information, files) used by the impacted component, this metric refers to the loss of availability of the impacted component itself, such as a networked service (e.g., web, database, email)</data><data key="edge_extraction_method">minie</data><data key="edge_polarity">positive</data><data key="edge_modality">asserted</data></edge><edge id="oe_20223e0dd66ab10c" source="e_09f091e141fb1fa3" target="e_53dd9263602ab61d"><data key="edge_predicate_raw">apply to loss of</data><data key="edge_assertion_id">a_e396381cdec0b836</data><data key="edge_source_id">S52</data><data key="edge_source_url">https://www.first.org/cvss/v3.1/specification-document</data><data key="edge_chunk_id">S52_C09</data><data key="edge_json_path">None</data><data key="edge_evidence">While the Confidentiality and Integrity impact metrics apply to the loss of confidentiality or integrity of data (e.g., information, files) used by the impacted component, this metric refers to the loss of availability of the impacted component itself, such as a networked service (e.g., web, database, email)</data><data key="edge_extraction_method">minie</data><data key="edge_polarity">positive</data><data key="edge_modality">asserted</data></edge><edge id="oe_9eaf89d060a95ca3" source="e_61641163de7ce9bc" target="e_26e0466f06957bd3"><data key="edge_predicate_raw">be used by</data><data key="edge_assertion_id">a_73beaaa030087dfc</data><data key="edge_source_id">S52</data><data key="edge_source_url">https://www.first.org/cvss/v3.1/specification-document</data><data key="edge_chunk_id">S52_C09</data><data key="edge_json_path">None</data><data key="edge_evidence">While the Confidentiality and Integrity impact metrics apply to the loss of confidentiality or integrity of data (e.g., information, files) used by the impacted component, this metric refers to the loss of availability of the impacted component itself, such as a networked service (e.g., web, database, email)</data><data key="edge_extraction_method">minie</data><data key="edge_polarity">positive</data><data key="edge_modality">asserted</data></edge><edge id="oe_f72618e678124e58" source="e_4676679afd99eed0" target="e_398e95f2f11b74fa"><data key="edge_predicate_raw">refers to loss of availability of impacted component itself such as networked service While</data><data key="edge_assertion_id">a_408005151babf63e</data><data key="edge_source_id">S52</data><data key="edge_source_url">https://www.first.org/cvss/v3.1/specification-document</data><data key="edge_chunk_id">S52_C09</data><data key="edge_json_path">None</data><data key="edge_evidence">While the Confidentiality and Integrity impact metrics apply to the loss of confidentiality or integrity of data (e.g., information, files) used by the impacted component, this metric refers to the loss of availability of the impacted component itself, such as a networked service (e.g., web, database, email)</data><data key="edge_extraction_method">minie</data><data key="edge_polarity">positive</data><data key="edge_modality">asserted</data></edge><edge id="oe_22f4080351485e0f" source="e_4676679afd99eed0" target="e_b6ca085d15d6ffbc"><data key="edge_predicate_raw">refers to</data><data key="edge_assertion_id">a_5e61940a04b1fa44</data><data key="edge_source_id">S52</data><data key="edge_source_url">https://www.first.org/cvss/v3.1/specification-document</data><data key="edge_chunk_id">S52_C09</data><data key="edge_json_path">None</data><data key="edge_evidence">While the Confidentiality and Integrity impact metrics apply to the loss of confidentiality or integrity of data (e.g., information, files) used by the impacted component, this metric refers to the loss of availability of the impacted component itself, such as a networked service (e.g., web, database, email)</data><data key="edge_extraction_method">minie<