><edge id="oe_1194a86a2f271be9" source="e_768bf52735c34131" target="e_06f17e13a1b43871"><data key="edge_predicate_raw">modify Environmental Score prior to applying</data><data key="edge_assertion_id">a_43a559b97ebd4c48</data><data key="edge_source_id">S52</data><data key="edge_source_url">https://www.first.org/cvss/v3.1/specification-document</data><data key="edge_chunk_id">S52_C14</data><data key="edge_json_path">None</data><data key="edge_evidence">That is, these metrics modify the Environmental Score by overriding Base metric values, prior to applying the Environmental Security Requirements</data><data key="edge_extraction_method">minie</data><data key="edge_polarity">positive</data><data key="edge_modality">asserted</data></edge><edge id="oe_59e391b44c0c22af" source="e_768bf52735c34131" target="e_26f020227348bd77"><data key="edge_predicate_raw">modify</data><data key="edge_assertion_id">a_149808e24c3392e3</data><data key="edge_source_id">S52</data><data key="edge_source_url">https://www.first.org/cvss/v3.1/specification-document</data><data key="edge_chunk_id">S52_C14</data><data key="edge_json_path">None</data><data key="edge_evidence">That is, these metrics modify the Environmental Score by overriding Base metric values, prior to applying the Environmental Security Requirements</data><data key="edge_extraction_method">minie</data><data key="edge_polarity">positive</data><data key="edge_modality">asserted</data></edge><edge id="oe_15952e57e32655db" source="e_1db208fac24377d1" target="e_5ad6c123e5abaf11"><data key="edge_predicate_raw">be to run listening service with administrator privileges For</data><data key="edge_assertion_id">a_76c1504328e9fe8e</data><data key="edge_source_id">S52</data><data key="edge_source_url">https://www.first.org/cvss/v3.1/specification-document</data><data key="edge_chunk_id">S52_C14</data><data key="edge_json_path">None</data><data key="edge_evidence">For example, the default configuration for a vulnerable component may be to run a listening service with administrator privileges, for which a compromise might grant an attacker Confidentiality, Integrity, and Availability impacts that are all High</data><data key="edge_extraction_method">minie</data><data key="edge_polarity">positive</data><data key="edge_modality">possible</data></edge><edge id="oe_721a701d1c972bab" source="e_1db208fac24377d1" target="e_5ad6c123e5abaf11"><data key="edge_predicate_raw">be to run Availability impacts For</data><data key="edge_assertion_id">a_b528205c59e57588</data><data key="edge_source_id">S52</data><data key="edge_source_url">https://www.first.org/cvss/v3.1/specification-document</data><data key="edge_chunk_id">S52_C14</data><data key="edge_json_path">None</data><data key="edge_evidence">For example, the default configuration for a vulnerable component may be to run a listening service with administrator privileges, for which a compromise might grant an attacker Confidentiality, Integrity, and Availability impacts that are all High</data><data key="edge_extraction_method">minie</data><data key="edge_polarity">positive</data><data key="edge_modality">possible</data></edge><edge id="oe_ecb7bc31793dec20" source="e_1db208fac24377d1" target="e_24724c67123f239d"><data key="edge_predicate_raw">be to run listening service with</data><data key="edge_assertion_id">a_d156e235e75e7182</data><data key="edge_source_id">S52</data><data key="edge_source_url">https://www.first.org/cvss/v3.1/specification-document</data><data key="edge_chunk_id">S52_C14</data><data key="edge_json_path">None</data><data key="edge_evidence">For example, the default configuration for a vulnerable component may be to run a listening service with administrator privileges, for which a compromise might grant an attacker Confidentiality, Integrity, and Availability impacts that are all High</data><data key="edge_extraction_method">minie</data><data key="edge_polarity">positive</data><data key="edge_modality">possible</data></edge><edge id="oe_6ac2b08d202d66f2" source="e_1db208fac24377d1" target="e_349144947774f114"><data key="edge_predicate_raw">be to run</data><data key="edge_assertion_id">a_1a04c71b9d05df4c</data><data key="edge_source_id">S52</data><data key="edge_source_url">https://www.first.org/cvss/v3.1/specification-document</data><data key="edge_chunk_id">S52_C14</data><data key="edge_json_path">None</data><data key="edge_evidence">For example, the default configuration for a vulnerable component may be to run a listening service with administrator privileges, for which a compromise might grant an attacker Confidentiality, Integrity, and Availability impacts that are all High</data><data key="edge_extraction_method">minie</data><data key="edge_polarity">positive</data><data key="edge_modality">possible</data></edge><edge id="oe_9726f966bc9074a1" source="e_2777340d458412d6" target="e_24724c67123f239d"><data key="edge_predicate_raw">grant attacker Confidentiality listening service with</data><data key="edge_assertion_id">a_fa47af53cd123d02</data><data key="edge_source_id">S52</data><data key="edge_source_url">https://www.first.org/cvss/v3.1/specification-document</data><data key="edge_chunk_id">S52_C14</data><data key="edge_json_path">None</data><data key="edge_evidence">For example, the default configuration for a vulnerable component may be to run a listening service with administrator privileges, for which a compromise might grant an attacker Confidentiality, Integrity, and Availability impacts that are all High</data><data key="edge_extraction_method">minie</data><data key="edge_polarity">positive</data><data key="edge_modality">possible</data></edge><edge id="oe_490ccb824d97cb09" source="e_2777340d458412d6" target="e_349144947774f114"><data key="edge_predicate_raw">grant attacker Confidentiality</data><data key="edge_assertion_id">a_8bf3bbb81e9b8492</data><data key="edge_source_id">S52</data><data key="edge_source_url">https://www.first.org/cvss/v3.1/specification-document</data><data key="edge_chunk_id">S52_C14</data><data key="edge_json_path">None</data><data key="edge_evidence">For example, the default configuration for a vulnerable component may be to run a listening service with administrator privileges, for which a compromise might grant an attacker Confidentiality, Integrity, and Availability impacts that are all High</data><data key="edge_extraction_method">minie</data><data key="edge_polarity">positive</data><data key="edge_modality">possible</data></edge><edge id="oe_2dcde2baba1a011a" source="e_2cbef1015e8443fb" target="e_040dc8c7ec38f443"><data key="edge_predicate_raw">be running with</data><data key="edge_assertion_id">a_60cb981953e82a43</data><data key="edge_source_id">S52</data><data key="edge_source_url">https://www.first.org/cvss/v3.1/specification-document</data><data key="edge_chunk_id">S52_C14</data><data key="edge_json_path">None</data><data key="edge_evidence">Yet, in the analyst’s environment, that same Internet service might be running with reduced privileges; in that case, the Modified Confidentiality, Modified Integrity, and Modified Availability might each be set to Low</data><data key="edge_extraction_method">minie</data><data key="edge_polarity">positive</data><data key="edge_modality">possible</data></edge><edge id="oe_312b4404b9a6c24b" source="e_2cbef1015e8443fb" target="e_1340cdfb57d36975"><data key="edge_predicate_raw">be running with reduced privileges in</data><data key="edge_assertion_id">a_0811d8099c9887d9</data><data key="edge_source_id">S52</data><data key="edge_source_url">https://www.first.org/cvss/v3.1/specification-document</data><data key="edge_chunk_id">S52_C14</data><data key="edge_json_path">None</data><data key="edge_evidence">Yet, in the analyst’s environment, that same Internet service might be running with reduced privileges; in that case, the Modified Confidentiality, Modified Integrity, and Modified Availability might each be set to Low</data><data key="edge_extraction_method">minie</data><data key="edge_polarity">positive</data><data key="edge_modality">possible</data></edge><edge id="oe_44dc562b1e5e6579" source="e_3194ef0752b4dc4c" target="e_afccd7a4fc5871a9"><data key="edge_predicate_raw">has corresponding Base value of</data><data key="edge_assertion_id">a_0154fc92f3c56508</data><data key="edge_source_id">S52</data><data key="edge_source_url">https://www.first.org/cvss/v3.1/specification-document</data><data key="edge_chunk_id">S52_C14</data><data key="edge_json_path">None</data><data key="edge_evidence">Each Modified Environmental metric has the same values as its corresponding Base metric, plus a value of Not Defined</data><data key="edge_extraction_method">minie</data><data key="edge_polarity">negative</data><data key="edge_modality">asserted</data></edge><edge id="oe_55009680f46949a6" source="e_a00feff6fcb1c982" target="e_b35718531dfb7863"><data key="edge_predicate_raw">uses</data><data key="edge_assertion_id">a_6ae23983d59ffabc</data><data key="edge_source_id">S52</data><data key="edge_source_url">https://www.first.org/cvss/v3.1/specification-document</data><data key="edge_chunk_id">S52_C14</data><data key="edge_json_path">None</data><data key="edge_evidence">Not Defined is the default and uses the metric value of the associated Base metric</data><data key="edge_extraction_method">heuristic</data><data key="edge_polarity">negative</data><data key="edge_modality">asserted</data></edge><edge id="oe_dc02df451bcf3846" source="e_043dd4607501db93" target="e_645548a290e9b0fc"><data key="edge_predicate_raw">is to define</data><data key="edge_assertion_id">a_4e7cc29364dd354e</data><data key="edge_source_id">S52</data><data key="edge_source_url">https://www.first.org/cvss/v3.1/specification-document</data><data key="edge_chunk_id">S52_C14</data><data key="edge_json_path">None</data><data key="edge_evidence">The intent of this metric is to define the mitigations in place for a given environment</data><data key="edge_extraction_method">minie</data><data key="edge_polarity">positive</data><data key="edge_modality">asserted</data></edge><edge id="oe_a7efac483e0c2fc0" source="e_043dd4607501db93" target="e_85401cc54ec45a4f"><data key="edge_predicate_raw">is to define mitigations in</data><data key="edge_assertion_id">a_92baae517f430c6a</data><data key="edge_source_id">S52</data><data key="edge_source_url">https://www.first.org/cvss/v3.1/specification-document</data><data key="edge_chunk_id">S52_C14</data><data key="edge_json_path">None</data><data key="edge_evidence">The intent of this metric is to define the mitigations in place for a given environment</data><data key="edge_extraction_method">minie</data><data key="edge_polarity">positive</data><data key="edge_modality">asserted</data></edge><edge id="oe_3bc239686cef58e9" source="e_596a3f18c38132af" target="e_db5858cf6e7acd99"><data key="edge_predicate_raw">be represent</data><data key="edge_assertion_id">a_6eb798da84301668</data><data key="edge_source_id">S52</data><data key="edge_source_url">https://www.first.org/cvss/v3.1/specification-document</data><data key="edge_chunk_id">S52_C14</data><data key="edge_json_path">None</data><data key="edge_evidence">It is acceptable to use the modified metrics to represent situations that increase the Base Score</data><data key="edge_extraction_method">minie</data><data key="edge_polarity">positive</data><data key="edge_modality">asserted</data></edge><edge id="oe_58e5662eaa4cfbb9" source="e_db5858cf6e7acd99" target="e_5dd63c0e6e0c1501"><data key="edge_predicate_raw">increase</data><data key="edge_assertion_id">a_ac389cadc3dab111</data><data key="edge_source_id">S52</data><data key="edge_source_url">https://www.first.org/cvss/v3.1/specification-document</data><data key="edge_chunk_id">S52_C14</data><data key="edge_json_path">None</data><data key="edge_evidence">It is acceptable to use the modified metrics to represent situations that increase the Base Score</data><data key="edge_extraction_method">minie</data><data key="edge_polarity">positive</data><data key="edge_modality">asserted</data></edge><edge id="oe_6b79b834d5d72463" source="e_f6498126c94c6f96" target="e_506193cfefade053"><data key="edge_predicate_raw">set</data><data key="edge_assertion_id">a_829aee24b237c44e</data><data key="edge_source_id">S52</data><data key="edge_source_url">https://www.first.org/cvss/v3.1/specification-document</data><data key="edge_chunk_id">S52_C14</data><data key="edge_json_path">None</data><data key="edge_evidence">The analyst can set Privileges Required to High and Modified Privileges Required to None to reflect this more serious condition in their particular environment</data><data key="edge_extraction_method">minie</data><data key="edge_polarity">positive</data><data key="edge_modality">possible</data></edge><edge id="oe_13aac2fe6f04474b" source="e_f6498126c94c6f96" target="e_8baba9b928c90883"><data key="edge_predicate_raw">set</data><data key="edge_assertion_id">a_e7e52912b5b3cbf4</data><data key="edge_source_id">S52</data><data key="edge_source_url">https://www.first.org/cvss/v3.1/specification-document</data><data key="edge_chunk_id">S52_C14</data><data key="edge_json_path">None</data><data key="edge_evidence">The analyst can set Privileges Required to High and Modified Privileges Required to None to reflect this more serious condition in their particular environment</data><data key="edge_extraction_method">minie</data><data key="edge_polarity">positive</data><data key="edge_modality">possible</data></edge><edge id="oe_d0497a821d6e4866" source="e_1b50c049dec6c218" target="e_b084bc0ae581622f"><data key="edge_predicate_raw">be Required to High Privileges Required to None to reflect more serious condition in</data><data key="edge_assertion_id">a_53ed212de1099c3a</data><data key="edge_source_id">S52</data><data key="edge_source_url">https://www.first.org/cvss/v3.1/specification-document</data><data key="edge_chunk_id">S52_C14</data><data key="edge_json_path">None</data><data key="edge_evidence">The analyst can set Privileges Required to High and Modified Privileges Required to None to reflect this more serious condition in their particular environment</data><data key="edge_extraction_method">minie</data><data key="edge_polarity">positive</data><data key="edge_modality">possible</data></edge><edge id="oe_e53be3bf0daa4f8a" source="e_1b50c049dec6c218" target="e_b084bc0ae581622f"><data key="edge_predicate_raw">be Required to Modified Privileges Required to None to reflect more serious condition in</data><data key="edge_assertion_id">a_f6cae13bef76cad7</data><data key="edge_source_id">S52</data><data key="edge_source_url">https://www.first.org/cvss/v3.1/specification-document</data><data key="edge_chunk_id">S52_C14</data><data key="edge_json_path">None</data><data key="edge_evidence">The analyst can set Privileges Required to High and Modified Privileges Required to None to reflect this more serious condition in their particular environment</data><data key="edge_extraction_method">minie</data><data key="edge_polarity">positive</data><data key="edge_modality">possible</data></edge><edge id="oe_585eb2d6e17f349d" source="e_6cb481a83536ac29" target="e_f90f01579634abed"><data key="edge_predicate_raw">be Required to</data><data key="edge_assertion_id">a_3e8bb0e2c711cbd4</data><data key="edge_source_id">S52</data><data key="edge_source_url">https://www.first.org/cvss/v3.1/specification-document</data><data key="edge_chunk_id">S52_C14</data><data key="edge_json_path">None</data><data key="edge_evidence">The analyst can set Privileges Required to High and Modified Privileges Required to None to reflect this more serious condition in their particular environment</data><data key="edge_extraction_method">minie</data><data key="edge_polarity">positive</data><data key="edge_modality">possible</data></edge><edge id="oe_ad6005eea11221e3" source="e_cbda6adb410f4617" target="e_f90f01579634abed"><data key="edge_predicate_raw">be Required to</data><data key="edge_assertion_id">a_7139abc6f2a50aa6</data><data key="edge_source_id">S52</data><data key="edge_source_url">https://www.first.org/cvss/v3.1/specification-document</data><data key="edge_chunk_id">S52_C14</data><data key="edge_json_path">None</data><data key="edge_evidence">The analyst can set Privileges Required to High and Modified Privileges Required to None to reflect this more serious condition in their particular environment</data><data key="edge_extraction_method">minie</data><data key="edge_polarity">positive</data><data key="edge_modality">possible</data></edge><edge id="oe_9db51f891a69fb28" source="e_5ddf9ee4443e80dd" target="e_ace64742206fb24b"><data key="edge_predicate_raw">publishing</data><data key="edge_assertion_id">a_81bdbda1d3f61ddf</data><data key="edge_source_id">S52</data><data key="edge_source_url">https://www.first.org/cvss/v3.1/specification-document</data><data key="edge_chunk_id">S52_C14</data><data key="edge_json_path">None</data><data key="edge_evidence">The use of these qualitative severity ratings is optional, and there is no requirement to include them when publishing CVSS scores</data><data key="edge_extraction_method">heuristic</data><data key="edge_polarity">negative</data><data key="edge_modality">asserted</data></edge><edge id="oe_ab22de6ccf337208" source="e_290d8da624d84fb0" target="e_2e1496c46b0c67cc"><data key="edge_predicate_raw">help</data><data key="edge_assertion_id">a_0d7fbe5fd952e43d</data><data key="edge_source_id">S52</data><data key="edge_source_url">https://www.first.org/cvss/v3.1/specification-document</data><data key="edge_chunk_id">S52_C14</data><data key="edge_json_path">None</data><data key="edge_evidence">They are intended to help organizations properly assess and prioritize their vulnerability management processes</data><data key="edge_extraction_method">minie</data><data key="edge_polarity">positive</data><data key="edge_modality">asserted</data></edge><edge id="oe_a2115e0b5714fc10" source="e_290d8da624d84fb0" target="e_40e21c1bf87487d6"><data key="edge_predicate_raw">help</data><data key="edge_assertion_id">a_93a87595afe53471</data><data key="edge_source_id">S52</data><data key="edge_source_url">https://www.first.org/cvss/v3.1/specification-document</data><data key="edge_chunk_id">S52_C14</data><data key="edge_json_path">None</data><data key="edge_evidence">They are intended to help organizations properly assess and prioritize their vulnerability management processes</data><data key="edge_extraction_method">minie</data><data key="edge_polarity">positive</data><data key="edge_modality">asserted</data></edge><edge id="oe_231191de57e38bb5" source="e_5ddf9ee4443e80dd" target="e_ace64742206fb24b"><data key="edge_predicate_raw">publishing</data><data key="edge_assertion_id">a_6be415539d54f1e3</data><data key="edge_source_id">S52</data><data key="edge_source_url">https://www.first.org/cvss/v3.1/specification-document</data><data key="edge_chunk_id">S52_C15</data><data key="edge_json_path">None</data><data key="edge_evidence">is optional, and there is no requirement to include them when publishing CVSS scores</data><data key="edge_extraction_method">heuristic</data><data key="edge_polarity">negative</data><data key="edge_modality">asserted</data></edge><edge id="oe_609628adca22ca25" source="e_ad16450d4d7b98f8" target="e_3871d9a29382ae85"><data key="edge_predicate_raw">is used to record CVSS metric information in</data><data key="edge_assertion_id">a_11b099da271ec53d</data><data key="edge_source_id">S52</data><data key="edge_source_url">https://www.first.org/cvss/v3.1/specification-document</data><data key="edge_chunk_id">S52_C15</data><data key="edge_json_path">None</data><data key="edge_evidence">It is commonly used to record or transfer CVSS metric information in a concise form</data><data key="edge_extraction_method">minie</data><data key="edge_polarity">positive</data><data key="edge_modality">asserted</data></edge><edge id="oe_978f0c75e5181a3a" source="e_ad16450d4d7b98f8" target="e_11d9e0f2a7ae327b"><data key="edge_predicate_raw">is used to record</data><data key="edge_assertion_id">a_42b39f523c0db2e5</data><data key="edge_source_id">S52</data><data key="edge_source_url">https://www.first.org/cvss/v3.1/specification-document</data><data key="edge_chunk_id">S52_C15</data><data key="edge_json_path">None</data><data key="edge_evidence">It is commonly used to record or transfer CVSS metric information in a concise form</data><data key="edge_extraction_method">minie</data><data key="edge_polarity">positive</data><data key="edge_modality">asserted</data></edge><edge id="oe_c20803855cc823f9" source="e_ad16450d4d7b98f8" target="e_69d96ed34aa1dab2"><data key="edge_predicate_raw">is used</data><data key="edge_assertion_id">a_c98abe79f9d3ad7a</data><data key="edge_source_id">S52</data><data key="edge_source_url">https://www.first.org/cvss/v3.1/specification-document</data><data key="edge_chunk_id">S52_C15</data><data key="edge_json_path">None</data><data key="edge_evidence">It is commonly used to record or transfer CVSS metric information in a concise form</data><data key="edge_extraction_method">minie</data><data key="edge_polarity">positive</data><data key="edge_modality">asserted</data></edge><edge id="oe_6c7f26b527e28020" source="e_ceef12725e7b8b39" target="e_6ab7b09e08984b56"><data key="edge_predicate_raw">follows in</data><data key="edge_assertion_id">a_fa8fbe11bf936d3f</data><data key="edge_source_id">S52</data><data key="edge_source_url">https://www.first.org/cvss/v3.1/specification-document</data><data key="edge_chunk_id">S52_C15</data><data key="edge_json_path">None</data><data key="edge_evidence">Metric information follows in the form of a set of metrics, each preceded by a forward slash, “/”, acting as a delimiter</data><data key="edge_extraction_method">minie</data><data key="edge_polarity">positive</data><data key="edge_modality">asserted</data></edge><edge id="oe_bc49bf2e06bc7a35" source="e_3194ef0752b4dc4c" target="e_84e82b5a59c3f406"><data key="edge_predicate_raw">has associated metric value in</data><data key="edge_assertion_id">a_b0d5b30a8d530863</data><data key="edge_source_id">S52</data><data key="edge_source_url">https://www.first.org/cvss/v3.1/specification-document</data><data key="edge_chunk_id">S52_C15</data><data key="edge_json_path">None</data><data key="edge_evidence">Each metric is a metric name in abbreviated form, a colon, “:”, and its associated metric value in abbreviated form</data><data key="edge_extraction_method">minie</data><data key="edge_polarity">positive</data><data key="edge_modality">asserted</data></edge><edge id="oe_7aaec7b96ea376d6" source="e_9e8758f7636f5ca5" target="e_1132648fd32b5522"><data key="edge_predicate_raw">are defined earlier in</data><data key="edge_assertion_id">a_a065f6c9d5feb14a</data><data key="edge_source_id">S52</data><data key="edge_source_url">https://www.first.org/cvss/v3.1/specification-document</data><data key="edge_chunk_id">S52_C15</data><data key="edge_json_path">None</data><data key="edge_evidence">The abbreviated forms are defined earlier in this specification (in parentheses after each metric name and metric value), and are summarized in the table below</data><data key="edge_extraction_method">minie</data><data key="edge_polarity">positive</data><data key="edge_modality">asserted</data></edge><edge id="oe_29316c152cc1d9a2" source="e_9e8758f7636f5ca5" target="e_534c943c598a31b3"><data key="edge_predicate_raw">are defined</data><data key="edge_assertion_id">a_93e86c4ed7c1580f</data><data key="edge_source_id">S52</data><data key="edge_source_url">https://www.first.org/cvss/v3.1/specification-document</data><data key="edge_chunk_id">S52_C15</data><data key="edge_json_path">None</data><data key="edge_evidence">The abbreviated forms are defined earlier in this specification (in parentheses after each metric name and metric value), and are summarized in the table below</data><data key="edge_extraction_method">minie</data><data key="edge_polarity">positive</data><data key="edge_modality">asserted</data></edge><edge id="oe_07d1a2ab92c5b745" source="e_075097bc32ffa89f" target="e_afccd7a4fc5871a9"><data key="edge_predicate_raw">are considered to have value of</data><data key="edge_assertion_id">a_40284b9a296f3e5d</data><data key="edge_source_id">S52</data><data key="edge_source_url">https://www.first.org/cvss/v3.1/specification-document</data><data key="edge_chunk_id">S52_C15</data><data key="edge_json_path">None</data><data key="edge_evidence">Temporal and Environmental metrics are optional, and omitted metrics are considered to have the value of Not Defined (X)</data><data key="edge_extraction_method">minie</data><data key="edge_polarity">negative</data><data key="edge_modality">asserted</data></edge><edge id="oe_12adaced19bcc73f" source="e_8c5bdfed19c88e1e" target="e_97d5b9fcbb9ac78b"><data key="edge_predicate_raw">be included in</data><data key="edge_assertion_id">a_0ae1a21939be916a</data><data key="edge_source_id">S52</data><data key="edge_source_url">https://www.first.org/cvss/v3.1/specification-document</data><data key="edge_chunk_id">S52_C15</data><data key="edge_json_path">None</data><data key="edge_evidence">Metrics with a value of Not Defined can be explicitly included in a vector string if desired</data><data key="edge_extraction_method">minie</data><data key="edge_polarity">negative</data><data key="edge_modality">possible</data></edge><edge id="oe_6d0c4f5225221817" source="e_8c5bdfed19c88e1e" target="e_5480893a3a1bed54"><data key="edge_predicate_raw">be included in vector string if</data><data key="edge_assertion_id">a_4d009db2ad6f6ff8</data><data key="edge_source_id">S52</data><data key="edge_source_url">https://www.first.org/cvss/v3.1/specification-document</data><data key="edge_chunk_id">S52_C15</data><data key="edge_json_path">None</data><data key="edge_evidence">Metrics with a value of Not Defined can be explicitly included in a vector string if desired</data><data key="edge_extraction_method">minie</data><data key="edge_polarity">negative</data><data key="edge_modality">possible</data></edge><edge id="oe_641f84ba82c05194" source="e_97d5b9fcbb9ac78b" target="e_942533ab55bfaf74"><data key="edge_predicate_raw">include same metric more than</data><data key="edge_assertion_id">a_e19a9bdc90dc3935</data><data key="edge_source_id">S52</data><data key="edge_source_url">https://www.first.org/cvss/v3.1/specification-document</data><data key="edge_chunk_id">S52_C15</data><data key="edge_json_path">None</data><data key="edge_evidence">A vector string must not include the same metric more than once</data><data key="edge_extraction_method">minie</data><data key="edge_polarity">negative</data><data key="edge_modality">asserted</data></edge><edge id="oe_f59ab34fefea52c3" source="e_f90f01579634abed" target="e_c4864c06dd486dbc"><data key="edge_predicate_raw">produce</data><data key="edge_assertion_id">a_0cc350230ea8ec70</data><data key="edge_source_id">S52</data><data key="edge_source_url">https://www.first.org/cvss/v3.1/specification-document</data><data key="edge_chunk_id">S52_C16</data><data key="edge_json_path">None</data><data key="edge_evidence">For example, a vulnerability with Base metric values of “Attack Vector: Network, Attack Complexity: Low, Privileges Required: High, User Interaction: None, Scope: Unchanged, Confidentiality: Low, Integrity: Low, Availability: None” and no specified Temporal or Environmental metrics would produce the following vector:</data><data key="edge_extraction_method">minie</data><data key="edge_polarity">negative</data><data key="edge_modality">asserted</data></edge><edge id="oe_58ddfecc3b4ef1f8" source="e_afccd7a4fc5871a9" target="e_c4864c06dd486dbc"><data key="edge_predicate_raw">produce</data><data key="edge_assertion_id">a_00a101e060e72924</data><data key="edge_source_id">S52</data><data key="edge_source_url">https://www.first.org/cvss/v3.1/specification-document</data><data key="edge_chunk_id">S52_C16</data><data key="edge_json_path">None</data><data key="edge_evidence">The same example with the addition of “Exploitability: Functional, Remediation Level: Not Defined” and with the metrics in a non-preferred ordering would produce the following vector:</data><data key="edge_extraction_method">minie</data><data key="edge_polarity">negative</data><data key="edge_modality">asserted</data></edge><edge id="oe_f55fa69b4f61fd81" source="e_db36aa209748ebc5" target="e_c4864c06dd486dbc"><data key="edge_predicate_raw">produce</data><data key="edge_assertion_id">a_bb13cdab2e844505</data><data key="edge_source_id">S52</data><data key="edge_source_url">https://www.first.org/cvss/v3.1/specification-document</data><data key="edge_chunk_id">S52_C16</data><data key="edge_json_path">None</data><data key="edge_evidence">The same example with the addition of “Exploitability: Functional, Remediation Level: Not Defined” and with the metrics in a non-preferred ordering would produce the following vector:</data><data key="edge_extraction_method">minie</data><data key="edge_polarity">negative</data><data key="edge_modality">asserted</data></edge><edge id="oe_f1a3a3af602b9605" source="e_b701b8d9e7fc2ef7" target="e_79a5b245db4e61f6"><data key="edge_predicate_raw">be defined as</data><data key="edge_assertion_id">a_2ac58ca34024724b</data><data key="edge_source_id">S52</data><data key="edge_source_url">https://www.first.org/cvss/v3.1/specification-document</data><data key="edge_chunk_id">S52_C16</data><data key="edge_json_path">None</data><data key="edge_evidence">They rely on helper functions defined as follows:</data><data key="edge_extraction_method">minie</data><data key="edge_polarity">positive</data><data key="edge_modality">asserted</data></edge><edge id="oe_bd7e1691a8945ebf" source="e_290d8da624d84fb0" target="e_79a5b245db4e61f6"><data key="edge_predicate_raw">rely on helper functions defined as</data><data key="edge_assertion_id">a_ffc86b16e878d65a</data><data key="edge_source_id">S52</data><data key="edge_source_url">https://www.first.org/cvss/v3.1/specification-document</data><data key="edge_chunk_id">S52_C16</data><data key="edge_json_path">None</data><data key="edge_evidence">They rely on helper functions defined as follows:</data><data key="edge_extraction_method">minie</data><data key="edge_polarity">positive</data><data key="edge_modality">asserted</data></edge><edge id="oe_3864919b98eb96cd" source="e_0dd1994901856e68" target="e_d2e639db66675776"><data key="edge_predicate_raw">is equal higher than</data><data key="edge_assertion_id">a_2f1a526901e17de5</data><data key="edge_source_id">S52</data><data key="edge_source_url">https://www.first.org/cvss/v3.1/specification-document</data><data key="edge_chunk_id">S52_C16</data><data key="edge_json_path">None</data><data key="edge_evidence">- Roundup returns the smallest number, specified to 1 decimal place, that is equal to or higher than its input</data><data key="edge_extraction_method">minie</data><data key="edge_polarity">positive</data><data key="edge_modality">asserted</data></edge><edge id="oe_09a1e39f5d34ae97" source="e_3062ac9cf856f91a" target="e_266db05dee124d64"><data key="edge_predicate_raw">be used in equations with</data><data key="edge_assertion_id">a_50911f591df3ee69</data><data key="edge_source_id">S52</data><data key="edge_source_url">https://www.first.org/cvss/v3.1/specification-document</data><data key="edge_chunk_id">S52_C16</data><data key="edge_json_path">None</data><data key="edge_evidence">Substitute Individual metrics used in equations with the associated constant listed in Section 7.4</data><data key="edge_extraction_method">minie</data><data key="edge_polarity">positive</data><data key="edge_modality">asserted</data></edge><edge id="oe_9de89307c3945505" source="e_016e1eb518d9e09e" target="e_aeb2050fed2c22c1"><data key="edge_predicate_raw">depends on sub-formulas for</data><data key="edge_assertion_id">a_621467cc7525171f</data><data key="edge_source_id">S52</data><data key="edge_source_url">https://www.first.org/cvss/v3.1/specification-document</data><data key="edge_chunk_id">S52_C16</data><data key="edge_json_path">None</data><data key="edge_evidence">The Environmental Score formula depends on sub-formulas for Modified Impact Sub-Score (MISS), ModifiedImpact, and ModifiedExploitability, all of which are defined below:</data><data key="edge_extraction_method">minie</data><data key="edge_polarity">positive</data><data key="edge_modality">asserted</data></edge><edge id="oe_b9c3f8d16ce0d07b" source="e_016e1eb518d9e09e" target="e_478d0e20bdfaeabd"><data key="edge_predicate_raw">depends on sub-formulas for</data><data key="edge_assertion_id">a_a4f77a3caf9a0aaa</data><data key="edge_source_id">S52</data><data key="edge_source_url">https://www.first.org/cvss/v3.1/specification-document</data><data key="edge_chunk_id">S52_C16</data><data key="edge_json_path">None</data><data key="edge_evidence">The Environmental Score formula depends on sub-formulas for Modified Impact Sub-Score (MISS), ModifiedImpact, and ModifiedExploitability, all of which are defined below:</data><data key="edge_extraction_method">minie</data><data key="edge_polarity">positive</data><data key="edge_modality">asserted</data></edge><edge id="oe_7850be853fb9450c" source="e_016e1eb518d9e09e" target="e_8711e986a53d88ec"><data key="edge_predicate_raw">depends on sub-formulas for</data><data key="edge_assertion_id">a_4167e1645bb951a1</data><data key="edge_source_id">S52</data><data key="edge_source_url">https://www.first.org/cvss/v3.1/specification-document</data><data key="edge_chunk_id">S52_C16</data><data key="edge_json_path">None</data><data key="edge_evidence">The Environmental Score formula depends on sub-formulas for Modified Impact Sub-Score (MISS), ModifiedImpact, and ModifiedExploitability, all of which are defined below:</data><data key="edge_extraction_method">minie</data><data key="edge_polarity">positive</data><data key="edge_modality">asserted</data></edge><edge id="oe_5b5f9be1167043b6" source="e_016e1eb518d9e09e" target="e_1c91229f829a5a65"><data key="edge_predicate_raw">depends on</data><data key="edge_assertion_id">a_3bff285a32c826ec</data><data key="edge_source_id">S52</data><data key="edge_source_url">https://www.first.org/cvss/v3.1/specification-document</data><data key="edge_chunk_id">S52_C16</data><data key="edge_json_path">None</data><data key="edge_evidence">The Environmental Score formula depends on sub-formulas for Modified Impact Sub-Score (MISS), ModifiedImpact, and ModifiedExploitability, all of which are defined below:</data><data key="edge_extraction_method">minie</data><data key="edge_polarity">positive</data><data key="edge_modality">asserted</data></edge><edge id="oe_242e22475d7fe467" source="e_b82be424e7d21f94" target="e_fa82717f64d9c8f8"><data key="edge_predicate_raw">is used in</data><data key="edge_assertion_id">a_04653d93577930c3</data><data key="edge_source_id">S52</data><data key="edge_source_url">https://www.first.org/cvss/v3.1/specification-document</data><data key="edge_chunk_id">S52_C17</data><data key="edge_json_path">None</data><data key="edge_evidence">Each metric value has an associated constant which is used in the formulas, as defined in Table 16</data><data key="edge_extraction_method">minie</data><data key="edge_polarity">positive</data><data key="edge_modality">asserted</data></edge><edge id="oe_19f3d15e7fcd9331" source="e_fa203e179c5c81e8" target="e_67f1649aba40d451"><data key="edge_predicate_raw">framed lookup table by</data><data key="edge_assertion_id">a_3b07d14b83c8b270</data><data key="edge_source_id">S52</data><data key="edge_source_url">https://www.first.org/cvss/v3.1/specification-document</data><data key="edge_chunk_id">S52_C17</data><data key="edge_json_path">None</data><data key="edge_evidence">To produce the CVSS v3.1 formula, the CVSS Special Interest Group (SIG) framed the lookup table by assigning metric values to real vulnerabilities, and a severity group (low, medium, high, critical)</data><data key="edge_extraction_method">minie</data><data key="edge_polarity">positive</data><data key="edge_modality">asserted</data></edge><edge id="oe_3a08cd1ac241be5d" source="e_fa203e179c5c81e8" target="e_5d29e070ca4b816a"><data key="edge_predicate_raw">framed lookup table to</data><data key="edge_assertion_id">a_be047796c2f4f33e</data><data key="edge_source_id">S52</data><data key="edge_source_url">https://www.first.org/cvss/v3.1/specification-document</data><data key="edge_chunk_id">S52_C17</data><data key="edge_json_path">None</data><data key="edge_evidence">To produce the CVSS v3.1 formula, the CVSS Special Interest Group (SIG) framed the lookup table by assigning metric values to real vulnerabilities, and a severity group (low, medium, high, critical)</data><data key="edge_extraction_method">minie</data><data key="edge_polarity">positive</data><data key="edge_modality">asserted</data></edge><edge id="oe_087e2642e64f6329" source="e_fa203e179c5c81e8" target="e_487f2d8360640345"><data key="edge_predicate_raw">framed</data><data key="edge_assertion_id">a_75116df916ec35dc</data><data key="edge_source_id">S52</data><data key="edge_source_url">https://www.first.org/cvss/v3.1/specification-document</data><data key="edge_chunk_id">S52_C17</data><data key="edge_json_path">None</data><data key="edge_evidence">To produce the CVSS v3.1 formula, the CVSS Special Interest Group (SIG) framed the lookup table by assigning metric values to real vulnerabilities, and a severity group (low, medium, high, critical)</data><data key="edge_extraction_method">minie</data><data key="edge_polarity">positive</data><data key="edge_modality">asserted</data></edge><edge id="oe_fb582c8701ea99b4" source="e_3c6f55c088fab9eb" target="e_9fc2c1fad4a8c45c"><data key="edge_predicate_raw">collaborated with Deloitte &amp; Touche LLP to adjust</data><data key="edge_assertion_id">a_252d65791e0f9f33</data><data key="edge_source_id">S52</data><data key="edge_source_url">https://www.first.org/cvss/v3.1/specification-document</data><data key="edge_chunk_id">S52_C17</data><data key="edge_json_path">None</data><data key="edge_evidence">Having defined the acceptable numeric ranges for each severity level, the SIG then collaborated with Deloitte &amp; Touche LLP to adjust formula parameters in order to align the metric combinations to the SIG's proposed severity ratings</data><data key="edge_extraction_method">minie</data><data key="edge_polarity">positive</data><data key="edge_modality">asserted</data></edge><edge id="oe_8b954f0300418882" source="e_3c6f55c088fab9eb" target="e_8204267493148c65"><data key="edge_predicate_raw">collaborated with Deloitte &amp; Touche LLP to adjust</data><data key="edge_assertion_id">a_6c2a3a36d3b65e24</data><data key="edge_source_id">S52</data><data key="edge_source_url">https://www.first.org/cvss/v3.1/specification-document</data><data key="edge_chunk_id">S52_C17</data><data key="edge_json_path">None</data><data key="edge_evidence">Having defined the acceptable numeric ranges for each severity level, the SIG then collaborated with Deloitte &amp; Touche LLP to adjust formula parameters in order to align the metric combinations to the SIG's proposed severity ratings</data><data key="edge_extraction_method">minie</data><data key="edge_polarity">positive</data><data key="edge_modality">asserted</data></edge><edge id="oe_6fe01da243fb291f" source="e_3c6f55c088fab9eb" target="e_9fc2c1fad4a8c45c"><data key="edge_predicate_raw">collaborated to adjust</data><data key="edge_assertion_id">a_4647e0b63b8a84ce</data><data key="edge_source_id">S52</data><data key="edge_source_url">https://www.first.org/cvss/v3.1/specification-document</data><data key="edge_chunk_id">S52_C17</data><data key="edge_json_path">None</data><data key="edge_evidence">Having defined the acceptable numeric ranges for each severity level, the SIG then collaborated with Deloitte &amp; Touche LLP to adjust formula parameters in order to align the metric combinations to the SIG's proposed severity ratings</data><data key="edge_extraction_method">minie</data><data key="edge_polarity">positive</data><data key="edge_modality">asserted</data></edge><edge id="oe_7f6bf7faeaa3a54c" source="e_3c6f55c088fab9eb" target="e_8204267493148c65"><data key="edge_predicate_raw">collaborated to adjust</data><data key="edge_assertion_id">a_e3c92526a7c5af00</data><data key="edge_source_id">S52</data><data key="edge_source_url">https://www.first.org/cvss/v3.1/specification-document</data><data key="edge_chunk_id">S52_C17</data><data key="edge_json_path">None</data><data key="edge_evidence">Having defined the acceptable numeric ranges for each severity level, the SIG then collaborated with Deloitte &amp; Touche LLP to adjust formula parameters in order to align the metric combinations to the SIG's proposed severity ratings</data><data key="edge_extraction_method">minie</data><data key="edge_polarity">positive</data><data key="edge_modality">asserted</data></edge><edge id="oe_7199a466898713cb" source="e_309a302506ac609b" target="e_7356d92070d51099"><data key="edge_predicate_raw">are derived from severity ranking of</data><data key="edge_assertion_id">a_8aad442257c2a13d</data><data key="edge_source_id">S52</data><data key="edge_source_url">https://www.first.org/cvss/v3.1/specification-document</data><data key="edge_chunk_id">S52_C18</data><data key="edge_json_path">None</data><data key="edge_evidence">In addition, some numeric scores may be omitted because the weights and calculations are derived from the severity ranking of metric combinations</data><data key="edge_extraction_method">minie</data><data key="edge_polarity">positive</data><data key="edge_modality">possible</data></edge><edge id="oe_8d164795d199383e" source="e_c17865531da3b697" target="e_7356d92070d51099"><data key="edge_predicate_raw">are derived from severity ranking of</data><data key="edge_assertion_id">a_3a1a9caeaeb0b2e8</data><data key="edge_source_id">S52</data><data key="edge_source_url">https://www.first.org/cvss/v3.1/specification-document</data><data key="edge_chunk_id">S52_C18</data><data key="edge_json_path">None</data><data key="edge_evidence">In addition, some numeric scores may be omitted because the weights and calculations are derived from the severity ranking of metric combinations</data><data key="edge_extraction_method">minie</data><data key="edge_polarity">positive</data><data key="edge_modality">possible</data></edge><edge id="oe_29a56664d5c063a6" source="e_7356d92070d51099" target="e_0a5e9171334653ee"><data key="edge_predicate_raw">deviate from</data><data key="edge_assertion_id">a_b06ad50a03d63708</data><data key="edge_source_id">S52</data><data key="edge_source_url">https://www.first.org/cvss/v3.1/specification-document</data><data key="edge_chunk_id">S52_C18</data><data key="edge_json_path">None</data><data key="edge_evidence">Further, in some cases, metric combinations may deviate from the desired severity threshold</data><data key="edge_extraction_method">minie</data><data key="edge_polarity">positive</data><data key="edge_modality">possible</data></edge><edge id="oe_5ad13ee9a638ea6d" source="e_df687578390b832a" target="e_7d44960f0247fa70"><data key="edge_predicate_raw">is available because</data><data key="edge_assertion_id">a_ee46adddccf7448f</data><data key="edge_source_id">S52</data><data key="edge_source_url">https://www.first.org/cvss/v3.1/specification-document</data><data key="edge_chunk_id">S52_C18</data><data key="edge_json_path">None</data><data key="edge_evidence">This is unavoidable and a simple correction is not readily available because adjustments made to one metric value or equation parameter in order to fix a deviation, cause other, potentially more severe deviations</data><data key="edge_extraction_method">minie</data><data key="edge_polarity">negative</data><data key="edge_modality">possible</data></edge><edge id="oe_cc645d07535b8dd4" source="e_b97141d40853ffbe" target="e_6dbe4bcf657c2d47"><data key="edge_predicate_raw">be made to</data><data key="edge_assertion_id">a_2f3ed07657d20b06</data><data key="edge_source_id">S52</data><data key="edge_source_url">https://www.first.org/cvss/v3.1/specification-document</data><data key="edge_chunk_id">S52_C18</data><data key="edge_json_path">None</data><data key="edge_evidence">This is unavoidable and a simple correction is not readily available because adjustments made to one metric value or equation parameter in order to fix a deviation, cause other, potentially more severe deviations</data><data key="edge_extraction_method">minie</data><data key="edge_polarity">negative</data><data key="edge_modality">possible</data></edge><edge id="oe_da444a7feeca2321" source="e_ff15eb2d1cc0b638" target="e_964bd9992c248607"><data key="edge_predicate_raw">was value By</data><data key="edge_assertion_id">a_7f5415afe1b49433</data><data key="edge_source_id">S52</data><data key="edge_source_url">https://www.first.org/cvss/v3.1/specification-document</data><data key="edge_chunk_id">S52_C18</data><data key="edge_json_path">None</data><data key="edge_evidence">By consensus, and as was done with CVSS v2.0, the acceptable deviation was a value of 0.5</data><data key="edge_extraction_method">minie</data><data key="edge_polarity">positive</data><data key="edge_modality">asserted</data></edge><edge id="oe_29ee4b8e22f5cd18" source="e_309a302506ac609b" target="e_280d8a0cc8bf0e3b"><data key="edge_predicate_raw">produce numeric score within</data><data key="edge_assertion_id">a_5b637d6f14b92eb0</data><data key="edge_source_id">S52</data><data key="edge_source_url">https://www.first.org/cvss/v3.1/specification-document</data><data key="edge_chunk_id">S52_C18</data><data key="edge_json_path">None</data><data key="edge_evidence">That is, all the metric value combinations used to derive the weights and calculation will produce a numeric score within its assigned severity level, or within 0.5 of that assigned level</data><data key="edge_extraction_method">minie</data><data key="edge_polarity">positive</data><data key="edge_modality">asserted</data></edge><edge id="oe_caa4c7d881228ec0" source="e_aa8dd8286cfcce2c" target="e_280d8a0cc8bf0e3b"><data key="edge_predicate_raw">produce numeric score within</data><data key="edge_assertion_id">a_636ab444229b45dc</data><data key="edge_source_id">S52</data><data key="edge_source_url">https://www.first.org/cvss/v3.1/specification-document</data><data key="edge_chunk_id">S52_C18</data><data key="edge_json_path">None</data><data key="edge_evidence">That is, all the metric value combinations used to derive the weights and calculation will produce a numeric score within its assigned severity level, or within 0.5 of that assigned level</data><data key="edge_extraction_method">minie</data><data key="edge_polarity">positive</data><data key="edge_modality">asserted</data></edge><edge id="oe_f45ccd7afa61d81b" source="e_6866d8b38df1e948" target="e_7b4f67c17e442588"><data key="edge_predicate_raw">be rated as</data><data key="edge_assertion_id">a_27b5e21645c55a62</data><data key="edge_source_id">S52</data><data key="edge_source_url">https://www.first.org/cvss/v3.1/specification-document</data><data key="edge_chunk_id">S52_C18</data><data key="edge_json_path">None</data><data key="edge_evidence">For example, a combination expected to be rated as a “high” may have a numeric score between 6.6 and 9.3</data><data key="edge_extraction_method">minie</data><data key="edge_polarity">positive</data><data key="edge_modality">possible</data></edge><edge id="oe_9214e110fd9cac10" source="e_e163460c91338b08" target="e_e728d16d31738f1e"><data key="edge_predicate_raw">is due to</data><data key="edge_assertion_id">a_59b5076326400c26</data><data key="edge_source_id">S52</data><data key="edge_source_url">https://www.first.org/cvss/v3.1/specification-document</data><data key="edge_chunk_id">S52_C18</data><data key="edge_json_path">None</data><data key="edge_evidence">This is due to small inaccuracies that occur when using floating point arithmetic</data><data key="edge_extraction_method">minie</data><data key="edge_polarity">positive</data><data key="edge_modality">asserted</data></edge><edge id="oe_815044ec64c0c16d" source="e_e728d16d31738f1e" target="e_83705eff70727464"><data key="edge_predicate_raw">occur when</data><data key="edge_assertion_id">a_248946f58715684a</data><data key="edge_source_id">S52</data><data key="edge_source_url">https://www.first.org/cvss/v3.1/specification-document</data><data key="edge_chunk_id">S52_C18</data><data key="edge_json_path">None</data><data key="edge_evidence">This is due to small inaccuracies that occur when using floating point arithmetic</data><data key="edge_extraction_method">minie</data><data key="edge_polarity">positive</data><data key="edge_modality">asserted</data></edge><edge id="oe_9270bcd5fc76786d" source="e_24fe0c38a43aa772" target="e_ff08da02a44a38de"><data key="edge_predicate_raw">take steps to avoid types of</data><data key="edge_assertion_id">a_b1a059c379aff748</data><data key="edge_source_id">S52</data><data key="edge_source_url">https://www.first.org/cvss/v3.1/specification-document</data><data key="edge_chunk_id">S52_C18</data><data key="edge_json_path">None</data><data key="edge_evidence">Implementers of CVSS formulas must take steps to avoid these types of problems</data><data key="edge_extraction_method">minie</data><data key="edge_polarity">positive</data><data key="edge_modality">asserted</data></edge><edge id="oe_2681ad11b4645cea" source="e_24fe0c38a43aa772" target="e_ff08da02a44a38de"><data key="edge_predicate_raw">be avoid types of</data><data key="edge_assertion_id">a_d3b2b0a4a459eb93</data><data key="edge_source_id">S52</data><data key="edge_source_url">https://www.first.org/cvss/v3.1/specification-document</data><data key="edge_chunk_id">S52_C18</data><data key="edge_json_path">None</data><data key="edge_evidence">Implementers of CVSS formulas must take steps to avoid these types of problems</data><data key="edge_extraction_method">minie</data><data key="edge_polarity">positive</data><data key="edge_modality">asserted</data></edge><edge id="oe_db4b36b34a097141" source="e_9662ce797ce8ed04" target="e_c07551c1a5dc2087"><data key="edge_predicate_raw">required</data><data key="edge_assertion_id">a_b6082d86efd849ce</data><data key="edge_source_id">S52</data><data key="edge_source_url">https://www.first.org/cvss/v3.1/specification-document</data><data key="edge_chunk_id">S52_C18</data><data key="edge_json_path">None</data><data key="edge_evidence">Different techniques may be required for different languages and platforms, and some may offer standard functionality that minimizes or fully avoids such problems</data><data key="edge_extraction_method">heuristic</data><data key="edge_polarity">positive</data><data key="edge_modality">possible</data></edge><edge id="oe_66e72fcf49bc9db7" source="e_ff6a44f2e94df2dd" target="e_2a9bcc55be633561"><data key="edge_predicate_raw">convert it to</data><data key="edge_assertion_id">a_f9ddaa176230f3cc</data><data key="edge_source_id">S52</data><data key="edge_source_url">https://www.first.org/cvss/v3.1/specification-document</data><data key="edge_chunk_id">S52_C18</data><data key="edge_json_path">None</data><data key="edge_evidence">A suggested approach is for the Roundup function to first multiply its input by 100,000 and convert it to the nearest integer</data><data key="edge_extraction_method">minie</data><data key="edge_polarity">positive</data><data key="edge_modality">asserted</data></edge><edge id="oe_6492c5d8e608c261" source="e_ff6a44f2e94df2dd" target="e_ad16450d4d7b98f8"><data key="edge_predicate_raw">convert</data><data key="edge_assertion_id">a_cf73a2235b2db050</data><data key="edge_source_id">S52</data><data key="edge_source_url">https://www.first.org/cvss/v3.1/specification-document</data><data key="edge_chunk_id">S52_C18</data><data key="edge_json_path">None</data><data key="edge_evidence">A suggested approach is for the Roundup function to first multiply its input by 100,000 and convert it to the nearest integer</data><data key="edge_extraction_method">minie</data><data key="edge_polarity">positive</data><data key="edge_modality">asserted</data></edge><edge id="oe_8f1907075de1e7ac" source="e_4b8f5cd9a2ae463d" target="e_8ac97c2d48c70556"><data key="edge_predicate_raw">is subject to floating</data><data key="edge_assertion_id">a_5c28e9e4c760b18b</data><data key="edge_source_id">S52</data><data key="edge_source_url">https://www.first.org/cvss/v3.1/specification-document</data><data key="edge_chunk_id">S52_C18</data><data key="edge_json_path">None</data><data key="edge_evidence">The rounding up should then be performed using only integer arithmetic, which is not subject to floating point inaccuracies</data><data key="edge_extraction_method">minie</data><data key="edge_polarity">negative</data><data key="edge_modality">asserted</data></edge><edge id="oe_47675121574df11b" source="e_99f76ce9f5fe44e5" target="e_c737b7b2fd84b12c"><data key="edge_predicate_raw">be in to use</data><data key="edge_assertion_id">a_b83fbdffa8dc10a8</data><data key="edge_source_id">S52</data><data key="edge_source_url">https://www.first.org/cvss/v3.1/specification-document</data><data key="edge_chunk_id">S52_C19</data><data key="edge_json_path">None</data><data key="edge_evidence">If false, the integer is incremented by 0.1 before being returned, though line 6 performs this on numbers ten times bigger than the result will be in order to use integer arithmetic</data><data key="edge_extraction_method">minie</data><data key="edge_polarity">positive</data><data key="edge_modality">asserted</data></edge><edge id="oe_9bfebe775f976dd9" source="e_29f374d3ae492bbc" target="e_a660fee5996f9ee6"><data key="edge_predicate_raw">recognizes</data><data key="edge_assertion_id">a_6df1d50ad0ce59f5</data><data key="edge_source_id">S52</data><data key="edge_source_url">https://www.first.org/cvss/v3.1/specification-document</data><data key="edge_chunk_id">S52_C19</data><data key="edge_json_path">No